window.CP_GLOSSARY = {"items":"<li id=\"lk-term-15-cfr\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-15-cfr\" data-alias=\"CFR|Code of Federal Regulations|15 CFR 742.6|part 742|part 740|part 734|supplement no. 5 to part 740|supplement no. 5\" data-text=\"15 cfr cfr, code of federal regulations, 15 cfr 742.6, part 742, part 740, part 734, supplement no. 5 to part 740, supplement no. 5 the code of federal regulations is the standing text of us rules, sorted into titles and parts. title 15 holds the export administration regulations. part 734 says what is subject to them. part 740 lists the license exceptions, and its supplement no. 5 lists the nineteen destinations eligible for license exception aia. part 742 sets the licensing policy for each control.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">15 CFR</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-300-mm\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-300-mm\" data-alias=\"300-millimeter|12-inch wafer|12-inch wafers|12-inch equivalent|200 mm|8-inch|8-inch-equivalent|450 mm|150 mm\" data-text=\"300 mm 300-millimeter, 12-inch wafer, 12-inch wafers, 12-inch equivalent, 200 mm, 8-inch, 8-inch-equivalent, 450 mm, 150 mm 300 mm is the diameter of the standard wafer, about twelve inches. older fabs run 200 mm, or 8-inch, wafers. the last increase in wafer size, to 300 mm, came in 2002.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">300 mm</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-3a090\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-3a090\" data-alias=\"3A090.a|3A090.b|3A090.c|4A090|4A090.a|ECCN 3A090|ECCN 4A090\" data-text=\"3a090 3a090.a, 3a090.b, 3a090.c, 4a090, 4a090.a, eccn 3a090, eccn 4a090 3a090 is the entry in the us export control list that covers advanced ai chips, defined by their total processing performance and performance density. its part c, added in december 2024, covers high bandwidth memory. 4a090 covers the computers built from the chips. a chip that falls under 3a090.a needs a license for china. the ai diffusion rule of january 2025 extended that requirement to every destination. but bis says it enforces the requirement only for country groups d:1, d:4 and d:5 and for firms headquartered in d:5 or macau.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">3A090</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-3b001\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-3b001\" data-alias=\"3B090|3B001.c.1|3B001.d.9|3B001.d.10|3B001.d.5\" data-text=\"3b001 3b090, 3b001.c.1, 3b001.d.9, 3b001.d.10, 3b001.d.5 3b001 is the main entry in the us export control list for chipmaking equipment. it is written as process specifications, such as an etch tool that cuts sideways or a deposition tool that coats holes more than 200 times deeper than they are wide. bis created 3b090 in october 2022 and folded it into 3b001 and 3b002 in october 2023 (88 fr 73424). the related 3d and 3e entries cover the software and know-how that go with the tools.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">3B001</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-abf\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-abf\" data-alias=\"Ajinomoto Build-up Film|build-up film|ABF build-up film|ABF substrate|ABF substrates\" data-text=\"abf ajinomoto build-up film, build-up film, abf build-up film, abf substrate, abf substrates the insulating film inside the substrate, the small layered board that the chips in a high-end package sit on. the board is built up in layers, and a sheet of this epoxy film, about 10 micrometers thick, separates each layer of copper wiring from the next. the japanese food company ajinomoto first developed it in 1999.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ABF</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-absolics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Absolics\" data-text=\"absolics covington united states private substrates and pcbs glass core substrates a subsidiary of korea's skc with a final chips act award of up to $75 million for a 120,000-square-foot glass core substrate plant in covington, georgia. as of october 2026, nist's project page expected the plant's production capacity to come online in 2027. nist says the glass substrates allow smaller, more densely packed and shorter connections, for faster and more energy-efficient computing. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Absolics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-accelerator\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-accelerator\" data-alias=\"AI accelerator|XPU\" data-text=\"accelerator ai accelerator, xpu, accelerators a chip built to do the one kind of arithmetic machine learning needs, multiplying large grids of numbers, far faster than a general-purpose processor can. nvidia's graphics processors, google's tensor processing units and amazon's trainium are all accelerators.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">accelerator</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-accton-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Accton Technology\" data-alias=\"Accton|智邦科技\" data-text=\"accton technology 智邦科技 hsinchu taiwan 2345.tw interconnect and networking white-box switch manufacturing a leading contract maker of white-box data center switches, building the hardware that hyperscalers run their own network software on. accton and its peers build most 800g switch boxes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Accton Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Interconnect</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-acm-research\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"ACM Research\" data-alias=\"盛美半导体\" data-text=\"acm research 盛美半导体 fremont united states acmr deposition and etch wafer cleaning, plating and packaging tools makes single-wafer cleaning systems using megasonic and bubble technologies, plus electroplating and advanced packaging tools. it is us-listed but manufactures and sells largely in china. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ACM Research</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-adeka\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Adeka\" data-alias=\"株式会社ADEKA\" data-text=\"adeka 株式会社adeka tokyo japan 4401.t photoresist and materials ald and cvd precursor chemicals makes the organometallic precursor molecules that atomic layer deposition tools use to build films one atomic layer at a time, including metal films and the high-k insulating layers in transistor gates. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Adeka</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-advanced-energy-industries\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Advanced Energy Industries\" data-alias=\"Advanced Energy\" data-text=\"advanced energy industries denver united states aeis equipment subsystems and components plasma power delivery and precision power makes the rf and dc power supplies and matching networks that strike and hold the plasmas used in etch and deposition, plus precision power for data-center equipment. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Advanced Energy Industries</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-advanced-packaging\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-advanced-packaging\" data-alias=\"2.5D packaging|3D packaging|2.5D|2.5D work|advanced packaging plants\" data-text=\"advanced packaging 2.5d packaging, 3d packaging, 2.5d, 2.5d work, advanced packaging plants the steps that assemble several finished chips into one component, sitting side by side or stacked, wired together closely enough to behave like a single larger chip. ordinary packaging only puts one chip into a protective case with contacts on the bottom.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">advanced packaging</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-advantest\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Advantest\" data-alias=\"株式会社アドバンテスト\" data-text=\"advantest 株式会社アドバンテスト tokyo japan 6857.t test soc and memory automated test equipment makes automated test equipment for logic and memory, including the v93000 platform used to test ai accelerators and the testers used for hbm. test time on ai dies is long and rising. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Advantest</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-aehr-test-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Aehr Test Systems\" data-alias=\"Aehr Test\" data-text=\"aehr test systems fremont united states aehr test wafer-level burn-in and reliability test makes wafer-level burn-in systems, which stress an entire wafer at high temperature and voltage to find early-life failures. they are used for silicon carbide, photonics and ai processors. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Aehr Test Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-affiliates-rule\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-affiliates-rule\" data-alias=\"50 percent rule|affiliates of listed entities\" data-text=\"affiliates rule affiliates rule, 50 percent rule, affiliates of listed entities the affiliates rule extended the entity list to any company anywhere in the world that is at least half owned by a listed firm. the aim was to stop a listed company from buying through a subsidiary. it took effect on 29 september 2025 and was suspended for a year six weeks later.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Affiliates Rule</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-agc-inc\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"AGC Inc.\" data-alias=\"AGC|AGC株式会社\" data-text=\"agc inc. agc株式会社 tokyo japan 5201.t photomasks euv and duv mask blanks, synthetic quartz the main supplier of euv mask blanks besides hoya, and a major maker of synthetic quartz substrates and photomask glass. agc says it is the only blank maker that produces euv blanks in-house from the glass material through the coating. its glass expertise comes from a much larger architectural and automotive glass business. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AGC Inc.</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ai-diffusion-rule\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ai-diffusion-rule\" data-alias=\"AI Diffusion|diffusion rule|Framework for Artificial Intelligence Diffusion|AI Diffusion framework\" data-text=\"ai diffusion rule ai diffusion, diffusion rule, framework for artificial intelligence diffusion, ai diffusion framework the ai diffusion rule, published on 15 january 2025, required a license to ship the most capable ai chips anywhere in the world. its exceptions allowed unlimited shipments to nineteen destinations, capped volumes elsewhere and none to china. it also controlled the weights of frontier ai models.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AI Diffusion rule</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-air-liquide\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Air Liquide\" data-text=\"air liquide paris france ai.pa chemicals and gases electronic specialty gases and advanced precursors supplies ultra-pure bulk gases, specialty etch and deposition gases and ald precursors, with on-site plants at most leading-edge fabs. it also supplies the fluorinated gases used in plasma etch. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Air Liquide</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-air-products\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Air Products\" data-text=\"air products allentown united states apd chemicals and gases bulk gases and on-site supply supplies bulk nitrogen, oxygen, hydrogen and helium to fabs through on-site generation, and specialty gases for etch and deposition. it is one of three global suppliers with the scale to serve a gigafab. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Air Products</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ajinomoto\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Ajinomoto\" data-alias=\"味の素株式会社\" data-text=\"ajinomoto 味の素株式会社 tokyo japan 2802.t substrates and pcbs abf build-up film dielectric makes ajinomoto build-up film (abf), the insulating layer between the copper layers of flip-chip package substrates. ajinomoto, a food company, developed the material from its amino acid chemistry. it told investors in june 2026 that abf has held over 95 percent of its market since its launch. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ajinomoto</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-alchip-technologies\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Alchip Technologies\" data-alias=\"Alchip|世芯電子\" data-text=\"alchip technologies 世芯電子 taipei taiwan 3661.tw ai accelerator vendors asic design services and backend implementation a design services firm that takes a customer's ai accelerator design through physical layout, tape-out and supply at tsmc, including 2.5d packaging. it is one of the few firms with production experience on reticle-limit ai dies, the largest chips a lithography tool can print in one exposure. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Alchip Technologies</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ald\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ald\" data-alias=\"atomic layer deposition\" data-text=\"ald atomic layer deposition a way of coating a chip a fraction of an atomic layer at a time. each pulse of gas sticks to the surface and stops once the surface is covered. so the film comes out the same thickness on the floor and on the walls of a hole more than 50 times deeper than it is wide.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ALD</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-alphawave-semi\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Alphawave Semi\" data-alias=\"Alphawave|Alphawave\" data-text=\"alphawave semi london united kingdom private ip and architecture high-speed serdes and chiplet connectivity ip supplies multi-gigabit connection ip (serdes, pcie, ucie and ethernet) that moves data between chiplets and between accelerators. qualcomm bought it to build data-center silicon. alphawave\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Alphawave Semi</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">IP and architecture</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-aws-trainium2\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"aws-trainium2\" data-alias=\"Trainium2|Trainium\" data-text=\"amazon (annapurna labs) trainium2 trainium n5 (per semianalysis) hbm3e, 24 gb per stack (per semianalysis)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Amazon (Annapurna Labs) Trainium2</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-aws-trainium3\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"aws-trainium3\" data-alias=\"Trainium3|Trainium\" data-text=\"amazon (annapurna labs) trainium3 trainium 3 nm (aws) hbm3e (12-high, 9.6 gbps pin speed)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Amazon (Annapurna Labs) Trainium3</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-amd\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"AMD\" data-text=\"amd santa clara united states amd ai accelerator vendors merchant gpus, server cpus and rack systems designs the instinct mi355x and mi400 accelerators and epyc server cpus. since buying zt systems in 2025 it also designs rack-scale ai systems. it is the only company other than nvidia that sells ai accelerators on the open market at scale. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AMD</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-amd-mi300x\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"amd-mi300x\" data-alias=\"Instinct MI300X|MI300X\" data-text=\"amd instinct mi300x cdna 3 (mi300 series) n5 (8 accelerator dies) plus n6 (4 i/o dies) hbm3\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AMD Instinct MI300X</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-amd-mi325x\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"amd-mi325x\" data-alias=\"Instinct MI325X|MI325X\" data-text=\"amd instinct mi325x cdna 3 (mi300 series) n5 (8 accelerator dies) plus n6 (4 i/o dies) hbm3e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AMD Instinct MI325X</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-amd-mi355x\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"amd-mi355x\" data-alias=\"Instinct MI355X|MI355X\" data-text=\"amd instinct mi355x cdna 4 (mi350 series) tsmc 3 nm (8 xcds) plus 6 nm (2 i/o dies) hbm3e (12-high)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AMD Instinct MI355X</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-amd-mi455x\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"amd-mi455x\" data-alias=\"Instinct MI455X|MI455X\" data-text=\"amd instinct mi455x cdna 5 (mi400 series) tsmc 2 nm plus 3 nm finfet (amd's own wording; it has not published the die-by-die split) hbm4\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AMD Instinct MI455X</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-amec\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"AMEC\" data-alias=\"中微公司\" data-text=\"amec 中微公司 shanghai china 688012.ss deposition and etch plasma etch and mocvd advanced micro-fabrication equipment makes capacitively and inductively coupled plasma etch systems used at chinese logic and memory fabs, plus mocvd reactors for leds. its etchers are the most competitive chinese tools at advanced nodes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AMEC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-amkor-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Amkor Technology\" data-alias=\"Amkor\" data-text=\"amkor technology tempe united states amkr advanced packaging and osat osat assembly, test and advanced packaging packages and tests other companies' chips at plants across asia. in its annual report for 2025 it described itself as the world's largest us-headquartered osat (outsourced semiconductor assembly and test firm). its new advanced packaging plant in peoria, arizona, was planned under an october 2024 memorandum of understanding with tsmc to serve customers of tsmc's arizona fabs. the two firms announced a long-term partnership in june 2026. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Amkor Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-amphenol\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Amphenol\" data-text=\"amphenol wallingford united states aph interconnect and networking high-speed connectors, cables and backplanes makes the high-speed connectors, cable assemblies and backplane systems that carry 112 gbps signals between boards in an ai rack. the nvlink spine that links the gpus in a rack-scale system is built from cables and connectors. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Amphenol</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Interconnect</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-annapurna-labs\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Annapurna Labs\" data-text=\"annapurna labs austin united states private ai accelerator vendors hyperscaler in-house training and inference silicon amazon's chip design arm. it designs the trainium training chips, inferentia inference chips and the nitro data processing units used across aws. trainium 3 is the current generation. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Annapurna Labs</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ansys\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Ansys\" data-text=\"ansys canonsburg united states private design and eda multiphysics, thermal and power integrity simulation makes the thermal, electromagnetic and structural simulation software used to model how a 1 kw accelerator package heats, warps and delivers power. its redhawk tool is the standard for power integrity signoff, the final check that power reaches every part of a chip as designed. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ansys</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Design and EDA</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-applied-materials\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Applied Materials\" data-text=\"applied materials santa clara united states amat deposition and etch deposition, epitaxy, cmp, implant and e-beam metrology makes tools for physical and chemical vapor deposition, epitaxy, ion implantation, chemical mechanical planarization and electron beam inspection. its tools cover more process steps than any other vendor's. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Applied Materials</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-arf\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-arf\" data-alias=\"argon fluoride|argon fluoride laser|193 nm|193-nanometer\" data-text=\"arf argon fluoride, argon fluoride laser, 193 nm, 193-nanometer arf stands for argon fluoride, the gas mixture inside the laser that gives deep ultraviolet lithography its 193-nanometer light. scanners, the machines that print each layer, use this light in two ways. a dry scanner shines it through air, and an immersion scanner through a thin film of water between lens and wafer, which prints finer lines. arf scanners print most of the fine layers on any chip made without extreme ultraviolet.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ArF</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-arista-networks\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Arista Networks\" data-text=\"arista networks santa clara united states anet interconnect and networking data center ethernet switches builds ethernet switches with high port counts, mostly on broadcom's tomahawk switch chips, that hyperscalers use for ai back-end networks as an alternative to infiniband. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Arista Networks</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Interconnect</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-arm-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Arm Holdings\" data-alias=\"Arm\" data-text=\"arm holdings cambridge united kingdom arm ip and architecture cpu instruction set and core ip licenses the cpu architecture and cores used in the host processors that feed data to ai accelerators. these include nvidia's grace and vera cpus and the arm cores inside the server chips that large cloud companies design. it also licenses the interconnect and system ip around them. in 2026 it launched the arm agi cpu, its first production chip. by may 2026, asrock, lenovo, quanta and supermicro were taking orders for servers built on it. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Arm Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">IP and architecture</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ase-technology-holding\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"ASE Technology Holding\" data-alias=\"ASE Technology|ASE|日月光投資控股\" data-text=\"ase technology holding 日月光投資控股 kaohsiung taiwan 3711.tw advanced packaging and osat osat assembly, test and fan-out packaging packages and tests chips for fabless firms and foundries, and is adding 2.5d and fan-out capacity for ai parts. it calls itself the leading provider of semiconductor assembly and testing services. it absorbed siliconware precision industries (spil) in 2018. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ASE Technology Holding</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-asetek\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Asetek\" data-text=\"asetek aalborg dk astk.ol power and cooling liquid cooling systems developed direct-to-chip liquid cooling for servers and high performance computing, licensing and supplying pumps, cold plates and rack coolant distribution units. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Asetek</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-asic\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-asic\" data-alias=\"application-specific integrated circuit|custom silicon|ASICs|custom accelerator|custom accelerators|custom chip|custom AI silicon|custom AI ASICs\" data-text=\"asic application-specific integrated circuit, custom silicon, asics, custom accelerator, custom accelerators, custom chip, custom ai silicon, custom ai asics a chip designed for one company's own workload and not sold on the open market. google's tensor processing unit and amazon's trainium are chips of this kind. an nvidia part sold to any customer is not.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ASIC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-asm-international\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"ASM International\" data-alias=\"ASM\" data-text=\"asm international almere netherlands asm.as deposition and etch atomic layer deposition and epitaxy makes atomic layer deposition (ald) tools, which grow films one atomic layer at a time. chipmakers use ald to build gate-all-around transistors and high-k dielectrics. asm also makes epitaxy and plasma-enhanced ald tools. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ASM International</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-asml\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"ASML\" data-text=\"asml veldhoven netherlands asml lithography euv and immersion duv scanners the only maker of extreme ultraviolet (euv) lithography scanners, the machines that print circuit patterns onto wafers. it also makes immersion deep ultraviolet (duv) scanners. chipmakers use its euv systems for the most critical layers on the most advanced logic and memory chips. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ASML</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Lithography</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-asmpt\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"ASMPT\" data-alias=\"ASM太平洋科技\" data-text=\"asmpt asm太平洋科技 singapore singapore 0522.hk advanced packaging and osat bonding, packaging and smt equipment supplies die bonders, thermocompression bonders, wire bonders and surface mount equipment, and is one of the firms competing to supply hybrid bonders for advanced packaging. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ASMPT</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-astera-labs\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Astera Labs\" data-text=\"astera labs san jose united states alab interconnect and networking pcie and cxl retimers, fabric switches makes the retimers, smart cable modules and fabric switches that keep pcie, cxl and ethernet links intact across the distances inside an ai rack. over those distances the signal degrades, and a retimer cleans it up and sends it on. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Astera Labs</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Interconnect</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-at-s\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"AT&amp;S\" data-text=\"at&amp;s leoben austria ats.vi substrates and pcbs ic substrates and high-end pcbs makes ic substrates and advanced pcbs, with abf substrate plants in chongqing, china, and kulim, malaysia. it is the only european firm in high-end ic substrates. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AT&amp;S</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ate\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ate\" data-alias=\"automated test equipment|automatic test equipment\" data-text=\"ate automated test equipment, automatic test equipment, tester automated test equipment, or ate, is the machine that connects to a chip, on the wafer or in its package, feeds it test patterns and checks whether the answers coming back are right. advantest's july 2026 investor guide counts test as the only manufacturing step that puts electrical signals through the chip.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ATE</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-at\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"AT\" data-alias=\"AT|Austrian\" data-text=\"austria at at austrian country the mask writers and substrates that two extreme chokepoints depend on\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Austria</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-axt\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"AXT\" data-text=\"axt fremont united states axti optics and photonics indium phosphide and gallium arsenide substrates makes the indium phosphide wafers that lasers for optical links are grown on. it is listed in the us but does all its manufacturing in china. china has required export permits for indium phosphide substrates since february 2025. in its filing for the quarter to june 2026, axt called the permits the most significant challenge it faces. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">AXT</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ayar-labs\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Ayar Labs\" data-text=\"ayar labs santa clara united states private optics and photonics in-package optical i/o builds optical input and output chiplets that put light directly into the processor package, replacing electrical serdes with fiber at the package edge. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ayar Labs</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-back-end\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-back-end\" data-alias=\"back end of line|BEOL|back-end|back-end fabs|back-end tools\" data-text=\"back end back end of line, beol, back-end, back-end fabs, back-end tools inside a fab, the back end of line is the second half of making a chip, the dozen or more layers of copper wiring stacked above the transistors. in the industry at large, the back end means everything after the wafer leaves the fab: grinding, dicing, packaging and test.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">back end</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-backside-power-delivery\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-backside-power-delivery\" data-alias=\"backside power|backside vias|PowerVia|Super Power Rail|backside power network\" data-text=\"backside power delivery backside power, backside vias, powervia, super power rail, backside power network backside power delivery moves a chip's power wiring to the underside of the wafer, so the wiring above the transistors carries only signals. after the transistors and signal wiring are built, the wafer is bonded face down to a second wafer and ground thin, and the power wires are built on its back. power arrives through tiny holes etched up from below, clear of the crowded top.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">backside power delivery</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-base-die\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-base-die\" data-alias=\"base chip|base logic die|logic base die|HBM base die\" data-text=\"base die base chip, base logic die, logic base die, hbm base die the base die is the bottom chip of an hbm stack, the one that manages the memory dies above it and talks to the processor on their behalf. for hbm4, sk hynix moved it to tsmc's advanced logic process so it can hold more functions. samsung's hbm4, shipped from february 2026, uses a 4 nm logic base die.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">base die</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-baseboard\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-baseboard\" data-alias=\"SXM|OAM|HGX|HGX baseboard\" data-text=\"baseboard baseboards, sxm, oam, hgx, hgx baseboard a baseboard is the large circuit board that eight accelerator modules bolt onto inside a server. it carries their power and the links between them. on nvidia's baseboard, switch chips let any two modules reach each other at full speed. nvidia's module is called sxm and its baseboard hgx. the open-standard equivalents are oam and ubb.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">baseboard</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-be-semiconductor-industries\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"BE Semiconductor Industries\" data-alias=\"BE Semiconductor|Besi\" data-text=\"be semiconductor industries duiven netherlands besi.as advanced packaging and osat die bonding and hybrid bonding equipment makes die attach, flip chip and thermocompression bonders, and leads in hybrid bonding tools that join dies copper pad to copper pad without solder. hybrid bonding is how logic dies are stacked in tsmc's soic and future hbm. besi\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">BE Semiconductor Industries</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-bga\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-bga\" data-alias=\"ball grid array|FC-BGA|flip-chip BGA\" data-text=\"bga ball grid array, fc-bga, flip-chip bga a way of joining a packaged chip to a circuit board using a grid of small solder balls across the underside in place of a row of pins around the edge. heating the assembly melts every ball at once into a permanent joint.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">BGA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-big-fund\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-big-fund\" data-alias=\"National Integrated Circuit Industry Investment Fund|National Integrated Circuit Fund|third chip fund|China's third chip fund\" data-text=\"big fund national integrated circuit industry investment fund, national integrated circuit fund, third chip fund, china's third chip fund the big fund is the nickname for china's national integrated circuit industry investment fund, the state vehicle that puts government money into chinese chip firms. its third round, raised in may 2024, came to 344 billion yuan, about $47 billion.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Big Fund</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-bill-of-materials\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-bill-of-materials\" data-alias=\"BOM\" data-text=\"bill of materials bom the itemized list of every purchased part in a finished product and what each part cost, the way a builder's invoice prices lumber, wiring and fixtures separately.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">bill of materials</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-biren-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Biren Technology\" data-alias=\"Biren|壁仞科技\" data-text=\"biren technology 壁仞科技 shanghai china 6082.hk ai accelerator vendors general-purpose gpus for ai training designs the br100 series general-purpose gpus for ai training and high-performance computing. export controls forced it to redesign its chips so they no longer use tsmc's most advanced processes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Biren Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-bis\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-bis\" data-alias=\"Bureau of Industry and Security|part of the US Department of Commerce\" data-text=\"bis bureau of industry and security, part of the us department of commerce the us government office that decides which technologies may be exported, to whom, and on what conditions. it writes the rules, issues the licenses and brings the enforcement cases.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">BIS</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-broadcom\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Broadcom\" data-text=\"broadcom palo alto united states avgo ai accelerator vendors custom ai asics (xpus) plus ethernet switch silicon co-designs and supplies the custom ai accelerators used by google, meta and other hyperscalers. it is also a leading seller of ethernet switch chips, including its tomahawk and jericho lines, and it supplies the pcie and serdes ip that connect ai clusters. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Broadcom</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-burn-in\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-burn-in\" data-alias=\"burn in|wafer-level burn-in|burn-in test\" data-text=\"burn-in burn in, wafer-level burn-in, burn-in test burn-in runs a chip hot and at raised voltage for minutes to days, so that any part that would fail early fails in the factory before it is shipped. it can run on the wafer or in the package. aehr, a maker of burn-in systems, says its lead ai customer is moving all burn-in for its accelerators from the system level to the wafer.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">burn-in</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-busbar\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-busbar\" data-alias=\"copper busbar|copper busbars\" data-text=\"busbar busbars, copper busbar, copper busbars a busbar is a thick bar of solid copper that carries large currents down the back of a rack to the boards that need them. an ordinary cable carrying the same current would overheat. at the 54 volts used inside racks such as the gb300 nvl72, a one-megawatt rack would need up to 200 kilograms of busbar, by nvidia's estimate.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">busbar</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-cadence-design-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Cadence Design Systems\" data-alias=\"Cadence Design|Cadence\" data-text=\"cadence design systems san jose united states cdns design and eda digital and analog implementation, verification, ip the second-largest of the three main makers of chip design (eda) software, strong in analog and custom design, simulation and hardware emulation. designers verify large ai chips on its palladium and protium emulation systems, which run a design in hardware before it goes to the fab. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cadence Design Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Design and EDA</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-cambricon-siyuan-590\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"cambricon-siyuan-590\" data-alias=\"Siyuan 590|590|MLU590\" data-text=\"cambricon siyuan 590 (mlu590) siyuan n+2 7 nm class hbm (generation not disclosed)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cambricon Siyuan 590 (MLU590)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-cambricon-technologies\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Cambricon Technologies\" data-alias=\"Cambricon|寒武纪\" data-text=\"cambricon technologies 寒武纪 beijing china 688256.ss ai accelerator vendors merchant ai training and inference chips designs the siyuan training and inference accelerators and sells them to chinese cloud operators. among listed chinese companies that design ai chips for sale to other firms, it is the largest. it is on the us entity list, which restricts us exports to it, and has its chips made in china. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cambricon Technologies</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-camtek\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Camtek\" data-text=\"camtek migdal haemek israel camt metrology and inspection advanced packaging inspection and metrology makes inspection and metrology systems for bumping, wafer-level packaging and hbm assembly, including tools that measure bump height and coplanarity across a wafer. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Camtek</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-ca\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"CA\" data-alias=\"CA|Canadian\" data-text=\"canada ca ca canadian country \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Canada</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-canon\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Canon\" data-alias=\"キヤノン株式会社\" data-text=\"canon キヤノン株式会社 tokyo japan 7751.t lithography i-line and krf steppers, nanoimprint lithography makes i-line and krf steppers for mature nodes and packaging. it is also commercializing nanoimprint lithography, which stamps a pattern into the resist. nanoimprint needs no euv optics, but it has defect and throughput limits. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Canon</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Lithography</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-capex\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-capex\" data-alias=\"capital expenditure|capital spending\" data-text=\"capex capital expenditure, capital spending money a company spends on long-lived physical assets such as buildings, machines and servers, as distinct from salaries and other running costs.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">capex</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-carl-zeiss-smt\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Carl Zeiss SMT\" data-alias=\"Zeiss\" data-text=\"carl zeiss smt oberkochen germany private equipment subsystems and components euv projection optics, illuminators and mask metrology makes the multilayer mirrors and projection optics inside every euv scanner, polished to atomic-scale flatness, plus the larger anamorphic optics for high-na euv scanners. zeiss smt exclusively supplies the optics for asml's euv scanners. it also makes aims euv, which checks how a mask will print under the scanner's own imaging conditions, and merit systems that repair masks. zeiss\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Carl Zeiss SMT</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-case-by-case-review\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-case-by-case-review\" data-alias=\"case by case|case-by-case|reviewed case by case\" data-text=\"case-by-case review case by case, case-by-case, reviewed case by case case-by-case review means a license is required and each application is judged on its own, with no presumption either way. since january 2026 nvidia's h200 and amd's mi325x have been reviewed this way for china, with conditions attached to each approval.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">case-by-case review</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-celestica\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Celestica\" data-text=\"celestica toronto canada cls systems and servers hyperscale hardware and switch manufacturing builds servers, storage and 800g ethernet switches for hyperscalers on a contract basis, and has grown strongly with ai networking demand. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Celestica</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-cerebras-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Cerebras Systems\" data-alias=\"Cerebras\" data-text=\"cerebras systems sunnyvale united states cbrs ai accelerator vendors wafer-scale ai processors builds the wafer scale engine, a single processor that covers almost an entire 300 mm wafer. it keeps its memory on the chip as sram instead of using separate hbm stacks. it sells systems and inference cloud capacity. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cerebras Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-cerebras-wse3-turbo\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"cerebras-wse3-turbo\" data-alias=\"WSE-3 Turbo|WSE-3|CS-4|Wafer Scale Engine\" data-text=\"cerebras wse-3 turbo (cs-4) wafer scale engine n5 on-wafer sram only, no hbm\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cerebras WSE-3 Turbo (CS-4)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-cn\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"CN\" data-alias=\"CN|PRC|Chinese\" data-text=\"china cn cn prc chinese country the largest market, now building its own tools, memory and chips\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">China</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-chip\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-chip\" data-alias=\"semiconductor chip\" data-text=\"chip chips, microchip, microchips, semiconductor chip a chip is a small rectangle of silicon, usually smaller than a fingernail, that carries a complete electronic circuit, often made of billions of transistors. it is cut from a wafer after the circuit has been built up on it layer by layer.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">chip</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-chipbond-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Chipbond Technology\" data-alias=\"Chipbond|頎邦科技\" data-text=\"chipbond technology 頎邦科技 hsinchu taiwan 6147.two advanced packaging and osat gold bumping and display driver packaging specializes in gold and copper bumping and chip-on-film packaging, mainly for display driver ics, and provides bumping services used in wider advanced packaging flows. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Chipbond Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-chiplet\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-chiplet\" data-text=\"chiplet chiplets one of several smaller pieces that a chip has been deliberately split into, each manufactured separately and then wired back together inside a single package. a chip built this way is like a house assembled from prefabricated rooms.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">chiplet</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-chips-act\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-chips-act\" data-alias=\"CHIPS and Science Act|CHIPS incentives|CHIPS money|CHIPS Act grants|CHIPS authorization|CHIPS Act support|CHIPS award\" data-text=\"chips act chips and science act, chips incentives, chips money, chips act grants, chips authorization, chips act support, chips award the chips and science act authorized about $52.7 billion of us federal money for the chip industry. by july 2025 the commerce department had awarded $30.9 billion of direct funding to 19 companies for 40 projects.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CHIPS Act</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-chokepoint\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-chokepoint\" data-text=\"chokepoint chokepoints a step in the supply chain where so few firms or countries can do the work that losing one of them stops everybody.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">chokepoint</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-chroma-ate\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Chroma ATE\" data-alias=\"致茂電子\" data-text=\"chroma ate 致茂電子 taoyuan taiwan 2360.tw test test instruments, handlers and system-level test makes automated test equipment, power test instruments and system-level test (slt) platforms, including the burn-in and slt systems used for ai processors and power components. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Chroma ATE</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-cisco-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Cisco Systems\" data-alias=\"Cisco\" data-text=\"cisco systems san jose united states csco interconnect and networking networking systems and silicon one switch chips sells data center switches and routers and designs its own silicon one switch chips, giving it a second in-house alternative to switch chips bought from chip vendors for ai networks. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cisco Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Interconnect</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-cmos\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-cmos\" data-alias=\"complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor|complementary MOS\" data-text=\"cmos complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor, complementary mos cmos, short for complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor, is the standard way of building digital circuits from pairs of transistors. each n-type transistor, which switches on when the voltage on its gate is high, is matched with a p-type transistor, which switches on when that voltage is low. in either logic state one side of the circuit is off, so little current flows except while it switches.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CMOS</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-cmp\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-cmp\" data-alias=\"chemical mechanical polishing|chemical mechanical planarization|polishing slurry|polishing slurries|CMP slurry|CMP pads\" data-text=\"cmp chemical mechanical polishing, chemical mechanical planarization, polishing slurry, polishing slurries, slurry, slurries, cmp slurry, cmp pads, planarization chemical mechanical polishing, or cmp, rubs a wafer's surface flat again after each new layer goes on, using a pad and a liquid full of fine grit called slurry. without it the next layer would be printed on a surface too bumpy to focus on.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CMP</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-co-packaged-optics\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-co-packaged-optics\" data-alias=\"co-packaged|co-packaging|CPO|plug-in modules|plug-in optics\" data-text=\"co-packaged optics co-packaged, co-packaging, cpo, plug-in modules, plug-in optics co-packaged optics puts the parts that turn electrical signals into light and back onto the switch chip's own package instead of into plug-in modules at the front of the box. broadcom keeps the lasers that supply the light in separate modules that can be replaced in the field.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">co-packaged optics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-coater-developer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-coater-developer\" data-alias=\"coater-developer|coater and developer|coater/developer track|track tool|track tools\" data-text=\"coater/developer coater-developer, coater and developer, coater/developer track, track tool, track tools a coater/developer, or track, is the machine that spins a thin coat of photoresist onto the wafer before it enters the scanner. after the wafer comes out, the same machine washes away the exposed parts, so every printed layer passes through it twice.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">coater/developer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-coefficient-of-thermal-expansion\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-coefficient-of-thermal-expansion\" data-alias=\"CTE|thermal expansion|expansion mismatch|low-CTE\" data-text=\"coefficient of thermal expansion cte, thermal expansion, expansion mismatch, low-cte the coefficient of thermal expansion is how much a material expands for each degree it warms. silicon barely expands and epoxy expands more, so when the two are bonded and heated, the package bends.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">coefficient of thermal expansion</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-coherent-corp\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Coherent Corp\" data-alias=\"Coherent\" data-text=\"coherent corp saxonburg united states cohr optics and photonics lasers, optical components and transceivers makes indium phosphide lasers, vcsels, optical components and transceiver modules. it is one of the few module makers that also makes the laser chips inside them, including at an indium phosphide wafer fab in sherman, texas. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Coherent Corp</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-cohu\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Cohu\" data-text=\"cohu poway united states cohu test test handlers, contactors and interface makes the handlers that move devices in and out of testers, along with thermal subsystems, contactors and interface boards. for ai chips that run hot, handling and thermal control are as important as the tester itself. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cohu</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-comet-group\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Comet Group\" data-alias=\"Comet\" data-text=\"comet group flamatt switzerland cotn.sw equipment subsystems and components rf impedance matching and x-ray inspection makes rf power delivery components, vacuum capacitors and impedance matching networks for plasma tools, and x-ray systems used to inspect solder joints and packages. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Comet Group</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-compute-threshold\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-compute-threshold\" data-alias=\"training compute threshold\" data-text=\"compute threshold training compute threshold a limit set on the amount of arithmetic used to train an ai model. it counts operations, whichever chips run them. the ai diffusion rule of january 2025 made one an export control. eccn 4e091 covers &quot;'parameters' for an artificial intelligence model trained utilizing 10^26 or more 'operations'&quot;. the rules require a license to send such parameters to every destination worldwide (15 cfr 742.6(a)(13)). article 51(2) of the eu ai act sets europe's line ten times lower. it presumes a model has high-impact capabilities when the cumulative computation used for training is &quot;greater than 10^25&quot; floating point operations.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">compute threshold</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-concentration\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-concentration\" data-alias=\"concentration band\" data-text=\"concentration concentration band a four-band judgment of how many firms could credibly supply a stage today, taken at the narrowest step inside it. extreme means three or fewer, or one firm holding more than half the stage. high means four to six, with the top two taking most of the revenue. moderate means seven or more, none of them dominant. low means many, with the scarce input something another industry sells at volume. where a figure exists for the top country's share of the segment, it is a second check. when the two disagree, the supplier count wins.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Concentration</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-consignee\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-consignee\" data-alias=\"named consignee|named consignees|ultimate consignee\" data-text=\"consignee consignees, named consignee, named consignees, ultimate consignee the consignee is the party a shipment is sent to, the name on the export license. a named consignee, such as g42 in the united arab emirates, can receive controlled chips on the terms attached to its own name.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">consignee</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-coolit-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"CoolIT Systems\" data-alias=\"CoolIT\" data-text=\"coolit systems calgary canada private power and cooling direct liquid cooling makes direct-to-chip liquid cooling cold plates, coolant distribution units and manifolds for servers, and is one of the specialists the server odms buy from. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CoolIT Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-corning\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Corning\" data-text=\"corning corning united states glw optics and photonics optical fiber, cable and glass substrates makes the optical fiber and cabling that connect data center halls and campuses, and develops glass substrates for semiconductor packaging. it also holds the majority stake in hemlock semiconductor. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Corning</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-country-groups\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-country-groups\" data-alias=\"Country Group|Country Group D:5|D:5|A:5|D:1|D:3|D:4|arms-embargoed countries\" data-text=\"country groups country group, country group d:5, d:5, a:5, d:1, d:3, d:4, arms-embargoed countries the groups that us export rules sort the world's countries into, published as supplement no. 1 to 15 cfr part 740. a:5 and a:6 list close partners. d:1, d:4 and d:5 are the national security, missile technology and arms-embargoed groups. e:1 and e:2 are the most restricted. a country can be in several groups at once, and the license requirement usually depends on which.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Country Groups</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-cowos\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-cowos\" data-alias=\"chip on wafer on substrate\" data-text=\"cowos chip on wafer on substrate tsmc's method for mounting logic chips and memory stacks side by side on a shared interposer, a layer of fine wiring, then mounting that interposer on a rigid base board. in cowos-s the interposer is one piece of silicon. in cowos-l, used for nvidia's blackwell and rubin, it is layers of fine copper wiring with small embedded silicon bridges. nearly every high-end ai accelerator is built this way.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CoWoS</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-credo-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Credo Technology\" data-alias=\"Credo\" data-text=\"credo technology san jose united states crdo interconnect and networking serdes, active electrical cables and optical dsps supplies high-speed serdes ip, active electrical cables and retimers used for 400g and 800g links inside and between ai racks. its active electrical cables are copper and carry signals up to 7 meters between neighboring racks, replacing optics over those distances at lower power. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Credo Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Interconnect</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-critical-dimension\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-critical-dimension\" data-alias=\"critical dimensions|CD-SEM|critical-dimension|line width|line-width|line widths\" data-text=\"critical dimension critical dimensions, cd, cd-sem, critical-dimension, line width, line-width, line widths the critical dimension is the width of the finest printed feature on a layer. a cd-sem is an electron microscope built to measure it across a wafer without cutting anything.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">critical dimension</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-csis\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-csis\" data-alias=\"Center for Strategic and International Studies\" data-text=\"csis center for strategic and international studies csis, the center for strategic and international studies, is a bipartisan, nonprofit policy research organization in washington, d.c., founded in 1962. its technology researchers publish assessments of china's chipmaking and of us export controls.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CSIS</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-cvd\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-cvd\" data-alias=\"chemical vapor deposition|PECVD|plasma-enhanced chemical vapor deposition|MOCVD|CVD precursor\" data-text=\"cvd chemical vapor deposition, pecvd, plasma-enhanced chemical vapor deposition, mocvd, cvd precursor, precursor, precursors chemical vapor deposition, or cvd, grows a film by flowing gases over a hot wafer so they react on its surface and leave a solid layer behind. the plasma-enhanced version, pecvd, runs cooler. the gases used are called precursors.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CVD</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-cxmt\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"CXMT\" data-alias=\"长鑫存储\" data-text=\"cxmt 长鑫存储 hefei china 688825.ss memory chinese dram and early hbm china's only significant dram maker, producing ddr4 and ddr5 and working toward hbm. it has scaled capacity quickly enough to move commodity dram prices. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">CXMT</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-cymer\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Cymer\" data-text=\"cymer san diego united states private lithography duv excimer light sources and euv tin plasma sources builds the light sources for lithography: excimer lasers for duv scanners and the laser-produced tin plasma source that generates 13.5 nm euv light. the euv source is the hardest subsystem in the machine. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Cymer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Lithography</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-d-matrix\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"d-Matrix\" data-text=\"d-matrix santa clara united states private ai accelerator vendors digital in-memory compute inference accelerators builds inference accelerators that compute inside sram, which cuts the energy spent moving model weights. they are aimed at batch inference, which runs many requests to a large language model at once. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">d-Matrix</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-dai-nippon-printing\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Dai Nippon Printing\" data-alias=\"大日本印刷株式会社\" data-text=\"dai nippon printing 大日本印刷株式会社 tokyo japan 7912.t photomasks photomasks and lead frames makes photomasks, including euv masks, plus lead frames and other electronic components. like toppan, it applied the precision of commercial printing to semiconductor patterning. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Dai Nippon Printing</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-de-minimis\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-de-minimis\" data-text=\"de minimis the share of controlled american content a foreign-made item may contain before us export rules, the ear, apply to it. under 15 cfr 734.4 the general threshold is 25 percent of the item's value, and 10 percent for the most restricted destinations. above the threshold the item falls under the ear, and below it the item does not.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">de minimis</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-defect-density\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-defect-density\" data-alias=\"defects per square centimeter\" data-text=\"defect density d0, defects per square centimeter the average number of chip-killing flaws per square centimeter of processed wafer. it is a fab's quality score, inferred from how many chips come out working.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">defect density</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-dell-technologies\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Dell Technologies\" data-alias=\"Dell\" data-text=\"dell technologies round rock united states dell systems and servers ai servers and integrated systems sells poweredge ai servers and integrated rack systems to enterprises and ai cloud operators, adding services, financing and deployment on top of the hardware. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Dell Technologies</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-delta-electronics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Delta Electronics\" data-alias=\"Delta|台達電子\" data-text=\"delta electronics 台達電子 taipei taiwan 2308.tw power and cooling power supplies, power shelves and thermal systems a global leader in switching power supplies and a maker of the power shelves and busbars used in ai racks, plus fans, cold plates and coolant distribution units. it supplies equipment for the 800-volt dc power architecture that nvidia has moved toward. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Delta Electronics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-denial-order\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-denial-order\" data-text=\"denial order an order from bis that shuts a named party out of trade in us-controlled items, as a sanction or a protective measure, with no license policy involved. under 15 cfr 764.3 it restricts the party's exports, reexports and in-country transfers of items subject to the ear, and its access to them. it can also suspend or revoke the party's outstanding licenses. there is no application to file. orders can be issued outright or suspended and later activated.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">denial order</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-deposition\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-deposition\" data-text=\"deposition adding a layer of material to a wafer. machines knock atoms off a solid target so they land on the surface, react gases at the surface so a film grows there, or plate metal out of a liquid. it is how the insulators, the wires and the parts of each transistor are built up.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">deposition</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-dicing\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-dicing\" data-alias=\"wafer dicing|dicing saw|dicing saws|wafer grinding|wafer grinders|wafer thinning\" data-text=\"dicing wafer dicing, dicing saw, dicing saws, grinding, wafer grinding, grinders, wafer grinders, thinning, wafer thinning dicing cuts a finished wafer into its individual dies with a diamond saw or a laser. grinding, done first, thins the wafer from the back, and for stacked memory it goes on until the copper columns inside the dies come through.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">dicing</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-die\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-die\" data-alias=\"singular of dice\" data-text=\"die singular of dice, dies one rectangular chip cut out of a wafer. hundreds are printed side by side on the same disc and then sliced apart, and each separated rectangle is a die.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">die</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-dielectric\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-dielectric\" data-alias=\"dielectric etch|dielectric properties|insulating layer\" data-text=\"dielectric dielectrics, dielectric etch, dielectric properties, insulator, insulating layer a dielectric is an insulator: a material that does not conduct, such as the glassy oxides and nitrides between a chip's wires or the epoxy in a package substrate. dielectric etch cuts holes and trenches through those insulating layers so the wires can be laid in.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">dielectric</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-disco-corporation\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Disco Corporation\" data-alias=\"Disco|株式会社ディスコ\" data-text=\"disco corporation 株式会社ディスコ tokyo japan 6146.t advanced packaging and osat wafer dicing, grinding and laser cutting makes the dicing saws, laser dicers and back-grinders that cut wafers into dies and thin them for stacking. hbm and other 3d stacks need wafers thinned to tens of micrometers. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Disco Corporation</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-dongjin-semichem\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Dongjin Semichem\" data-alias=\"동진쎄미켐\" data-text=\"dongjin semichem 동진쎄미켐 seoul south korea 005290.kq photoresist and materials photoresist and thinner for korean fabs korea's main domestic photoresist maker, covering i-line, krf and arf grades with euv under development. it expanded after japan restricted exports of key materials to korea in 2019. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Dongjin Semichem</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-dram\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-dram\" data-alias=\"dynamic random-access memory\" data-text=\"dram dynamic random-access memory a computer's main working memory. each bit is a charge held in a microscopic capacitor that leaks, so the chip has to refresh its contents constantly. it forgets everything when the power goes off.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">DRAM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-duv\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-duv\" data-alias=\"deep ultraviolet|deep-ultraviolet|DUV scanner|DUV scanners|DUV tools\" data-text=\"duv deep ultraviolet, deep-ultraviolet, duv scanner, duv scanners, duv tools chipmaking light from gas lasers, at 248 or 193 nanometers, and the machines that print with it, which still make up most lithography tools. filling the gap between lens and wafer with water sharpens the image, a method called immersion.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">DUV</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ear\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ear\" data-alias=\"Export Administration Regulations\" data-text=\"ear export administration regulations the body of us rules that governs the export of commercial goods, software and technology, including items with both civilian and military uses. the bureau of industry and security writes and enforces them. they run from 15 cfr part 730 to part 774. part 734 sets what they cover, part 742 the license requirements, part 744 the end-use and end-user controls, part 740 the exceptions and part 764 the penalties.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">EAR</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ear99\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ear99\" data-text=\"ear99 the label for an item that falls under us export rules but is not named on the commerce control list, the catalog of controlled items. the label is defined at 15 cfr 734.3(c). it is a catch-all category, but an ear99 item still needs a license if it is going to a listed party or a controlled end use.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">EAR99</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-eaton\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Eaton\" data-text=\"eaton dublin ireland etn power and cooling power distribution, switchgear and ups makes switchgear, busway, transformers, ups systems and power distribution units for data centers, a segment that has become supply constrained as ai campuses scale. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Eaton</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-eccn\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-eccn\" data-alias=\"Export Control Classification Number\" data-text=\"eccn export control classification number the catalog number that us export rules assign to a controlled item, similar to a customs tariff code but for security-sensitive technology. number 3a090 covers advanced computing chips and 3b001 covers chipmaking equipment.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ECCN</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-eda\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-eda\" data-alias=\"electronic design automation|chip design software\" data-text=\"eda electronic design automation, chip design software the software that turns a description of what a chip should do into the exact pattern of shapes to be printed on silicon. it also proves the design will work before anyone commits money to masks and wafers.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">EDA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-edwards-vacuum\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Edwards Vacuum\" data-text=\"edwards vacuum burgess hill united kingdom private equipment subsystems and components dry vacuum pumps and abatement systems supplies the dry pumps that hold process chambers at vacuum and the abatement systems that destroy the toxic and greenhouse gases leaving them. a leading-edge fab runs thousands of pumps continuously. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Edwards Vacuum</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-electron-beam\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-electron-beam\" data-alias=\"electron-beam|e-beam|electron beams|multi-beam|e-beam inspection|electron-beam metrology\" data-text=\"electron beam electron-beam, e-beam, electron beams, multi-beam, multibeam, e-beam inspection, electron-beam metrology an electron beam is a stream of electrons focused to a spot far smaller than any spot of light. mask shops use it to write the pattern onto a photomask, and fabs use it to inspect wafers for defects light cannot see and to measure line widths. a multi-beam tool fires many beams at once, because a single beam is slow.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">electron beam</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-electronic-grade\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-electronic-grade\" data-alias=\"electronic grade|semiconductor-grade|semiconductor grade|solar-grade|solar grade\" data-text=\"electronic-grade electronic grade, semiconductor-grade, semiconductor grade, solar-grade, solar grade electronic-grade, or semiconductor-grade, silicon is refined until its metal impurities are no more than a few parts per billion, pure enough for chips. solar-grade silicon is a less pure grade made for solar cells.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">electronic-grade</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-emea\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-emea\" data-text=\"emea emea stands for europe, the middle east and africa, one region in the breakdowns that companies publish of where their sales go.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">EMEA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-empyrean-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Empyrean Technology\" data-alias=\"Empyrean|华大九天\" data-text=\"empyrean technology 华大九天 beijing china 301269.sz design and eda analog and flat-panel eda, china domestic substitution a chinese eda vendor. in its 2025 annual report, filed in april 2026, it says it has complete design tool chains for analog, memory, radio-frequency and flat-panel display circuits. the same report says its digital tools cover 80 percent of the main tools for digital design. it is the main company in china's effort to replace the american eda tools that export controls can cut off. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Empyrean Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Design and EDA</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-end-use-and-end-user-controls\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-end-use-and-end-user-controls\" data-alias=\"end user|end users|end-user|end use|military end user\" data-text=\"end-use and end-user controls end user, end users, end-user, end use, military end user export rules that depend on who the buyer is and what they will do with the item, whatever the item is. the same tool can ship freely to one customer and need a license that will be refused for another.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">end-use and end-user controls</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-entegris\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Entegris\" data-text=\"entegris billerica united states entg chemicals and gases filtration, wafer handling and process chemistries makes the filters, purifiers, fluid handling components, wafer carriers and specialty coatings that keep contamination out of a fab. it also sells cmp slurries, a business it gained by buying cmc materials. fabs use up its products continuously. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Entegris</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-entity-list\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-entity-list\" data-alias=\"entity-list|Entity-Listed|Entity List additions|listed entity|listed entities|listed firm|listed firms\" data-text=\"entity list entity-list, entity-listed, entity list additions, listed entity, listed entities, listed firm, listed firms a published list of foreign companies, institutes and individuals. anyone anywhere, american or foreign, needs a license to send them an item subject to the ear. each entry states its own license review policy. most carry a presumption of denial, meaning the license will normally be refused. smic's entry, as amended in december 2024, is a presumption of denial for all items. the exception is tools designed for 200 mm wafer production and bound for a 200 mm plant, which are reviewed case by case. the list is supplement no. 4 to 15 cfr part 744, and the license requirement is in 15 cfr 744.11.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Entity List</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-eoptolink-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Eoptolink Technology\" data-alias=\"Eoptolink|新易盛\" data-text=\"eoptolink technology 新易盛 chengdu china 300502.sz optics and photonics high-speed optical transceivers a major supplier of 400g, 800g and 1.6t optical transceivers to cloud and ai data center operators, and one of the fastest growing chinese optics firms. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Eoptolink Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-epitaxy\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-epitaxy\" data-alias=\"epitaxial wafer|epitaxial wafers|epitaxial layer\" data-text=\"epitaxy epitaxial, epitaxial wafer, epitaxial wafers, epitaxial layer, epi epitaxy grows a fresh layer of crystal on top of a wafer, atom by atom, so the new layer continues the crystal beneath it with almost no flaws. an epitaxial wafer is a plain wafer with that extra layer, and the transistors are built in it.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">epitaxy</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-eswin-material\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Eswin Material\" data-alias=\"西安奕材\" data-text=\"eswin material 西安奕材 xi'an china 688783.ss silicon and wafers 300 mm polished and epitaxial wafers mainland china's largest maker of 300 mm wafers. it says it ranked sixth in the world with about 7.7 percent of global 300 mm shipments in the first half of 2026, up from about 6 percent in 2024. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Eswin Material</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-etch\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-etch\" data-alias=\"dry etch\" data-text=\"etch etching, etched, etches, etcher, etchers, dry etch removing material from a wafer wherever the printed pattern says it should not be. most etch tools turn a gas into a plasma whose ions and fragments eat one material and leave the material beside it alone.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">etch</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-etched\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Etched\" data-text=\"etched cupertino united states private ai accelerator vendors transformer-specific asic designing sohu, a custom chip (asic) that hard-wires the transformer architecture into silicon. the transformer is the model design behind large language models. sohu gives up flexibility to do more work per watt. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Etched</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ethernet\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ethernet\" data-alias=\"Ultra Ethernet|Spectrum-X|Spectrum-X Ethernet|Tomahawk|Ethernet switch\" data-text=\"ethernet ultra ethernet, spectrum-x, spectrum-x ethernet, tomahawk, ethernet switch ethernet is the ordinary networking standard of offices and the internet, now made fast and reliable enough to link the servers of an ai cluster. its switch chips, such as broadcom's tomahawk, route traffic between thousands of accelerators.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ethernet</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-euv\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-euv\" data-alias=\"extreme ultraviolet|extreme-ultraviolet|EUV scanner|EUV scanners|extreme ultraviolet lithography\" data-text=\"euv extreme ultraviolet, extreme-ultraviolet, euv scanner, euv scanners, extreme ultraviolet lithography the light that prints the finest layers of every leading-edge chip, and the machines that print with it. its wavelength is 13.5 nanometers, and shorter light draws finer lines. air and glass both absorb it, so the machine works in a vacuum and carries the light on mirrors. the light comes from droplets of molten tin, 50,000 a second, each hit twice by a laser.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">EUV</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ev-group\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"EV Group\" data-text=\"ev group st. florian am inn austria private advanced packaging and osat wafer bonding and nanoimprint lithography makes wafer bonding systems, including the fusion and hybrid bonding tools used for 3d integration, plus lithography systems for advanced packaging and photonics. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">EV Group</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-export-control\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-export-control\" data-alias=\"export controls|export licensing|export license|export licenses|export licence|export licences|export-control\" data-text=\"export control export controls, export licensing, export license, export licenses, export licence, export licences, export-control an export control is a rule that requires the government's permission for a sale. the government names an item and a country or a buyer. from then on its own companies must hold a license before they ship that item to that country or buyer. the united states extends some of these rules to goods made abroad with american technology.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">export control</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-fab\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-fab\" data-alias=\"fabrication plant|wafer fab|chip factory|chip factories\" data-text=\"fab fabrication plant, wafer fab, fabs, chip factory, chip factories the factory where wafers are processed into chips. it is a cleanroom where each wafer moves from machine to machine in a sealed pod for months. the building costs tens of billions of dollars.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">fab</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-fabless\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-fabless\" data-text=\"fabless a chip company that designs and sells chips but owns no factory, paying a contract manufacturer, a foundry, to make them. nvidia, amd, apple, qualcomm and broadcom all work this way.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">fabless</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-fabrinet\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Fabrinet\" data-text=\"fabrinet bangkok thailand fn optics and photonics contract manufacturing of optical modules a contract manufacturer of optical modules and photonic assemblies, building transceivers and optical engines for the largest networking and ai vendors from plants in thailand. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Fabrinet</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-federal-register\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-federal-register\" data-alias=\"89 FR|91 FR|88 FR|Federal Register notice\" data-text=\"federal register fr, 89 fr, 91 fr, 88 fr, federal register notice the federal register is the us government's daily journal, where every new rule is published. an export rule can take effect a few days before it is printed there, as the uae rule did in july 2026. a citation such as 89 fr 96790 means volume 89, page 96790, and is the usual way to cite a rule.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Federal Register</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ferrotec-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Ferrotec Holdings\" data-alias=\"Ferrotec|フェローテックホールディングス\" data-text=\"ferrotec holdings フェローテックホールディングス tokyo japan 6890.t equipment subsystems and components quartz, ceramics, ferrofluidic seals and thermoelectrics supplies quartz and ceramic chamber consumables, ferrofluidic vacuum feedthroughs, electrostatic chucks and thermoelectric coolers, with much of its manufacturing in china. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ferrotec Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-finfet\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-finfet\" data-alias=\"fin field-effect transistor\" data-text=\"finfet fin field-effect transistor a transistor whose channel, the strip that current flows through, stands on edge like a shark fin. the gate, the electrode that switches the current, wraps around three sides of the fin instead of resting on one. more contact means firmer control and less leakage when the switch is meant to be off.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">FinFET</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-flops\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-flops\" data-alias=\"floating point operations per second|TFLOPS|PFLOPS|FLOP\" data-text=\"flops floating point operations per second, tflops, pflops, flop, teraflops a count of how many arithmetic operations on floating-point numbers, numbers with a fractional part, a chip can perform each second, the way horsepower counts an engine's output.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">FLOPS</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-foreign-direct-product-rule\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-foreign-direct-product-rule\" data-alias=\"FDPR|FDP rule|foreign-produced direct product rule|direct product rule|foreign-produced item rules|foreign-produced item rule|foreign-produced item\" data-text=\"foreign direct product rule fdpr, fdp rule, foreign-produced direct product rule, direct product rule, foreign-produced item rules, foreign-produced item rule, foreign-produced item a us rule that puts a foreign-made item under american control when two tests are both met. the first is about the product: the item was made directly from specified us technology or software, or in a plant that was. the second is about the destination: the item is going somewhere, or to someone, the rule names. the mechanics are in 15 cfr 734.9.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">foreign direct product rule</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-formfactor\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"FormFactor\" data-text=\"formfactor livermore united states form test probe cards and test systems supplies the mems probe cards that make temporary electrical contact with thousands of pads on a wafer during testing, including hbm and logic probe cards. it is a leading probe card maker, with $637.9 million of revenue in its probe card segment in 2025. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">FormFactor</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-foundry\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-foundry\" data-alias=\"pure-play foundry|contract chipmaker|pure-play|pure play|pure-play model|contract chipmaking\" data-text=\"foundry pure-play foundry, contract chipmaker, foundries, pure-play, pure play, pure-play model, contract chipmaking a company, or a division of one, that manufactures chips designed by other companies. a pure-play foundry, the model tsmc pioneered after its founding in 1987, makes no products of its own. the model works because no chip company sells enough of one product to fill a modern fab on its own.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">foundry</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-fp8-and-fp4\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-fp8-and-fp4\" data-alias=\"8-bit and 4-bit floating point|FP8|FP4|FP16|BF16|INT8|number formats\" data-text=\"fp8 and fp4 8-bit and 4-bit floating point, fp8, fp4, fp16, bf16, int8, number formats ways of writing a number using only 8 or 4 binary digits, or bits, far fewer than standard formats use. each number is less precise, but the chip can perform and store far more of them. that trade-off suits machine learning, which can work with less exact numbers.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">FP8 and FP4</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-fr\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"FR\" data-alias=\"FR|French\" data-text=\"france fr fr french country \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">France</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-front-end\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-front-end\" data-alias=\"front end of line|FEOL|front-end|front-end wafers\" data-text=\"front end front end of line, feol, front-end, front-end wafers the front end of line is the first half of making a chip, the steps that build the transistors in the silicon. in the industry at large, the front end means the whole wafer fab, as against the back end where chips are packaged and tested.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">front end</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-fujifilm\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Fujifilm\" data-alias=\"富士フイルム\" data-text=\"fujifilm 富士フイルム tokyo japan 4901.t photoresist and materials photoresist, cmp slurry and cleaning chemicals makes photoresist, developers, cmp polishing slurries, polyimides and cleaning chemicals. it built this large electronic materials business from its photographic film chemistry. electronic materials are a minority of group revenue but a major share of world supply. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Fujifilm</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-fujimi-incorporated\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Fujimi Incorporated\" data-alias=\"Fujimi|株式会社フジミインコーポレーテッド\" data-text=\"fujimi incorporated 株式会社フジミインコーポレーテッド kiyosu japan 5384.t photoresist and materials cmp slurries and polishing materials makes the abrasive slurries used to polish silicon wafers and to planarize (polish flat) the metal and insulating layers built up during chip fabrication. fujimi tunes each slurry for the process step and the customer. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Fujimi Incorporated</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-furiosaai\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"FuriosaAI\" data-alias=\"퓨리오사AI\" data-text=\"furiosaai 퓨리오사ai seoul south korea private ai accelerator vendors inference accelerators builds the rngd inference accelerator, which uses hbm3 memory and an architecture designed around tensor contraction, the core math of ai models. it is aimed at companies running inference where power is limited. it turned down an acquisition offer from meta in 2025. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">FuriosaAI</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-gallium-and-germanium\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-gallium-and-germanium\" data-text=\"gallium and germanium gallium, germanium, antimony gallium and germanium are metals used in electronics. gallium goes into compound chips such as radio parts, leds and lasers, and germanium into fiber optics, infrared optics, semiconductors and solar cells. both are recovered as byproducts, gallium from processing bauxite and germanium from certain zinc ores and coal.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">gallium and germanium</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-gate-all-around\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-gate-all-around\" data-alias=\"GAA|nanosheet transistor|RibbonFET at Intel|RibbonFET|GAA transistor|gate-all-around transistors\" data-text=\"gate-all-around gaa, nanosheet transistor, ribbonfet at intel, nanosheet, nanosheets, ribbonfet, gaa transistor, gate-all-around transistors a transistor in which the gate, the electrode that switches the current, wraps all the way around the channel that current flows through. in a finfet, the design it replaces, the gate touches three sides. surrounding the channel gives the gate firmer control than a fin allows, so less current leaks when the switch is off.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">gate-all-around</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-gb-s\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-gb-s\" data-alias=\"TB/s|Tbps|gigabytes per second|terabytes per second|gigabits per second|terabits per second\" data-text=\"gb/s tb/s, gb/s, tbps, gigabytes per second, terabytes per second, gigabits per second, terabits per second gb/s is gigabytes per second, the measure of how much data a link or a memory can move. tb/s is a thousand times more. a lowercase b, as in gb/s or tbps, counts bits, each an eighth of a byte. one hbm4 stack moves over 2 tb/s. nvlink 6 gives each gpu 3,600 gb/s, according to nvidia's january 2026 rubin launch.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">GB/s</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ge-vernova\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"GE Vernova\" data-text=\"ge vernova cambridge united states gev power and cooling gas turbines, grid equipment including transformers, and generation builds gas turbines, grid equipment and wind turbines. it is a main supplier of the new generating capacity being contracted specifically to power ai data centers. it bought the remaining half of the transformer maker prolec ge in the first half of 2026. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">GE Vernova</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-de\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"DE\" data-alias=\"DE|German\" data-text=\"germany de de german country the optics inside every euv scanner, and specialty chemicals\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Germany</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-gigaphoton\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Gigaphoton\" data-alias=\"ギガフォトン株式会社\" data-text=\"gigaphoton ギガフォトン株式会社 oyama japan private lithography excimer lasers for duv lithography makes arf and krf excimer laser light sources for duv scanners, including asml immersion tools. it describes itself as the world's leading excimer laser light source manufacturer. it also offers retrofit sources for installed duv tools. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Gigaphoton</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Lithography</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-glass-cloth\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-glass-cloth\" data-alias=\"T-glass|low-expansion glass|glass fiber cloth|low-expansion glass cloth\" data-text=\"glass cloth t-glass, low-expansion glass, glass fiber cloth, low-expansion glass cloth glass cloth is a woven fabric of fine glass fibers that gives a substrate core or circuit board its stiffness. t-glass is a special grade that barely expands when heated, which helps keep a large package flat.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">glass cloth</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-global-unichip\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Global Unichip\" data-alias=\"創意電子\" data-text=\"global unichip 創意電子 hsinchu taiwan 3443.tw ai accelerator vendors asic design services, tsmc-affiliated tsmc's design services affiliate. it does the physical design and ip integration for customers' custom ai chips (asics) and delivers the finished chips, made on tsmc processes and packaging. its ties to tsmc give it early access to new processes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Global Unichip</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-globalfoundries\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"GlobalFoundries\" data-text=\"globalfoundries malta united states gfs foundry specialty and mature-node foundry runs mature and specialty processes for rf, automotive, power and silicon photonics from fabs in new york, vermont, germany and singapore. it stopped developing leading-edge processes in 2018. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">GlobalFoundries</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-globalwafers\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"GlobalWafers\" data-alias=\"環球晶圓\" data-text=\"globalwafers 環球晶圓 hsinchu taiwan 6488.two silicon and wafers silicon wafers, soi and compound substrates the third-largest wafer maker, with fabs in taiwan, japan, the us and europe. it built a new 300 mm plant in sherman, texas, with chips act support. in its annual report for 2025 it ranked itself third and put its shipments at about 15 to 20 percent of global semiconductor wafer output. it also supplies silicon-on-insulator (soi) and compound semiconductor substrates. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">GlobalWafers</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-gold-circuit-electronics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Gold Circuit Electronics\" data-alias=\"Gold Circuit|金像電子\" data-text=\"gold circuit electronics 金像電子 taoyuan taiwan 2368.tw substrates and pcbs server and networking pcbs makes high-layer-count printed circuit boards for servers and networking, and has grown with ai server baseboard and switch board demand. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Gold Circuit Electronics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-google\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Google\" data-text=\"google mountain view united states private ai accelerator vendors hyperscaler in-house tpu designs the tensor processing unit (tpu), and announced the eighth generation, the tpu 8t and tpu 8i, in april 2026. it uses tpus in its own data centers and offers them to cloud customers. broadcom and mediatek work with it on the physical design, which turns a chip design into a layout, and on manufacturing at tsmc. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-google-tpu-8i\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"google-tpu-8i\" data-alias=\"TPU 8i|Zebrafish\" data-text=\"google tpu 8i (zebrafish) tpu n3 (per semianalysis, for the eighth generation as a whole) hbm (generation not stated) plus 384 mb on-die vmem\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google TPU 8i (Zebrafish)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-google-tpu-8t\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"google-tpu-8t\" data-alias=\"TPU 8t\" data-text=\"google tpu 8t tpu n3 (per semianalysis, for the eighth generation as a whole) hbm (generation not stated) plus 128 mb on-chip vmem\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google TPU 8t</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-google-tpu-v4\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"google-tpu-v4\" data-alias=\"TPU v4\" data-text=\"google tpu v4 tpu 7 nm hbm2\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google TPU v4</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-google-tpu-v5e\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"google-tpu-v5e\" data-alias=\"TPU v5e|v5e\" data-text=\"google tpu v5e tpu hbm2\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google TPU v5e</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-google-tpu-v5p\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"google-tpu-v5p\" data-alias=\"TPU v5p|v5p\" data-text=\"google tpu v5p tpu n5 (per semianalysis) hbm (google does not state the generation)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google TPU v5p</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-google-tpu-v6e\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"google-tpu-v6e\" data-alias=\"TPU v6e|v6e|Trillium\" data-text=\"google tpu v6e (trillium) tpu n5 (per semianalysis) hbm3 (per semianalysis)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google TPU v6e (Trillium)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-google-tpu-v7-ironwood\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"google-tpu-v7-ironwood\" data-alias=\"TPU v7|Ironwood\" data-text=\"google tpu v7 (ironwood) tpu n3e (per semianalysis) hbm3e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Google TPU v7 (Ironwood)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-gpu\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-gpu\" data-alias=\"graphics processing unit|GPUs\" data-text=\"gpu graphics processing unit, gpus a processor originally built to draw video game images by doing thousands of simple calculations at once. neural networks turned out to need the same kind of arithmetic, so the gpu became the default ai processor.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">GPU</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-groq\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Groq\" data-text=\"groq mountain view united states private ai accelerator vendors deterministic inference accelerators (lpu) designs the language processing unit (lpu), an inference chip that uses large on-chip sram and no hbm, and whose compiler schedules every operation in advance. it sells few chips. instead it runs ai models in its own cloud and charges customers per token of text processed. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Groq</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-groq-lpu\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"groq-lpu\" data-alias=\"LPU|Language Processing Unit\" data-text=\"groq lpu language processing unit 14 nm on the first-generation groqchip on-die sram only, no hbm. 230 mb per chip on the 14 nm groqchip; groq's current rack figure of 128 gb across 256 lpus implies 500 mb per chip\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Groq LPU</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-gross-margin\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-gross-margin\" data-text=\"gross margin the share of a sale left over after paying what it cost to make the thing, before research, sales and overheads are counted. a 70 percent gross margin means $70 of every $100 of revenue is left after manufacturing cost.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">gross margin</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hanmi-semiconductor\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hanmi Semiconductor\" data-alias=\"Hanmi|한미반도체\" data-text=\"hanmi semiconductor 한미반도체 incheon south korea 042700.ks advanced packaging and osat thermocompression bonders for hbm makes the thermocompression bonders used to stack hbm dies, including dual-head models, and supplies sk hynix and micron. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hanmi Semiconductor</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-hbm\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-hbm\" data-alias=\"high bandwidth memory|high-bandwidth memory|HBM3E|HBM4|HBM4E|HBM stack|HBM stacks|memory stacks|stacked memory\" data-text=\"hbm high bandwidth memory, high-bandwidth memory, hbm3e, hbm4, hbm4e, hbm stack, hbm stacks, memory stacks, stacked memory stacked memory built for ai chips. up to sixteen memory chips are stacked into a cube and wired together through copper-filled holes made in each chip before stacking. the cube sits a few millimeters from the processor. it holds the model the chip is running, the numbers called weights, and hands them to the processor over 1,024 or more wires at once.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">HBM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hemlock-semiconductor\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hemlock Semiconductor\" data-alias=\"Hemlock\" data-text=\"hemlock semiconductor hemlock united states private silicon and wafers ultra-high-purity polysilicon feedstock makes the ultra-pure polysilicon that is melted to grow the crystal ingots wafers are cut from. only a few plants worldwide make semiconductor-grade material. siltronic names hemlock among the five major suppliers of electronic-grade silicon in 2025. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hemlock Semiconductor</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hewlett-packard-enterprise\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hewlett Packard Enterprise\" data-alias=\"HPE\" data-text=\"hewlett packard enterprise spring united states hpe systems and servers ai servers, supercomputers and networking builds ai servers and cray supercomputers with direct liquid cooling, and since acquiring juniper networks also supplies data center networking. hpe\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hewlett Packard Enterprise</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-high-na-euv\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-high-na-euv\" data-alias=\"high numerical aperture extreme ultraviolet|ASML EXE series|High-NA|High NA|High-NA scanners|High-NA machine|High-NA tools\" data-text=\"high-na euv high numerical aperture extreme ultraviolet, asml exe series, high-na, high na, high-na scanners, high-na machine, high-na tools the next generation of extreme ultraviolet machine, whose larger mirrors collect light over a wider angle and so print smaller features. the wider optics also halve the area the machine can print in one exposure, so a large chip has to be stitched together from two exposures.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">High-NA EUV</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-high-performance-computing\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-high-performance-computing\" data-alias=\"HPC|HPC platform|high-performance computers\" data-text=\"high-performance computing hpc, hpc platform, high-performance computers high-performance computing is the industry's name for the heavy end of the market: supercomputers, ai accelerators and the server processors beside them. a foundry's hpc platform is the version of a node tuned for those chips.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">high-performance computing</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-high-volume-manufacturing\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-high-volume-manufacturing\" data-alias=\"HVM|volume production|mass production|high volume|in volume|production ramp\" data-text=\"high-volume manufacturing hvm, volume production, mass production, high volume, in volume, production ramp high-volume manufacturing is the point where a new process or product stops being a trial and is made in volume for sale. output then climbs to full rate during the ramp.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">high-volume manufacturing</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hisilicon\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"HiSilicon\" data-alias=\"海思半导体\" data-text=\"hisilicon 海思半导体 shenzhen china private ai accelerator vendors ascend ai accelerators huawei's chip design arm. it designs the ascend 910c and the announced 950 and 960 accelerators. smic makes its chips without euv lithography tools, and that limits yield and volume. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">HiSilicon</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hitachi-energy\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hitachi Energy\" data-text=\"hitachi energy zurich switzerland private power and cooling grid equipment and large transformers makes the high voltage transformers, switchgear and grid connection equipment that data center campuses need to draw hundreds of megawatts. transformer lead times run to several years. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hitachi Energy</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hitachi-high-tech\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hitachi High-Tech\" data-alias=\"株式会社日立ハイテク\" data-text=\"hitachi high-tech 株式会社日立ハイテク tokyo japan private metrology and inspection cd-sem metrology and etch systems the largest supplier of critical dimension scanning electron microscopes (cd-sems), which measure feature widths after lithography and etch. it also makes plasma etch systems and electron beam review tools. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hitachi High-Tech</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hon-hai-precision\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hon Hai Precision\" data-alias=\"Hon Hai|Foxconn|鴻海精密工業\" data-text=\"hon hai precision 鴻海精密工業 new taipei taiwan 2317.tw systems and servers ai server and rack integration builds nvidia servers and rack-scale systems, with assembly in taiwan, mexico, the us and southeast asia. it is the largest electronics contract manufacturer and the world's largest ai server provider. foxconn\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hon Hai Precision</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-horiba\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Horiba\" data-alias=\"株式会社堀場製作所\" data-text=\"horiba 株式会社堀場製作所 kyoto japan 6856.t equipment subsystems and components mass flow controllers and in-line analysis supplies mass flow controllers, which meter process gases into chambers to within a fraction of a percent. it also supplies residual gas analyzers and liquid concentration monitors used across the fab. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Horiba</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hoya\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hoya\" data-alias=\"HOYA株式会社\" data-text=\"hoya hoya株式会社 tokyo japan 7741.t photomasks euv and duv mask blanks makes the ultra-flat low-thermal-expansion glass blanks, coated with molybdenum-silicon multilayers, that become euv photomasks. hoya says it holds an exceptionally high share of the euv mask blank market. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hoya</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hua-hong-semiconductor\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hua Hong Semiconductor\" data-alias=\"Hua Hong|华虹半导体\" data-text=\"hua hong semiconductor 华虹半导体 shanghai china 1347.hk foundry mature-node specialty foundry a foundry focused on mature-node specialty processes, including power management, embedded memory and analog. it is mainland china's second largest pure-play foundry and the world's fifth largest by 2025 sales. it does not make leading-edge logic. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hua Hong Semiconductor</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hua-tian-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hua Tian Technology\" data-alias=\"Hua Tian|华天科技\" data-text=\"hua tian technology 华天科技 tianshui china 002185.sz advanced packaging and osat osat assembly and test a chinese osat that ranks among the ten largest in the world. it provides wire bond, flip chip and fan-out packaging from plants in tianshui, xi'an, kunshan and nanjing. it also packages chips through unisem, a malaysian firm it acquired in 2019. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hua Tian Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-huawei-ascend-910b\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"huawei-ascend-910b\" data-alias=\"Ascend 910B|910B\" data-text=\"huawei (hisilicon) ascend 910b ascend smic n+2 7 nm class, per cset; semianalysis judges most 910b and 910c dies were actually made on tsmc n7 hbm2e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Huawei (HiSilicon) Ascend 910B</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-huawei-ascend-910c\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"huawei-ascend-910c\" data-alias=\"Ascend 910C|910C\" data-text=\"huawei (hisilicon) ascend 910c ascend smic n+2 7 nm class as intended; semianalysis judges most 910b and 910c dies were actually made on tsmc n7 hbm2e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Huawei (HiSilicon) Ascend 910C</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-huawei-ascend-950dt\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"huawei-ascend-950dt\" data-alias=\"Ascend 950DT|950DT\" data-text=\"huawei (hisilicon) ascend 950dt ascend 950 hizq 2.0, huawei’s own high-bandwidth memory\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Huawei (HiSilicon) Ascend 950DT</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-huawei-ascend-950pr\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"huawei-ascend-950pr\" data-alias=\"Ascend 950PR|950PR\" data-text=\"huawei (hisilicon) ascend 950pr ascend 950 hibl 1.0, huawei's own high-bandwidth memory\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Huawei (HiSilicon) Ascend 950PR</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-hybrid-bonding\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-hybrid-bonding\" data-alias=\"direct bond interconnect|SoIC|Foveros Direct|copper pad to copper pad\" data-text=\"hybrid bonding direct bond interconnect, soic, foveros direct, copper pad to copper pad joining two chips by bonding their copper pads, and the glass-like insulator around them, directly to each other, with no solder in between. removing the solder lets connections be packed much more tightly and shortens the path heat has to travel out.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">hybrid bonding</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-hydrogen-fluoride\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-hydrogen-fluoride\" data-alias=\"hydrofluoric acid|ultra-high-purity hydrofluoric acid|high-purity hydrogen fluoride\" data-text=\"hydrogen fluoride hydrofluoric acid, hf, ultra-high-purity hydrofluoric acid, high-purity hydrogen fluoride hydrogen fluoride is a gas that dissolves glass, and hydrofluoric acid is its solution in water. fabs use both to strip oxide layers and clean wafers between steps. like other cleaning chemicals, it is purified until metal impurities are down to parts per trillion.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">hydrogen fluoride</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-hygon-information-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Hygon Information Technology\" data-alias=\"Hygon Information|Hygon|海光信息\" data-text=\"hygon information technology 海光信息 tianjin china 688041.ss ai accelerator vendors x86 server cpus and dcu accelerators makes x86-compatible server cpus, derived from an amd license, and the deep computing unit (dcu) accelerator line. it supplies chinese government and state enterprise data centers. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Hygon Information Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-hyperscaler\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-hyperscaler\" data-text=\"hyperscaler hyperscalers one of the handful of companies that run data centers at global scale, such as amazon, microsoft, google, meta and oracle.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">hyperscaler</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-i-line\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-i-line\" data-alias=\"g-line|i-line steppers|i-line scanners\" data-text=\"i-line g-line, i-line steppers, i-line scanners i-line is the coarsest of the main lithography lights, 365 nanometers from a mercury lamp, named for one line in the lamp's spectrum. it prints the widest features on a chip and much of a package.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">i-line</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ibiden\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Ibiden\" data-alias=\"イビデン株式会社\" data-text=\"ibiden イビデン株式会社 ogaki japan 4062.t substrates and pcbs fc-bga package substrates makes the highest-layer-count flip-chip bga substrates, the multilayer boards a processor die sits on. it supplies substrates for large ai packages and is expanding capacity, first mainly at its gama plant, which it said in august 2026 would start operating in stages from the end of fiscal 2027. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ibiden</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ichor-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Ichor Holdings\" data-alias=\"Ichor\" data-text=\"ichor holdings fremont united states ichr equipment subsystems and components gas and fluid delivery subsystems designs and builds the gas panels, weldments and chemical delivery modules that route process gases into etch and deposition chambers. it is an outsourced manufacturing partner to the large tool vendors. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ichor Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-idm\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-idm\" data-alias=\"integrated device manufacturer|integrated device maker|integrated device makers\" data-text=\"idm integrated device manufacturer, integrated device maker, integrated device makers a chip company that both designs its products and manufactures them in its own factories. intel, samsung and micron are examples.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">IDM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-iluvatar-corex\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Iluvatar CoreX\" data-alias=\"天数智芯\" data-text=\"iluvatar corex 天数智芯 shanghai china 9903.hk ai accelerator vendors gpgpu for ai training and inference designs the tiangai and zhikai general-purpose ai accelerators for chinese data centers, built to work with mainstream ai frameworks. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Iluvatar CoreX</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-imagination-technologies\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Imagination Technologies\" data-alias=\"Imagination\" data-text=\"imagination technologies kings langley united kingdom private ip and architecture gpu and neural accelerator ip licenses gpu and neural network accelerator ip for edge and automotive silicon. its ownership by a china-linked fund made it an early test case for technology transfer scrutiny in the uk. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Imagination Technologies</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">IP and architecture</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-immersion-lithography\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-immersion-lithography\" data-alias=\"immersion DUV|ArF immersion|immersion scanner|immersion scanners|immersion tools|immersion DUV scanners|immersion deep-ultraviolet\" data-text=\"immersion lithography immersion duv, arf immersion, immersion scanner, immersion scanners, immersion tools, immersion duv scanners, immersion deep-ultraviolet immersion lithography prints with a thin layer of ultrapure water between the scanner's lens and the wafer. the water lets the lens focus light at a wider angle than air allows, so the same light prints finer lines. it is the most advanced form of deep ultraviolet lithography, one step below extreme ultraviolet.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">immersion lithography</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ims-nanofabrication\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"IMS Nanofabrication\" data-text=\"ims nanofabrication brunn am gebirge austria private photomasks multi-beam mask writers builds the multi-beam electron mask writers that pattern euv masks with hundreds of thousands of parallel beamlets. on cset's count it led the market for all electron-beam mask writers in 2025. nuflare is the only other maker of multi-beam writers. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">IMS Nanofabrication</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-in-country-transfer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-in-country-transfer\" data-alias=\"transfer (in-country)\" data-text=\"in-country transfer transfer (in-country) a change in the end use or the end user of an item inside one foreign country, defined at 15 cfr 734.16. nothing crosses a border. a server legally imported into a country for one customer is transferred when it is resold, or repurposed, for another.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">in-country transfer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-indium-phosphide\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-indium-phosphide\" data-alias=\"InP\" data-text=\"indium phosphide inp, indium indium phosphide is a crystal grown from the metal indium and phosphorus. it gives off light when current passes through it, which silicon cannot do efficiently. the lasers inside the fastest optical modules are made of it.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">indium phosphide</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-inference\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-inference\" data-alias=\"inference chip|inference chips|inference accelerator|inference accelerators|training and inference\" data-text=\"inference inference chip, inference chips, inference accelerator, inference accelerators, training and inference inference is running a finished ai model to answer requests, such as a prompt. training, a run of weeks on a cluster of accelerators, builds the model first. to write each word of an answer, the chip reads the whole model from memory, does a little arithmetic and waits for the next read. training reuses each number it fetches, so it fetches little and computes a lot.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">inference</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-infineon\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Infineon\" data-text=\"infineon neubiberg germany ifx.de power and cooling power semiconductors and power stages supplies the mosfets, gallium nitride devices and power stages used from the grid connection through the rack power shelf to the point-of-load regulator. it is the largest power semiconductor maker, according to omdia figures infineon published in august 2026. those figures give it 17.3 percent of the $32.5 billion market for power discretes and modules in 2025, against 7.2 percent for onsemi. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Infineon</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-infiniband\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-infiniband\" data-alias=\"Quantum-2|Quantum-X800\" data-text=\"infiniband quantum-2, quantum-x800 infiniband is a networking standard long used in supercomputers, with low delay and no dropped packets. ai clusters relied on it to link thousands of servers before ethernet caught up, and nvidia still sells both.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">InfiniBand</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-innolight-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Innolight Technology\" data-alias=\"Innolight|中际旭创\" data-text=\"innolight technology 中际旭创 suzhou china 300308.sz optics and photonics 800g and 1.6t optical transceivers a world-leading maker of high-speed optical transceiver modules for data centers, shipping 800g and 1.6t modules to hyperscalers. ai clusters need one or more optical modules per accelerator. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Innolight Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-inpria\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Inpria\" data-text=\"inpria corvallis united states private photoresist and materials metal-oxide euv photoresist developed tin-oxide euv resists that absorb euv photons far more efficiently than organic chemically amplified resists. higher absorption cuts the light dose needed and sharpens resolution on high-na euv tools. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Inpria</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-intel\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Intel\" data-text=\"intel santa clara united states intc ai accelerator vendors server cpus and ai accelerators designs xeon server cpus and the gaudi accelerator line. xeon chips are still the host cpus in most ai clusters. its product business is separate from intel foundry, the company's manufacturing arm. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Intel</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-intel-foundry\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Intel Foundry\" data-text=\"intel foundry santa clara united states private foundry leading-edge logic foundry and packaging intel's manufacturing arm, running the 18a process with ribbonfet gate-all-around and powervia backside power, plus emib and foveros packaging. most of its output is still intel's own chips. outside customers provided only $293 million of its $5.765 billion of segment revenue in the quarter to 27 june 2026. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Intel Foundry</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-intel-gaudi2\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"intel-gaudi2\" data-alias=\"Gaudi 2|Gaudi\" data-text=\"intel gaudi 2 gaudi 7 nm (intel states the node in the gaudi 3 white paper and does not name the foundry for gaudi 2) hbm2e plus 48 mb on-die sram\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Intel Gaudi 2</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-intel-gaudi3\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"intel-gaudi3\" data-alias=\"Gaudi 3|Gaudi\" data-text=\"intel gaudi 3 gaudi tsmc 5 nm hbm2e plus 96 mb on-die sram\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Intel Gaudi 3</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-interposer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-interposer\" data-alias=\"silicon interposer|silicon carrier\" data-text=\"interposer interposers, silicon interposer, silicon carrier a layer of wiring with no transistors, used as a miniature circuit board underneath several chips so they can be connected at a density no ordinary board could reach. it is either one piece of silicon or layers of fine copper wiring, often with small silicon bridges.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">interposer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-inventec\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Inventec\" data-alias=\"英業達\" data-text=\"inventec 英業達 taipei taiwan 2356.tw systems and servers ai server odm builds ai and general purpose servers for cloud operators and oems, with manufacturing in taiwan, mexico, the czech republic and malaysia. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Inventec</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ion-implantation\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ion-implantation\" data-alias=\"ion implanter|ion implanters|implant layers\" data-text=\"ion implantation ion implanter, ion implanters, implant, implant layers, implantation a way of changing how silicon conducts by firing atoms into it. an ion implanter shoots charged atoms of boron, phosphorus or arsenic into the wafer, where they lodge just under the surface. the patches they land in then conduct the way the design needs.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ion implantation</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ip\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ip\" data-alias=\"silicon IP|IP blocks|licensed blocks|licensed circuit blocks|semiconductor IP|IP catalog|intellectual property\" data-text=\"ip silicon ip, ip blocks, licensed blocks, licensed circuit blocks, semiconductor ip, ip catalog, intellectual property in chip design, ip, short for intellectual property, means a ready-made block of circuitry, such as a processor core or a memory interface, that a design house licenses. arm sells processor ip, and other firms sell the blocks that talk to memory, pcie or another chiplet.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">IP</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-is-informed-letter\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-is-informed-letter\" data-alias=\"is informed letter|is-informed letters|by letter\" data-text=\"is-informed letter is informed letter, is-informed letters, by letter a letter from bis to one named company imposing a license requirement on a specific export, without any rule being published. bis's power to send one is written into the regulations themselves, for example 15 cfr 744.23(b), which lets bis inform a person individually, with no amendment to the ear.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">is-informed letter</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-il\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"IL\" data-alias=\"IL|Israeli\" data-text=\"israel il il israeli country metrology and inspection tools, and chip design centers\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Israel</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-jabil\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Jabil\" data-text=\"jabil st. petersburg united states jbl systems and servers contract manufacturing and liquid cooling hardware a large contract manufacturer building ai data center hardware including server racks, power distribution and liquid cooling components such as cold plates and manifolds. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Jabil</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-jp\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"JP\" data-alias=\"JP|Japanese\" data-text=\"japan jp jp japanese country wafers, photoresist, masks and etch tools, which every fab needs\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Japan</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-jcet-group\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"JCET Group\" data-alias=\"JCET|长电科技\" data-text=\"jcet group 长电科技 jiangyin china 600584.ss advanced packaging and osat osat assembly, test and fan-out packaging a leading chinese assembly and test firm, offering wire bond, flip chip, fan-out and system-in-package assembly. its revenue reached a record rmb 38.87 billion in 2025. it acquired stats chippac in 2015 to gain advanced packaging capability. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">JCET Group</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-jedec\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-jedec\" data-alias=\"JESD270-4|JEDEC standard\" data-text=\"jedec jesd270-4, jedec standard jedec is the industry body that writes the standards for memory chips, so that a memory stack from any maker fits any processor built to the same specification. its hbm4 standard, published in april 2025, sets the width and speed of the interface.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">JEDEC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-jenoptik\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Jenoptik\" data-text=\"jenoptik jena germany jen.de equipment subsystems and components optical systems and metrology components supplies precision optics, laser components and optical measurement modules used inside lithography and inspection tools, and makes its own micro-optics. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Jenoptik</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-jsr-corporation\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"JSR Corporation\" data-alias=\"JSR|JSR株式会社\" data-text=\"jsr corporation jsr株式会社 tokyo japan private photoresist and materials arf, krf and euv photoresist a japanese maker of photoresist, the light-sensitive coating that chip patterns are printed into. it owns inpria, an oregon maker of metal-oxide resist for extreme ultraviolet (euv) printing. a company controlled by the japan investment corporation bought 84.36 percent of its shares in a tender offer that closed on 16 april 2024. its shares were delisted from the tokyo stock exchange on 25 june 2024. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">JSR Corporation</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-jx-advanced-metals\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"JX Advanced Metals\" data-alias=\"JX金属\" data-text=\"jx advanced metals jx金属 tokyo japan 5016.t photoresist and materials sputtering targets and ultra-high-purity metals supplies the ultra-high-purity copper, tantalum and titanium sputtering targets used to deposit the metal interconnect on a chip, along with high-purity treated rolled copper foil for substrates. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">JX Advanced Metals</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-kanto-denka-kogyo\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Kanto Denka Kogyo\" data-alias=\"関東電化工業\" data-text=\"kanto denka kogyo 関東電化工業 tokyo japan 4047.t chemicals and gases fluorinated etch gases makes fluorine-based specialty gases including tungsten hexafluoride and carbon fluorides used for plasma etch and chamber cleaning. it is one of a small number of qualified sources for several of these molecules. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Kanto Denka Kogyo</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-kilowatt\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-kilowatt\" data-text=\"kilowatt kw, kilowatts, megawatt, mw, megawatts, gigawatt, gw, gigawatts a kilowatt is a thousand watts. a megawatt is a thousand kilowatts, and a gigawatt a thousand megawatts, about the output of one large power station. a gb300 nvl72 rack draws up to 142 kilowatts. the largest data center campuses are planned in gigawatts.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">kilowatt</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-king-yuan-electronics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"King Yuan Electronics\" data-alias=\"King Yuan|京元電子\" data-text=\"king yuan electronics 京元電子 miaoli taiwan 2449.tw advanced packaging and osat wafer sort and final test services tests logic chips, including ai accelerators, both on the wafer (wafer sort) and after packaging (final test). in 2026 it described itself as the world's largest pure-play chip test house and second worldwide in test revenue. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">King Yuan Electronics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-kinsus-interconnect\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Kinsus Interconnect\" data-alias=\"景碩科技\" data-text=\"kinsus interconnect 景碩科技 taoyuan taiwan 3189.tw substrates and pcbs ic substrates and flexible circuits makes flip-chip and wire bond ic substrates and flexible printed circuits, supplying processor and networking chip customers from plants in taiwan and china. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Kinsus Interconnect</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-kioxia\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Kioxia\" data-alias=\"キオクシア株式会社\" data-text=\"kioxia キオクシア株式会社 tokyo japan 285a.t memory 3d nand flash the former toshiba memory, making 3d nand at yokkaichi and kitakami in a long-running joint venture with sandisk. its bics8 generation targets enterprise ssds. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Kioxia</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-kla\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"KLA\" data-text=\"kla milpitas united states klac metrology and inspection wafer and reticle inspection, process control supplies process control equipment: optical and electron beam wafer inspection, reticle inspection, overlay and film metrology. its tools find the defects that determine yield on large dies. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">KLA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-known-good-die\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-known-good-die\" data-alias=\"KGD|good die|good dies|known good die\" data-text=\"known-good die kgd, good die, good dies, known good die a bare chip tested thoroughly enough, before assembly, to be trusted inside something expensive. in an ordinary product a faulty chip wastes one chip. inside a package that joins a dozen expensive pieces, one bad die throws away all of them.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">known-good die</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-kokusai-electric\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Kokusai Electric\" data-alias=\"株式会社Kokusai Electric\" data-text=\"kokusai electric 株式会社kokusai electric tokyo japan 6525.t deposition and etch batch ald and vertical furnaces makes batch vertical furnaces and batch ald systems that process dozens of wafers at once. memory makers use them widely for dram and 3d nand film steps where throughput matters more than single-wafer control. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Kokusai Electric</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-krf\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-krf\" data-alias=\"krypton fluoride|krypton fluoride laser|248 nm|248-nanometer\" data-text=\"krf krypton fluoride, krypton fluoride laser, 248 nm, 248-nanometer krf is krypton fluoride, the gas in an older lithography laser that shines at 248 nanometers. krf scanners print the coarser layers of a chip, where lines are far apart.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">KrF</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-kulicke-and-soffa\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Kulicke and Soffa\" data-text=\"kulicke and soffa singapore singapore klic advanced packaging and osat wire bonders and advanced assembly makes wire bonders, the standard tool of low-cost packaging, and is developing thermocompression and fluxless bonding systems for advanced packages. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Kulicke and Soffa</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-lam-research\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Lam Research\" data-text=\"lam research fremont united states lrcx deposition and etch plasma etch, deposition and wafer clean the largest supplier of plasma etch systems. according to cset, it had 41.1 percent of the $21.9 billion dry etch tool market in 2025, against 23.4 percent for tokyo electron. its line includes the high aspect ratio etch used to drill 3d nand channels and dram capacitors, plus atomic layer deposition, electroplating and cryogenic etch tools. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Lam Research</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-laminate\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-laminate\" data-alias=\"copper-clad laminate|copper-clad laminates|low-loss laminate|core laminate\" data-text=\"laminate laminates, copper-clad laminate, copper-clad laminates, low-loss laminate, core laminate a laminate is a stiff sheet made by pressing glass cloth and resin together, usually with copper foil bonded to its faces. it is the material a circuit board or a substrate core is cut from. a low-loss laminate absorbs little of the signal passing through the wires on it.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">laminate</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-large-power-transformer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-large-power-transformer\" data-alias=\"large power transformers\" data-text=\"large power transformer large power transformers, transformer, transformers, switchgear, substation a large power transformer is a machine that changes grid electricity from one voltage to another, for example from transmission voltage down to a level a data center can use. switchgear is the heavy switching and protection equipment around it. together they make up the substation at the gate of the campus.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">large power transformer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-lasertec\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Lasertec\" data-alias=\"レーザーテック株式会社\" data-text=\"lasertec レーザーテック株式会社 yokohama japan 6920.t metrology and inspection euv mask blank and pattern inspection makes actinic inspection tools, which use euv light to inspect euv mask blanks and patterned masks. its actis a150 was the world's first actinic euv patterned mask inspection system. in october 2025 it launched the actis a200hit series, which it says triples the a150's inspection speed. these tools detect printable phase defects, flaws in a mask's reflective layers that duv-based mask inspection cannot find. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Lasertec</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-lead-time\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-lead-time\" data-alias=\"lead times|delivery time\" data-text=\"lead time lead times, delivery time lead time is the wait between placing an order and receiving it. a wafer clears a leading-edge fab in months, while in 2024 a large power transformer commonly took three years.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">lead time</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-leading-edge\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-leading-edge\" data-alias=\"leading-edge|at the leading edge|advanced node|advanced nodes|advanced-node\" data-text=\"leading edge leading-edge, at the leading edge, advanced node, advanced nodes, advanced-node the leading edge is the newest generation of chipmaking process in volume production. in 2026 that means the 3 nm and 2 nm nodes, made only by tsmc, samsung and intel. a leading-edge chip is one built on it.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">leading edge</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-lenovo\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Lenovo\" data-alias=\"联想集团\" data-text=\"lenovo 联想集团 beijing china 0992.hk systems and servers ai servers and liquid cooling builds ai servers and its neptune warm-water liquid cooling systems, selling into enterprises and research computing worldwide from plants in china, hungary, mexico and the us. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Lenovo</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-lg-innotek\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"LG Innotek\" data-alias=\"엘지이노텍\" data-text=\"lg innotek 엘지이노텍 seoul south korea 011070.ks substrates and pcbs fc-bga substrates and camera modules entered high-end flip-chip bga substrates in 2022 with a plant in gumi, adding a third korean source alongside samsung electro-mechanics. its larger business is optical modules for smartphones. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">LG Innotek</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-license-exception\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-license-exception\" data-text=\"license exception license exception a written carve-out in export rules that lets a shipment go without an individual license, if it meets stated conditions. the ones that matter for ai chips and chipmaking tools are nac and aca (15 cfr 740.8), hbm (740.25), aia and lpp (740.27 and 740.29), iec (740.24) and rpl (740.10). aia and lpp let the top band of accelerators ship to allies, and elsewhere in small volumes. iec covers countries that adopt matching controls, and rpl covers servicing and spare parts.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">license exception</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-license-exception-aca\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-license-exception-aca\" data-alias=\"ACA|Advanced Computing Authorized\" data-text=\"license exception aca aca, advanced computing authorized an export rule that lets ai chips other than top-band data center chips ship to most of the world with no license and no advance notice. it covers the same chips as its companion exception nac, and every destination except macau, country group d:5 and firms headquartered in either. the top-band data center chips in eccn 3a090.a are excluded. bis split it from nac at 15 cfr 740.8 in april 2024. the ai diffusion rule widened it in january 2025 to the whole world outside macau and d:5.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">License Exception ACA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-license-exception-acm\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-license-exception-acm\" data-alias=\"ACM|Advanced Compute Manufacturing\" data-text=\"license exception acm acm, advanced compute manufacturing license exception acm, for advanced compute manufacturing, lets controlled ai chips and related items go without a license to private-sector firms that develop, make or store them. the items must be bound for customers outside macau and country group d:5. it was created alongside license exceptions aia and lpp.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">License Exception ACM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-license-exception-aia\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-license-exception-aia\" data-alias=\"AIA|Artificial Intelligence Authorization\" data-text=\"license exception aia aia, artificial intelligence authorization license exception aia, for artificial intelligence authorization, lets the top band of ai chips ship without a license to nineteen destinations. they are listed in supplement no. 5 to part 740, and the united states is among them. the ai diffusion rule created it in january 2025 as the exception inside a worldwide license requirement.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">License Exception AIA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-license-exception-hbm\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-license-exception-hbm\" data-text=\"license exception hbm an export rule that lets high bandwidth memory go to a packaging site with no license, to be packaged beside a chip. it applies if the memory's bandwidth density is below 3.3 gb/s per square millimeter, measured over the area of the package or stack. the exporter must be headquartered in the united states or country group a:5. if the memory is bound for macau or country group d:5, the chip's designer must buy it. the stacks must go straight to the packaging site. it does not cover packaging at a facility in macau or d:5 that also makes advanced-node chips. it sits at 15 cfr 740.25.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">License Exception HBM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-license-exception-lpp\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-license-exception-lpp\" data-alias=\"LPP|Low Processing Performance\" data-text=\"license exception lpp lpp, low processing performance an export rule that lets a buyer almost anywhere receive a capped amount of top-band ai chips each year without a license. the cap is 26,900,000 tpp, the export rules' measure of computing power, per ultimate consignee per calendar year. macau, country group d:5 and firms headquartered in either are excluded, and it does not cover transfers within a country. the ai diffusion rule created it in january 2025, at 15 cfr 740.29.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">License Exception LPP</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-license-exception-nac\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-license-exception-nac\" data-alias=\"NAC|Notified Advanced Computing\" data-text=\"license exception nac nac, notified advanced computing an export rule that lets ai chips other than top-band data center chips ship to macau and country group d:5, and to firms headquartered there, with no license. the exporter must notify bis at least 25 calendar days ahead, and the shipment can go if bis does not say a license is needed. the top-band data center chips in eccn 3a090.a and the memory in 3a090.c are excluded. it sits at 15 cfr 740.8.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">License Exception NAC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-lightmatter\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Lightmatter\" data-text=\"lightmatter mountain view united states private optics and photonics photonic interconnect and compute develops photonic interposers and optical interconnect that route light beneath stacked dies, aiming to remove the bandwidth limit between accelerators in a package. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Lightmatter</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-linde\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Linde\" data-text=\"linde woking united kingdom lin chemicals and gases bulk and electronic specialty gases the world's largest industrial gas company. it supplies fabs with nitrogen, hydrogen, helium and rare gases such as the neon used in excimer lasers, usually from plants built next to the fab. gas supply contracts run for a decade or more. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Linde</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-liquid-cooling\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-liquid-cooling\" data-alias=\"direct-to-chip cooling|cold plate cooling|cold plate|cold plates|liquid-cooled|direct-to-chip liquid|direct liquid cooling\" data-text=\"liquid cooling direct-to-chip cooling, cold plate cooling, cold plate, cold plates, liquid-cooled, direct-to-chip liquid, direct liquid cooling taking heat out of a processor by pumping liquid through a cold plate on the chip package, instead of blowing air across a finned heatsink. a building loop then carries the heat outdoors.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">liquid cooling</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-lithography\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-lithography\" data-text=\"lithography photolithography printing a circuit pattern onto a wafer by shining light through a patterned plate and projecting a shrunken image of it onto a light-sensitive coating. it works like photography at the scale of nanometers, repeated once for every layer of the chip.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">lithography</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-logic-chip\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-logic-chip\" data-alias=\"logic chips|logic die|logic dies\" data-text=\"logic chip logic chips, logic die, logic dies a logic chip is one that computes, such as a processor, a graphics processor or an ai accelerator. memory chips, such as dram and nand flash, store data instead.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">logic chip</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-lot\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-lot\" data-alias=\"wafer lot|wafer lots|per lot\" data-text=\"lot lots, wafer lot, wafer lots, per lot a lot is the batch of wafers a fab moves through its machines together, usually 25 in one sealed carrier. recipes, inspections and yield are tracked lot by lot.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">lot</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-lumentum\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Lumentum\" data-text=\"lumentum san jose united states lite optics and photonics lasers, photonic components and transceivers supplies indium phosphide lasers, electro-absorption modulated lasers and optical modules for data center and telecom links, and is expanding capacity for ai cluster demand. it makes laser chips at a wafer fab in sagamihara, japan. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Lumentum</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Optics and photonics</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-luxshare-precision\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Luxshare Precision\" data-alias=\"Luxshare|立讯精密\" data-text=\"luxshare precision 立讯精密 dongguan china 002475.sz interconnect and networking connectors, cable assemblies and modules a large chinese contract manufacturer of connectors, high-speed cable assemblies and modules, and a growing supplier of ai server interconnect hardware alongside its consumer electronics work. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Luxshare Precision</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Interconnect</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-macau\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-macau\" data-alias=\"Macao|China or Macau|China and Macau\" data-text=\"macau macao, china or macau, china and macau macau is a chinese city with its own customs territory, like hong kong, so goods can enter it under separate rules. us export controls name china and macau together to close that route, and treat a firm headquartered in either the same way.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Macau</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-my\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"MY\" data-alias=\"MY|Malaysian\" data-text=\"malaysia my my malaysian country test and assembly, the last stage before the server\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Malaysia</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-marvell-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Marvell Technology\" data-alias=\"Marvell\" data-text=\"marvell technology santa clara united states mrvl ai accelerator vendors custom ai silicon, optical dsps and interconnect designs custom ai accelerators and infrastructure chips for hyperscalers, plus networking chips such as optical dsps, retimers and ethernet controllers for ai clusters. it ranks second to broadcom in custom ai chips and competes with it directly to design hyperscalers' accelerators. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Marvell Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-mask-blank\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-mask-blank\" data-alias=\"mask blanks|EUV blank|EUV blanks|photomask blank|photomask blanks|blank plate|DUV blanks\" data-text=\"mask blank mask blanks, euv blank, euv blanks, photomask blank, photomask blanks, blank plate, duv blanks a mask blank is a photomask before any pattern is on it. it is a six-inch square of very flat glass carrying the film that the pattern will be cut into. for extreme ultraviolet that film sits on a mirror of about forty pairs of ultrathin layers, and a particle buried in the mirror cannot be repaired.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">mask blank</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-mask-shop\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-mask-shop\" data-alias=\"mask shops|mask making|mask maker|mask makers\" data-text=\"mask shop mask shops, mask making, mask maker, mask makers a mask shop is the factory that turns a finished chip design into its set of photomasks. it writes each plate with an electron beam, inspects it and repairs it.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">mask shop</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-mask-writer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-mask-writer\" data-alias=\"mask writers|multi-beam writer|multi-beam writers|electron-beam writer|e-beam writer|mask writing\" data-text=\"mask writer mask writers, multi-beam writer, multi-beam writers, electron-beam writer, e-beam writer, mask writing a mask writer is the machine that uses electrons to draw a chip's pattern into the resist on a photomask blank. a single-beam writer flashes one shape at a time, while nuflare's multi-beam writer for the most advanced masks controls 260,000 beams at once.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">mask writer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-mature-node\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-mature-node\" data-alias=\"mature nodes|mature-node|mature logic|older nodes|older lines|trailing edge\" data-text=\"mature node mature nodes, mature-node, mature logic, older nodes, older lines, trailing edge a mature node is an older chipmaking process, 28 nm and above, that has run for years and competes on price. most of the world's wafers come off these lines, making power chips, analog parts and microcontrollers.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">mature node</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-mediatek\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"MediaTek\" data-alias=\"聯發科技\" data-text=\"mediatek 聯發科技 hsinchu taiwan 2454.tw ai accelerator vendors custom asic and mobile socs best known for its smartphone chips, mediatek also designs custom ai chips (asics) and works on google's tpu program. it has experience designing high-volume chips on advanced nodes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">MediaTek</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-memory-bandwidth-density\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-memory-bandwidth-density\" data-alias=\"bandwidth density|bandwidth-density\" data-text=\"memory bandwidth density bandwidth density, bandwidth-density memory bandwidth density is how much data a memory stack can move each second divided by the area of its package or stack, in gigabytes per second per square millimeter. the december 2024 rule controls any stack above 2, and bis said every hbm stack then in production exceeded that.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">memory bandwidth density</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-memory-wall\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-memory-wall\" data-text=\"memory wall the widening gap between how fast a processor can calculate and how fast memory can feed it numbers to work on. the cost of arithmetic has fallen faster than the cost of moving numbers.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">memory wall</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-merck-kgaa\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Merck KGaA\" data-text=\"merck kgaa darmstadt germany mrk.de chemicals and gases electronic materials, deposition gases and specialty chemicals its electronics division supplies deposition precursors, specialty gases, cmp slurries and dielectrics. merck built the division around its acquisitions of versum materials and az electronic materials. it sells one of the broadest ranges of materials of any single supplier. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Merck KGaA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-meta-mtia-300\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"meta-mtia-300\" data-alias=\"MTIA 300|300\" data-text=\"meta mtia 300 mtia hbm3e (12-high)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Meta MTIA 300</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-meta-mtia-400\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"meta-mtia-400\" data-alias=\"MTIA 400|400\" data-text=\"meta mtia 400 mtia hbm (generation not stated)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Meta MTIA 400</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-meta-mtia-v2\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"meta-mtia-v2\" data-alias=\"MTIA v2\" data-text=\"meta mtia v2 mtia 5 nm lpddr5 on the board, plus 256 mb of on-die sram. no hbm\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Meta MTIA v2</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-meta-platforms\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Meta Platforms\" data-text=\"meta platforms menlo park united states meta ai accelerator vendors hyperscaler in-house inference accelerator designs the mtia inference accelerator for its recommendation and ranking workloads, built with broadcom at tsmc. meta is also one of the largest buyers of gpus from outside chip vendors. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Meta Platforms</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-metal-oxide-resist\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-metal-oxide-resist\" data-alias=\"metal-oxide resists|metal oxide resist|tin-oxide resist|metal-oxide EUV photoresist\" data-text=\"metal-oxide resist metal-oxide resists, metal oxide resist, tin-oxide resist, metal-oxide euv photoresist a metal-oxide resist is a photoresist built on clusters with a tin-oxide core. it absorbs more extreme ultraviolet light than a chemically amplified resist. that helps because an euv dose arrives as relatively few photons.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">metal-oxide resist</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-metax\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"MetaX\" data-alias=\"沐曦集成电路\" data-text=\"metax 沐曦集成电路 shanghai china 688802.ss ai accelerator vendors gpgpu for training and inference a chinese designer of general-purpose gpus, whose xiyun and xisi lines are built for ai training and inference in chinese data centers. it offers a cuda-compatible software stack. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">MetaX</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-meti\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-meti\" data-alias=\"Ministry of Economy|Trade and Industry|Japan's Ministry of Economy|Trade and Industry\" data-text=\"meti ministry of economy, trade and industry, japan's ministry of economy, trade and industry meti is japan's ministry of economy, trade and industry, the ministry that writes japan's export controls and funds its chip industry. it put advanced chipmaking equipment under export license from july 2023. it also supports the chipmaker rapidus and new capacity for mask blanks, the glass plates that photomasks are made from.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">METI</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-metrology\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-metrology\" data-alias=\"process control|when grouped with inspection|metrology and inspection|inspection tools\" data-text=\"metrology process control, when grouped with inspection, metrology and inspection, inspection tools measuring what a factory actually built: how wide a printed line came out, how thick a film is, whether this layer sits exactly on top of the last one. inspection is the related job of finding flaws.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">metrology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-microbump\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-microbump\" data-alias=\"solder bump|solder bumps|bump metrology\" data-text=\"microbump microbumps, solder bump, solder bumps, bumps, bump, bump metrology a microbump is a dot of solder that joins a die to the interposer or substrate beneath it. in intel's 2.5d packages microbumps sit 36 microns apart, less than half a hair's width. each one is an electrical connection that has to survive as the package heats and cools.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">microbump</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-micron-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Micron Technology\" data-alias=\"Micron\" data-text=\"micron technology boise united states mu memory dram, hbm and nand the only american maker of leading-edge dram and the third hbm supplier, with fabs in the us, japan, taiwan and singapore. it has chips act support for new capacity in idaho and new york. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Micron Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-micronics-japan\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Micronics Japan\" data-alias=\"株式会社日本マイクロニクス\" data-text=\"micronics japan 株式会社日本マイクロニクス tokyo japan 6871.t test probe cards for memory test makes probe cards specialized for memory wafer test, including cards that test many dram and hbm dies in parallel, plus display test equipment. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Micronics Japan</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-microsoft-azure-silicon\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Microsoft Azure Silicon\" data-text=\"microsoft azure silicon redmond united states private ai accelerator vendors hyperscaler in-house accelerator designs the maia accelerator family and the cobalt arm server cpu for microsoft's azure cloud. it also designs the 'sidekick' racks that sit beside the servers and supply the liquid cooling they need. maia 200 is the current generation. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Microsoft Azure Silicon</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-microsoft-maia-100\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"microsoft-maia-100\" data-alias=\"Maia 100|100\" data-text=\"microsoft maia 100 maia 5 nm hbm2e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Microsoft Maia 100</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-microsoft-maia-200\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"microsoft-maia-200\" data-alias=\"Maia 200|200\" data-text=\"microsoft maia 200 maia n3 (microsoft says 'the latest tsmc n3 process technology'; it has not named the variant) hbm3e plus 272 mb on-die sram\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Microsoft Maia 200</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-mitsubishi-gas-chemical\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Mitsubishi Gas Chemical\" data-alias=\"Mitsubishi Gas|三菱瓦斯化学株式会社\" data-text=\"mitsubishi gas chemical 三菱瓦斯化学株式会社 tokyo japan 4182.t substrates and pcbs bt resin and copper-clad laminates invented bt resin, the laminate material used in memory and many package substrates, and supplies copper-clad laminates and specialty chemicals for electronics. in october 2024 it estimated that its bt resins held about 40 percent of the substrate materials market. it also promotes a low-warpage copper-clad laminate for flip-chip bga substrates, which carry cpus and gpus. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Mitsubishi Gas Chemical</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-mitsubishi-power\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Mitsubishi Power\" data-text=\"mitsubishi power tokyo japan 7011.t power and cooling gas turbines and power generation equipment makes gas turbines from the 30 mw class to the 563 mw class. it is the power systems brand of mitsubishi heavy industries. in its 2025 annual report, ge vernova names mitsubishi power and siemens energy among the key competitors of its power generation business. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Mitsubishi Power</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-mitsui-chemicals\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Mitsui Chemicals\" data-alias=\"三井化学株式会社\" data-text=\"mitsui chemicals 三井化学株式会社 tokyo japan 4183.t photomasks euv pellicles and semiconductor materials supplies euv pellicles, the thin membranes that keep particles off a photomask while it is exposed. euv pellicles must transmit over 90 percent of 13.5 nm light and survive high source power. only a few suppliers make them. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Mitsui Chemicals</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-mks-instruments\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"MKS Instruments\" data-text=\"mks instruments andover united states mksi equipment subsystems and components rf power, flow control, lasers and plating chemistry supplies the rf generators, mass flow controllers, pressure gauges, vacuum components and ozone systems inside process tools. through atotech it also supplies the electroplating chemistry used for copper interconnect and substrates. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">MKS Instruments</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-mm\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-mm\" data-alias=\"mm2|square millimeters|square millimeter\" data-text=\"mm² mm2, square millimeters, square millimeter mm² means square millimeters, the unit chip areas are given in. a lithography scanner prints at most 858 mm² in one shot, and each compute die in an nvidia b200 is about 800 mm². in 2028 tsmc plans to start making chip packages whose base layer, the wiring that links the chips, covers 14 scanner shots.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">mm²</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-model-weights\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-model-weights\" data-alias=\"frontier model weights|trained weights\" data-text=\"model weights weights, frontier model weights, trained weights model weights are the billions of numbers that make up a trained ai model. they are the file that runs on the chips, so copying the weights copies the model.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">model weights</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-mofcom\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-mofcom\" data-alias=\"Ministry of Commerce|China's Ministry of Commerce\" data-text=\"mofcom ministry of commerce, china's ministry of commerce mofcom is china's ministry of commerce, the ministry that writes and administers china's own export controls. its notices put gallium, germanium and seven rare earths under license. in december 2024 it banned exports of gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard materials to the united states.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">MOFCOM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-monolithic-power-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Monolithic Power Systems\" data-alias=\"Monolithic Power\" data-text=\"monolithic power systems kirkland united states mpwr power and cooling point-of-load power management ics makes the multiphase voltage regulator and power module chips that convert 12 or 48 volts down to the sub-one-volt rails an accelerator core needs, at currents above 1,000 amperes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Monolithic Power Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-moore-threads\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Moore Threads\" data-alias=\"摩尔线程\" data-text=\"moore threads 摩尔线程 beijing china 688795.ss ai accelerator vendors general-purpose gpus for graphics and ai builds full-function gpus with a cuda-like software layer, aimed at replacing nvidia in chinese workstations and training clusters. it listed on shanghai's star market after being placed on the us entity list. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Moore Threads</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-moore-threads-mtt-s5000\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"moore-threads-mtt-s5000\" data-alias=\"MTT S5000|S5000\" data-text=\"moore threads mtt s5000 pinghu \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Moore Threads MTT S5000</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-morita-chemical-industries\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Morita Chemical Industries\" data-alias=\"Morita Chemical|Morita|森田化学工業\" data-text=\"morita chemical industries 森田化学工業 osaka japan private chemicals and gases high-purity hydrogen fluoride and fluorine compounds a japanese maker of hydrofluoric acid and fluorine compounds. its electronics grades are used to etch silicon oxide film and to clean semiconductor material. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Morita Chemical Industries</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-mpi-corporation\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"MPI Corporation\" data-alias=\"MPI|旺矽科技\" data-text=\"mpi corporation 旺矽科技 hsinchu taiwan 6223.two test probe cards and probe stations supplies vertical probe cards, engineering probe stations and thermal test systems, serving taiwanese foundry and osat test operations. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">MPI Corporation</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-multipatterning\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-multipatterning\" data-alias=\"double patterning|quadruple patterning|self-aligned double patterning|self-aligned quadruple patterning|SADP|SAQP|LELE|multiple patterning|multi-patterning|several passes|several exposures|multiply exposed|DUV multipatterning\" data-text=\"multipatterning double patterning, quadruple patterning, self-aligned double patterning, self-aligned quadruple patterning, sadp, saqp, lele, multiple patterning, multi-patterning, several passes, several exposures, multiply exposed, duv multipatterning building one chip layer in several patterning steps, because a single exposure cannot print lines that close together. it comes in two kinds. litho-etch multipatterning splits the layer's pattern across two or three masks, then prints and etches each part separately. self-aligned double or quadruple patterning prints one coarser pattern, then deposits and etches thin spacer films along its edges to halve or quarter the line spacing. cut masks then remove the parts of lines the circuit does not need.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">multipatterning</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nan-ya-pcb\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nan Ya PCB\" data-alias=\"南亞電路板\" data-text=\"nan ya pcb 南亞電路板 taoyuan taiwan 8046.tw substrates and pcbs abf substrates and printed circuit boards produces abf and bt ic substrates and high-layer-count printed circuit boards, and is one of the main ic substrate makers worldwide. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nan Ya PCB</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-nand\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-nand\" data-alias=\"3D NAND|NAND flash|flash memory|128-layer NAND\" data-text=\"nand 3d nand, nand flash, flash memory, 128-layer nand nand is the memory that keeps data when the power is off. it is the storage inside a phone, a laptop drive or a data center disk. 3d nand stacks its cells in many layers, made by etching holes far deeper than they are wide. it is slow next to dram and is not used inside an ai accelerator.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">NAND</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-nanometer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-nanometer\" data-text=\"nanometer nm, nanometers, microns, micrometer, micrometers, angstrom, angstroms, picometer, picometers a nanometer is a billionth of a meter. a micron, or micrometer, is a thousand nanometers, an angstrom is a tenth of a nanometer, and a picometer is a thousandth. lithography light is measured in nanometers, package bumps in microns, and mirror flatness in picometers.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">nanometer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nanya-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nanya Technology\" data-alias=\"Nanya|南亞科技\" data-text=\"nanya technology 南亞科技 new taipei taiwan 2408.tw memory commodity and specialty dram taiwan's dram maker, producing commodity and specialty dram at mature nodes. it does not make hbm and is a generation or more behind the three leading dram makers. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nanya Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-national-silicon-industry-group\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"National Silicon Industry Group\" data-alias=\"National Silicon Industry|沪硅产业\" data-text=\"national silicon industry group 沪硅产业 shanghai china 688126.ss silicon and wafers 300 mm wafers for chinese fabs china's state-backed silicon wafer group, which owns shanghai zing semiconductor (300 mm wafers) and okmetic in finland (specialty wafers). it is china's domestic alternative to japanese wafer supply. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">National Silicon Industry Group</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-naura-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Naura Technology\" data-alias=\"Naura|北方华创\" data-text=\"naura technology 北方华创 beijing china 002371.sz deposition and etch etch, deposition, clean and furnace systems china's largest semiconductor equipment maker, with plasma etch, deposition (pvd, cvd and ald), furnace and cleaning tools. as chinese fabs replaced foreign tools with local ones, naura rose into the world's top ten chipmaking equipment suppliers by sales in 2025. that year three chinese firms made the global top 20, up from one in 2022. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Naura Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-neon\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-neon\" data-alias=\"neon gas|semiconductor-grade neon\" data-text=\"neon neon gas, semiconductor-grade neon neon, mixed with krypton or argon and fluorine, is the gas inside the lasers that give deep ultraviolet scanners their light. a fab uses it by the cylinder, and those scanners cannot print without it.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">neon</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-nl\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"NL\" data-alias=\"NL|Dutch|Holland\" data-text=\"netherlands nl nl dutch holland country the only maker of euv scanners, the machines that print the finest layers\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Netherlands</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nidec\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nidec\" data-alias=\"ニデック株式会社\" data-text=\"nidec ニデック株式会社 kyoto japan 6594.t power and cooling fans, pumps and thermal modules makes precision motors, high static pressure server fans, pumps and liquid cooling modules, and supplies the coolant distribution hardware used in dense ai racks. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nidec</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nikon\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nikon\" data-alias=\"株式会社ニコン\" data-text=\"nikon 株式会社ニコン tokyo japan 7731.t lithography arf immersion, arf and krf scanners, i-line steppers, digital lithography makes arf immersion, arf, krf and i-line lithography systems. it now has a small share of the leading-edge market. but its tools are still used to make chips on older (mature-node) processes, and nikon services them. its current lineup includes no euv system. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nikon</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Lithography</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nippon-sanso-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nippon Sanso Holdings\" data-alias=\"Nippon Sanso|Nippon Sanso|日本酸素ホールディングス\" data-text=\"nippon sanso holdings 日本酸素ホールディングス tokyo japan 4091.t chemicals and gases electronic specialty and bulk gases the parent of taiyo nippon sanso, supplying bulk and electronic specialty gases in japan, the us and asia. it is a major source of the high-purity gases japanese and taiwanese fabs consume. nippon sanso\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nippon Sanso Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-nitrogen-trifluoride\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-nitrogen-trifluoride\" data-alias=\"NF3\" data-text=\"nitrogen trifluoride nf3 nitrogen trifluoride is a gas that cleans process chambers between wafers. split apart in a plasma, it releases fluorine that scours the deposits off the inside of the chamber.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">nitrogen trifluoride</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nittobo\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nittobo\" data-alias=\"日東紡績株式会社\" data-text=\"nittobo 日東紡績株式会社 tokyo japan 3110.t substrates and pcbs low-cte t-glass fiber and glass cloth weaves the ultra-fine low thermal expansion glass cloth, known as t-glass, that reinforces high-end package substrates and server boards. its fiber keeps large substrates flat as they heat. in august 2025 it decided to expand glass fiber cloth production at its fukushima enterprise center, with the added output starting in the fourth quarter of its fiscal 2026. it says chinese and taiwanese companies are aggressively catching up with it in special glass. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nittobo</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-nm-class\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-nm-class\" data-alias=\"5 nm-class|7 nm-class|2 nm-class|nanometer-class|nm class\" data-text=\"nm-class 5 nm-class, 7 nm-class, 2 nm-class, nanometer-class, nm class nm-class, as in 7 nm-class, means a process roughly as dense as the foundries' 7 nm generation. the label is used when a maker's own name for the node is different.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">nm-class</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-node\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-node\" data-alias=\"process node|technology node|for example N2 or 18A\" data-text=\"node process node, technology node, for example n2 or 18a, nodes the name a foundry gives one generation of its manufacturing process. the number in the name no longer measures anything on the chip. smic's n+3, a 7 nm-class process, spaces its narrowest wires closer together than intel's panther lake chips on 18a do.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">node</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nova-ltd\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nova Ltd\" data-alias=\"Nova\" data-text=\"nova ltd rehovot israel nvmi metrology and inspection optical cd and materials metrology supplies optical critical dimension scatterometry and x-ray metrology used to measure three-dimensional structures such as gate-all-around nanosheets and high aspect ratio memory holes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nova Ltd</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nuflare-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"NuFlare Technology\" data-alias=\"NuFlare|株式会社ニューフレアテクノロジー\" data-text=\"nuflare technology 株式会社ニューフレアテクノロジー yokohama japan private photomasks electron-beam mask writers and inspection makes variable-shaped-beam and multi-beam electron mask writers and mask inspection systems. its mbm series competes with ims nanofabrication in multi-beam mask writing. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">NuFlare Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-nvidia\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Nvidia\" data-text=\"nvidia santa clara united states nvda ai accelerator vendors merchant gpus and rack-scale ai systems designs the blackwell and rubin gpus, the nvlink connections that join many gpus into one system, and the nvl72 rack systems. most ai training and a large share of inference run on this hardware. it also makes the cuda software stack that ties developers to its hardware. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-a100\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-a100\" data-alias=\"A100|Ampere\" data-text=\"nvidia a100 (80 gb sxm) ampere n7 hbm2e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia A100 (80 GB SXM)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-a800\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-a800\" data-alias=\"A800|A100|Ampere\" data-text=\"nvidia a800 (china variant of the a100) ampere n7 hbm2e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia A800 (China variant of the A100)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-b200\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-b200\" data-alias=\"B200|Blackwell\" data-text=\"nvidia b200 blackwell 4np (custom n4p) hbm3e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia B200</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-b300\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-b300\" data-alias=\"B300|GB300|NVL72|Blackwell Ultra\" data-text=\"nvidia b300 (gb300 nvl72) blackwell ultra 4np (custom n4p) hbm3e (12-high)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia B300 (GB300 NVL72)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-h100\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-h100\" data-alias=\"H100|SXM5|Hopper\" data-text=\"nvidia h100 (sxm5) hopper 4n (custom n5-derived) hbm3\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia H100 (SXM5)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-h20\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-h20\" data-alias=\"H20|Hopper\" data-text=\"nvidia h20 (hgx h20, china variant) hopper 4n (custom n5-derived) hbm3\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia H20 (HGX H20, China variant)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-h200-china\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-h200-china\" data-alias=\"H200|Hopper\" data-text=\"nvidia h200 (china-licensed configuration) hopper 4n (custom n5-derived) hbm3e\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia H200 (China-licensed configuration)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-h800\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-h800\" data-alias=\"H800|H100|Hopper\" data-text=\"nvidia h800 (china variant of the h100) hopper 4n (custom n5-derived) hbm3\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia H800 (China variant of the H100)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-nvidia-vr200\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"nvidia-vr200\" data-alias=\"Rubin|VR200\" data-text=\"nvidia rubin (vr200) rubin 3np, from tsmc’s n3p (per semianalysis) hbm4 (12-high)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Nvidia Rubin (VR200)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-nvl72\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-nvl72\" data-alias=\"GB200 NVL72|GB300 NVL72|Vera Rubin NVL72\" data-text=\"nvl72 gb200 nvl72, gb300 nvl72, vera rubin nvl72 nvidia's rack-sized product, with 72 accelerators in 18 compute trays joined through nine switch trays so that software can treat the whole rack as one computer. the gb300 version draws up to 142 kilowatts.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">NVL72</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-nvlink\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-nvlink\" data-alias=\"NVSwitch|NVLink 5|NVLink 6|NV-HBI\" data-text=\"nvlink nvswitch, nvlink 5, nvlink 6, nv-hbi nvidia's own high-speed connection between its accelerators, which lets dozens of them act as one. nvlink 6 carries 3,600 gigabytes per second per gpu, according to nvidia's january 2026 rubin launch.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">NVLink</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-oci-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"OCI Holdings\" data-alias=\"OCI|오씨아이홀딩스\" data-text=\"oci holdings 오씨아이홀딩스 seoul south korea 010060.ks silicon and wafers polysilicon and electronic-grade chemicals a korean chemical group that makes polysilicon and fab chemicals, including high-purity hydrogen peroxide and phosphoric acid. most of its polysilicon goes to solar customers. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">OCI Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-odm\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-odm\" data-alias=\"original design manufacturer|ODMs|contract manufacturer|contract manufacturers|contract manufacturing|EMS|server ODM\" data-text=\"odm original design manufacturer, odms, contract manufacturer, contract manufacturers, contract manufacturing, ems, server odm an odm, for original design manufacturer, is a firm such as foxconn, quanta or wistron that designs and builds servers and racks to a customer's specification. the customer's name goes on the box. a contract manufacturer does the assembly only.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ODM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-oligopoly\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-oligopoly\" data-alias=\"three-firm oligopoly\" data-text=\"oligopoly oligopolies, duopoly, three-firm oligopoly an oligopoly is a market with only a few sellers, so each one's decisions move the price. a duopoly has two. dram, industrial gases, substrates and chip testers are all oligopolies.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">oligopoly</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-onto-innovation\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Onto Innovation\" data-text=\"onto innovation wilmington united states onto metrology and inspection optical metrology, inspection and lithography software supplies optical film metrology, macro defect inspection and packaging inspection, with a strong position in advanced packaging metrology. it was formed from rudolph technologies and nanometrics. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Onto Innovation</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-chip-openai-jalapeno\" data-kind=\"chip\" data-key=\"openai-jalapeno\" data-alias=\"Jalapeño|OpenAI Intelligence Processor\" data-text=\"openai with broadcom jalapeño openai intelligence processor n3p compute die, n3e i/o chiplet (per semianalysis) hbm4 (per semianalysis)\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">OpenAI with Broadcom Jalapeño</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">AI chip</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-operating-margin\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-operating-margin\" data-alias=\"operating profit|operating loss|operating income\" data-text=\"operating margin operating profit, operating loss, operating income operating margin is the share of revenue left after paying both the cost of making the product and the cost of running the company, research and sales included. it is lower than gross margin, which counts only the cost of making.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">operating margin</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-optical-transceiver\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-optical-transceiver\" data-alias=\"optical module|pluggable optics|optical transceivers|optical modules|800G optical transceivers\" data-text=\"optical transceiver optical module, pluggable optics, optical transceivers, transceiver, transceivers, optical modules, 800g optical transceivers a small device that turns electrical signals into laser light for sending down a glass fiber, and turns them back at the far end. every network link longer than a few meters in a large ai cluster needs one at each end.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">optical transceiver</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-osat\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-osat\" data-alias=\"outsourced semiconductor assembly and test|OSATs|outsourced assembly and test|assembly and test firms|assembly and test contractor|assembly and test houses\" data-text=\"osat outsourced semiconductor assembly and test, osats, outsourced assembly and test, assembly and test firms, assembly and test contractor, assembly and test houses a contract firm that takes finished wafers, cuts them into chips, seals the chips into packages and tests them. it is the back end of chipmaking, done for hire.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">OSAT</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-overlay\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-overlay\" data-alias=\"overlay error\" data-text=\"overlay overlay error, alignment how precisely one printed layer of a chip lands on top of the layer beneath it. before each exposure the scanner finds marks printed in earlier layers and lines the new layer up on them to within a few nanometers, across a disc 300 millimeters wide.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">overlay</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-panasonic-industry\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Panasonic Industry\" data-alias=\"パナソニック インダストリー\" data-text=\"panasonic industry パナソニック インダストリー osaka japan private substrates and pcbs copper-clad laminates and electronic materials makes the megtron series of low-loss copper-clad laminates used in high-speed server and switch boards. at 112 gbps, too much signal loss in the board makes a link fail. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Panasonic Industry</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-panel-level-packaging\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-panel-level-packaging\" data-alias=\"panel-level|panel level packaging|rectangular panel|rectangular panels\" data-text=\"panel-level packaging panel-level, panel level packaging, rectangular panel, rectangular panels panel-level packaging builds packages on a large rectangular sheet instead of a round wafer, so far less area is wasted at the edges and many more packages fit on one carrier. it gets around the size limits of a 300 mm wafer.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">panel-level packaging</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-park-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Park Systems\" data-alias=\"Park|파크시스템스\" data-text=\"park systems 파크시스템스 gwacheon south korea 140860.kq metrology and inspection atomic force microscopy makes the automated atomic force microscopes fabs use to measure surface roughness, step height and defect profiles at sub-nanometer resolution. it acquired the ellipsometry maker accurion in 2022 and the holographic microscopy maker lyncée tec in 2025. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Park Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-pcie\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-pcie\" data-alias=\"PCI Express|PCIe 6|PCIe 7\" data-text=\"pcie pci express, pcie 6, pcie 7 pcie is the standard connector and link that joins a processor to the cards inside a computer, an accelerator included. in an ai server it carries data between the host processor and the gpus, while faster private links join the gpus to each other.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">PCIe</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-pdk\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-pdk\" data-alias=\"process design kit|process design kits\" data-text=\"pdk process design kit, process design kits a process design kit, or pdk, is the set of files a foundry gives designers to describe exactly what its factory can print on one process, or node. it gives the sizes, spacings and electrical behavior of every feature. design software is checked against it before a chip is accepted.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">PDK</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-pellicle\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-pellicle\" data-alias=\"EUV pellicle\" data-text=\"pellicle pellicles, euv pellicle a thin transparent membrane on a frame above a photomask, the patterned plate a chip layer is printed from. dust settles on it, far enough out of focus that it does not print, so the pattern stays clean. it works like a lens cap a photographer can shoot through.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">pellicle</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-performance-density\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-performance-density\" data-text=\"performance density an export control test of how densely a chip packs its computing power. it divides the chip's tpp, the export rules' measure of computing power, by its applicable die area in square millimeters. that area counts all logic dies made on a process with non-planar transistors, such as finfets. the test applies only to a chip that reaches 1,600 tpp. it replaced the 2022 test, which was based on interconnect bandwidth, the speed at which a chip exchanges data with its neighbors.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">performance density</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-pfeiffer-vacuum\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Pfeiffer Vacuum\" data-text=\"pfeiffer vacuum asslar germany pfv.de equipment subsystems and components turbomolecular pumps and leak detection makes turbomolecular pumps, which spin at tens of thousands of revolutions per minute to reach the high vacuum that etch, deposition and euv chambers require. it also makes leak detection instruments. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Pfeiffer Vacuum</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-photomask\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-photomask\" data-alias=\"mask set|mask sets|mask blank set\" data-text=\"photomask mask, reticle, mask set, photomasks, masks, mask sets, mask blank set the master template for one layer of a chip: a quartz plate, or for the shortest wavelengths a mirror, that carries the pattern projected onto the wafer. a chip needs dozens of them, at least one per layer. in july 2022 semianalysis put a full set above $1 million at 28 nm and above $10 million at 7 nm. in may 2026 it put a leading-edge set at $40 million.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">photomask</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-photoresist\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-photoresist\" data-alias=\"EUV resist|EUV resists|resist makers\" data-text=\"photoresist resist, resists, euv resist, euv resists, resist makers the light-sensitive coating that records a chip's pattern during lithography. a machine spins a thin film of it across the wafer. light shone through a stencil changes the film where it lands, and a wash removes those parts. what remains shows the next machine where to etch.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">photoresist</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-photronics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Photronics\" data-text=\"photronics brookfield united states plab photomasks merchant photomask manufacturing a merchant photomask maker, writing and inspecting masks for logic and display customers from plants in the us, taiwan, korea, china and europe. the foundries make most leading-edge masks in-house. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Photronics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-piotech\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Piotech\" data-alias=\"拓荆科技\" data-text=\"piotech 拓荆科技 shenyang china 688072.ss deposition and etch pecvd, ald and wafer bonding china's main domestic supplier of plasma-enhanced cvd and ald systems, and more recently hybrid wafer bonding tools aimed at 3d integration. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Piotech</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-pitch\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-pitch\" data-alias=\"half-pitch|gate pitch|metal pitch|wire pitch|line pitch\" data-text=\"pitch pitches, half-pitch, gate pitch, metal pitch, wire pitch, line pitch pitch is the distance from one line on a chip to the next, center to center, so it counts the line and the gap together. half-pitch is half that. a 16 nm pitch means lines 16 nanometers apart. the 2022 us rules set a dram threshold at 18 nm half-pitch.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">pitch</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-plasma\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-plasma\" data-alias=\"plasma etch|plasma-enhanced|plasma source\" data-text=\"plasma plasmas, plasma etch, plasma-enhanced, plasma source a plasma is a gas energized until some of its atoms or molecules break into charged particles. most etch steps and many deposition steps happen in a plasma that an electric field makes inside a vacuum chamber, though batch furnaces mostly work without one. in the chamber, neutral fragments called radicals do most of the chemistry, and charged ions give etch its direction. in an extreme ultraviolet machine, a laser vaporizes droplets of molten tin into a plasma that gives off the 13.5-nanometer light.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">plasma</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-polysilicon\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-polysilicon\" data-alias=\"polycrystalline silicon|electronic-grade polysilicon|semiconductor-grade polysilicon|polysilicon feedstock\" data-text=\"polysilicon polycrystalline silicon, electronic-grade polysilicon, semiconductor-grade polysilicon, polysilicon feedstock polysilicon is purified silicon that has not yet been grown into one crystal. it comes as gray rods made of many small crystals. it is the raw material that is melted down to pull the single crystal a wafer is cut from. the same material, at lower purity, goes into solar panels.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">polysilicon</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-power-shelf\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-power-shelf\" data-alias=\"power shelves|rack power shelf\" data-text=\"power shelf power shelves, rack power shelf a power shelf is a slide-in unit in a rack that converts the incoming supply to the voltage the boards use and feeds it to the busbar. a gb300 nvl72 rack draws its 142 kilowatts through eight of them at 33 kilowatts each.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">power shelf</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-powertech-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Powertech Technology\" data-alias=\"Powertech|力成科技\" data-text=\"powertech technology 力成科技 hsinchu taiwan 6239.tw advanced packaging and osat memory packaging and test specializes in memory assembly and test, including dram and nand packaging, and has been adding capacity for hbm-related and logic advanced packaging work. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Powertech Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-presumption-of-approval\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-presumption-of-approval\" data-alias=\"approval is presumed|presumed approval\" data-text=\"presumption of approval approval is presumed, presumed approval a presumption of approval means a license is still required but will normally be granted. it is the opposite of a presumption of denial, and one rule can contain both. hbm license applications for macau and country group d:5 are presumed approved when neither the buyer nor its ultimate parent is headquartered in either place, and presumed denied otherwise (15 cfr 742.6(b)(10)(ii)).\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">presumption of approval</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-presumption-of-denial\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-presumption-of-denial\" data-text=\"presumption of denial a license review policy in which the reviewing agencies start from the position that an application should be refused. an application can still be filed and will be considered, but the exporter has to overcome that starting position. it is the general policy for advanced computing chips going to china and macau under 15 cfr 742.6(b)(10), and for most entity list entries. since january 2026 export applications for some less powerful chips, such as the h200, are reviewed case by case instead.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">presumption of denial</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-primarius-technologies\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Primarius Technologies\" data-alias=\"Primarius|概伦电子\" data-text=\"primarius technologies 概伦电子 shanghai china 688206.ss design and eda device modeling, spice simulation and dtco a chinese eda vendor that makes device modeling, parameter extraction and fast spice circuit simulation software. device models describe how the transistors on a foundry's process behave, so chip designers can simulate their circuits on that process. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Primarius Technologies</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Design and EDA</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-printed-circuit-board\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-printed-circuit-board\" data-alias=\"PCB|PCBs|printed circuit boards|circuit board|circuit boards|high-multilayer PCB\" data-text=\"printed circuit board pcb, pcbs, printed circuit boards, circuit board, circuit boards, high-multilayer pcb a printed circuit board is the flat green or black card that electronic parts are soldered onto, with its wiring etched from copper sheets and stacked in layers. boards for ai servers can run past 30 layers.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">printed circuit board</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-probe-card\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-probe-card\" data-alias=\"probe cards\" data-text=\"probe card probe cards a circuit board carrying thousands of fine needles that press onto the contact pads of a chip while it is still part of the wafer. a tester drives signals into the chip through the needles. every card is custom-built for one chip design.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">probe card</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-pvd\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-pvd\" data-alias=\"physical vapor deposition|sputtering target|sputtering targets\" data-text=\"pvd physical vapor deposition, sputtering, sputtering target, sputtering targets, sputter physical vapor deposition, or pvd, coats a wafer with metal in a vacuum. it knocks atoms off a solid slab of metal, the sputtering target, and they fly across and land on the wafer as a thin film. it lays down the metal barriers and seed layers under a chip's copper wiring.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">PVD</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-qnity-electronics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Qnity Electronics\" data-alias=\"Qnity\" data-text=\"qnity electronics wilmington united states q photoresist and materials cmp slurries and pads, lithography and packaging materials dupont's former electronics business, an independent company since 1 november 2025. it supplies chemical mechanical planarization slurries and pads, lithographic materials, and metallization and other materials for chip packaging and circuit boards. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Qnity Electronics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-qualcomm\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Qualcomm\" data-text=\"qualcomm san diego united states qcom ai accelerator vendors edge ai socs and data-center inference accelerators designs snapdragon chips with built-in neural engines that run ai on phones and other devices. in 2025 it announced the ai200 and ai250 rack-scale inference accelerators. its purchase of alphawave added the high-speed connection (serdes) ip a data-center chip needs. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Qualcomm</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-qualification\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-qualification\" data-alias=\"qualification tests|qualification lock-in\" data-text=\"qualification qualify, qualifies, qualified, qualifying, requalify, requalification, qualification tests, qualification lock-in qualification is the testing a fab or a customer runs before it will accept a new material, tool or supplier. a resist, a slurry, a wafer source or a memory stack is approved for a set use, such as one layer in one fab's process, and switching means running the tests again.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">qualification</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-quanta-computer\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Quanta Computer\" data-alias=\"廣達電腦\" data-text=\"quanta computer 廣達電腦 taoyuan taiwan 2382.tw systems and servers ai server odm builds gpu baseboards, servers and full racks for hyperscalers and for nvidia reference systems, with plants in taiwan, the us, mexico and thailand. it is one of the largest ai server odms, the contract firms that design and build servers for other companies. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Quanta Computer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-rack\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-rack\" data-alias=\"rack-scale\" data-text=\"rack cabinet, racks, cabinets, rack-scale the standard steel frame that computing equipment is bolted into in a data center, roughly the size of a wardrobe. for ai, a whole rack is wired and sold as one machine, so the rack itself is the product.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">rack</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-rambus\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Rambus\" data-text=\"rambus san jose united states rmbs ip and architecture memory interface ip and controllers licenses the memory controller and interface (phy) ip that connects a processor to ddr5, lpddr and hbm memory. it also sells register clock drivers, the buffer chips on server memory modules. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Rambus</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">IP and architecture</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ramp\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ramp\" data-alias=\"ramp-up|yield at ramp\" data-text=\"ramp ramps, ramp-up, ramping, yield at ramp a ramp is the months in which a new process or product climbs from a few wafers a week to full output while the share of working chips rises. yield is lowest at the start of the ramp and improves as engineers find which steps lose dies.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ramp</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-rapidus\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Rapidus\" data-alias=\"ラピダス株式会社\" data-text=\"rapidus ラピダス株式会社 tokyo japan private foundry 2 nm pilot foundry runs a 2 nm gate-all-around pilot line in chitose, hokkaido, using ibm and imec technology and asml euv tools. it is japan's attempt to rebuild leading-edge logic manufacturing. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Rapidus</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-rare-earths\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-rare-earths\" data-alias=\"rare earth|rare-earth|rare earth elements|medium and heavy rare earths\" data-text=\"rare earths rare earth, rare-earth, rare earth elements, medium and heavy rare earths the rare earths are a group of metals, including samarium and yttrium, that go into the strong magnets in motors, disk drives and wind turbines, and into some lasers and glass.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">rare earths</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-rebellions\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Rebellions\" data-alias=\"리벨리온\" data-text=\"rebellions 리벨리온 seongnam south korea private ai accelerator vendors inference accelerators an ai chip startup building the rebel inference accelerator with samsung foundry and sk hynix hbm. it is the national champion for korean ai silicon. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Rebellions</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-redistribution-layer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-redistribution-layer\" data-alias=\"RDL|redistribution wiring|redistribution layers\" data-text=\"redistribution layer rdl, redistribution wiring, redistribution layers a redistribution layer is a thin sheet of fine copper wiring, laid down in resin, that spreads a die's tightly spaced connections out to a wider pattern the package can handle. cowos-r and cowos-l use it in place of a full silicon interposer.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">redistribution layer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-reexport\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-reexport\" data-text=\"reexport shipping an item that falls under us export rules, the ear, from one foreign country to another. the term is defined at 15 cfr 734.14. a memory stack subject to the ear moving from korea to china is a reexport, and it needs the same us license a shipment from texas would.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">reexport</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-resonac-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Resonac Holdings\" data-alias=\"Resonac|株式会社レゾナック\" data-text=\"resonac holdings 株式会社レゾナック tokyo japan 4004.t chemicals and gases etch gases, packaging materials and cmp slurries supplies high-purity etch gases, cmp slurries, die attach films, and the copper-clad laminates and encapsulants used in advanced packaging. it was formed from showa denko and hitachi chemical. it leads a consortium on panel-level packaging. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Resonac Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-reticle\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-reticle\" data-text=\"reticle photomask the patterned plate whose image a lithography machine projects onto the wafer, one chip layer at a time. in practice it means the same as photomask, but the word reticle stresses that the machine steps the same image again and again across the wafer.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">reticle</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-reticle-limit\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-reticle-limit\" data-alias=\"reticle size limit|reticle field|field size|reticle-limited|reticle size|times reticle\" data-text=\"reticle limit reticle size limit, reticle field, field size, reticle-limited, reticle size, reticles, times reticle the largest chip a lithography machine can print in a single exposure, about 858 square millimeters, or 26 by 33 millimeters. it is set by the machine's optics and is the same for every design. the newer high-na euv machines print half that area.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">reticle limit</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-risc-v\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-risc-v\" data-alias=\"RISC-V cores|RISC-V processor\" data-text=\"risc-v risc-v cores, risc-v processor risc-v is an open instruction set, the list of basic commands a processor understands, that anyone may use without a license. companies build their own processor cores on it, and nvidia now uses such cores for small control tasks inside every gpu.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">RISC-V</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-rtl\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-rtl\" data-alias=\"register-transfer level|register-transfer-level|register transfer level|RTL description|RTL code\" data-text=\"rtl register-transfer level, register-transfer-level, register transfer level, rtl description, rtl code rtl, for register-transfer level, is the code in which a chip is first written. it is text, in a language such as systemverilog, that describes what every storage element holds on every tick of the clock. software later turns it into transistors and wires.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">RTL</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sambanova-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SambaNova Systems\" data-alias=\"SambaNova\" data-text=\"sambanova systems palo alto united states private ai accelerator vendors reconfigurable dataflow accelerators builds reconfigurable dataflow units, ai chips that are set up to match how data flows through each model. they use a large three-tier memory system. sambanova sells them as an inference cloud service and as full systems for companies that want to run models on their own premises. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SambaNova Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-samsung-electro-mechanics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Samsung Electro-Mechanics\" data-alias=\"삼성전기\" data-text=\"samsung electro-mechanics 삼성전기 suwon south korea 009150.ks substrates and pcbs fc-bga substrates and mlccs makes flip-chip bga substrates for processors and ai accelerators, plus multilayer ceramic capacitors (mlccs) used in dense server power delivery. it is expanding fc-bga capacity in busan and vietnam. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Samsung Electro-Mechanics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-samsung-foundry\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Samsung Foundry\" data-alias=\"삼성 파운드리\" data-text=\"samsung foundry 삼성 파운드리 hwaseong south korea private foundry leading-edge logic foundry a foundry running its 2 nm class sf2 process in korea and building a fab in taylor, texas. its gate-all-around transistors, introduced at 3 nm, are in production. large ai customers keep qualifying it as a second source. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Samsung Foundry</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-samsung-memory\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Samsung Memory\" data-alias=\"삼성전자 메모리사업부\" data-text=\"samsung memory 삼성전자 메모리사업부 hwaseong south korea private memory dram, hbm and nand samsung electronics' memory business, supplying dram, nand and hbm. it began mass production of hbm4 in 2026 and says it was the first to ship commercial hbm4, at 11.7 gbps per pin. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Samsung Memory</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sandisk\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SanDisk\" data-text=\"sandisk milpitas united states sndk memory 3d nand flash and ssds manufactures 3d nand in a joint venture with kioxia and sells client and enterprise ssds. it became a standalone company again when western digital split its flash and disk businesses. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SanDisk</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-scale-out-network\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-scale-out-network\" data-alias=\"back-end network|cluster fabric|scale-out|scale out\" data-text=\"scale-out network back-end network, cluster fabric, scale-out, scale out the network that joins thousands of accelerator groups into one cluster, running at hundreds of gigabits per second over ethernet or infiniband. its ethernet versions use the same standard as ordinary data center networks.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">scale-out network</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-scale-up-network\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-scale-up-network\" data-alias=\"scale-up fabric|coherent domain|scale-up|scale up|scale-up domain|scale-up switch\" data-text=\"scale-up network scale-up fabric, coherent domain, scale-up, scale up, scale-up domain, scale-up switch the network that joins a group of accelerators, from a few dozen in one rack to thousands, so a model too large for a single chip can be spread across them. it runs at terabytes per second. in nvidia's gb300 nvl72 each gpu has nine times as much bandwidth on it as on the scale-out network.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">scale-up network</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-scanner\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-scanner\" data-alias=\"lithography scanner|lithography scanners|lithography machine|lithography system|lithography systems\" data-text=\"scanner scanners, stepper, steppers, lithography scanner, lithography scanners, lithography machine, lithography system, lithography systems a scanner is the lithography machine itself. it holds the photomask up to a light source and projects a shrunken image of one layer onto the wafer. mask and wafer sweep past each other in a narrow slit of light. an older stepper exposes the whole mask image at once instead of scanning. a standard euv scanner sells for around $200 million.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">scanner</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-schneider-electric\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Schneider Electric\" data-text=\"schneider electric rueil-malmaison france su.pa power and cooling electrical distribution, ups and cooling supplies medium and low voltage electrical distribution, uninterruptible power supplies under the apc brand, busway and liquid cooling for data centers, plus the design software operators plan with. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Schneider Electric</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-screen-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SCREEN Holdings\" data-alias=\"SCREEN|株式会社SCREENホールディングス\" data-text=\"screen holdings 株式会社screenホールディングス kyoto japan 7735.t deposition and etch wafer cleaning and surface preparation makes the single-wafer and batch cleaning systems that remove particles and residues between almost every process step. cleaning is the most frequently repeated operation in a fab. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SCREEN Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-second-source\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-second-source\" data-alias=\"second sources|second-source|multi-sourcing|dual source|single source|sole source|single-source\" data-text=\"second source second sources, second-source, multi-sourcing, dual source, single source, sole source, single-source a second source is a second supplier qualified for the same part or material, so that a fab can keep running if the first one stops shipping. a single-source part has none, and adding one means joint development and a fresh qualification.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">second source</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-semes\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SEMES\" data-alias=\"세메스\" data-text=\"semes 세메스 cheonan south korea private deposition and etch cleaning, track and packaging equipment supplies wafer cleaning, coater/developer track, etch and packaging systems, mainly to samsung. by its own description it is korea's largest maker of chip and display equipment, with sales of about krw 2.46 trillion in 2025. through semes, samsung keeps some tool technology in house. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SEMES</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-semitronix\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Semitronix\" data-alias=\"杭州广立微\" data-text=\"semitronix 杭州广立微 hangzhou china 301095.sz design and eda yield-analysis eda and test chips supplies test-chip design software, on-wafer electrical test systems and yield analysis tools used to measure and debug a new manufacturing process. its products fall between design software and metrology (measurement) equipment. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Semitronix</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Design and EDA</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-serdes\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-serdes\" data-alias=\"serializer-deserializer|high-speed serial links|serial links|serial link\" data-text=\"serdes serializer-deserializer, high-speed serial links, serial links, serial link a serdes, for serializer-deserializer, is the circuit at the edge of a chip that turns many slow parallel signals into one very fast stream over a single pair of wires. a serdes at the other end turns the stream back into parallel signals. every link out of an accelerator, to another chip, a switch or an optical module, runs through one.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SerDes</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-shenzhen-newway-photomask\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Shenzhen Newway Photomask\" data-alias=\"路维光电\" data-text=\"shenzhen newway photomask 路维光电 shenzhen china 688401.ss photomasks merchant photomasks for chips and displays a chinese merchant mask maker that photronics names among its competitors in chip and display masks. no chinese firm makes euv mask blanks or the tools that check euv masks. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Shenzhen Newway Photomask</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-shenzhen-qingyi-photomask\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Shenzhen Qingyi Photomask\" data-alias=\"清溢光电\" data-text=\"shenzhen qingyi photomask 清溢光电 shenzhen china 688138.ss photomasks merchant photomasks for chips and displays a chinese merchant mask maker that photronics names among its competitors in chip and display masks. no chinese firm makes euv mask blanks or the tools that check euv masks. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Shenzhen Qingyi Photomask</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-shin-etsu-chemical\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Shin-Etsu Chemical\" data-alias=\"Shin-Etsu|Shin-Etsu|信越化学工業\" data-text=\"shin-etsu chemical 信越化学工業 tokyo japan 4063.t silicon and wafers 300 mm polished and epitaxial wafers, photoresist, pellicles the world's largest silicon wafer maker by capacity and shipments. silicon wafers are the blank discs every logic and memory die is built on. shin-etsu held an estimated 22 percent of global 300 mm wafer capacity at the end of 2024, according to the october 2025 listing prospectus of the chinese wafer maker eswin. it also makes arf and euv photoresist, the light-sensitive coating chip patterns are printed into, and pellicles, the thin films that keep dust off photomasks. so it supplies three separate stages of the chain. shin-etsu\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Shin-Etsu Chemical</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-shinko-electric-industries\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Shinko Electric Industries\" data-alias=\"Shinko Electric|新光電気工業\" data-text=\"shinko electric industries 新光電気工業 nagano japan private substrates and pcbs fc-bga substrates and lead frames makes high-end flip-chip bga substrates, plus lead frames and interposers. other japanese makers of high-end substrates include ibiden and toppan. it was taken private in 2025 by a company owned mainly by funds of jic capital, a subsidiary of japan investment corporation. in september 2026 shinko agreed to buy japan display's mobara plant in chiba as a new core plant for its flip-chip package substrates. production there is scheduled for fiscal 2028. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Shinko Electric Industries</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-siemens-eda\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Siemens EDA\" data-text=\"siemens eda wilsonville united states private design and eda design for test, physical verification, calibre the third-largest maker of chip design (eda) software. its calibre tool is the de facto standard for physical verification, the check foundries use to confirm a layout follows their manufacturing rules before they accept it. it also sells design-for-test software. foundries write the rule files they give chip designers in calibre's format. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Siemens EDA</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Design and EDA</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-siemens-energy\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Siemens Energy\" data-text=\"siemens energy munich germany enr.de power and cooling turbines, grid technology and transformers supplies gas turbines, grid transmission equipment and transformers. its orders are booked years ahead because data center and electrification demand exceeds its manufacturing capacity. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Siemens Energy</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sifive\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SiFive\" data-text=\"sifive santa clara united states private ip and architecture risc-v processor ip sells risc-v cpu cores, including vector and matrix cores used as control processors inside ai accelerators. risc-v is the license-free alternative to arm, and chinese chip designers are adopting it heavily. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SiFive</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">IP and architecture</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-signoff\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-signoff\" data-alias=\"sign-off|static timing analysis|timing signoff|timing sign-off|physical verification|signed off\" data-text=\"signoff sign-off, static timing analysis, timing signoff, timing sign-off, physical verification, signed off signoff is the final set of automated checks a chip design must pass before tape-out. static timing analysis checks that every signal arrives in time at the clock speed promised. physical verification checks that every shape in the layout can be printed.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">signoff</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-silicon-bridge\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-silicon-bridge\" data-alias=\"silicon bridges|EMIB|silicon-bridge|local silicon bridges|embedded bridge\" data-text=\"silicon bridge silicon bridges, emib, silicon-bridge, local silicon bridges, embedded bridge a silicon bridge is a small sliver of silicon carrying dense wiring. it is set into the package only where two dies need thousands of connections between them, so the rest of the package can use cheaper wiring. intel calls its version emib, and tsmc's cowos-l uses the same idea.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">silicon bridge</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-silicon-shield\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-silicon-shield\" data-text=\"silicon shield the argument that taiwan's lead in advanced chipmaking deters an attack on the island, because so many countries rely on its chips.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">silicon shield</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-siltronic\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Siltronic\" data-text=\"siltronic munich germany waf.de silicon and wafers 300 mm polished and epitaxial wafers europe's silicon wafer maker, with 300 mm capacity in germany and a newer fab in singapore. its planned sale to globalwafers lapsed in 2022 when the german government did not grant investment clearance before the deadline. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Siltronic</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-sg\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"SG\" data-alias=\"SG|Singaporean\" data-text=\"singapore sg sg singaporean country test, assembly and mature-node fabs\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Singapore</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sk-hynix\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SK hynix\" data-alias=\"에스케이하이닉스\" data-text=\"sk hynix 에스케이하이닉스 icheon south korea 000660.ks memory hbm, dram and nand the largest supplier of high bandwidth memory (hbm), with a large conventional dram and nand business that includes solidigm. hbm is a stack of dram chips connected by through-silicon vias, copper columns that run through the chips. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SK hynix</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sk-siltron\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SK Siltron\" data-alias=\"에스케이실트론\" data-text=\"sk siltron 에스케이실트론 gumi south korea private silicon and wafers 300 mm silicon wafers and sic substrates korea's silicon wafer maker, supplying 300 mm wafers largely to samsung and sk hynix. it also makes silicon carbide substrates for power devices at a us plant in michigan. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SK Siltron</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sk-specialty\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SK Specialty\" data-alias=\"에스케이스페셜티\" data-text=\"sk specialty 에스케이스페셜티 yeongju south korea private chemicals and gases nitrogen trifluoride and specialty etch gases produces nitrogen trifluoride, the gas used to clean deposition chambers, plus tungsten hexafluoride and other specialty etch gases. the more wafers a fab runs through deposition, the more chamber cleaning gas it uses. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SK Specialty</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-skyverse-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Skyverse Technology\" data-alias=\"Skyverse|中科飞测\" data-text=\"skyverse technology 中科飞测 shenzhen china 688361.ss metrology and inspection domestic chinese wafer inspection and metrology a shenzhen maker of wafer defect inspection and film metrology tools, aiming to replace kla systems in chinese fabs. its coverage is strongest at mature nodes. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Skyverse Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-small-yard-high-fence\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-small-yard-high-fence\" data-alias=\"small yard with a high fence|small yard\" data-text=\"small yard, high fence small yard with a high fence, small yard the stated design of us technology controls: tightly restrict a narrow set of items that genuinely matter to national security, and leave the rest of trade alone.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">small yard, high fence</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-smee\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SMEE\" data-alias=\"上海微电子装备\" data-text=\"smee 上海微电子装备 shanghai china private lithography domestic chinese lithography scanners a chinese maker of lithography scanners, founded in 2002 in shanghai's zhangjiang park. it ships i-line and krf class tools for packaging and mature nodes. reports of a domestic immersion arf tool in production have not been independently confirmed. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SMEE</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Lithography</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-smic\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SMIC\" data-alias=\"中芯国际\" data-text=\"smic 中芯国际 shanghai china 0981.hk foundry chinese logic foundry china's largest foundry, producing 7 nm class logic using multipatterning on immersion duv because it cannot buy euv. cset reported in june 2024 that huawei's ascend 910b ai chip is believed to be made on its n+2 process. but semianalysis judged in april 2025 that most 910b and 910c chips were made at tsmc. it is on the us entity list. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SMIC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-soc\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-soc\" data-alias=\"system on a chip|system-on-chip|system-on-a-chip|SoCs\" data-text=\"soc system on a chip, system-on-chip, system-on-a-chip, socs a system on a chip, or soc, is a single chip that combines processor cores, a graphics processor and other circuit blocks that a device needs. the main processor in a smartphone is one.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SoC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-soitec\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Soitec\" data-text=\"soitec bernin france soi.pa silicon and wafers engineered substrates, soi and poi makes engineered substrates with its smart cut process, which moves a thin crystal layer from one wafer onto another. most are silicon-on-insulator for radio-frequency (rf) and automotive chips, or piezoelectric-on-insulator for radio filters. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Soitec</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-soulbrain\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Soulbrain\" data-alias=\"솔브레인\" data-text=\"soulbrain 솔브레인 seongnam south korea 357780.kq photoresist and materials high-purity etchants and electrolytes supplies high-purity hydrogen fluoride (hf) etchant, cvd precursors and cleaning chemicals to korean memory fabs. it localized hf production after the 2019 japanese export restrictions. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Soulbrain</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-kr\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"KR\" data-alias=\"KR|ROK|Korea|Korean|South Korean\" data-text=\"south korea kr kr rok korea korean south korean country memory, including the high-bandwidth stacks every accelerator needs\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">South Korea</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-specialty-gases\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-specialty-gases\" data-alias=\"specialty gas|electronic specialty gases|bulk gases|bulk gas|electronic gases|process gas|process gases\" data-text=\"specialty gases specialty gas, electronic specialty gases, bulk gases, bulk gas, electronic gases, process gas, process gases specialty gases are the gases a fab uses in small amounts, each for one job. silane, for example, carries silicon into the chamber to build a film, and nitrogen trifluoride cleans the chamber. they arrive in cylinders. bulk gases, such as nitrogen and oxygen, come by pipeline or from plants built at the fab.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">specialty gases</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-sram\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-sram\" data-alias=\"static random-access memory|on-chip memory|on-die SRAM|on-die memory|L2 cache\" data-text=\"sram static random-access memory, cache, on-chip memory, on-die sram, on-die memory, l2 cache sram is the fast memory built from transistors on the logic chip itself, used as a cache that holds the numbers a processor is about to need. it is far faster than the memory stacks beside the chip and holds far less.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SRAM</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-stella-chemifa\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Stella Chemifa\" data-alias=\"ステラケミファ\" data-text=\"stella chemifa ステラケミファ osaka japan 4109.t chemicals and gases ultra-high-purity hydrofluoric acid refines hydrofluoric acid to the purity needed to etch and clean silicon without leaving metal contamination. japan's 2019 decision to require export licenses for high-purity hf sent to korea showed how few qualified sources exist. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Stella Chemifa</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Chemicals and gases</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-subject-to-the-ear\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-subject-to-the-ear\" data-text=\"subject to the ear the test for whether an item falls under us export rules at all. under 15 cfr 734.3 it covers anything in the united states and anything of us origin wherever it is. it also covers foreign-made goods that contain more than a permitted share of controlled us content, and foreign-made goods caught by a foreign direct product rule. the test applies to the item, whatever the seller's nationality.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">subject to the EAR</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-substitutability\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-substitutability\" data-alias=\"substitutability rating\" data-text=\"substitutability substitutability rating a four-band rating of how hard it would be for a well-funded state or firm, starting today, to build an alternative to the leading suppliers at one stage of the supply chain. it is judged against four written tests. easy: a second supplier is qualified, meaning approved by customers, and shipping today at the leading node, the most advanced process. moderate: a second supplier exists but is not yet qualified at the leading node, and closing the gap takes about two to five years. hard: no second supplier exists at the leading node, the path to one is known, and closing the gap takes five to ten years. very hard: no second supplier exists, and the path depends on physics, decades of unwritten know-how or protected intellectual property. no one has yet repeated what the leaders did, and closing the gap takes ten years or more. the years are always counted for that same well-funded state or firm, and the count stops at qualification, which comes well after a prototype.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Substitutability</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-substrate\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-substrate\" data-alias=\"package substrate|IC substrate|build-up substrate|build-up substrates|package substrates|IC substrates|resin substrate\" data-text=\"substrate package substrate, ic substrate, substrates, build-up substrate, build-up substrates, package substrates, ic substrates, resin substrate the small, dense circuit board at the base of a chip package. the chips sit on it, and it spreads their microscopic connections out to the millimeter-scale solder balls a motherboard can accept. it is built up layer by layer from epoxy film, laser-drilled holes and plated copper.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">substrate</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sumco\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SUMCO\" data-alias=\"株式会社SUMCO\" data-text=\"sumco 株式会社sumco tokyo japan 3436.t silicon and wafers 300 mm polished and epitaxial wafers the second-largest silicon wafer maker by capacity and shipments. it makes only wafers, selling polished and epitaxial 300 mm wafers to logic and memory fabs worldwide. it held an estimated 20 percent of global 300 mm wafer capacity at the end of 2024, according to eswin's october 2025 listing prospectus. new capacity takes three to four years to add, and customers contract for it years ahead. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SUMCO</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-sumitomo-chemical\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Sumitomo Chemical\" data-alias=\"Sumitomo|住友化学\" data-text=\"sumitomo chemical 住友化学 tokyo japan 4005.t photoresist and materials photoresist and high-purity aluminum targets makes arf and euv photoresist and high-purity metals and compounds for fabs, though its petrochemical and agrochemical business is much larger. it is one of the four or five firms with euv resist that chipmakers have qualified for production. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Sumitomo Chemical</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-super-micro-computer\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Super Micro Computer\" data-alias=\"Supermicro\" data-text=\"super micro computer san jose united states smci systems and servers ai servers and liquid-cooled racks designs and builds ai servers and complete liquid-cooled racks, with final assembly in california, taiwan and malaysia. it was among the first to ship direct-to-chip liquid cooling at volume. supermicro\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Super Micro Computer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-suss-microtec\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"SUSS MicroTec\" data-text=\"suss microtec garching germany smhn.de advanced packaging and osat coaters, bonders and packaging lithography supplies photoresist coaters, developers, mask aligners and temporary bonding systems used in advanced packaging and mems, including the thick-resist processing that redistribution layers need. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">SUSS MicroTec</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-ch\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"CH\" data-alias=\"CH|Swiss\" data-text=\"switzerland ch ch swiss country \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Switzerland</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-synopsys\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Synopsys\" data-text=\"synopsys sunnyvale united states snps design and eda full-flow eda, silicon ip and simulation makes the synthesis, place-and-route, verification and signoff software that turns the code describing an ai accelerator's logic (its rtl) into a layout a fab can build. it also sells the largest commercial catalog of silicon ip, ready-made circuit blocks that chip designers license. its 2025 acquisition of ansys added multiphysics simulation for thermal and power integrity. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Synopsys</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Design and EDA</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-tw\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"TW\" data-alias=\"TW|Taiwanese\" data-text=\"taiwan tw tw taiwanese country makes nearly every leading-edge chip and packages most of them\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Taiwan</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-tape-out\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-tape-out\" data-alias=\"tape out|taped out|tapes out|tape-outs\" data-text=\"tape-out tape out, taped out, tapes out, tape-outs, tapeout the moment a chip design is declared finished and the pattern files are sent to the factory to be written into masks. the name survives from when the data physically left on a reel of magnetic tape.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">tape-out</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-tc-ncf\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-tc-ncf\" data-alias=\"MR-MUF|Advanced MR-MUF|TC-NCF bonding\" data-text=\"tc-ncf mr-muf, advanced mr-muf, tc-ncf bonding tc-ncf and mr-muf are two ways of joining the thinned memory chips in an hbm stack. in tc-ncf, thermocompression with non-conductive film, each chip is pressed onto the one below under heat, with a thin insulating film between them. samsung uses it for its twelve-high hbm3e. in mr-muf, used by sk hynix, the chips are stacked first, and a liquid protective material is injected between them and hardened.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">TC-NCF</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-technoprobe\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Technoprobe\" data-text=\"technoprobe cernusco lombardone italy tpro.mi test probe cards and probe heads makes probe cards, specializing in vertical mems probe heads used for high pin count logic and hbm test. it is the main european probe card maker and the closest competitor to formfactor. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Technoprobe</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tenstorrent\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Tenstorrent\" data-text=\"tenstorrent toronto canada private ai accelerator vendors risc-v ai processors and licensable ip builds ai accelerators around risc-v cores, with ethernet links that join many chips into one system. it also licenses the designs as ip so customers can build their own chips. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Tenstorrent</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Accelerator vendors</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-teradyne\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Teradyne\" data-text=\"teradyne north reading united states ter test automated test equipment supplies soc, memory and system-level test platforms, and forms the automated test equipment duopoly with advantest. it also sells industrial automation equipment through its robotics arm. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Teradyne</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-thermocompression-bonding\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-thermocompression-bonding\" data-alias=\"thermo-compression bonding|thermocompression bonder|thermocompression bonders|TCB|die bonder|die bonders\" data-text=\"thermocompression bonding thermocompression, thermo-compression bonding, thermocompression bonder, thermocompression bonders, tcb, die bonder, die bonders, bonder, bonders thermocompression bonding presses one die onto another, or onto a substrate, under heat and force until the tiny solder bumps between them melt and join. it is how memory dies are stacked to make high bandwidth memory (hbm) and a growing way to place chiplets on a package.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">thermocompression bonding</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-throughput\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-throughput\" data-alias=\"wafers an hour|wafers per hour|wafers-per-hour\" data-text=\"throughput wafers an hour, wafers per hour, wafers-per-hour throughput is how many wafers a machine can process in an hour. asml's nxe:3800e euv scanner reaches 220.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">throughput</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tokuyama\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Tokuyama\" data-alias=\"株式会社トクヤマ\" data-text=\"tokuyama 株式会社トクヤマ tokyo japan 4043.t silicon and wafers semiconductor-grade polysilicon and ipa japanese chemical maker supplying semiconductor-grade polysilicon from shunan and malaysia, plus high-purity isopropyl alcohol and other fab chemicals. it is one of the five major suppliers of electronic-grade silicon that siltronic names for 2025. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Tokuyama</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tokyo-electron\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Tokyo Electron\" data-alias=\"東京エレクトロン株式会社\" data-text=\"tokyo electron 東京エレクトロン株式会社 tokyo japan 8035.t deposition and etch coater/developer track, etch, deposition and clean makes the coater/developer track, which applies photoresist, develops it after exposure and is physically linked to every scanner in a fab. it also makes etch, deposition, cleaning and wafer bonding systems, and wafer probers for chip testing. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Tokyo Electron</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Deposition and etch</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tokyo-ohka-kogyo\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Tokyo Ohka Kogyo\" data-alias=\"TOK|東京応化工業\" data-text=\"tokyo ohka kogyo 東京応化工業 kawasaki japan 4186.t photoresist and materials photoresist and high-purity process chemicals makes photoresist for krf, arf immersion and euv lithography, plus developers, strippers and thick-film resists used in advanced packaging. it has supplied resist since the industry's early days. tok\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Tokyo Ohka Kogyo</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photoresist</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tokyo-seimitsu-accretech\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Tokyo Seimitsu (Accretech)\" data-alias=\"株式会社東京精密\" data-text=\"tokyo seimitsu (accretech) 株式会社東京精密 hachioji japan 7729.t test wafer probers, dicing machines and grinders makes probers, the machines that move each wafer under the probe card and hold it at a set temperature during wafer test, plus dicing machines and grinders. it sells as accretech and says it has the top global share in probers. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Tokyo Seimitsu (Accretech)</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Test</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tongfu-microelectronics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Tongfu Microelectronics\" data-alias=\"通富微电\" data-text=\"tongfu microelectronics 通富微电 nantong china 002156.sz advanced packaging and osat osat assembly and test, amd partner a chinese osat that packages a large share of amd's cpus and gpus through joint venture plants acquired from amd in 2016. it is developing 2.5d chiplet packaging. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Tongfu Microelectronics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-toppan-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Toppan Holdings\" data-alias=\"Toppan|TOPPANホールディングス\" data-text=\"toppan holdings toppanホールディングス tokyo japan 7911.t photomasks advanced photomasks and fc-bga substrates makes advanced photomasks through its photomask arm and is building flip-chip bga substrate capacity for ai packages. its photomask business became a separate company, tekscend photomask, which is listed in tokyo. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Toppan Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Photomasks</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tower-semiconductor\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Tower Semiconductor\" data-alias=\"Tower\" data-text=\"tower semiconductor migdal haemek israel tsem foundry specialty analog and silicon photonics foundry a specialty foundry for analog, rf, power and silicon photonics, including the photonic integrated circuits used in optical transceivers and co-packaged optics. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Tower Semiconductor</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-tpp\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-tpp\" data-alias=\"total processing performance\" data-text=\"tpp total processing performance total processing performance, the measure us export rules use for a chip's computing power. it starts from the number of multiply-accumulate operations, a multiply followed by an add, that the chip does each second. that number is doubled, multiplied by the number of bits in each operation, and added up across every processing unit on the chip. the definition is in eccn 3a090, in supplement no. 1 to 15 cfr part 774.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">TPP</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-tpu\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-tpu\" data-alias=\"Tensor Processing Unit|TPUs\" data-text=\"tpu tensor processing unit, tpus google's own ai chip, designed in-house for its data centers and cloud service. its eighth generation, announced in april 2026, is split into two chips, the tpu 8t for training and the tpu 8i for inference.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">TPU</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-transistor\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-transistor\" data-text=\"transistor transistors the switch every chip is built from. current runs through a channel between two terminals. a voltage on a third terminal, the gate, opens or closes that path, much as a tap opens or closes a pipe. one nvidia blackwell part contains 208 billion of them.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">transistor</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-transistor-density\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-transistor-density\" data-alias=\"logic density|chip density|transistors per square millimeter|density gain\" data-text=\"transistor density logic density, chip density, transistors per square millimeter, density gain transistor density is how many transistors fit in a square millimeter of chip. semianalysis measured smic's n+3 at 113.4 million, against 107.7 million for tsmc's n6. tsmc says n2p gives 1.2 times the logic density and 1.15 times the chip density of n3e. a16, which adds backside power, gives up to 1.10 times the chip density of n2p. tsmc says a14, planned for 2028, will give more than 20 percent more logic density than n2.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">transistor density</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-trumpf\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Trumpf\" data-text=\"trumpf ditzingen germany private equipment subsystems and components co2 drive lasers for euv sources builds the multi-kilowatt co2 laser amplifier chain that vaporizes tin droplets to create euv light. trumpf describes the laser system as internationally unique. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Trumpf</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-tsmc\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"TSMC\" data-alias=\"台灣積體電路製造\" data-text=\"tsmc 台灣積體電路製造 hsinchu taiwan 2330.tw foundry leading-edge logic foundry and advanced packaging manufactures almost every leading-edge ai accelerator, including those of nvidia, amd and broadcom and the custom chips of large cloud companies, on its n4, n3 and n2 processes. it also owns cowos and soic advanced packaging, and its packaging capacity is a tighter constraint than its wafer capacity. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">TSMC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-tsv\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-tsv\" data-alias=\"through-silicon via|TSVs|through-silicon vias|through silicon via|through silicon vias\" data-text=\"tsv through-silicon via, tsvs, through-silicon vias, through silicon via, through silicon vias a copper column that runs all the way through a chip so that power and signals can pass from its top face to its bottom face. it makes stacking chips vertically possible, in the way an elevator shaft makes a tall building usable.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">TSV</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ttm-technologies\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"TTM Technologies\" data-alias=\"TTM\" data-text=\"ttm technologies santa ana united states ttmi substrates and pcbs pcbs and rf components makes printed circuit boards for data center, aerospace and defense customers, including high-layer-count boards for ai and networking systems. by its own description it is one of the largest technology manufacturers in north america. it also offers ic substrates and is building an ultra-high-density circuit board plant in syracuse, new york, with volume production expected in the second half of 2026. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">TTM Technologies</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-twh\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-twh\" data-alias=\"terawatt-hour|terawatt-hours|terawatt hours\" data-text=\"twh terawatt-hour, terawatt-hours, terawatt hours a terawatt-hour is a billion kilowatt-hours, the unit national electricity use is counted in. us data centers used 192 twh in 2024, 4.7 percent of the country's electricity.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">TWh</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-ucie\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-ucie\" data-alias=\"Universal Chiplet Interconnect Express|UCIe 3.0\" data-text=\"ucie universal chiplet interconnect express, ucie 3.0 ucie is an open standard for the short, very fast link between two chiplets sitting side by side in one package. it lets chiplets from different vendors be wired together, the way pcie lets cards from different vendors share a computer.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">UCIe</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ultra-clean-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Ultra Clean Holdings\" data-alias=\"Ultra Clean\" data-text=\"ultra clean holdings hayward united states uctt equipment subsystems and components subsystem assembly and parts cleaning builds gas delivery systems, chemical modules and frame assemblies for process tools, and runs a large business cleaning and coating chamber parts between uses. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Ultra Clean Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-umc\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"UMC\" data-alias=\"聯華電子\" data-text=\"umc 聯華電子 hsinchu taiwan 2303.tw foundry mature-node foundry taiwan's second largest foundry, running processes of 28 nm and above for display drivers, power management, connectivity and automotive parts. it is expanding 12 nm capacity in partnership with intel. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">UMC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Foundry</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-unimicron\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Unimicron\" data-alias=\"欣興電子\" data-text=\"unimicron 欣興電子 taoyuan taiwan 3037.tw substrates and pcbs ic substrates and hdi boards one of the largest ic substrate makers, producing abf and bt substrates plus high density interconnect boards. it is adding abf capacity in taiwan and shenzhen for ai demand. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Unimicron</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-gb\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"GB\" data-alias=\"GB|UK|Britain|British\" data-text=\"united kingdom gb gb uk britain british country arm and the other processor designs that most chips license\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">United Kingdom</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-country-us\" data-kind=\"country\" data-key=\"US\" data-alias=\"US|USA|American\" data-text=\"united states us us usa american country designs the chips, makes most of the tools and is the biggest buyer\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">United States</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Country</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-us-person\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-us-person\" data-alias=\"US persons|U.S. person|U.S. persons\" data-text=\"us person us persons, u.s. person, u.s. persons in export law a us person is any american citizen, permanent resident or company, wherever in the world they are, and anyone in the united states. since october 2022 a us person may not service or support an advanced chip fab in china without a license.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">US person</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-utac-holdings\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"UTAC Holdings\" data-alias=\"UTAC\" data-text=\"utac holdings singapore singapore private advanced packaging and osat osat assembly and test a singapore-based osat providing assembly and test for analog, mixed-signal, automotive and memory devices from plants across southeast asia and china. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">UTAC Holdings</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Advanced packaging</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-utilization\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-utilization\" data-alias=\"utilization rate|fab utilization\" data-text=\"utilization utilization rate, fab utilization utilization is how full a fab's lines are running, as a share of what they could run. most of a fab's costs, such as paying off its tools, stay the same whether it runs full or half empty, so utilization largely decides whether it makes money.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">utilization</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-vat-group\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"VAT Group\" data-alias=\"VAT\" data-text=\"vat group haag switzerland vacn.sw equipment subsystems and components high-vacuum valves makes the high-vacuum isolation and control valves that seal and gate every process chamber. how many particles a valve sheds and how many cycles it lasts directly affect tool uptime and wafer defect counts. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">VAT Group</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-vdl-groep\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"VDL Groep\" data-text=\"vdl groep eindhoven netherlands private equipment subsystems and components precision mechanical modules and frames a dutch precision manufacturing group that builds large mechanical modules, frames and vacuum assemblies for asml scanners. it is one of the main suppliers in the brainport cluster around asml's base in veldhoven. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">VDL Groep</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Equipment subsystems</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-vertiv\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Vertiv\" data-text=\"vertiv westerville united states vrt power and cooling data center power and thermal management makes uninterruptible power supplies, busway power distribution, coolant distribution units and liquid cooling systems for data centers. it co-develops reference power and cooling designs with nvidia. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Vertiv</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Power and cooling</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-veu\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-veu\" data-alias=\"Validated End-User|Validated End User|Validated End-User status|VEU status|VEU cover|validated end users\" data-text=\"veu validated end-user, validated end user, validated end-user status, veu status, veu cover, validated end users an authorization that bis, the us commerce department office that licenses exports, grants to a named foreign facility, so approved items can ship to it without an individual license each time. the approved facilities are listed in supplement no. 7 to 15 cfr part 748, and the procedure is set out in 15 cfr 748.15.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">VEU</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Export control</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-vias\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-vias\" data-alias=\"copper vias|vertical vias|vertical copper vias\" data-text=\"vias copper vias, vertical vias, vertical copper vias vias are the small vertical holes, filled with metal, that connect one layer of wiring to the layer above or below it. a chip's wiring is full of them. an interposer has them through its whole thickness, and a package substrate has them drilled by laser through each sheet of film.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">vias</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-victory-giant-technology\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Victory Giant Technology\" data-alias=\"Victory Giant|胜宏科技\" data-text=\"victory giant technology 胜宏科技 huizhou china 300476.sz substrates and pcbs high-multilayer pcbs for ai servers makes high-layer-count printed circuit boards and supplies ai accelerator baseboards and switch boards to the server odms. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Victory Giant Technology</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-wacker-chemie\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Wacker Chemie\" data-text=\"wacker chemie munich germany wch.de silicon and wafers semiconductor-grade polysilicon one of the few producers of semiconductor-grade polysilicon, which it makes at burghausen in germany and in tennessee. its silicone and chemicals businesses bring in much more revenue than its electronic-grade polysilicon. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Wacker Chemie</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Silicon wafers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-wafer\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-wafer\" data-alias=\"silicon wafer|300 mm wafer|silicon wafers|300 mm wafers\" data-text=\"wafer silicon wafer, 300 mm wafer, wafers, silicon wafers, 300 mm wafers the polished disc of ultrapure silicon that chips are built on, 300 millimeters across for advanced chips. hundreds of chips are printed on one wafer and cut apart at the end.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">wafer</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-wafer-fab-equipment\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-wafer-fab-equipment\" data-alias=\"WFE|front-end equipment|equipment billings|wafer processing equipment|semiconductor equipment|chipmaking tools|chipmaking equipment\" data-text=\"wafer fab equipment wfe, front-end equipment, equipment billings, wafer processing equipment, semiconductor equipment, chipmaking tools, chipmaking equipment the collective name for the machines that process wafers inside a fab: printing systems, deposition and etch chambers, cleaning tools and measurement systems. it excludes the packaging and test machines used afterward.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">wafer fab equipment</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-wafer-sort\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-wafer-sort\" data-alias=\"wafer test|probe test|wafer probe\" data-text=\"wafer sort wafer test, probe test, wafer probe wafer sort is the first test a chip gets, while it is still on the wafer. thousands of needles on a probe card press onto the pads of one die, or of several dies at once, and a tester drives signals in and reads the answers. any die that answers wrong is marked and never packaged.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">wafer sort</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-wafers-per-month\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-wafers-per-month\" data-alias=\"wafers a month|wafer starts|wafer starts per month|WSPM|wafer starts a month|million wafers per month\" data-text=\"wafers per month wafers a month, wafer starts, wafer starts per month, wspm, wafer starts a month, million wafers per month wafers per month is how fab capacity is counted: the number of wafers a plant can start through its line each month. a tsmc gigafab runs more than 100,000. in september 2025 semianalysis conservatively put smic's capacity at 7 nm and below at 45,000 a month by the end of 2025. figures are often converted to 8-inch or 12-inch equivalents so plants with different wafer sizes can be compared.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">wafers per month</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-wet-chemicals\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-wet-chemicals\" data-alias=\"wet chemical|wet processing|wet clean|cleaning chemicals|process chemicals\" data-text=\"wet chemicals wet chemical, wet processing, wet clean, cleaning chemicals, process chemicals wet chemicals are the liquids a wafer is dipped in or sprayed with between steps: acids that strip a layer, solvents that remove resist, and ultrapure water rinses. wet processing is any step done in liquid.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">wet chemicals</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-winbond-electronics\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Winbond Electronics\" data-alias=\"Winbond|華邦電子\" data-text=\"winbond electronics 華邦電子 taichung taiwan 2344.tw memory specialty dram, nor flash and cube memory makes nor flash, specialty low-power dram and a customized ultra-bandwidth memory called cube aimed at edge ai devices that cannot afford hbm. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Winbond Electronics</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-wistron\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Wistron\" data-alias=\"緯創資通\" data-text=\"wistron 緯創資通 new taipei taiwan 3231.tw systems and servers ai server and gpu baseboard manufacturing builds gpu baseboards and ai servers, and grew quickly during the 2025 ai build-out. it also supplies liquid cooling loops and rack integration. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Wistron</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-wiwynn\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Wiwynn\" data-alias=\"緯穎科技\" data-text=\"wiwynn 緯穎科技 new taipei taiwan 6669.tw systems and servers hyperscale server and rack odm designs and builds hyperscale servers, storage and rack systems to open compute designs for cloud operators, including liquid-cooled ai racks. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Wiwynn</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-wuhan-jingce-electronic\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"Wuhan Jingce Electronic\" data-alias=\"武汉精测电子\" data-text=\"wuhan jingce electronic 武汉精测电子 wuhan china 300567.sz metrology and inspection domestic chinese metrology and display test makes semiconductor film metrology, electrical test and defect inspection tools for chinese fabs through its wuhan jingce semiconductor arm. it started in flat panel display test. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">Wuhan Jingce Electronic</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Metrology</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-wus-printed-circuit\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"WUS Printed Circuit\" data-alias=\"沪电股份\" data-text=\"wus printed circuit 沪电股份 kunshan china 002463.sz substrates and pcbs high-speed pcbs for servers and networking makes high-speed multilayer printed circuit boards for servers, switches and ai accelerators, and is a main supplier to networking equipment makers. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">WUS Printed Circuit</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Substrates and PCBs</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-term-yield\" data-kind=\"term\" data-key=\"gl-yield\" data-alias=\"die yield|packaging yield|package yield|stack yield\" data-text=\"yield die yield, yields, packaging yield, package yield, stack yield the percentage of chips on a wafer that work. flaws land at random, so the larger the chip the more likely it is to catch one, and yield falls steeply as chips get bigger.\"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">yield</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Term</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-ymtc\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"YMTC\" data-alias=\"长江存储\" data-text=\"ymtc 长江存储 wuhan china private memory chinese 3d nand china's 3d nand maker, using its xtacking architecture that bonds a separately made logic wafer onto the memory array. it has been on the us entity list since 2022. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">YMTC</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Memory</span></button></li><li id=\"lk-firm-zt-systems\" data-kind=\"firm\" data-key=\"ZT Systems\" data-text=\"zt systems secaucus united states private systems and servers rack-scale ai system design designs and validates rack-scale ai systems for hyperscalers. amd bought it for its systems engineering team, so that amd could ship complete racks. \"><button type=\"button\"><span class=\"lk-name\">ZT Systems</span><span class=\"lk-lab\">Systems and servers</span></button></li>","terms":"<div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-15-cfr\" data-term=\"15 cfr\" data-text=\"15 cfr cfr, code of federal regulations, 15 cfr 742.6, part 742, part 740, part 734, supplement no. 5 to part 740, supplement no. 5 the code of federal regulations is the standing text of us rules, sorted into titles and parts. title 15 holds the export administration regulations. part 734 says what is subject to them. part 740 lists the license exceptions, and its supplement no. 5 lists the nineteen destinations eligible for license exception aia. part 742 sets the licensing policy for each control. a rule announced in the federal register stays in the cfr until it is removed, so the unenforced ai diffusion rule still stands in the regulations.\">\n<dt>15 CFR<span class=\"aka\">CFR, Code of Federal Regulations, 15 CFR 742.6, part 742, part 740, part 734, supplement no. 5 to part 740, supplement no. 5</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The Code of Federal Regulations is the standing text of US rules, sorted into titles and parts. Title 15 holds the Export Administration Regulations. Part 734 says what is subject to them. Part 740 lists the license exceptions, and its supplement no. 5 lists the nineteen destinations eligible for License Exception AIA. Part 742 sets the licensing policy for each control.</p><p class=\"why\">A rule announced in the Federal Register stays in the CFR until it is removed, so the unenforced AI Diffusion rule still stands in the regulations.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-300-mm\" data-term=\"300 mm\" data-text=\"300 mm 300-millimeter, 12-inch wafer, 12-inch wafers, 12-inch equivalent, 200 mm, 8-inch, 8-inch-equivalent, 450 mm, 150 mm 300 mm is the diameter of the standard wafer, about twelve inches. older fabs run 200 mm, or 8-inch, wafers. the last increase in wafer size, to 300 mm, came in 2002. advanced chips start on 300 mm wafers. in semi's november 2020 world fab forecast, which cset cited in january 2021, they carried 99.7 percent of world fab capacity at 45 nm and below.\">\n<dt>300 mm<span class=\"aka\">300-millimeter, 12-inch wafer, 12-inch wafers, 12-inch equivalent, 200 mm, 8-inch, 8-inch-equivalent, 450 mm, 150 mm</span></dt>\n<dd><p>300 mm is the diameter of the standard wafer, about twelve inches. Older fabs run 200 mm, or 8-inch, wafers. The last increase in wafer size, to 300 mm, came in 2002.</p><p class=\"why\">Advanced chips start on 300 mm wafers. In SEMI's November 2020 World Fab Forecast, which CSET cited in January 2021, they carried 99.7 percent of world fab capacity at 45 nm and below.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"silicon-and-wafers/\">Read it in Silicon and Wafers →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-3a090\" data-term=\"3a090\" data-text=\"3a090 3a090.a, 3a090.b, 3a090.c, 4a090, 4a090.a, eccn 3a090, eccn 4a090 3a090 is the entry in the us export control list that covers advanced ai chips, defined by their total processing performance and performance density. its part c, added in december 2024, covers high bandwidth memory. 4a090 covers the computers built from the chips. a chip that falls under 3a090.a needs a license for china. the ai diffusion rule of january 2025 extended that requirement to every destination. but bis says it enforces the requirement only for country groups d:1, d:4 and d:5 and for firms headquartered in d:5 or macau. it decides which ai chips need a license for china, so designers now build chips around its thresholds.\">\n<dt>3A090<span class=\"aka\">3A090.a, 3A090.b, 3A090.c, 4A090, 4A090.a, ECCN 3A090, ECCN 4A090</span></dt>\n<dd><p>3A090 is the entry in the US export control list that covers advanced AI chips, defined by their total processing performance and performance density. Its part c, added in December 2024, covers high bandwidth memory. 4A090 covers the computers built from the chips. A chip that falls under 3A090.a needs a license for China. The AI Diffusion rule of January 2025 extended that requirement to every destination. But BIS says it enforces the requirement only for Country Groups D:1, D:4 and D:5 and for firms headquartered in D:5 or Macau.</p><p class=\"why\">It decides which AI chips need a license for China, so designers now build chips around its thresholds.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-3b001\" data-term=\"3b001\" data-text=\"3b001 3b090, 3b001.c.1, 3b001.d.9, 3b001.d.10, 3b001.d.5 3b001 is the main entry in the us export control list for chipmaking equipment. it is written as process specifications, such as an etch tool that cuts sideways or a deposition tool that coats holes more than 200 times deeper than they are wide. bis created 3b090 in october 2022 and folded it into 3b001 and 3b002 in october 2023 (88 fr 73424). the related 3d and 3e entries cover the software and know-how that go with the tools. it decides which chipmaking tools need an export license. it defines a tool by the process it can run, because the same chamber can add or remove material depending on its recipe.\">\n<dt>3B001<span class=\"aka\">3B090, 3B001.c.1, 3B001.d.9, 3B001.d.10, 3B001.d.5</span></dt>\n<dd><p>3B001 is the main entry in the US export control list for chipmaking equipment. It is written as process specifications, such as an etch tool that cuts sideways or a deposition tool that coats holes more than 200 times deeper than they are wide. BIS created 3B090 in October 2022 and folded it into 3B001 and 3B002 in October 2023 (88 FR 73424). The related 3D and 3E entries cover the software and know-how that go with the tools.</p><p class=\"why\">It decides which chipmaking tools need an export license. It defines a tool by the process it can run, because the same chamber can add or remove material depending on its recipe.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-abf\" data-term=\"abf\" data-text=\"abf ajinomoto build-up film, build-up film, abf build-up film, abf substrate, abf substrates the insulating film inside the substrate, the small layered board that the chips in a high-end package sit on. the board is built up in layers, and a sheet of this epoxy film, about 10 micrometers thick, separates each layer of copper wiring from the next. the japanese food company ajinomoto first developed it in 1999. ajinomoto told investors in june 2026 that its build-up film has held over 95 percent of its market since its launch. the company says practically all high-performance computers and servers rely on it.\">\n<dt>ABF<span class=\"aka\">Ajinomoto Build-up Film, build-up film, ABF build-up film, ABF substrate, ABF substrates</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The insulating film inside the substrate, the small layered board that the chips in a high-end package sit on. The board is built up in layers, and a sheet of this epoxy film, about 10 micrometers thick, separates each layer of copper wiring from the next. The Japanese food company Ajinomoto first developed it in 1999.</p><p class=\"why\">Ajinomoto told investors in June 2026 that its build-up film has held over 95 percent of its market since its launch. The company says practically all high-performance computers and servers rely on it.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"substrates-and-pcbs/\">Read it in Substrates and PCBs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-accelerator\" data-term=\"accelerator\" data-text=\"accelerator ai accelerator, xpu, accelerators a chip built to do the one kind of arithmetic machine learning needs, multiplying large grids of numbers, far faster than a general-purpose processor can. nvidia's graphics processors, google's tensor processing units and amazon's trainium are all accelerators. the whole supply chain exists to make accelerators, and export licenses are granted or refused for them.\">\n<dt>accelerator<span class=\"aka\">AI accelerator, XPU, accelerators</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A chip built to do the one kind of arithmetic machine learning needs, multiplying large grids of numbers, far faster than a general-purpose processor can. Nvidia's graphics processors, Google's Tensor Processing Units and Amazon's Trainium are all accelerators.</p><p class=\"why\">The whole supply chain exists to make accelerators, and export licenses are granted or refused for them.</p></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-advanced-packaging\" data-term=\"advanced packaging\" data-text=\"advanced packaging 2.5d packaging, 3d packaging, 2.5d, 2.5d work, advanced packaging plants the steps that assemble several finished chips into one component, sitting side by side or stacked, wired together closely enough to behave like a single larger chip. ordinary packaging only puts one chip into a protective case with contacts on the bottom. a modern ai accelerator needs more circuitry than a lithography machine can print in one exposure, and its memory must sit beside the logic, so it is assembled this way. epoch ai found that tsmc's cowos packaging and the memory itself were the main limits on ai chip production in 2025.\">\n<dt>advanced packaging<span class=\"aka\">2.5D packaging, 3D packaging, 2.5D, 2.5D work, advanced packaging plants</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The steps that assemble several finished chips into one component, sitting side by side or stacked, wired together closely enough to behave like a single larger chip. Ordinary packaging only puts one chip into a protective case with contacts on the bottom.</p><p class=\"why\">A modern AI accelerator needs more circuitry than a lithography machine can print in one exposure, and its memory must sit beside the logic, so it is assembled this way. Epoch AI found that TSMC's CoWoS packaging and the memory itself were the main limits on AI chip production in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-affiliates-rule\" data-term=\"affiliates rule\" data-text=\"affiliates rule affiliates rule, 50 percent rule, affiliates of listed entities the affiliates rule extended the entity list to any company anywhere in the world that is at least half owned by a listed firm. the aim was to stop a listed company from buying through a subsidiary. it took effect on 29 september 2025 and was suspended for a year six weeks later. it is suspended until 9 november 2026. if it returns, subsidiaries at least half owned by listed firms will again need licenses.\">\n<dt>Affiliates Rule<span class=\"aka\">affiliates rule, 50 percent rule, affiliates of listed entities</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The Affiliates Rule extended the Entity List to any company anywhere in the world that is at least half owned by a listed firm. The aim was to stop a listed company from buying through a subsidiary. It took effect on 29 September 2025 and was suspended for a year six weeks later.</p><p class=\"why\">It is suspended until 9 November 2026. If it returns, subsidiaries at least half owned by listed firms will again need licenses.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ai-diffusion-rule\" data-term=\"ai diffusion rule\" data-text=\"ai diffusion rule ai diffusion, diffusion rule, framework for artificial intelligence diffusion, ai diffusion framework the ai diffusion rule, published on 15 january 2025, required a license to ship the most capable ai chips anywhere in the world. its exceptions allowed unlimited shipments to nineteen destinations, capped volumes elsewhere and none to china. it also controlled the weights of frontier ai models. four months later bis said it would not enforce the rule. but it withdrew none of the text, so the license requirement and exceptions still stand in the regulations. bis says it enforces the requirement only for country groups d:1, d:4 and d:5 and for firms headquartered in d:5 or macau.\">\n<dt>AI Diffusion rule<span class=\"aka\">AI Diffusion, diffusion rule, Framework for Artificial Intelligence Diffusion, AI Diffusion framework</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The AI Diffusion rule, published on 15 January 2025, required a license to ship the most capable AI chips anywhere in the world. Its exceptions allowed unlimited shipments to nineteen destinations, capped volumes elsewhere and none to China. It also controlled the weights of frontier AI models.</p><p class=\"why\">Four months later BIS said it would not enforce the rule. But it withdrew none of the text, so the license requirement and exceptions still stand in the regulations. BIS says it enforces the requirement only for Country Groups D:1, D:4 and D:5 and for firms headquartered in D:5 or Macau.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ald\" data-term=\"ald\" data-text=\"ald atomic layer deposition a way of coating a chip a fraction of an atomic layer at a time. each pulse of gas sticks to the surface and stops once the surface is covered. so the film comes out the same thickness on the floor and on the walls of a hole more than 50 times deeper than it is wide. us regulators call atomic layer deposition an enabler of stacked memory and of finfet and gate-all-around logic, and export rules name some of its tools directly. chinese toolmakers held 2.6 percent of the market in 2025 on cset's count, most of it from piotech.\">\n<dt>ALD<span class=\"aka\">atomic layer deposition</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A way of coating a chip a fraction of an atomic layer at a time. Each pulse of gas sticks to the surface and stops once the surface is covered. So the film comes out the same thickness on the floor and on the walls of a hole more than 50 times deeper than it is wide.</p><p class=\"why\">US regulators call atomic layer deposition an enabler of stacked memory and of FinFET and gate-all-around logic, and export rules name some of its tools directly. Chinese toolmakers held 2.6 percent of the market in 2025 on CSET's count, most of it from Piotech.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-arf\" data-term=\"arf\" data-text=\"arf argon fluoride, argon fluoride laser, 193 nm, 193-nanometer arf stands for argon fluoride, the gas mixture inside the laser that gives deep ultraviolet lithography its 193-nanometer light. scanners, the machines that print each layer, use this light in two ways. a dry scanner shines it through air, and an immersion scanner through a thin film of water between lens and wafer, which prints finer lines. arf scanners print most of the fine layers on any chip made without extreme ultraviolet. arf immersion scanners made up 42 percent of asml's system sales in 2025. they are also the kind that a chinese state-owned firm was reported in july 2026 to be producing at home.\">\n<dt>ArF<span class=\"aka\">argon fluoride, argon fluoride laser, 193 nm, 193-nanometer</span></dt>\n<dd><p>ArF stands for argon fluoride, the gas mixture inside the laser that gives deep ultraviolet lithography its 193-nanometer light. Scanners, the machines that print each layer, use this light in two ways. A dry scanner shines it through air, and an immersion scanner through a thin film of water between lens and wafer, which prints finer lines. ArF scanners print most of the fine layers on any chip made without extreme ultraviolet.</p><p class=\"why\">ArF immersion scanners made up 42 percent of ASML's system sales in 2025. They are also the kind that a Chinese state-owned firm was reported in July 2026 to be producing at home.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-asic\" data-term=\"asic\" data-text=\"asic application-specific integrated circuit, custom silicon, asics, custom accelerator, custom accelerators, custom chip, custom ai silicon, custom ai asics a chip designed for one company's own workload and not sold on the open market. google's tensor processing unit and amazon's trainium are chips of this kind. an nvidia part sold to any customer is not. a custom chip is tuned to one company's workload, but a chip sold to everyone comes with mature software and a resale market. design houses such as broadcom and marvell turn the buyer's design into silicon and sell the finished chips to the buyer.\">\n<dt>ASIC<span class=\"aka\">application-specific integrated circuit, custom silicon, ASICs, custom accelerator, custom accelerators, custom chip, custom AI silicon, custom AI ASICs</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A chip designed for one company's own workload and not sold on the open market. Google's Tensor Processing Unit and Amazon's Trainium are chips of this kind. An Nvidia part sold to any customer is not.</p><p class=\"why\">A custom chip is tuned to one company's workload, but a chip sold to everyone comes with mature software and a resale market. Design houses such as Broadcom and Marvell turn the buyer's design into silicon and sell the finished chips to the buyer.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ate\" data-term=\"ate\" data-text=\"ate automated test equipment, automatic test equipment, tester automated test equipment, or ate, is the machine that connects to a chip, on the wafer or in its package, feeds it test patterns and checks whether the answers coming back are right. advantest's july 2026 investor guide counts test as the only manufacturing step that puts electrical signals through the chip. an ai accelerator joins a dozen expensive pieces, and one bad piece scraps them all. so each die is tested before assembly. advantest's april 2025 investor guide put advantest and teradyne at about 80 percent of the tester market.\">\n<dt>ATE<span class=\"aka\">automated test equipment, automatic test equipment, tester</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Automated test equipment, or ATE, is the machine that connects to a chip, on the wafer or in its package, feeds it test patterns and checks whether the answers coming back are right. Advantest's July 2026 investor guide counts test as the only manufacturing step that puts electrical signals through the chip.</p><p class=\"why\">An AI accelerator joins a dozen expensive pieces, and one bad piece scraps them all. So each die is tested before assembly. Advantest's April 2025 investor guide put Advantest and Teradyne at about 80 percent of the tester market.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-back-end\" data-term=\"back end\" data-text=\"back end back end of line, beol, back-end, back-end fabs, back-end tools inside a fab, the back end of line is the second half of making a chip, the dozen or more layers of copper wiring stacked above the transistors. in the industry at large, the back end means everything after the wafer leaves the fab: grinding, dicing, packaging and test. wiring is now as hard to make as the transistor. among the firms that package and test chips after they leave the fab, four of the ten largest by 2024 revenue are headquartered in china, in a trendforce ranking cited by cset.\">\n<dt>back end<span class=\"aka\">back end of line, BEOL, back-end, back-end fabs, back-end tools</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Inside a fab, the back end of line is the second half of making a chip, the dozen or more layers of copper wiring stacked above the transistors. In the industry at large, the back end means everything after the wafer leaves the fab: grinding, dicing, packaging and test.</p><p class=\"why\">Wiring is now as hard to make as the transistor. Among the firms that package and test chips after they leave the fab, four of the ten largest by 2024 revenue are headquartered in China, in a TrendForce ranking cited by CSET.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-backside-power-delivery\" data-term=\"backside power delivery\" data-text=\"backside power delivery backside power, backside vias, powervia, super power rail, backside power network backside power delivery moves a chip's power wiring to the underside of the wafer, so the wiring above the transistors carries only signals. after the transistors and signal wiring are built, the wafer is bonded face down to a second wafer and ground thin, and the power wires are built on its back. power arrives through tiny holes etched up from below, clear of the crowded top. it is one of the few remaining ways to make a chip faster without shrinking the transistor. intel ships it on its 18a process. tsmc says a16, its first process with it, will be production-ready in the second half of 2026.\">\n<dt>backside power delivery<span class=\"aka\">backside power, backside vias, PowerVia, Super Power Rail, backside power network</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Backside power delivery moves a chip's power wiring to the underside of the wafer, so the wiring above the transistors carries only signals. After the transistors and signal wiring are built, the wafer is bonded face down to a second wafer and ground thin, and the power wires are built on its back. Power arrives through tiny holes etched up from below, clear of the crowded top.</p><p class=\"why\">It is one of the few remaining ways to make a chip faster without shrinking the transistor. Intel ships it on its 18A process. TSMC says A16, its first process with it, will be production-ready in the second half of 2026.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-base-die\" data-term=\"base die\" data-text=\"base die base chip, base logic die, logic base die, hbm base die the base die is the bottom chip of an hbm stack, the one that manages the memory dies above it and talks to the processor on their behalf. for hbm4, sk hynix moved it to tsmc's advanced logic process so it can hold more functions. samsung's hbm4, shipped from february 2026, uses a 4 nm logic base die. sk hynix made its own base dies up to hbm3e, so the move gives tsmc a role inside a product it does not make.\">\n<dt>base die<span class=\"aka\">base chip, base logic die, logic base die, HBM base die</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The base die is the bottom chip of an HBM stack, the one that manages the memory dies above it and talks to the processor on their behalf. For HBM4, SK hynix moved it to TSMC's advanced logic process so it can hold more functions. Samsung's HBM4, shipped from February 2026, uses a 4 nm logic base die.</p><p class=\"why\">SK hynix made its own base dies up to HBM3E, so the move gives TSMC a role inside a product it does not make.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-baseboard\" data-term=\"baseboard\" data-text=\"baseboard baseboards, sxm, oam, hgx, hgx baseboard a baseboard is the large circuit board that eight accelerator modules bolt onto inside a server. it carries their power and the links between them. on nvidia's baseboard, switch chips let any two modules reach each other at full speed. nvidia's module is called sxm and its baseboard hgx. the open-standard equivalents are oam and ubb. with an eight-module baseboard, the eight accelerators in one server work as one unit. rack-scale systems such as the nvl72 drop the baseboard and join 72 gpus through switch trays in the rack.\">\n<dt>baseboard<span class=\"aka\">baseboards, SXM, OAM, HGX, HGX baseboard</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A baseboard is the large circuit board that eight accelerator modules bolt onto inside a server. It carries their power and the links between them. On Nvidia's baseboard, switch chips let any two modules reach each other at full speed. Nvidia's module is called SXM and its baseboard HGX. The open-standard equivalents are OAM and UBB.</p><p class=\"why\">With an eight-module baseboard, the eight accelerators in one server work as one unit. Rack-scale systems such as the NVL72 drop the baseboard and join 72 GPUs through switch trays in the rack.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-bga\" data-term=\"bga\" data-text=\"bga ball grid array, fc-bga, flip-chip bga a way of joining a packaged chip to a circuit board using a grid of small solder balls across the underside in place of a row of pins around the edge. heating the assembly melts every ball at once into a permanent joint. the number and spacing of those balls limit how much current and how many signals can reach a package.\">\n<dt>BGA<span class=\"aka\">ball grid array, FC-BGA, flip-chip BGA</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A way of joining a packaged chip to a circuit board using a grid of small solder balls across the underside in place of a row of pins around the edge. Heating the assembly melts every ball at once into a permanent joint.</p><p class=\"why\">The number and spacing of those balls limit how much current and how many signals can reach a package.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"substrates-and-pcbs/\">Read it in Substrates and PCBs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-big-fund\" data-term=\"big fund\" data-text=\"big fund national integrated circuit industry investment fund, national integrated circuit fund, third chip fund, china's third chip fund the big fund is the nickname for china's national integrated circuit industry investment fund, the state vehicle that puts government money into chinese chip firms. its third round, raised in may 2024, came to 344 billion yuan, about $47 billion. csis puts china's cumulative state funding for chips since 2014 at an estimated $150 billion. the money has built a domestic tool industry but no leading-edge node.\">\n<dt>Big Fund<span class=\"aka\">National Integrated Circuit Industry Investment Fund, National Integrated Circuit Fund, third chip fund, China's third chip fund</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The Big Fund is the nickname for China's National Integrated Circuit Industry Investment Fund, the state vehicle that puts government money into Chinese chip firms. Its third round, raised in May 2024, came to 344 billion yuan, about $47 billion.</p><p class=\"why\">CSIS puts China's cumulative state funding for chips since 2014 at an estimated $150 billion. The money has built a domestic tool industry but no leading-edge node.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-bill-of-materials\" data-term=\"bill of materials\" data-text=\"bill of materials bom the itemized list of every purchased part in a finished product and what each part cost, the way a builder's invoice prices lumber, wiring and fixtures separately. a bill of materials shows which suppliers get the money a buyer spends. epoch ai estimated in december 2025 that memory made up about half of the roughly $6,400 manufacturing cost of an nvidia b200.\">\n<dt>bill of materials<span class=\"aka\">BOM</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The itemized list of every purchased part in a finished product and what each part cost, the way a builder's invoice prices lumber, wiring and fixtures separately.</p><p class=\"why\">A bill of materials shows which suppliers get the money a buyer spends. Epoch AI estimated in December 2025 that memory made up about half of the roughly $6,400 manufacturing cost of an Nvidia B200.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"component-costs/\">Read it in The Economics of AI Chips →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-bis\" data-term=\"bis\" data-text=\"bis bureau of industry and security, part of the us department of commerce the us government office that decides which technologies may be exported, to whom, and on what conditions. it writes the rules, issues the licenses and brings the enforcement cases. bis wrote the us restrictions on selling ai chips and chipmaking tools to china in a series of rules. it can change a threshold by publishing a notice in the federal register, with no act of congress needed.\">\n<dt>BIS<span class=\"aka\">Bureau of Industry and Security, part of the US Department of Commerce</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The US government office that decides which technologies may be exported, to whom, and on what conditions. It writes the rules, issues the licenses and brings the enforcement cases.</p><p class=\"why\">BIS wrote the US restrictions on selling AI chips and chipmaking tools to China in a series of rules. It can change a threshold by publishing a notice in the Federal Register, with no act of Congress needed.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-burn-in\" data-term=\"burn-in\" data-text=\"burn-in burn in, wafer-level burn-in, burn-in test burn-in runs a chip hot and at raised voltage for minutes to days, so that any part that would fail early fails in the factory before it is shipped. it can run on the wafer or in the package. aehr, a maker of burn-in systems, says its lead ai customer is moving all burn-in for its accelerators from the system level to the wafer. one weak die in a package of a dozen expensive parts scraps all of them, so burn-in on the wafer protects everything else in the package.\">\n<dt>burn-in<span class=\"aka\">burn in, wafer-level burn-in, burn-in test</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Burn-in runs a chip hot and at raised voltage for minutes to days, so that any part that would fail early fails in the factory before it is shipped. It can run on the wafer or in the package. Aehr, a maker of burn-in systems, says its lead AI customer is moving all burn-in for its accelerators from the system level to the wafer.</p><p class=\"why\">One weak die in a package of a dozen expensive parts scraps all of them, so burn-in on the wafer protects everything else in the package.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-busbar\" data-term=\"busbar\" data-text=\"busbar busbars, copper busbar, copper busbars a busbar is a thick bar of solid copper that carries large currents down the back of a rack to the boards that need them. an ordinary cable carrying the same current would overheat. at the 54 volts used inside racks such as the gb300 nvl72, a one-megawatt rack would need up to 200 kilograms of busbar, by nvidia's estimate. nvidia is moving its racks to 800 volts, which cuts the current, so a megawatt rack will not need bars that heavy.\">\n<dt>busbar<span class=\"aka\">busbars, copper busbar, copper busbars</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A busbar is a thick bar of solid copper that carries large currents down the back of a rack to the boards that need them. An ordinary cable carrying the same current would overheat. At the 54 volts used inside racks such as the GB300 NVL72, a one-megawatt rack would need up to 200 kilograms of busbar, by Nvidia's estimate.</p><p class=\"why\">Nvidia is moving its racks to 800 volts, which cuts the current, so a megawatt rack will not need bars that heavy.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-capex\" data-term=\"capex\" data-text=\"capex capital expenditure, capital spending money a company spends on long-lived physical assets such as buildings, machines and servers, as distinct from salaries and other running costs. the largest cloud companies' capex pays for the chips, racks and buildings of the ai buildout. alphabet, amazon, meta, microsoft and oracle spent $448.2 billion of capital in 2025, the sum of epoch ai's quarterly figures. epoch ai says they will spend $770 billion in 2026 if the trend continues.\">\n<dt>capex<span class=\"aka\">capital expenditure, capital spending</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Money a company spends on long-lived physical assets such as buildings, machines and servers, as distinct from salaries and other running costs.</p><p class=\"why\">The largest cloud companies' capex pays for the chips, racks and buildings of the AI buildout. Alphabet, Amazon, Meta, Microsoft and Oracle spent $448.2 billion of capital in 2025, the sum of Epoch AI's quarterly figures. Epoch AI says they will spend $770 billion in 2026 if the trend continues.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-case-by-case-review\" data-term=\"case-by-case review\" data-text=\"case-by-case review case by case, case-by-case, reviewed case by case case-by-case review means a license is required and each application is judged on its own, with no presumption either way. since january 2026 nvidia's h200 and amd's mi325x have been reviewed this way for china, with conditions attached to each approval. it is the middle ground between an open market and a presumption of denial. in early 2026 the united states settled on it for chips such as the h200 bound for china.\">\n<dt>case-by-case review<span class=\"aka\">case by case, case-by-case, reviewed case by case</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Case-by-case review means a license is required and each application is judged on its own, with no presumption either way. Since January 2026 Nvidia's H200 and AMD's MI325X have been reviewed this way for China, with conditions attached to each approval.</p><p class=\"why\">It is the middle ground between an open market and a presumption of denial. In early 2026 the United States settled on it for chips such as the H200 bound for China.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-chip\" data-term=\"chip\" data-text=\"chip chips, microchip, microchips, semiconductor chip a chip is a small rectangle of silicon, usually smaller than a fingernail, that carries a complete electronic circuit, often made of billions of transistors. it is cut from a wafer after the circuit has been built up on it layer by layer. the supply chain is every firm and country that takes part in making chips, and some of them can stop production.\">\n<dt>chip<span class=\"aka\">chips, microchip, microchips, semiconductor chip</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A chip is a small rectangle of silicon, usually smaller than a fingernail, that carries a complete electronic circuit, often made of billions of transistors. It is cut from a wafer after the circuit has been built up on it layer by layer.</p><p class=\"why\">The supply chain is every firm and country that takes part in making chips, and some of them can stop production.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"silicon-and-wafers/\">Read it in Silicon and Wafers →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-chiplet\" data-term=\"chiplet\" data-text=\"chiplet chiplets one of several smaller pieces that a chip has been deliberately split into, each manufactured separately and then wired back together inside a single package. a chip built this way is like a house assembled from prefabricated rooms. many large accelerators need more circuitry than a lithography machine can print in one exposure, so they are built from chiplets. that makes packaging, the step that joins the chiplets, the hard part. epoch ai found that tsmc's cowos packaging and memory were the main limits on ai chip production in 2025.\">\n<dt>chiplet<span class=\"aka\">chiplets</span></dt>\n<dd><p>One of several smaller pieces that a chip has been deliberately split into, each manufactured separately and then wired back together inside a single package. A chip built this way is like a house assembled from prefabricated rooms.</p><p class=\"why\">Many large accelerators need more circuitry than a lithography machine can print in one exposure, so they are built from chiplets. That makes packaging, the step that joins the chiplets, the hard part. Epoch AI found that TSMC's CoWoS packaging and memory were the main limits on AI chip production in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-chips-act\" data-term=\"chips act\" data-text=\"chips act chips and science act, chips incentives, chips money, chips act grants, chips authorization, chips act support, chips award the chips and science act authorized about $52.7 billion of us federal money for the chip industry. by july 2025 the commerce department had awarded $30.9 billion of direct funding to 19 companies for 40 projects. its grants paid a median 14.2 percent of each funded project's capital cost. in august 2025, $5.7 billion of grants awarded to intel but not yet paid went into the government's $8.9 billion purchase of a 9.9 percent stake in intel.\">\n<dt>CHIPS Act<span class=\"aka\">CHIPS and Science Act, CHIPS incentives, CHIPS money, CHIPS Act grants, CHIPS authorization, CHIPS Act support, CHIPS award</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The CHIPS and Science Act authorized about $52.7 billion of US federal money for the chip industry. By July 2025 the Commerce Department had awarded $30.9 billion of direct funding to 19 companies for 40 projects.</p><p class=\"why\">Its grants paid a median 14.2 percent of each funded project's capital cost. In August 2025, $5.7 billion of grants awarded to Intel but not yet paid went into the government's $8.9 billion purchase of a 9.9 percent stake in Intel.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-chokepoint\" data-term=\"chokepoint\" data-text=\"chokepoint chokepoints a step in the supply chain where so few firms or countries can do the work that losing one of them stops everybody. one sanction or one factory fire at a chokepoint reaches the whole industry, and so does a government policy aimed at one.\">\n<dt>chokepoint<span class=\"aka\">chokepoints</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A step in the supply chain where so few firms or countries can do the work that losing one of them stops everybody.</p><p class=\"why\">One sanction or one factory fire at a chokepoint reaches the whole industry, and so does a government policy aimed at one.</p></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-cmos\" data-term=\"cmos\" data-text=\"cmos complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor, complementary mos cmos, short for complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor, is the standard way of building digital circuits from pairs of transistors. each n-type transistor, which switches on when the voltage on its gate is high, is matched with a p-type transistor, which switches on when that voltage is low. in either logic state one side of the circuit is off, so little current flows except while it switches. cmos became the dominant technology for making chips because its circuits drew close to zero power while idle, which kept heat in check as chips packed in more transistors. finfet and gate-all-around transistors are newer shapes for the same n-type and p-type pairs.\">\n<dt>CMOS<span class=\"aka\">complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor, complementary MOS</span></dt>\n<dd><p>CMOS, short for complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor, is the standard way of building digital circuits from pairs of transistors. Each n-type transistor, which switches on when the voltage on its gate is high, is matched with a p-type transistor, which switches on when that voltage is low. In either logic state one side of the circuit is off, so little current flows except while it switches.</p><p class=\"why\">CMOS became the dominant technology for making chips because its circuits drew close to zero power while idle, which kept heat in check as chips packed in more transistors. FinFET and gate-all-around transistors are newer shapes for the same n-type and p-type pairs.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-cmp\" data-term=\"cmp\" data-text=\"cmp chemical mechanical polishing, chemical mechanical planarization, polishing slurry, polishing slurries, slurry, slurries, cmp slurry, cmp pads, planarization chemical mechanical polishing, or cmp, rubs a wafer's surface flat again after each new layer goes on, using a pad and a liquid full of fine grit called slurry. without it the next layer would be printed on a surface too bumpy to focus on. japanese companies held 51 percent of polishing-slurry sales in 2023, counted by company nationality. cset's january 2021 brief, drawing on 2019 market reports, put dupont and cabot microelectronics at about 56 percent of a $790 million slurry market. cabot was renamed cmc materials in october 2020, and entegris bought it in july 2022. dupont's electronics business became qnity electronics in november 2025.\">\n<dt>CMP<span class=\"aka\">chemical mechanical polishing, chemical mechanical planarization, polishing slurry, polishing slurries, slurry, slurries, CMP slurry, CMP pads, planarization</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Chemical mechanical polishing, or CMP, rubs a wafer's surface flat again after each new layer goes on, using a pad and a liquid full of fine grit called slurry. Without it the next layer would be printed on a surface too bumpy to focus on.</p><p class=\"why\">Japanese companies held 51 percent of polishing-slurry sales in 2023, counted by company nationality. CSET's January 2021 brief, drawing on 2019 market reports, put DuPont and Cabot Microelectronics at about 56 percent of a $790 million slurry market. Cabot was renamed CMC Materials in October 2020, and Entegris bought it in July 2022. DuPont's electronics business became Qnity Electronics in November 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-co-packaged-optics\" data-term=\"co-packaged optics\" data-text=\"co-packaged optics co-packaged, co-packaging, cpo, plug-in modules, plug-in optics co-packaged optics puts the parts that turn electrical signals into light and back onto the switch chip's own package instead of into plug-in modules at the front of the box. broadcom keeps the lasers that supply the light in separate modules that can be replaced in the field. broadcom and nvidia are moving the optics onto the switch package partly to cut the power the optics use. broadcom says its tomahawk 6 davisson cuts optical interconnect power by 70 percent.\">\n<dt>co-packaged optics<span class=\"aka\">co-packaged, co-packaging, CPO, plug-in modules, plug-in optics</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Co-packaged optics puts the parts that turn electrical signals into light and back onto the switch chip's own package instead of into plug-in modules at the front of the box. Broadcom keeps the lasers that supply the light in separate modules that can be replaced in the field.</p><p class=\"why\">Broadcom and Nvidia are moving the optics onto the switch package partly to cut the power the optics use. Broadcom says its Tomahawk 6 Davisson cuts optical interconnect power by 70 percent.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-coater-developer\" data-term=\"coater/developer\" data-text=\"coater/developer coater-developer, coater and developer, coater/developer track, track tool, track tools a coater/developer, or track, is the machine that spins a thin coat of photoresist onto the wafer before it enters the scanner. after the wafer comes out, the same machine washes away the exposed parts, so every printed layer passes through it twice. no pattern can be printed without it. tokyo electron's own results put its share of the market at 91 percent in 2025.\">\n<dt>coater/developer<span class=\"aka\">coater-developer, coater and developer, coater/developer track, track tool, track tools</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A coater/developer, or track, is the machine that spins a thin coat of photoresist onto the wafer before it enters the scanner. After the wafer comes out, the same machine washes away the exposed parts, so every printed layer passes through it twice.</p><p class=\"why\">No pattern can be printed without it. Tokyo Electron's own results put its share of the market at 91 percent in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-coefficient-of-thermal-expansion\" data-term=\"coefficient of thermal expansion\" data-text=\"coefficient of thermal expansion cte, thermal expansion, expansion mismatch, low-cte the coefficient of thermal expansion is how much a material expands for each degree it warms. silicon barely expands and epoxy expands more, so when the two are bonded and heated, the package bends. warpage control, keeping a package from bending, means matching expansion across die, bridge, interposer and substrate. it gets harder as packages grow.\">\n<dt>coefficient of thermal expansion<span class=\"aka\">CTE, thermal expansion, expansion mismatch, low-CTE</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The coefficient of thermal expansion is how much a material expands for each degree it warms. Silicon barely expands and epoxy expands more, so when the two are bonded and heated, the package bends.</p><p class=\"why\">Warpage control, keeping a package from bending, means matching expansion across die, bridge, interposer and substrate. It gets harder as packages grow.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"substrates-and-pcbs/\">Read it in Substrates and PCBs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-compute-threshold\" data-term=\"compute threshold\" data-text=\"compute threshold training compute threshold a limit set on the amount of arithmetic used to train an ai model. it counts operations, whichever chips run them. the ai diffusion rule of january 2025 made one an export control. eccn 4e091 covers &quot;'parameters' for an artificial intelligence model trained utilizing 10^26 or more 'operations'&quot;. the rules require a license to send such parameters to every destination worldwide (15 cfr 742.6(a)(13)). article 51(2) of the eu ai act sets europe's line ten times lower. it presumes a model has high-impact capabilities when the cumulative computation used for training is &quot;greater than 10^25&quot; floating point operations. every other control threshold measures a chip, but this one measures the model the chips train. article 51(3) of the ai act lets the european commission change the eu figure by delegated act. such an act takes effect unless the european parliament or the council objects within three months (article 97(6)). bis said in may 2025 that it would not enforce the ai diffusion rule, but 4e091 still stands in the regulations.\">\n<dt>compute threshold<span class=\"aka\">training compute threshold</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A limit set on the amount of arithmetic used to train an AI model. It counts operations, whichever chips run them. The AI Diffusion rule of January 2025 made one an export control. ECCN 4E091 covers &quot;'Parameters' for an artificial intelligence model trained utilizing 10^26 or more 'operations'&quot;. The rules require a license to send such parameters to every destination worldwide (15 CFR 742.6(a)(13)). Article 51(2) of the EU AI Act sets Europe's line ten times lower. It presumes a model has high-impact capabilities when the cumulative computation used for training is &quot;greater than 10^25&quot; floating point operations.</p><p class=\"why\">Every other control threshold measures a chip, but this one measures the model the chips train. Article 51(3) of the AI Act lets the European Commission change the EU figure by delegated act. Such an act takes effect unless the European Parliament or the Council objects within three months (Article 97(6)). BIS said in May 2025 that it would not enforce the AI Diffusion rule, but 4E091 still stands in the regulations.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-concentration\" data-term=\"concentration\" data-text=\"concentration concentration band a four-band judgment of how many firms could credibly supply a stage today, taken at the narrowest step inside it. extreme means three or fewer, or one firm holding more than half the stage. high means four to six, with the top two taking most of the revenue. moderate means seven or more, none of them dominant. low means many, with the scarce input something another industry sells at volume. where a figure exists for the top country's share of the segment, it is a second check. when the two disagree, the supplier count wins. the fewer the firms that can do a stage, the more one accident or one license decision affects the whole chain.\">\n<dt>Concentration<span class=\"aka\">concentration band</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A four-band judgment of how many firms could credibly supply a stage today, taken at the narrowest step inside it. Extreme means three or fewer, or one firm holding more than half the stage. High means four to six, with the top two taking most of the revenue. Moderate means seven or more, none of them dominant. Low means many, with the scarce input something another industry sells at volume. Where a figure exists for the top country's share of the segment, it is a second check. When the two disagree, the supplier count wins.</p><p class=\"why\">The fewer the firms that can do a stage, the more one accident or one license decision affects the whole chain.</p></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-consignee\" data-term=\"consignee\" data-text=\"consignee consignees, named consignee, named consignees, ultimate consignee the consignee is the party a shipment is sent to, the name on the export license. a named consignee, such as g42 in the united arab emirates, can receive controlled chips on the terms attached to its own name. the july 2026 uae rule names the emirati government, g42 and eight us-headquartered ai companies as consignees who can take controlled ai chips without a license. the license-free treatment is tied to those named buyers.\">\n<dt>consignee<span class=\"aka\">consignees, named consignee, named consignees, ultimate consignee</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The consignee is the party a shipment is sent to, the name on the export license. A named consignee, such as G42 in the United Arab Emirates, can receive controlled chips on the terms attached to its own name.</p><p class=\"why\">The July 2026 UAE rule names the Emirati government, G42 and eight US-headquartered AI companies as consignees who can take controlled AI chips without a license. The license-free treatment is tied to those named buyers.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-country-groups\" data-term=\"country groups\" data-text=\"country groups country group, country group d:5, d:5, a:5, d:1, d:3, d:4, arms-embargoed countries the groups that us export rules sort the world's countries into, published as supplement no. 1 to 15 cfr part 740. a:5 and a:6 list close partners. d:1, d:4 and d:5 are the national security, missile technology and arms-embargoed groups. e:1 and e:2 are the most restricted. a country can be in several groups at once, and the license requirement usually depends on which. us license rules for ai chips are written in terms of these groups. chips in the 3a090.b band, the band below the top one, need a license for d:1, d:4 and d:5 destinations not also in a:5 or a:6 (15 cfr 742.6(a)(6)(iii)(b)). the uae moved from d:3 and d:4 into a:5 in july 2026. but the rule names the uae, so these chips still need a license there, except for approved emirati consignees (15 cfr 742.6(a)(6)(iii)(b)).\">\n<dt>Country Groups<span class=\"aka\">Country Group, Country Group D:5, D:5, A:5, D:1, D:3, D:4, arms-embargoed countries</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The groups that US export rules sort the world's countries into, published as supplement no. 1 to 15 CFR part 740. A:5 and A:6 list close partners. D:1, D:4 and D:5 are the national security, missile technology and arms-embargoed groups. E:1 and E:2 are the most restricted. A country can be in several groups at once, and the license requirement usually depends on which.</p><p class=\"why\">US license rules for AI chips are written in terms of these groups. Chips in the 3A090.b band, the band below the top one, need a license for D:1, D:4 and D:5 destinations not also in A:5 or A:6 (15 CFR 742.6(a)(6)(iii)(B)). The UAE moved from D:3 and D:4 into A:5 in July 2026. But the rule names the UAE, so these chips still need a license there, except for approved Emirati consignees (15 CFR 742.6(a)(6)(iii)(B)).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-cowos\" data-term=\"cowos\" data-text=\"cowos chip on wafer on substrate tsmc's method for mounting logic chips and memory stacks side by side on a shared interposer, a layer of fine wiring, then mounting that interposer on a rigid base board. in cowos-s the interposer is one piece of silicon. in cowos-l, used for nvidia's blackwell and rubin, it is layers of fine copper wiring with small embedded silicon bridges. nearly every high-end ai accelerator is built this way. epoch ai found that tsmc's cowos packaging and memory were the main limits on ai chip production in 2025. it estimates that nvidia used 60.3 percent of all cowos that year. semianalysis judged in march 2026 that cowos supply was easing, but in july 2026 tsmc said its packaging capacity was so tight that it limited customers' growth.\">\n<dt>CoWoS<span class=\"aka\">chip on wafer on substrate</span></dt>\n<dd><p>TSMC's method for mounting logic chips and memory stacks side by side on a shared interposer, a layer of fine wiring, then mounting that interposer on a rigid base board. In CoWoS-S the interposer is one piece of silicon. In CoWoS-L, used for Nvidia's Blackwell and Rubin, it is layers of fine copper wiring with small embedded silicon bridges. Nearly every high-end AI accelerator is built this way.</p><p class=\"why\">Epoch AI found that TSMC's CoWoS packaging and memory were the main limits on AI chip production in 2025. It estimates that Nvidia used 60.3 percent of all CoWoS that year. SemiAnalysis judged in March 2026 that CoWoS supply was easing, but in July 2026 TSMC said its packaging capacity was so tight that it limited customers' growth.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-critical-dimension\" data-term=\"critical dimension\" data-text=\"critical dimension critical dimensions, cd, cd-sem, critical-dimension, line width, line-width, line widths the critical dimension is the width of the finest printed feature on a layer. a cd-sem is an electron microscope built to measure it across a wafer without cutting anything. fabs measure it to tell whether each lithography and etch step came out the right width. in 2025 hitachi held 71.9 percent of the market for the tools that measure it, by cset's count. they are the one kind of inspection or measurement tool that japan leads.\">\n<dt>critical dimension<span class=\"aka\">critical dimensions, CD, CD-SEM, critical-dimension, line width, line-width, line widths</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The critical dimension is the width of the finest printed feature on a layer. A CD-SEM is an electron microscope built to measure it across a wafer without cutting anything.</p><p class=\"why\">Fabs measure it to tell whether each lithography and etch step came out the right width. In 2025 Hitachi held 71.9 percent of the market for the tools that measure it, by CSET's count. They are the one kind of inspection or measurement tool that Japan leads.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"metrology-and-inspection/\">Read it in Metrology and Inspection →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-csis\" data-term=\"csis\" data-text=\"csis center for strategic and international studies csis, the center for strategic and international studies, is a bipartisan, nonprofit policy research organization in washington, d.c., founded in 1962. its technology researchers publish assessments of china's chipmaking and of us export controls. its reports judge how far chinese chipmakers are from replacing foreign tools. in september 2025 csis judged that extreme ultraviolet machines remained firmly out of china's reach despite massive state investment, including $43 billion that china announced for developing its own.\">\n<dt>CSIS<span class=\"aka\">Center for Strategic and International Studies</span></dt>\n<dd><p>CSIS, the Center for Strategic and International Studies, is a bipartisan, nonprofit policy research organization in Washington, D.C., founded in 1962. Its technology researchers publish assessments of China's chipmaking and of US export controls.</p><p class=\"why\">Its reports judge how far Chinese chipmakers are from replacing foreign tools. In September 2025 CSIS judged that extreme ultraviolet machines remained firmly out of China's reach despite massive state investment, including $43 billion that China announced for developing its own.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-cvd\" data-term=\"cvd\" data-text=\"cvd chemical vapor deposition, pecvd, plasma-enhanced chemical vapor deposition, mocvd, cvd precursor, precursor, precursors chemical vapor deposition, or cvd, grows a film by flowing gases over a hot wafer so they react on its surface and leave a solid layer behind. the plasma-enhanced version, pecvd, runs cooler. the gases used are called precursors. cvd made up $11.2 billion of a $26.2 billion deposition tool market in 2025, most of it the plasma-enhanced kind. chinese toolmakers' share of the deposition tool market rose from 2 to 7 percent between 2019 and 2024.\">\n<dt>CVD<span class=\"aka\">chemical vapor deposition, PECVD, plasma-enhanced chemical vapor deposition, MOCVD, CVD precursor, precursor, precursors</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Chemical vapor deposition, or CVD, grows a film by flowing gases over a hot wafer so they react on its surface and leave a solid layer behind. The plasma-enhanced version, PECVD, runs cooler. The gases used are called precursors.</p><p class=\"why\">CVD made up $11.2 billion of a $26.2 billion deposition tool market in 2025, most of it the plasma-enhanced kind. Chinese toolmakers' share of the deposition tool market rose from 2 to 7 percent between 2019 and 2024.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-de-minimis\" data-term=\"de minimis\" data-text=\"de minimis  the share of controlled american content a foreign-made item may contain before us export rules, the ear, apply to it. under 15 cfr 734.4 the general threshold is 25 percent of the item's value, and 10 percent for the most restricted destinations. above the threshold the item falls under the ear, and below it the item does not. it decides whether foreign-made goods with some us content fall under american rules. the foreign direct product rules work differently and catch an item whatever its share of us content. under 15 cfr 734.4(a)(3), equipment in eccn 3b993.f.1 has no de minimis level when it is bound for advanced-node chip production. the exception is equipment first exported from a country that also controls it.\">\n<dt>de minimis</dt>\n<dd><p>The share of controlled American content a foreign-made item may contain before US export rules, the EAR, apply to it. Under 15 CFR 734.4 the general threshold is 25 percent of the item's value, and 10 percent for the most restricted destinations. Above the threshold the item falls under the EAR, and below it the item does not.</p><p class=\"why\">It decides whether foreign-made goods with some US content fall under American rules. The foreign direct product rules work differently and catch an item whatever its share of US content. Under 15 CFR 734.4(a)(3), equipment in ECCN 3B993.f.1 has no de minimis level when it is bound for advanced-node chip production. The exception is equipment first exported from a country that also controls it.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-defect-density\" data-term=\"defect density\" data-text=\"defect density d0, defects per square centimeter the average number of chip-killing flaws per square centimeter of processed wafer. it is a fab's quality score, inferred from how many chips come out working. ai accelerators have some of the largest dies in production, and yield, the share of dies that work, falls steeply as die area times defect density grows. in a textbook example at 0.8 defects per square centimeter, 49.2 percent of dies 1 centimeter on a side come out flawless, against 11.3 percent of dies 2 centimeters on a side. the share that can be sold is higher on chips that carry spare blocks.\">\n<dt>defect density<span class=\"aka\">D0, defects per square centimeter</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The average number of chip-killing flaws per square centimeter of processed wafer. It is a fab's quality score, inferred from how many chips come out working.</p><p class=\"why\">AI accelerators have some of the largest dies in production, and yield, the share of dies that work, falls steeply as die area times defect density grows. In a textbook example at 0.8 defects per square centimeter, 49.2 percent of dies 1 centimeter on a side come out flawless, against 11.3 percent of dies 2 centimeters on a side. The share that can be sold is higher on chips that carry spare blocks.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"metrology-and-inspection/\">Read it in Metrology and Inspection →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-denial-order\" data-term=\"denial order\" data-text=\"denial order  an order from bis that shuts a named party out of trade in us-controlled items, as a sanction or a protective measure, with no license policy involved. under 15 cfr 764.3 it restricts the party's exports, reexports and in-country transfers of items subject to the ear, and its access to them. it can also suspend or revoke the party's outstanding licenses. there is no application to file. orders can be issued outright or suspended and later activated. it can cut a named party off from every item subject to the ear. the order activated against zte in april 2018 stayed in force until bis terminated it 89 days later as part of a settlement (83 fr 17644; 83 fr 34825).\">\n<dt>denial order</dt>\n<dd><p>An order from BIS that shuts a named party out of trade in US-controlled items, as a sanction or a protective measure, with no license policy involved. Under 15 CFR 764.3 it restricts the party's exports, reexports and in-country transfers of items subject to the EAR, and its access to them. It can also suspend or revoke the party's outstanding licenses. There is no application to file. Orders can be issued outright or suspended and later activated.</p><p class=\"why\">It can cut a named party off from every item subject to the EAR. The order activated against ZTE in April 2018 stayed in force until BIS terminated it 89 days later as part of a settlement (83 FR 17644; 83 FR 34825).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-deposition\" data-term=\"deposition\" data-text=\"deposition  adding a layer of material to a wafer. machines knock atoms off a solid target so they land on the surface, react gases at the surface so a film grows there, or plate metal out of a liquid. it is how the insulators, the wires and the parts of each transistor are built up. making one chip takes 1,000 to 1,500 steps by a 2025 industry estimate, and many of them are deposition and etch. ai hardware needs films that reach the bottom of deeper holes. four firms make most of the tools, but deposition is among the tool types where chinese makers gained the most share between 2019 and 2024.\">\n<dt>deposition</dt>\n<dd><p>Adding a layer of material to a wafer. Machines knock atoms off a solid target so they land on the surface, react gases at the surface so a film grows there, or plate metal out of a liquid. It is how the insulators, the wires and the parts of each transistor are built up.</p><p class=\"why\">Making one chip takes 1,000 to 1,500 steps by a 2025 industry estimate, and many of them are deposition and etch. AI hardware needs films that reach the bottom of deeper holes. Four firms make most of the tools, but deposition is among the tool types where Chinese makers gained the most share between 2019 and 2024.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-dicing\" data-term=\"dicing\" data-text=\"dicing wafer dicing, dicing saw, dicing saws, grinding, wafer grinding, grinders, wafer grinders, thinning, wafer thinning dicing cuts a finished wafer into its individual dies with a diamond saw or a laser. grinding, done first, thins the wafer from the back, and for stacked memory it goes on until the copper columns inside the dies come through. stacked high bandwidth memory (hbm) depends on that grinding. disco of japan held 87 percent of the world market for dicing saws and wafer grinders in 2025, by cset's count.\">\n<dt>dicing<span class=\"aka\">wafer dicing, dicing saw, dicing saws, grinding, wafer grinding, grinders, wafer grinders, thinning, wafer thinning</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Dicing cuts a finished wafer into its individual dies with a diamond saw or a laser. Grinding, done first, thins the wafer from the back, and for stacked memory it goes on until the copper columns inside the dies come through.</p><p class=\"why\">Stacked high bandwidth memory (HBM) depends on that grinding. Disco of Japan held 87 percent of the world market for dicing saws and wafer grinders in 2025, by CSET's count.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-die\" data-term=\"die\" data-text=\"die singular of dice, dies one rectangular chip cut out of a wafer. hundreds are printed side by side on the same disc and then sliced apart, and each separated rectangle is a die. cost and yield are counted per die. a gpu die that fills the largest area one exposure can print loses far more silicon to one fatal defect than a small chip does.\">\n<dt>die<span class=\"aka\">singular of dice, dies</span></dt>\n<dd><p>One rectangular chip cut out of a wafer. Hundreds are printed side by side on the same disc and then sliced apart, and each separated rectangle is a die.</p><p class=\"why\">Cost and yield are counted per die. A GPU die that fills the largest area one exposure can print loses far more silicon to one fatal defect than a small chip does.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"silicon-and-wafers/\">Read it in Silicon and Wafers →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-dielectric\" data-term=\"dielectric\" data-text=\"dielectric dielectrics, dielectric etch, dielectric properties, insulator, insulating layer a dielectric is an insulator: a material that does not conduct, such as the glassy oxides and nitrides between a chip's wires or the epoxy in a package substrate. dielectric etch cuts holes and trenches through those insulating layers so the wires can be laid in. how much signal a dielectric absorbs sets how fast a substrate or circuit board can run. so the suppliers of laminates, the insulating sheets these boards are made from, matter to ai systems.\">\n<dt>dielectric<span class=\"aka\">dielectrics, dielectric etch, dielectric properties, insulator, insulating layer</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A dielectric is an insulator: a material that does not conduct, such as the glassy oxides and nitrides between a chip's wires or the epoxy in a package substrate. Dielectric etch cuts holes and trenches through those insulating layers so the wires can be laid in.</p><p class=\"why\">How much signal a dielectric absorbs sets how fast a substrate or circuit board can run. So the suppliers of laminates, the insulating sheets these boards are made from, matter to AI systems.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-dram\" data-term=\"dram\" data-text=\"dram dynamic random-access memory a computer's main working memory. each bit is a charge held in a microscopic capacitor that leaks, so the chip has to refresh its contents constantly. it forgets everything when the power goes off. hbm is a stack of dram chips, and the three leading dram makers, sk hynix, samsung and micron, make nearly all of it. sk hynix says the shift of production capacity to hbm left ordinary dram, the kind in pcs and phones, undersupplied. the company says the shortage helped drive a significant price recovery from the third quarter of 2025.\">\n<dt>DRAM<span class=\"aka\">dynamic random-access memory</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A computer's main working memory. Each bit is a charge held in a microscopic capacitor that leaks, so the chip has to refresh its contents constantly. It forgets everything when the power goes off.</p><p class=\"why\">HBM is a stack of DRAM chips, and the three leading DRAM makers, SK hynix, Samsung and Micron, make nearly all of it. SK hynix says the shift of production capacity to HBM left ordinary DRAM, the kind in PCs and phones, undersupplied. The company says the shortage helped drive a significant price recovery from the third quarter of 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-duv\" data-term=\"duv\" data-text=\"duv deep ultraviolet, deep-ultraviolet, duv scanner, duv scanners, duv tools chipmaking light from gas lasers, at 248 or 193 nanometers, and the machines that print with it, which still make up most lithography tools. filling the gap between lens and wafer with water sharpens the image, a method called immersion. a fab without extreme ultraviolet machines can reach leading-edge logic only with immersion deep ultraviolet and several passes per layer, as smic does. so dutch export licensing covers the most advanced immersion tools.\">\n<dt>DUV<span class=\"aka\">deep ultraviolet, deep-ultraviolet, DUV scanner, DUV scanners, DUV tools</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Chipmaking light from gas lasers, at 248 or 193 nanometers, and the machines that print with it, which still make up most lithography tools. Filling the gap between lens and wafer with water sharpens the image, a method called immersion.</p><p class=\"why\">A fab without extreme ultraviolet machines can reach leading-edge logic only with immersion deep ultraviolet and several passes per layer, as SMIC does. So Dutch export licensing covers the most advanced immersion tools.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ear\" data-term=\"ear\" data-text=\"ear export administration regulations the body of us rules that governs the export of commercial goods, software and technology, including items with both civilian and military uses. the bureau of industry and security writes and enforces them. they run from 15 cfr part 730 to part 774. part 734 sets what they cover, part 742 the license requirements, part 744 the end-use and end-user controls, part 740 the exceptions and part 764 the penalties. american export rules on chips and chipmaking tools are amendments to these regulations, made by notice in the federal register with no act of congress.\">\n<dt>EAR<span class=\"aka\">Export Administration Regulations</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The body of US rules that governs the export of commercial goods, software and technology, including items with both civilian and military uses. The Bureau of Industry and Security writes and enforces them. They run from 15 CFR part 730 to part 774. Part 734 sets what they cover, part 742 the license requirements, part 744 the end-use and end-user controls, part 740 the exceptions and part 764 the penalties.</p><p class=\"why\">American export rules on chips and chipmaking tools are amendments to these regulations, made by notice in the Federal Register with no act of Congress.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ear99\" data-term=\"ear99\" data-text=\"ear99  the label for an item that falls under us export rules but is not named on the commerce control list, the catalog of controlled items. the label is defined at 15 cfr 734.3(c). it is a catch-all category, but an ear99 item still needs a license if it is going to a listed party or a controlled end use. an ear99 item can usually ship without a license, but a listed buyer, a controlled end use or an embargoed destination can still require one. so exporters of unlisted items have to follow the end-user controls in part 744 of the ear too.\">\n<dt>EAR99</dt>\n<dd><p>The label for an item that falls under US export rules but is not named on the Commerce Control List, the catalog of controlled items. The label is defined at 15 CFR 734.3(c). It is a catch-all category, but an EAR99 item still needs a license if it is going to a listed party or a controlled end use.</p><p class=\"why\">An EAR99 item can usually ship without a license, but a listed buyer, a controlled end use or an embargoed destination can still require one. So exporters of unlisted items have to follow the end-user controls in part 744 of the EAR too.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-eccn\" data-term=\"eccn\" data-text=\"eccn export control classification number the catalog number that us export rules assign to a controlled item, similar to a customs tariff code but for security-sensitive technology. number 3a090 covers advanced computing chips and 3b001 covers chipmaking equipment. an item's classification number determines whether it needs a license. so the technical thresholds written into each number set which products are controlled.\">\n<dt>ECCN<span class=\"aka\">Export Control Classification Number</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The catalog number that US export rules assign to a controlled item, similar to a customs tariff code but for security-sensitive technology. Number 3A090 covers advanced computing chips and 3B001 covers chipmaking equipment.</p><p class=\"why\">An item's classification number determines whether it needs a license. So the technical thresholds written into each number set which products are controlled.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-eda\" data-term=\"eda\" data-text=\"eda electronic design automation, chip design software the software that turns a description of what a chip should do into the exact pattern of shapes to be printed on silicon. it also proves the design will work before anyone commits money to masks and wafers. three vendors sell the only software that covers every step of designing a leading-edge chip. since october 2022 software made for designing chips with gate-all-around transistors has needed a us export license. in may 2025 the us government sent letters to the three vendors requiring a license for all their sales to china, and it lifted the requirement on 2 july.\">\n<dt>EDA<span class=\"aka\">electronic design automation, chip design software</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The software that turns a description of what a chip should do into the exact pattern of shapes to be printed on silicon. It also proves the design will work before anyone commits money to masks and wafers.</p><p class=\"why\">Three vendors sell the only software that covers every step of designing a leading-edge chip. Since October 2022 software made for designing chips with gate-all-around transistors has needed a US export license. In May 2025 the US government sent letters to the three vendors requiring a license for all their sales to China, and it lifted the requirement on 2 July.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-electron-beam\" data-term=\"electron beam\" data-text=\"electron beam electron-beam, e-beam, electron beams, multi-beam, multibeam, e-beam inspection, electron-beam metrology an electron beam is a stream of electrons focused to a spot far smaller than any spot of light. mask shops use it to write the pattern onto a photomask, and fabs use it to inspect wafers for defects light cannot see and to measure line widths. a multi-beam tool fires many beams at once, because a single beam is slow. in 2023 intel called austria's ims nanofabrication the established leader in the multi-beam writers that advanced euv masks require. since december 2024 us rules have controlled wafer inspection tools that use two or more beams to find defects 21 nm across or smaller.\">\n<dt>electron beam<span class=\"aka\">electron-beam, e-beam, electron beams, multi-beam, multibeam, e-beam inspection, electron-beam metrology</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An electron beam is a stream of electrons focused to a spot far smaller than any spot of light. Mask shops use it to write the pattern onto a photomask, and fabs use it to inspect wafers for defects light cannot see and to measure line widths. A multi-beam tool fires many beams at once, because a single beam is slow.</p><p class=\"why\">In 2023 Intel called Austria's IMS Nanofabrication the established leader in the multi-beam writers that advanced EUV masks require. Since December 2024 US rules have controlled wafer inspection tools that use two or more beams to find defects 21 nm across or smaller.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"photomasks-and-pellicles/\">Read it in Photomasks and Pellicles →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-electronic-grade\" data-term=\"electronic-grade\" data-text=\"electronic-grade electronic grade, semiconductor-grade, semiconductor grade, solar-grade, solar grade electronic-grade, or semiconductor-grade, silicon is refined until its metal impurities are no more than a few parts per billion, pure enough for chips. solar-grade silicon is a less pure grade made for solar cells. every chip starts from it. the commerce department found in 2026 that semiconductor-grade polysilicon makes up only 2.4 percent of global production. the german wafer maker siltronic names five major suppliers for 2025: wacker, hemlock, oci, tokuyama and mitsubishi. none of them is chinese.\">\n<dt>electronic-grade<span class=\"aka\">electronic grade, semiconductor-grade, semiconductor grade, solar-grade, solar grade</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Electronic-grade, or semiconductor-grade, silicon is refined until its metal impurities are no more than a few parts per billion, pure enough for chips. Solar-grade silicon is a less pure grade made for solar cells.</p><p class=\"why\">Every chip starts from it. The Commerce Department found in 2026 that semiconductor-grade polysilicon makes up only 2.4 percent of global production. The German wafer maker Siltronic names five major suppliers for 2025: Wacker, Hemlock, OCI, Tokuyama and Mitsubishi. None of them is Chinese.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"silicon-and-wafers/\">Read it in Silicon and Wafers →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-emea\" data-term=\"emea\" data-text=\"emea  emea stands for europe, the middle east and africa, one region in the breakdowns that companies publish of where their sales go. asml is based in the netherlands, yet tools shipped to emea made up 1 percent of its net system sales in 2025, against 33 percent for china.\">\n<dt>EMEA</dt>\n<dd><p>EMEA stands for Europe, the Middle East and Africa, one region in the breakdowns that companies publish of where their sales go.</p><p class=\"why\">ASML is based in the Netherlands, yet tools shipped to EMEA made up 1 percent of its net system sales in 2025, against 33 percent for China.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-end-use-and-end-user-controls\" data-term=\"end-use and end-user controls\" data-text=\"end-use and end-user controls end user, end users, end-user, end use, military end user export rules that depend on who the buyer is and what they will do with the item, whatever the item is. the same tool can ship freely to one customer and need a license that will be refused for another. a company can lose access to us-controlled items because of who owns it or what its site produces. in september 2025 us rules were extended to firms at least 50 percent owned by listed entities, though the extension is suspended until 9 november 2026.\">\n<dt>end-use and end-user controls<span class=\"aka\">end user, end users, end-user, end use, military end user</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Export rules that depend on who the buyer is and what they will do with the item, whatever the item is. The same tool can ship freely to one customer and need a license that will be refused for another.</p><p class=\"why\">A company can lose access to US-controlled items because of who owns it or what its site produces. In September 2025 US rules were extended to firms at least 50 percent owned by listed entities, though the extension is suspended until 9 November 2026.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-entity-list\" data-term=\"entity list\" data-text=\"entity list entity-list, entity-listed, entity list additions, listed entity, listed entities, listed firm, listed firms a published list of foreign companies, institutes and individuals. anyone anywhere, american or foreign, needs a license to send them an item subject to the ear. each entry states its own license review policy. most carry a presumption of denial, meaning the license will normally be refused. smic's entry, as amended in december 2024, is a presumption of denial for all items. the exception is tools designed for 200 mm wafer production and bound for a 200 mm plant, which are reviewed case by case. the list is supplement no. 4 to 15 cfr part 744, and the license requirement is in 15 cfr 744.11. it names an organization, so it is one of the simplest tools the us government has. in september 2025 the us extended each listing to companies at least 50 percent owned by listed firms, but that extension is suspended until 9 november 2026 (90 fr 50857).\">\n<dt>Entity List<span class=\"aka\">entity-list, Entity-Listed, Entity List additions, listed entity, listed entities, listed firm, listed firms</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A published list of foreign companies, institutes and individuals. Anyone anywhere, American or foreign, needs a license to send them an item subject to the EAR. Each entry states its own license review policy. Most carry a presumption of denial, meaning the license will normally be refused. SMIC's entry, as amended in December 2024, is a presumption of denial for all items. The exception is tools designed for 200 mm wafer production and bound for a 200 mm plant, which are reviewed case by case. The list is supplement no. 4 to 15 CFR part 744, and the license requirement is in 15 CFR 744.11.</p><p class=\"why\">It names an organization, so it is one of the simplest tools the US government has. In September 2025 the US extended each listing to companies at least 50 percent owned by listed firms, but that extension is suspended until 9 November 2026 (90 FR 50857).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-epitaxy\" data-term=\"epitaxy\" data-text=\"epitaxy epitaxial, epitaxial wafer, epitaxial wafers, epitaxial layer, epi epitaxy grows a fresh layer of crystal on top of a wafer, atom by atom, so the new layer continues the crystal beneath it with almost no flaws. an epitaxial wafer is a plain wafer with that extra layer, and the transistors are built in it. flaws in that layer can make the transistors leak current. the industry association semi credits the 2025 rise in wafer shipments to ai demand for advanced epitaxial wafers for logic chips and polished wafers for high-bandwidth memory.\">\n<dt>epitaxy<span class=\"aka\">epitaxial, epitaxial wafer, epitaxial wafers, epitaxial layer, epi</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Epitaxy grows a fresh layer of crystal on top of a wafer, atom by atom, so the new layer continues the crystal beneath it with almost no flaws. An epitaxial wafer is a plain wafer with that extra layer, and the transistors are built in it.</p><p class=\"why\">Flaws in that layer can make the transistors leak current. The industry association SEMI credits the 2025 rise in wafer shipments to AI demand for advanced epitaxial wafers for logic chips and polished wafers for high-bandwidth memory.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"silicon-and-wafers/\">Read it in Silicon and Wafers →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-etch\" data-term=\"etch\" data-text=\"etch etching, etched, etches, etcher, etchers, dry etch removing material from a wafer wherever the printed pattern says it should not be. most etch tools turn a gas into a plasma whose ions and fragments eat one material and leave the material beside it alone. wrap-around transistors need etch that cuts sideways while sparing the material beside it. stacked memory needs holes far deeper than they are wide. so us rules control etch tools by selectivity, meaning how well a tool cuts one material while sparing another, and by hole shape.\">\n<dt>etch<span class=\"aka\">etching, etched, etches, etcher, etchers, dry etch</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Removing material from a wafer wherever the printed pattern says it should not be. Most etch tools turn a gas into a plasma whose ions and fragments eat one material and leave the material beside it alone.</p><p class=\"why\">Wrap-around transistors need etch that cuts sideways while sparing the material beside it. Stacked memory needs holes far deeper than they are wide. So US rules control etch tools by selectivity, meaning how well a tool cuts one material while sparing another, and by hole shape.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ethernet\" data-term=\"ethernet\" data-text=\"ethernet ultra ethernet, spectrum-x, spectrum-x ethernet, tomahawk, ethernet switch ethernet is the ordinary networking standard of offices and the internet, now made fast and reliable enough to link the servers of an ai cluster. its switch chips, such as broadcom's tomahawk, route traffic between thousands of accelerators. broadcom has doubled the bandwidth of its ethernet switch chips every generation, from 25.6 tbps on one chip in tomahawk 4 in 2019 to 102.4 in tomahawk 6 in 2025.\">\n<dt>Ethernet<span class=\"aka\">Ultra Ethernet, Spectrum-X, Spectrum-X Ethernet, Tomahawk, Ethernet switch</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Ethernet is the ordinary networking standard of offices and the internet, now made fast and reliable enough to link the servers of an AI cluster. Its switch chips, such as Broadcom's Tomahawk, route traffic between thousands of accelerators.</p><p class=\"why\">Broadcom has doubled the bandwidth of its Ethernet switch chips every generation, from 25.6 Tbps on one chip in Tomahawk 4 in 2019 to 102.4 in Tomahawk 6 in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-euv\" data-term=\"euv\" data-text=\"euv extreme ultraviolet, extreme-ultraviolet, euv scanner, euv scanners, extreme ultraviolet lithography the light that prints the finest layers of every leading-edge chip, and the machines that print with it. its wavelength is 13.5 nanometers, and shorter light draws finer lines. air and glass both absorb it, so the machine works in a vacuum and carries the light on mirrors. the light comes from droplets of molten tin, 50,000 a second, each hit twice by a laser. the finest layers set how densely transistors and wires pack, so the most advanced ai chips depend on euv. only asml makes the machines, and export controls block it from shipping them to chinese chipmakers.\">\n<dt>EUV<span class=\"aka\">extreme ultraviolet, extreme-ultraviolet, EUV scanner, EUV scanners, extreme ultraviolet lithography</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The light that prints the finest layers of every leading-edge chip, and the machines that print with it. Its wavelength is 13.5 nanometers, and shorter light draws finer lines. Air and glass both absorb it, so the machine works in a vacuum and carries the light on mirrors. The light comes from droplets of molten tin, 50,000 a second, each hit twice by a laser.</p><p class=\"why\">The finest layers set how densely transistors and wires pack, so the most advanced AI chips depend on EUV. Only ASML makes the machines, and export controls block it from shipping them to Chinese chipmakers.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-export-control\" data-term=\"export control\" data-text=\"export control export controls, export licensing, export license, export licenses, export licence, export licences, export-control an export control is a rule that requires the government's permission for a sale. the government names an item and a country or a buyer. from then on its own companies must hold a license before they ship that item to that country or buyer. the united states extends some of these rules to goods made abroad with american technology. it works only when the controlling country's firms make something the buyer cannot get elsewhere.\">\n<dt>export control<span class=\"aka\">export controls, export licensing, export license, export licenses, export licence, export licences, export-control</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An export control is a rule that requires the government's permission for a sale. The government names an item and a country or a buyer. From then on its own companies must hold a license before they ship that item to that country or buyer. The United States extends some of these rules to goods made abroad with American technology.</p><p class=\"why\">It works only when the controlling country's firms make something the buyer cannot get elsewhere.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-fab\" data-term=\"fab\" data-text=\"fab fabrication plant, wafer fab, fabs, chip factory, chip factories the factory where wafers are processed into chips. it is a cleanroom where each wafer moves from machine to machine in a sealed pod for months. the building costs tens of billions of dollars. in 2023 bcg estimated that a new 2 nm-class fab finished in 2026 would cost $35 to $43 billion to own over ten years. semianalysis judged in december 2025 that finding enough workers remained a major challenge for tsmc in arizona. tsmc has yet to build one of its largest fabs outside taiwan.\">\n<dt>fab<span class=\"aka\">fabrication plant, wafer fab, fabs, chip factory, chip factories</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The factory where wafers are processed into chips. It is a cleanroom where each wafer moves from machine to machine in a sealed pod for months. The building costs tens of billions of dollars.</p><p class=\"why\">In 2023 BCG estimated that a new 2 nm-class fab finished in 2026 would cost $35 to $43 billion to own over ten years. SemiAnalysis judged in December 2025 that finding enough workers remained a major challenge for TSMC in Arizona. TSMC has yet to build one of its largest fabs outside Taiwan.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-fabless\" data-term=\"fabless\" data-text=\"fabless  a chip company that designs and sells chips but owns no factory, paying a contract manufacturer, a foundry, to make them. nvidia, amd, apple, qualcomm and broadcom all work this way. the fabless model concentrates manufacturing in a handful of foundries. so a designer's supply, its costs and where its chips are made all depend on a company it does not control.\">\n<dt>fabless</dt>\n<dd><p>A chip company that designs and sells chips but owns no factory, paying a contract manufacturer, a foundry, to make them. Nvidia, AMD, Apple, Qualcomm and Broadcom all work this way.</p><p class=\"why\">The fabless model concentrates manufacturing in a handful of foundries. So a designer's supply, its costs and where its chips are made all depend on a company it does not control.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-federal-register\" data-term=\"federal register\" data-text=\"federal register fr, 89 fr, 91 fr, 88 fr, federal register notice the federal register is the us government's daily journal, where every new rule is published. an export rule can take effect a few days before it is printed there, as the uae rule did in july 2026. a citation such as 89 fr 96790 means volume 89, page 96790, and is the usual way to cite a rule. us export rules change by notices published there, with no act of congress needed.\">\n<dt>Federal Register<span class=\"aka\">FR, 89 FR, 91 FR, 88 FR, Federal Register notice</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The Federal Register is the US government's daily journal, where every new rule is published. An export rule can take effect a few days before it is printed there, as the UAE rule did in July 2026. A citation such as 89 FR 96790 means volume 89, page 96790, and is the usual way to cite a rule.</p><p class=\"why\">US export rules change by notices published there, with no act of Congress needed.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-finfet\" data-term=\"finfet\" data-text=\"finfet fin field-effect transistor a transistor whose channel, the strip that current flows through, stands on edge like a shark fin. the gate, the electrode that switches the current, wraps around three sides of the fin instead of resting on one. more contact means firmer control and less leakage when the switch is meant to be off. tsmc's leading-edge processes used finfets until n2, its first process with gate-all-around transistors, entered volume production in late 2025. the october 2022 us rules used finfet or 16/14 nm logic as one of their thresholds for an advanced fab.\">\n<dt>FinFET<span class=\"aka\">fin field-effect transistor</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A transistor whose channel, the strip that current flows through, stands on edge like a shark fin. The gate, the electrode that switches the current, wraps around three sides of the fin instead of resting on one. More contact means firmer control and less leakage when the switch is meant to be off.</p><p class=\"why\">TSMC's leading-edge processes used FinFETs until N2, its first process with gate-all-around transistors, entered volume production in late 2025. The October 2022 US rules used FinFET or 16/14 nm logic as one of their thresholds for an advanced fab.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-flops\" data-term=\"flops\" data-text=\"flops floating point operations per second, tflops, pflops, flop, teraflops a count of how many arithmetic operations on floating-point numbers, numbers with a fractional part, a chip can perform each second, the way horsepower counts an engine's output. it is the standard unit of ai compute, but two chips' figures can be compared only when the number format behind each, such as 8-bit or 16-bit, is stated. us export rules use their own score, tpp, which weights each operation by its bit length.\">\n<dt>FLOPS<span class=\"aka\">floating point operations per second, TFLOPS, PFLOPS, FLOP, teraflops</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A count of how many arithmetic operations on floating-point numbers, numbers with a fractional part, a chip can perform each second, the way horsepower counts an engine's output.</p><p class=\"why\">It is the standard unit of AI compute, but two chips' figures can be compared only when the number format behind each, such as 8-bit or 16-bit, is stated. US export rules use their own score, TPP, which weights each operation by its bit length.</p></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-foreign-direct-product-rule\" data-term=\"foreign direct product rule\" data-text=\"foreign direct product rule fdpr, fdp rule, foreign-produced direct product rule, direct product rule, foreign-produced item rules, foreign-produced item rule, foreign-produced item a us rule that puts a foreign-made item under american control when two tests are both met. the first is about the product: the item was made directly from specified us technology or software, or in a plant that was. the second is about the destination: the item is going somewhere, or to someone, the rule names. the mechanics are in 15 cfr 734.9. the rule lets us controls reach goods made outside the united states. without it, a buyer on the entity list could escape us controls by ordering chips from a supplier outside the united states. with it, a chip made in taiwan on american tools for huawei needs a us license. for listed firms the rule reaches only those whose entry carries a footnote naming it, such as huawei's (15 cfr 734.9(e)).\">\n<dt>foreign direct product rule<span class=\"aka\">FDPR, FDP rule, foreign-produced direct product rule, direct product rule, foreign-produced item rules, foreign-produced item rule, foreign-produced item</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A US rule that puts a foreign-made item under American control when two tests are both met. The first is about the product: the item was made directly from specified US technology or software, or in a plant that was. The second is about the destination: the item is going somewhere, or to someone, the rule names. The mechanics are in 15 CFR 734.9.</p><p class=\"why\">The rule lets US controls reach goods made outside the United States. Without it, a buyer on the Entity List could escape US controls by ordering chips from a supplier outside the United States. With it, a chip made in Taiwan on American tools for Huawei needs a US license. For listed firms the rule reaches only those whose entry carries a footnote naming it, such as Huawei's (15 CFR 734.9(e)).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-foundry\" data-term=\"foundry\" data-text=\"foundry pure-play foundry, contract chipmaker, foundries, pure-play, pure play, pure-play model, contract chipmaking a company, or a division of one, that manufactures chips designed by other companies. a pure-play foundry, the model tsmc pioneered after its founding in 1987, makes no products of its own. the model works because no chip company sells enough of one product to fill a modern fab on its own. all six of tsmc's largest plants are in taiwan. taiwan held 69 percent of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022, so political events there affect the whole chip supply.\">\n<dt>foundry<span class=\"aka\">pure-play foundry, contract chipmaker, foundries, pure-play, pure play, pure-play model, contract chipmaking</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A company, or a division of one, that manufactures chips designed by other companies. A pure-play foundry, the model TSMC pioneered after its founding in 1987, makes no products of its own. The model works because no chip company sells enough of one product to fill a modern fab on its own.</p><p class=\"why\">All six of TSMC's largest plants are in Taiwan. Taiwan held 69 percent of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022, so political events there affect the whole chip supply.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-fp8-and-fp4\" data-term=\"fp8 and fp4\" data-text=\"fp8 and fp4 8-bit and 4-bit floating point, fp8, fp4, fp16, bf16, int8, number formats ways of writing a number using only 8 or 4 binary digits, or bits, far fewer than standard formats use. each number is less precise, but the chip can perform and store far more of them. that trade-off suits machine learning, which can work with less exact numbers. lower precision raises a chip's headline speed, so a performance figure quoted without its number format cannot be compared. us export rules allow for this by weighting each operation by its bit length.\">\n<dt>FP8 and FP4<span class=\"aka\">8-bit and 4-bit floating point, FP8, FP4, FP16, BF16, INT8, number formats</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Ways of writing a number using only 8 or 4 binary digits, or bits, far fewer than standard formats use. Each number is less precise, but the chip can perform and store far more of them. That trade-off suits machine learning, which can work with less exact numbers.</p><p class=\"why\">Lower precision raises a chip's headline speed, so a performance figure quoted without its number format cannot be compared. US export rules allow for this by weighting each operation by its bit length.</p></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-front-end\" data-term=\"front end\" data-text=\"front end front end of line, feol, front-end, front-end wafers the front end of line is the first half of making a chip, the steps that build the transistors in the silicon. in the industry at large, the front end means the whole wafer fab, as against the back end where chips are packaged and tested. semianalysis judged in march 2026 that front-end capacity had overtaken packaging as the main bottleneck on ai chip output. but tsmc said in july 2026 that its packaging capacity still limited customers' growth.\">\n<dt>front end<span class=\"aka\">front end of line, FEOL, front-end, front-end wafers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The front end of line is the first half of making a chip, the steps that build the transistors in the silicon. In the industry at large, the front end means the whole wafer fab, as against the back end where chips are packaged and tested.</p><p class=\"why\">SemiAnalysis judged in March 2026 that front-end capacity had overtaken packaging as the main bottleneck on AI chip output. But TSMC said in July 2026 that its packaging capacity still limited customers' growth.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-gallium-and-germanium\" data-term=\"gallium and germanium\" data-text=\"gallium and germanium gallium, germanium, antimony gallium and germanium are metals used in electronics. gallium goes into compound chips such as radio parts, leds and lasers, and germanium into fiber optics, infrared optics, semiconductors and solar cells. both are recovered as byproducts, gallium from processing bauxite and germanium from certain zinc ores and coal. the us geological survey put china's share of world production of primary low-purity gallium at 99 percent in february 2026. china has required licenses to export both metals since august 2023. its december 2024 ban on exports of both to the united states is suspended until 27 november 2026.\">\n<dt>gallium and germanium<span class=\"aka\">gallium, germanium, antimony</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Gallium and germanium are metals used in electronics. Gallium goes into compound chips such as radio parts, LEDs and lasers, and germanium into fiber optics, infrared optics, semiconductors and solar cells. Both are recovered as byproducts, gallium from processing bauxite and germanium from certain zinc ores and coal.</p><p class=\"why\">The US Geological Survey put China's share of world production of primary low-purity gallium at 99 percent in February 2026. China has required licenses to export both metals since August 2023. Its December 2024 ban on exports of both to the United States is suspended until 27 November 2026.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-gate-all-around\" data-term=\"gate-all-around\" data-text=\"gate-all-around gaa, nanosheet transistor, ribbonfet at intel, nanosheet, nanosheets, ribbonfet, gaa transistor, gate-all-around transistors a transistor in which the gate, the electrode that switches the current, wraps all the way around the channel that current flows through. in a finfet, the design it replaces, the gate touches three sides. surrounding the channel gives the gate firmer control than a fin allows, so less current leaks when the switch is off. only tsmc, intel and samsung make it in volume. it needs etch that cuts sideways, which us export rules control. customers building 2 nm gate-all-around capacity lifted asm international, the leader in atomic layer deposition, to record revenue in 2025.\">\n<dt>gate-all-around<span class=\"aka\">GAA, nanosheet transistor, RibbonFET at Intel, nanosheet, nanosheets, RibbonFET, GAA transistor, gate-all-around transistors</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A transistor in which the gate, the electrode that switches the current, wraps all the way around the channel that current flows through. In a FinFET, the design it replaces, the gate touches three sides. Surrounding the channel gives the gate firmer control than a fin allows, so less current leaks when the switch is off.</p><p class=\"why\">Only TSMC, Intel and Samsung make it in volume. It needs etch that cuts sideways, which US export rules control. Customers building 2 nm gate-all-around capacity lifted ASM International, the leader in atomic layer deposition, to record revenue in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-gb-s\" data-term=\"gb/s\" data-text=\"gb/s tb/s, gb/s, tbps, gigabytes per second, terabytes per second, gigabits per second, terabits per second gb/s is gigabytes per second, the measure of how much data a link or a memory can move. tb/s is a thousand times more. a lowercase b, as in gb/s or tbps, counts bits, each an eighth of a byte. one hbm4 stack moves over 2 tb/s. nvlink 6 gives each gpu 3,600 gb/s, according to nvidia's january 2026 rubin launch. the october 2022 us rule caught chips with a processing score of 4,800 or more and an input and output rate of 600 gb/s or more (87 fr 62186). since january 2026, chips with total dram bandwidth below 6,500 gb/s and a processing score, or tpp, below 21,000 can be licensed case by case for china (91 fr 1684).\">\n<dt>GB/s<span class=\"aka\">TB/s, Gb/s, Tbps, gigabytes per second, terabytes per second, gigabits per second, terabits per second</span></dt>\n<dd><p>GB/s is gigabytes per second, the measure of how much data a link or a memory can move. TB/s is a thousand times more. A lowercase b, as in Gb/s or Tbps, counts bits, each an eighth of a byte. One HBM4 stack moves over 2 TB/s. NVLink 6 gives each GPU 3,600 GB/s, according to Nvidia's January 2026 Rubin launch.</p><p class=\"why\">The October 2022 US rule caught chips with a processing score of 4,800 or more and an input and output rate of 600 GB/s or more (87 FR 62186). Since January 2026, chips with total DRAM bandwidth below 6,500 GB/s and a processing score, or TPP, below 21,000 can be licensed case by case for China (91 FR 1684).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-glass-cloth\" data-term=\"glass cloth\" data-text=\"glass cloth t-glass, low-expansion glass, glass fiber cloth, low-expansion glass cloth glass cloth is a woven fabric of fine glass fibers that gives a substrate core or circuit board its stiffness. t-glass is a special grade that barely expands when heated, which helps keep a large package flat. nitto boseki of japan claims an overwhelming advantage in low-expansion glass cloth. it says demand seems to have risen about two to three times since its fiscal 2024 to 2027 plan was set.\">\n<dt>glass cloth<span class=\"aka\">T-glass, low-expansion glass, glass fiber cloth, low-expansion glass cloth</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Glass cloth is a woven fabric of fine glass fibers that gives a substrate core or circuit board its stiffness. T-glass is a special grade that barely expands when heated, which helps keep a large package flat.</p><p class=\"why\">Nitto Boseki of Japan claims an overwhelming advantage in low-expansion glass cloth. It says demand seems to have risen about two to three times since its fiscal 2024 to 2027 plan was set.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"substrates-and-pcbs/\">Read it in Substrates and PCBs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-gpu\" data-term=\"gpu\" data-text=\"gpu graphics processing unit, gpus a processor originally built to draw video game images by doing thousands of simple calculations at once. neural networks turned out to need the same kind of arithmetic, so the gpu became the default ai processor. nvidia used 60.3 percent of all cowos packaging in 2025, on epoch ai's estimate. the us required a license for nvidia's h20 in april 2025. since january 2026 it has reviewed applications to sell the h200 to buyers in china case by case.\">\n<dt>GPU<span class=\"aka\">graphics processing unit, GPUs</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A processor originally built to draw video game images by doing thousands of simple calculations at once. Neural networks turned out to need the same kind of arithmetic, so the GPU became the default AI processor.</p><p class=\"why\">Nvidia used 60.3 percent of all CoWoS packaging in 2025, on Epoch AI's estimate. The US required a license for Nvidia's H20 in April 2025. Since January 2026 it has reviewed applications to sell the H200 to buyers in China case by case.</p></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-gross-margin\" data-term=\"gross margin\" data-text=\"gross margin  the share of a sale left over after paying what it cost to make the thing, before research, sales and overheads are counted. a 70 percent gross margin means $70 of every $100 of revenue is left after manufacturing cost. gross margin shows which firms have pricing power. in quarters ending june to september 2026, micron's was 86.8 percent and nvidia's 75.0 percent. the assembly and test houses amkor and ase were at 16.8 to 27.3 percent, counting ase's packaging and test segment alone.\">\n<dt>gross margin</dt>\n<dd><p>The share of a sale left over after paying what it cost to make the thing, before research, sales and overheads are counted. A 70 percent gross margin means $70 of every $100 of revenue is left after manufacturing cost.</p><p class=\"why\">Gross margin shows which firms have pricing power. In quarters ending June to September 2026, Micron's was 86.8 percent and Nvidia's 75.0 percent. The assembly and test houses Amkor and ASE were at 16.8 to 27.3 percent, counting ASE's packaging and test segment alone.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"component-costs/\">Read it in The Economics of AI Chips →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-hbm\" data-term=\"hbm\" data-text=\"hbm high bandwidth memory, high-bandwidth memory, hbm3e, hbm4, hbm4e, hbm stack, hbm stacks, memory stacks, stacked memory stacked memory built for ai chips. up to sixteen memory chips are stacked into a cube and wired together through copper-filled holes made in each chip before stacking. the cube sits a few millimeters from the processor. it holds the model the chip is running, the numbers called weights, and hands them to the processor over 1,024 or more wires at once. to write each word of an answer, the chip reads the whole model from this memory, along with the record of the conversation so far. a larger model or a longer conversation needs more memory, so the size and speed of hbm usually set how many people one chip can serve. hbm is the largest line in the bill of materials of an nvidia b200. sk hynix, samsung and micron make nearly all of it.\">\n<dt>HBM<span class=\"aka\">high bandwidth memory, high-bandwidth memory, HBM3E, HBM4, HBM4E, HBM stack, HBM stacks, memory stacks, stacked memory</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Stacked memory built for AI chips. Up to sixteen memory chips are stacked into a cube and wired together through copper-filled holes made in each chip before stacking. The cube sits a few millimeters from the processor. It holds the model the chip is running, the numbers called weights, and hands them to the processor over 1,024 or more wires at once.</p><p class=\"why\">To write each word of an answer, the chip reads the whole model from this memory, along with the record of the conversation so far. A larger model or a longer conversation needs more memory, so the size and speed of HBM usually set how many people one chip can serve. HBM is the largest line in the bill of materials of an Nvidia B200. SK hynix, Samsung and Micron make nearly all of it.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-high-na-euv\" data-term=\"high-na euv\" data-text=\"high-na euv high numerical aperture extreme ultraviolet, asml exe series, high-na, high na, high-na scanners, high-na machine, high-na tools the next generation of extreme ultraviolet machine, whose larger mirrors collect light over a wider angle and so print smaller features. the wider optics also halve the area the machine can print in one exposure, so a large chip has to be stitched together from two exposures. it cuts the smallest printable feature from 13 nanometers to 8, and tsmc expects more ai chip layers to need it. each machine sells for an estimated $350 to $400 million. intel says it uses high-na in volume production for select layers of some 18a products. tsmc plans to use it in high-volume manufacturing from 2030.\">\n<dt>High-NA EUV<span class=\"aka\">high numerical aperture extreme ultraviolet, ASML EXE series, High-NA, High NA, High-NA scanners, High-NA machine, High-NA tools</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The next generation of extreme ultraviolet machine, whose larger mirrors collect light over a wider angle and so print smaller features. The wider optics also halve the area the machine can print in one exposure, so a large chip has to be stitched together from two exposures.</p><p class=\"why\">It cuts the smallest printable feature from 13 nanometers to 8, and TSMC expects more AI chip layers to need it. Each machine sells for an estimated $350 to $400 million. Intel says it uses High-NA in volume production for select layers of some 18A products. TSMC plans to use it in high-volume manufacturing from 2030.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-high-performance-computing\" data-term=\"high-performance computing\" data-text=\"high-performance computing hpc, hpc platform, high-performance computers high-performance computing is the industry's name for the heavy end of the market: supercomputers, ai accelerators and the server processors beside them. a foundry's hpc platform is the version of a node tuned for those chips. ai accelerators are part of this segment and need package substrates with more layers than earlier hpc chips. ajinomoto, which makes the insulating film between those layers, counts 11 layers of it on each side of the core in a 2026 ai package substrate, against nine on each side of an hpc substrate around 2023.\">\n<dt>high-performance computing<span class=\"aka\">HPC, HPC platform, high-performance computers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>High-performance computing is the industry's name for the heavy end of the market: supercomputers, AI accelerators and the server processors beside them. A foundry's HPC platform is the version of a node tuned for those chips.</p><p class=\"why\">AI accelerators are part of this segment and need package substrates with more layers than earlier HPC chips. Ajinomoto, which makes the insulating film between those layers, counts 11 layers of it on each side of the core in a 2026 AI package substrate, against nine on each side of an HPC substrate around 2023.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-high-volume-manufacturing\" data-term=\"high-volume manufacturing\" data-text=\"high-volume manufacturing hvm, volume production, mass production, high volume, in volume, production ramp high-volume manufacturing is the point where a new process or product stops being a trial and is made in volume for sale. output then climbs to full rate during the ramp. foundries announce the date a process reaches it, and before then the process makes only prototypes, as rapidus's 2 nm line did in 2025.\">\n<dt>high-volume manufacturing<span class=\"aka\">HVM, volume production, mass production, high volume, in volume, production ramp</span></dt>\n<dd><p>High-volume manufacturing is the point where a new process or product stops being a trial and is made in volume for sale. Output then climbs to full rate during the ramp.</p><p class=\"why\">Foundries announce the date a process reaches it, and before then the process makes only prototypes, as Rapidus's 2 nm line did in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-hybrid-bonding\" data-term=\"hybrid bonding\" data-text=\"hybrid bonding direct bond interconnect, soic, foveros direct, copper pad to copper pad joining two chips by bonding their copper pads, and the glass-like insulator around them, directly to each other, with no solder in between. removing the solder lets connections be packed much more tightly and shortens the path heat has to travel out. an sk hynix tech note puts microbumps about 20 micrometers apart and hybrid-bonded pads under 1 micrometer apart. it expects full-scale use in hbm at hbm4e or hbm5, where stacks are projected to pass twenty layers.\">\n<dt>hybrid bonding<span class=\"aka\">direct bond interconnect, SoIC, Foveros Direct, copper pad to copper pad</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Joining two chips by bonding their copper pads, and the glass-like insulator around them, directly to each other, with no solder in between. Removing the solder lets connections be packed much more tightly and shortens the path heat has to travel out.</p><p class=\"why\">An SK hynix tech note puts microbumps about 20 micrometers apart and hybrid-bonded pads under 1 micrometer apart. It expects full-scale use in HBM at HBM4E or HBM5, where stacks are projected to pass twenty layers.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-hydrogen-fluoride\" data-term=\"hydrogen fluoride\" data-text=\"hydrogen fluoride hydrofluoric acid, hf, ultra-high-purity hydrofluoric acid, high-purity hydrogen fluoride hydrogen fluoride is a gas that dissolves glass, and hydrofluoric acid is its solution in water. fabs use both to strip oxide layers and clean wafers between steps. like other cleaning chemicals, it is purified until metal impurities are down to parts per trillion. when japan put it under individual export licenses for south korea in 2019, japan's exports of it to south korea fell 87.9 percent. south korea bought more from the united states and taiwan and made more at home.\">\n<dt>hydrogen fluoride<span class=\"aka\">hydrofluoric acid, HF, ultra-high-purity hydrofluoric acid, high-purity hydrogen fluoride</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Hydrogen fluoride is a gas that dissolves glass, and hydrofluoric acid is its solution in water. Fabs use both to strip oxide layers and clean wafers between steps. Like other cleaning chemicals, it is purified until metal impurities are down to parts per trillion.</p><p class=\"why\">When Japan put it under individual export licenses for South Korea in 2019, Japan's exports of it to South Korea fell 87.9 percent. South Korea bought more from the United States and Taiwan and made more at home.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-hyperscaler\" data-term=\"hyperscaler\" data-text=\"hyperscaler hyperscalers one of the handful of companies that run data centers at global scale, such as amazon, microsoft, google, meta and oracle. they pay for the ai buildout. alphabet, amazon, meta, microsoft and oracle spent $448.2 billion of capital in 2025, the sum of epoch ai's quarterly figures.\">\n<dt>hyperscaler<span class=\"aka\">hyperscalers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>One of the handful of companies that run data centers at global scale, such as Amazon, Microsoft, Google, Meta and Oracle.</p><p class=\"why\">They pay for the AI buildout. Alphabet, Amazon, Meta, Microsoft and Oracle spent $448.2 billion of capital in 2025, the sum of Epoch AI's quarterly figures.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-i-line\" data-term=\"i-line\" data-text=\"i-line g-line, i-line steppers, i-line scanners i-line is the coarsest of the main lithography lights, 365 nanometers from a mercury lamp, named for one line in the lamp's spectrum. it prints the widest features on a chip and much of a package. smee, the established chinese scanner maker, is strongest in i-line, and even there it holds about 4 percent of the world market.\">\n<dt>i-line<span class=\"aka\">g-line, i-line steppers, i-line scanners</span></dt>\n<dd><p>i-line is the coarsest of the main lithography lights, 365 nanometers from a mercury lamp, named for one line in the lamp's spectrum. It prints the widest features on a chip and much of a package.</p><p class=\"why\">SMEE, the established Chinese scanner maker, is strongest in i-line, and even there it holds about 4 percent of the world market.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-idm\" data-term=\"idm\" data-text=\"idm integrated device manufacturer, integrated device maker, integrated device makers a chip company that both designs its products and manufactures them in its own factories. intel, samsung and micron are examples. an integrated maker that also makes chips for other companies competes with its own customers. its own products take the best capacity, so fewer customers trust it with a flagship design.\">\n<dt>IDM<span class=\"aka\">integrated device manufacturer, integrated device maker, integrated device makers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A chip company that both designs its products and manufactures them in its own factories. Intel, Samsung and Micron are examples.</p><p class=\"why\">An integrated maker that also makes chips for other companies competes with its own customers. Its own products take the best capacity, so fewer customers trust it with a flagship design.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-immersion-lithography\" data-term=\"immersion lithography\" data-text=\"immersion lithography immersion duv, arf immersion, immersion scanner, immersion scanners, immersion tools, immersion duv scanners, immersion deep-ultraviolet immersion lithography prints with a thin layer of ultrapure water between the scanner's lens and the wafer. the water lets the lens focus light at a wider angle than air allows, so the same light prints finer lines. it is the most advanced form of deep ultraviolet lithography, one step below extreme ultraviolet. dutch export licensing covers the most advanced immersion scanners. reuters reported in july 2026, citing one unnamed source, that a chinese state-owned firm had started producing its own immersion scanners.\">\n<dt>immersion lithography<span class=\"aka\">immersion DUV, ArF immersion, immersion scanner, immersion scanners, immersion tools, immersion DUV scanners, immersion deep-ultraviolet</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Immersion lithography prints with a thin layer of ultrapure water between the scanner's lens and the wafer. The water lets the lens focus light at a wider angle than air allows, so the same light prints finer lines. It is the most advanced form of deep ultraviolet lithography, one step below extreme ultraviolet.</p><p class=\"why\">Dutch export licensing covers the most advanced immersion scanners. Reuters reported in July 2026, citing one unnamed source, that a Chinese state-owned firm had started producing its own immersion scanners.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-in-country-transfer\" data-term=\"in-country transfer\" data-text=\"in-country transfer transfer (in-country) a change in the end use or the end user of an item inside one foreign country, defined at 15 cfr 734.16. nothing crosses a border. a server legally imported into a country for one customer is transferred when it is resold, or repurposed, for another. controls on in-country transfers catch hardware diverted after it has arrived. so a license granted for a named chinese customer does not cover the hardware if it passes to someone else. reexports and in-country transfers of advanced chips to macau or country group d:5 keep a presumption of denial, meaning a license will normally be refused (91 fr 1684). that holds even where an export from the united states would be reviewed case by case (91 fr 1684).\">\n<dt>in-country transfer<span class=\"aka\">transfer (in-country)</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A change in the end use or the end user of an item inside one foreign country, defined at 15 CFR 734.16. Nothing crosses a border. A server legally imported into a country for one customer is transferred when it is resold, or repurposed, for another.</p><p class=\"why\">Controls on in-country transfers catch hardware diverted after it has arrived. So a license granted for a named Chinese customer does not cover the hardware if it passes to someone else. Reexports and in-country transfers of advanced chips to Macau or Country Group D:5 keep a presumption of denial, meaning a license will normally be refused (91 FR 1684). That holds even where an export from the United States would be reviewed case by case (91 FR 1684).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-indium-phosphide\" data-term=\"indium phosphide\" data-text=\"indium phosphide inp, indium indium phosphide is a crystal grown from the metal indium and phosphorus. it gives off light when current passes through it, which silicon cannot do efficiently. the lasers inside the fastest optical modules are made of it. china produced about 70 percent of the world's indium in 2025. in february 2025 it put indium under new export restrictions and began requiring export permits for indium phosphide substrates. in march 2026 nvidia agreed to invest $2 billion each in coherent and lumentum, alongside purchase commitments for their lasers.\">\n<dt>indium phosphide<span class=\"aka\">InP, indium</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Indium phosphide is a crystal grown from the metal indium and phosphorus. It gives off light when current passes through it, which silicon cannot do efficiently. The lasers inside the fastest optical modules are made of it.</p><p class=\"why\">China produced about 70 percent of the world's indium in 2025. In February 2025 it put indium under new export restrictions and began requiring export permits for indium phosphide substrates. In March 2026 Nvidia agreed to invest $2 billion each in Coherent and Lumentum, alongside purchase commitments for their lasers.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-inference\" data-term=\"inference\" data-text=\"inference inference chip, inference chips, inference accelerator, inference accelerators, training and inference inference is running a finished ai model to answer requests, such as a prompt. training, a run of weeks on a cluster of accelerators, builds the model first. to write each word of an answer, the chip reads the whole model from memory, does a little arithmetic and waits for the next read. training reuses each number it fetches, so it fetches little and computes a lot. in inference, memory size and speed usually set how many people one chip can serve.\">\n<dt>inference<span class=\"aka\">inference chip, inference chips, inference accelerator, inference accelerators, training and inference</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Inference is running a finished AI model to answer requests, such as a prompt. Training, a run of weeks on a cluster of accelerators, builds the model first. To write each word of an answer, the chip reads the whole model from memory, does a little arithmetic and waits for the next read. Training reuses each number it fetches, so it fetches little and computes a lot.</p><p class=\"why\">In inference, memory size and speed usually set how many people one chip can serve.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-infiniband\" data-term=\"infiniband\" data-text=\"infiniband quantum-2, quantum-x800 infiniband is a networking standard long used in supercomputers, with low delay and no dropped packets. ai clusters relied on it to link thousands of servers before ethernet caught up, and nvidia still sells both. the choice between infiniband and ethernet decides who sells the switch chips. broadcom has doubled the bandwidth of its ethernet switch chips with each generation since 2019.\">\n<dt>InfiniBand<span class=\"aka\">Quantum-2, Quantum-X800</span></dt>\n<dd><p>InfiniBand is a networking standard long used in supercomputers, with low delay and no dropped packets. AI clusters relied on it to link thousands of servers before Ethernet caught up, and Nvidia still sells both.</p><p class=\"why\">The choice between InfiniBand and Ethernet decides who sells the switch chips. Broadcom has doubled the bandwidth of its Ethernet switch chips with each generation since 2019.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-interposer\" data-term=\"interposer\" data-text=\"interposer interposers, silicon interposer, silicon carrier a layer of wiring with no transistors, used as a miniature circuit board underneath several chips so they can be connected at a density no ordinary board could reach. it is either one piece of silicon or layers of fine copper wiring, often with small silicon bridges. hbm connects over 1,024 or 2,048 wires, too many for a resin board, so memory and logic sit together on an interposer. its area caps how much fits in one package. in april 2026 tsmc was producing cowos at 5.5 times the reticle, the largest area a lithography machine prints in one exposure.\">\n<dt>interposer<span class=\"aka\">interposers, silicon interposer, silicon carrier</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A layer of wiring with no transistors, used as a miniature circuit board underneath several chips so they can be connected at a density no ordinary board could reach. It is either one piece of silicon or layers of fine copper wiring, often with small silicon bridges.</p><p class=\"why\">HBM connects over 1,024 or 2,048 wires, too many for a resin board, so memory and logic sit together on an interposer. Its area caps how much fits in one package. In April 2026 TSMC was producing CoWoS at 5.5 times the reticle, the largest area a lithography machine prints in one exposure.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ion-implantation\" data-term=\"ion implantation\" data-text=\"ion implantation ion implanter, ion implanters, implant, implant layers, implantation a way of changing how silicon conducts by firing atoms into it. an ion implanter shoots charged atoms of boron, phosphorus or arsenic into the wafer, where they lodge just under the surface. the patches they land in then conduct the way the design needs. every modern chip process relies on it. implanters are export-controlled. in february 2026 applied materials agreed to pay a penalty of about $252 million over implanters shipped to a chinese customer on the entity list.\">\n<dt>ion implantation<span class=\"aka\">ion implanter, ion implanters, implant, implant layers, implantation</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A way of changing how silicon conducts by firing atoms into it. An ion implanter shoots charged atoms of boron, phosphorus or arsenic into the wafer, where they lodge just under the surface. The patches they land in then conduct the way the design needs.</p><p class=\"why\">Every modern chip process relies on it. Implanters are export-controlled. In February 2026 Applied Materials agreed to pay a penalty of about $252 million over implanters shipped to a Chinese customer on the Entity List.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ip\" data-term=\"ip\" data-text=\"ip silicon ip, ip blocks, licensed blocks, licensed circuit blocks, semiconductor ip, ip catalog, intellectual property in chip design, ip, short for intellectual property, means a ready-made block of circuitry, such as a processor core or a memory interface, that a design house licenses. arm sells processor ip, and other firms sell the blocks that talk to memory, pcie or another chiplet. each licensed block must be proven on a new process before a chip can use it. the memory interface is a demanding one, because it has to hold its timing across thousands of solder bumps into a stacked memory die.\">\n<dt>IP<span class=\"aka\">silicon IP, IP blocks, licensed blocks, licensed circuit blocks, semiconductor IP, IP catalog, intellectual property</span></dt>\n<dd><p>In chip design, IP, short for intellectual property, means a ready-made block of circuitry, such as a processor core or a memory interface, that a design house licenses. Arm sells processor IP, and other firms sell the blocks that talk to memory, PCIe or another chiplet.</p><p class=\"why\">Each licensed block must be proven on a new process before a chip can use it. The memory interface is a demanding one, because it has to hold its timing across thousands of solder bumps into a stacked memory die.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-is-informed-letter\" data-term=\"is-informed letter\" data-text=\"is-informed letter is informed letter, is-informed letters, by letter a letter from bis to one named company imposing a license requirement on a specific export, without any rule being published. bis's power to send one is written into the regulations themselves, for example 15 cfr 744.23(b), which lets bis inform a person individually, with no amendment to the ear. it imposes a control at once, with no published rule. bis imposed the april 2025 license requirement for nvidia's h20 this way, and the public learned of it from nvidia's own filing.\">\n<dt>is-informed letter<span class=\"aka\">is informed letter, is-informed letters, by letter</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A letter from BIS to one named company imposing a license requirement on a specific export, without any rule being published. BIS's power to send one is written into the regulations themselves, for example 15 CFR 744.23(b), which lets BIS inform a person individually, with no amendment to the EAR.</p><p class=\"why\">It imposes a control at once, with no published rule. BIS imposed the April 2025 license requirement for Nvidia's H20 this way, and the public learned of it from Nvidia's own filing.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-jedec\" data-term=\"jedec\" data-text=\"jedec jesd270-4, jedec standard jedec is the industry body that writes the standards for memory chips, so that a memory stack from any maker fits any processor built to the same specification. its hbm4 standard, published in april 2025, sets the width and speed of the interface. makers now ship hbm4 faster than the standard's 8 gb/s per pin. samsung's runs at 11.7, sk hynix's above 10 and micron's above 11. each customer runs its own qualification tests, so meeting the standard does not by itself win an order.\">\n<dt>JEDEC<span class=\"aka\">JESD270-4, JEDEC standard</span></dt>\n<dd><p>JEDEC is the industry body that writes the standards for memory chips, so that a memory stack from any maker fits any processor built to the same specification. Its HBM4 standard, published in April 2025, sets the width and speed of the interface.</p><p class=\"why\">Makers now ship HBM4 faster than the standard's 8 Gb/s per pin. Samsung's runs at 11.7, SK hynix's above 10 and Micron's above 11. Each customer runs its own qualification tests, so meeting the standard does not by itself win an order.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-kilowatt\" data-term=\"kilowatt\" data-text=\"kilowatt kw, kilowatts, megawatt, mw, megawatts, gigawatt, gw, gigawatts a kilowatt is a thousand watts. a megawatt is a thousand kilowatts, and a gigawatt a thousand megawatts, about the output of one large power station. a gb300 nvl72 rack draws up to 142 kilowatts. the largest data center campuses are planned in gigawatts. ai deals are now counted in gigawatts too, as when openai and broadcom announced 10 gigawatts of accelerators. power equipment now arrives more slowly than the chips.\">\n<dt>kilowatt<span class=\"aka\">kW, kilowatts, megawatt, MW, megawatts, gigawatt, GW, gigawatts</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A kilowatt is a thousand watts. A megawatt is a thousand kilowatts, and a gigawatt a thousand megawatts, about the output of one large power station. A GB300 NVL72 rack draws up to 142 kilowatts. The largest data center campuses are planned in gigawatts.</p><p class=\"why\">AI deals are now counted in gigawatts too, as when OpenAI and Broadcom announced 10 gigawatts of accelerators. Power equipment now arrives more slowly than the chips.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-known-good-die\" data-term=\"known-good die\" data-text=\"known-good die kgd, good die, good dies, known good die a bare chip tested thoroughly enough, before assembly, to be trusted inside something expensive. in an ordinary product a faulty chip wastes one chip. inside a package that joins a dozen expensive pieces, one bad die throws away all of them. as packages grow toward about ten large compute dies and 20 memory stacks, a bad die found only after assembly scraps more parts. so chipmakers move testing and burn-in, running chips hot to force early failures, back onto the wafer.\">\n<dt>known-good die<span class=\"aka\">KGD, good die, good dies, known good die</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A bare chip tested thoroughly enough, before assembly, to be trusted inside something expensive. In an ordinary product a faulty chip wastes one chip. Inside a package that joins a dozen expensive pieces, one bad die throws away all of them.</p><p class=\"why\">As packages grow toward about ten large compute dies and 20 memory stacks, a bad die found only after assembly scraps more parts. So chipmakers move testing and burn-in, running chips hot to force early failures, back onto the wafer.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-krf\" data-term=\"krf\" data-text=\"krf krypton fluoride, krypton fluoride laser, 248 nm, 248-nanometer krf is krypton fluoride, the gas in an older lithography laser that shines at 248 nanometers. krf scanners print the coarser layers of a chip, where lines are far apart. krf tools print coarser layers such as implant layers. asml sold 78 of them in 2025, and canon also makes them.\">\n<dt>KrF<span class=\"aka\">krypton fluoride, krypton fluoride laser, 248 nm, 248-nanometer</span></dt>\n<dd><p>KrF is krypton fluoride, the gas in an older lithography laser that shines at 248 nanometers. KrF scanners print the coarser layers of a chip, where lines are far apart.</p><p class=\"why\">KrF tools print coarser layers such as implant layers. ASML sold 78 of them in 2025, and Canon also makes them.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-laminate\" data-term=\"laminate\" data-text=\"laminate laminates, copper-clad laminate, copper-clad laminates, low-loss laminate, core laminate a laminate is a stiff sheet made by pressing glass cloth and resin together, usually with copper foil bonded to its faces. it is the material a circuit board or a substrate core is cut from. a low-loss laminate absorbs little of the signal passing through the wires on it. how much signal the laminate absorbs has become a main design limit on the boards that link gpus.\">\n<dt>laminate<span class=\"aka\">laminates, copper-clad laminate, copper-clad laminates, low-loss laminate, core laminate</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A laminate is a stiff sheet made by pressing glass cloth and resin together, usually with copper foil bonded to its faces. It is the material a circuit board or a substrate core is cut from. A low-loss laminate absorbs little of the signal passing through the wires on it.</p><p class=\"why\">How much signal the laminate absorbs has become a main design limit on the boards that link GPUs.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"substrates-and-pcbs/\">Read it in Substrates and PCBs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-large-power-transformer\" data-term=\"large power transformer\" data-text=\"large power transformer large power transformers, transformer, transformers, switchgear, substation a large power transformer is a machine that changes grid electricity from one voltage to another, for example from transmission voltage down to a level a data center can use. switchgear is the heavy switching and protection equipment around it. together they make up the substation at the gate of the campus. in 2024 lead times of 36 months were commonly quoted, against under a year before the pandemic. of the units put into us service in 2019, 82 percent were imported.\">\n<dt>large power transformer<span class=\"aka\">large power transformers, transformer, transformers, switchgear, substation</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A large power transformer is a machine that changes grid electricity from one voltage to another, for example from transmission voltage down to a level a data center can use. Switchgear is the heavy switching and protection equipment around it. Together they make up the substation at the gate of the campus.</p><p class=\"why\">In 2024 lead times of 36 months were commonly quoted, against under a year before the pandemic. Of the units put into US service in 2019, 82 percent were imported.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-lead-time\" data-term=\"lead time\" data-text=\"lead time lead times, delivery time lead time is the wait between placing an order and receiving it. a wafer clears a leading-edge fab in months, while in 2024 a large power transformer commonly took three years. chip supply and power equipment are both constrained. micron said in its report for the quarter to may 2026 that ai-driven memory and storage growth was outpacing industry supply. waits for large power equipment run to years.\">\n<dt>lead time<span class=\"aka\">lead times, delivery time</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Lead time is the wait between placing an order and receiving it. A wafer clears a leading-edge fab in months, while in 2024 a large power transformer commonly took three years.</p><p class=\"why\">Chip supply and power equipment are both constrained. Micron said in its report for the quarter to May 2026 that AI-driven memory and storage growth was outpacing industry supply. Waits for large power equipment run to years.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-leading-edge\" data-term=\"leading edge\" data-text=\"leading edge leading-edge, at the leading edge, advanced node, advanced nodes, advanced-node the leading edge is the newest generation of chipmaking process in volume production. in 2026 that means the 3 nm and 2 nm nodes, made only by tsmc, samsung and intel. a leading-edge chip is one built on it. gate-all-around transistors are the design used at 2 nm, and only tsmc, intel and samsung make them in volume. in 2024 the united states put a worldwide license requirement on the technology for building them.\">\n<dt>leading edge<span class=\"aka\">leading-edge, at the leading edge, advanced node, advanced nodes, advanced-node</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The leading edge is the newest generation of chipmaking process in volume production. In 2026 that means the 3 nm and 2 nm nodes, made only by TSMC, Samsung and Intel. A leading-edge chip is one built on it.</p><p class=\"why\">Gate-all-around transistors are the design used at 2 nm, and only TSMC, Intel and Samsung make them in volume. In 2024 the United States put a worldwide license requirement on the technology for building them.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-license-exception\" data-term=\"license exception\" data-text=\"license exception license exception a written carve-out in export rules that lets a shipment go without an individual license, if it meets stated conditions. the ones that matter for ai chips and chipmaking tools are nac and aca (15 cfr 740.8), hbm (740.25), aia and lpp (740.27 and 740.29), iec (740.24) and rpl (740.10). aia and lpp let the top band of accelerators ship to allies, and elsewhere in small volumes. iec covers countries that adopt matching controls, and rpl covers servicing and spare parts. exceptions let the us government adjust its controls without rewriting them and ease the rules for allies. license exception iec, added in september 2024, covers exports to and by countries that have put equivalent controls in place (89 fr 72926).\">\n<dt>license exception<span class=\"aka\">license exception</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A written carve-out in export rules that lets a shipment go without an individual license, if it meets stated conditions. The ones that matter for AI chips and chipmaking tools are NAC and ACA (15 CFR 740.8), HBM (740.25), AIA and LPP (740.27 and 740.29), IEC (740.24) and RPL (740.10). AIA and LPP let the top band of accelerators ship to allies, and elsewhere in small volumes. IEC covers countries that adopt matching controls, and RPL covers servicing and spare parts.</p><p class=\"why\">Exceptions let the US government adjust its controls without rewriting them and ease the rules for allies. License Exception IEC, added in September 2024, covers exports to and by countries that have put equivalent controls in place (89 FR 72926).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-license-exception-aca\" data-term=\"license exception aca\" data-text=\"license exception aca aca, advanced computing authorized an export rule that lets ai chips other than top-band data center chips ship to most of the world with no license and no advance notice. it covers the same chips as its companion exception nac, and every destination except macau, country group d:5 and firms headquartered in either. the top-band data center chips in eccn 3a090.a are excluded. bis split it from nac at 15 cfr 740.8 in april 2024. the ai diffusion rule widened it in january 2025 to the whole world outside macau and d:5. it lets these chips reach most of the world with no license or advance notice. nac keeps a notice requirement for macau and d:5. before april 2024 nac did both jobs, so an older table that shows one exception describes what is now two.\">\n<dt>License Exception ACA<span class=\"aka\">ACA, Advanced Computing Authorized</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An export rule that lets AI chips other than top-band data center chips ship to most of the world with no license and no advance notice. It covers the same chips as its companion exception NAC, and every destination except Macau, Country Group D:5 and firms headquartered in either. The top-band data center chips in ECCN 3A090.a are excluded. BIS split it from NAC at 15 CFR 740.8 in April 2024. The AI Diffusion rule widened it in January 2025 to the whole world outside Macau and D:5.</p><p class=\"why\">It lets these chips reach most of the world with no license or advance notice. NAC keeps a notice requirement for Macau and D:5. Before April 2024 NAC did both jobs, so an older table that shows one exception describes what is now two.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-license-exception-acm\" data-term=\"license exception acm\" data-text=\"license exception acm acm, advanced compute manufacturing license exception acm, for advanced compute manufacturing, lets controlled ai chips and related items go without a license to private-sector firms that develop, make or store them. the items must be bound for customers outside macau and country group d:5. it was created alongside license exceptions aia and lpp. it keeps the ai diffusion rule's worldwide license requirement from catching chips that are only passing through factories and warehouses on their way to an eligible customer.\">\n<dt>License Exception ACM<span class=\"aka\">ACM, Advanced Compute Manufacturing</span></dt>\n<dd><p>License Exception ACM, for Advanced Compute Manufacturing, lets controlled AI chips and related items go without a license to private-sector firms that develop, make or store them. The items must be bound for customers outside Macau and Country Group D:5. It was created alongside License Exceptions AIA and LPP.</p><p class=\"why\">It keeps the AI Diffusion rule's worldwide license requirement from catching chips that are only passing through factories and warehouses on their way to an eligible customer.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-license-exception-aia\" data-term=\"license exception aia\" data-text=\"license exception aia aia, artificial intelligence authorization license exception aia, for artificial intelligence authorization, lets the top band of ai chips ship without a license to nineteen destinations. they are listed in supplement no. 5 to part 740, and the united states is among them. the ai diffusion rule created it in january 2025 as the exception inside a worldwide license requirement. bis said in may 2025 that it would not enforce the ai diffusion rule. but the rule was never repealed, so aia still stands in the regulations. bis says it enforces the worldwide requirement only for country groups d:1, d:4 and d:5 and for firms headquartered in d:5 or macau.\">\n<dt>License Exception AIA<span class=\"aka\">AIA, Artificial Intelligence Authorization</span></dt>\n<dd><p>License Exception AIA, for Artificial Intelligence Authorization, lets the top band of AI chips ship without a license to nineteen destinations. They are listed in supplement no. 5 to part 740, and the United States is among them. The AI Diffusion rule created it in January 2025 as the exception inside a worldwide license requirement.</p><p class=\"why\">BIS said in May 2025 that it would not enforce the AI Diffusion rule. But the rule was never repealed, so AIA still stands in the regulations. BIS says it enforces the worldwide requirement only for Country Groups D:1, D:4 and D:5 and for firms headquartered in D:5 or Macau.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-license-exception-hbm\" data-term=\"license exception hbm\" data-text=\"license exception hbm  an export rule that lets high bandwidth memory go to a packaging site with no license, to be packaged beside a chip. it applies if the memory's bandwidth density is below 3.3 gb/s per square millimeter, measured over the area of the package or stack. the exporter must be headquartered in the united states or country group a:5. if the memory is bound for macau or country group d:5, the chip's designer must buy it. the stacks must go straight to the packaging site. it does not cover packaging at a facility in macau or d:5 that also makes advanced-node chips. it sits at 15 cfr 740.25. it lets chinese packaging houses stay in the supply chain of american and allied chip designers. but a sale of the same stacks to a chinese buyer still needs a license. hbm needs a license only for macau and country group d:5, and the exception was written into the december 2024 rule that first controlled hbm (89 fr 96790).\">\n<dt>License Exception HBM</dt>\n<dd><p>An export rule that lets high bandwidth memory go to a packaging site with no license, to be packaged beside a chip. It applies if the memory's bandwidth density is below 3.3 GB/s per square millimeter, measured over the area of the package or stack. The exporter must be headquartered in the United States or Country Group A:5. If the memory is bound for Macau or Country Group D:5, the chip's designer must buy it. The stacks must go straight to the packaging site. It does not cover packaging at a facility in Macau or D:5 that also makes advanced-node chips. It sits at 15 CFR 740.25.</p><p class=\"why\">It lets Chinese packaging houses stay in the supply chain of American and allied chip designers. But a sale of the same stacks to a Chinese buyer still needs a license. HBM needs a license only for Macau and Country Group D:5, and the exception was written into the December 2024 rule that first controlled HBM (89 FR 96790).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-license-exception-lpp\" data-term=\"license exception lpp\" data-text=\"license exception lpp lpp, low processing performance an export rule that lets a buyer almost anywhere receive a capped amount of top-band ai chips each year without a license. the cap is 26,900,000 tpp, the export rules' measure of computing power, per ultimate consignee per calendar year. macau, country group d:5 and firms headquartered in either are excluded, and it does not cover transfers within a country. the ai diffusion rule created it in january 2025, at 15 cfr 740.29. it lets buyers outside the nineteen destinations in supplement no. 5 to part 740 take top ai chips in small amounts with no license application. bis said in may 2025 that it would not enforce the ai diffusion rule, but it withdrew none of the text. so lpp still stands in the regulations beside the rule's other exceptions, aia and acm, and the nineteen-destination list.\">\n<dt>License Exception LPP<span class=\"aka\">LPP, Low Processing Performance</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An export rule that lets a buyer almost anywhere receive a capped amount of top-band AI chips each year without a license. The cap is 26,900,000 TPP, the export rules' measure of computing power, per ultimate consignee per calendar year. Macau, Country Group D:5 and firms headquartered in either are excluded, and it does not cover transfers within a country. The AI Diffusion rule created it in January 2025, at 15 CFR 740.29.</p><p class=\"why\">It lets buyers outside the nineteen destinations in supplement no. 5 to part 740 take top AI chips in small amounts with no license application. BIS said in May 2025 that it would not enforce the AI Diffusion rule, but it withdrew none of the text. So LPP still stands in the regulations beside the rule's other exceptions, AIA and ACM, and the nineteen-destination list.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-license-exception-nac\" data-term=\"license exception nac\" data-text=\"license exception nac nac, notified advanced computing an export rule that lets ai chips other than top-band data center chips ship to macau and country group d:5, and to firms headquartered there, with no license. the exporter must notify bis at least 25 calendar days ahead, and the shipment can go if bis does not say a license is needed. the top-band data center chips in eccn 3a090.a and the memory in 3a090.c are excluded. it sits at 15 cfr 740.8. it lets these chips reach the restricted destinations without a license application. since april 2024 section 740.8 has held two exceptions, nac for the restricted destinations and aca for everywhere else.\">\n<dt>License Exception NAC<span class=\"aka\">NAC, Notified Advanced Computing</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An export rule that lets AI chips other than top-band data center chips ship to Macau and Country Group D:5, and to firms headquartered there, with no license. The exporter must notify BIS at least 25 calendar days ahead, and the shipment can go if BIS does not say a license is needed. The top-band data center chips in ECCN 3A090.a and the memory in 3A090.c are excluded. It sits at 15 CFR 740.8.</p><p class=\"why\">It lets these chips reach the restricted destinations without a license application. Since April 2024 section 740.8 has held two exceptions, NAC for the restricted destinations and ACA for everywhere else.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-liquid-cooling\" data-term=\"liquid cooling\" data-text=\"liquid cooling direct-to-chip cooling, cold plate cooling, cold plate, cold plates, liquid-cooled, direct-to-chip liquid, direct liquid cooling taking heat out of a processor by pumping liquid through a cold plate on the chip package, instead of blowing air across a finned heatsink. a building loop then carries the heat outdoors. nvidia's gb300 nvl72 rack is liquid cooled, and its rubin platform is entirely liquid cooled. nvidia says every cloud provider and data center operator building for rubin is moving to liquid cooling.\">\n<dt>liquid cooling<span class=\"aka\">direct-to-chip cooling, cold plate cooling, cold plate, cold plates, liquid-cooled, direct-to-chip liquid, direct liquid cooling</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Taking heat out of a processor by pumping liquid through a cold plate on the chip package, instead of blowing air across a finned heatsink. A building loop then carries the heat outdoors.</p><p class=\"why\">Nvidia's GB300 NVL72 rack is liquid cooled, and its Rubin platform is entirely liquid cooled. Nvidia says every cloud provider and data center operator building for Rubin is moving to liquid cooling.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-lithography\" data-term=\"lithography\" data-text=\"lithography photolithography printing a circuit pattern onto a wafer by shining light through a patterned plate and projecting a shrunken image of it onto a light-sensitive coating. it works like photography at the scale of nanometers, repeated once for every layer of the chip. only one company, asml, makes the machines for its finest layers, and those layers set how densely transistors and wires pack.\">\n<dt>lithography<span class=\"aka\">photolithography</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Printing a circuit pattern onto a wafer by shining light through a patterned plate and projecting a shrunken image of it onto a light-sensitive coating. It works like photography at the scale of nanometers, repeated once for every layer of the chip.</p><p class=\"why\">Only one company, ASML, makes the machines for its finest layers, and those layers set how densely transistors and wires pack.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-logic-chip\" data-term=\"logic chip\" data-text=\"logic chip logic chips, logic die, logic dies a logic chip is one that computes, such as a processor, a graphics processor or an ai accelerator. memory chips, such as dram and nand flash, store data instead. us export rules set separate lines for logic and memory. the october 2022 rule covered equipment for fabs in china making logic chips at 16/14 nm or below. it also covered fabs making dram at 18 nm half-pitch or below, or nand with 128 or more layers. asml's 2025 system sales were €16,054.1 million to logic chipmakers and €8,420.2 million to memory makers.\">\n<dt>logic chip<span class=\"aka\">logic chips, logic die, logic dies</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A logic chip is one that computes, such as a processor, a graphics processor or an AI accelerator. Memory chips, such as DRAM and NAND flash, store data instead.</p><p class=\"why\">US export rules set separate lines for logic and memory. The October 2022 rule covered equipment for fabs in China making logic chips at 16/14 nm or below. It also covered fabs making DRAM at 18 nm half-pitch or below, or NAND with 128 or more layers. ASML's 2025 system sales were €16,054.1 million to logic chipmakers and €8,420.2 million to memory makers.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-lot\" data-term=\"lot\" data-text=\"lot lots, wafer lot, wafer lots, per lot a lot is the batch of wafers a fab moves through its machines together, usually 25 in one sealed carrier. recipes, inspections and yield are tracked lot by lot. a fab decides how many wafers in each lot it can afford to inspect. that choice sets how much it spends on process control, the measuring that keeps each step on target.\">\n<dt>lot<span class=\"aka\">lots, wafer lot, wafer lots, per lot</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A lot is the batch of wafers a fab moves through its machines together, usually 25 in one sealed carrier. Recipes, inspections and yield are tracked lot by lot.</p><p class=\"why\">A fab decides how many wafers in each lot it can afford to inspect. That choice sets how much it spends on process control, the measuring that keeps each step on target.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"metrology-and-inspection/\">Read it in Metrology and Inspection →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-macau\" data-term=\"macau\" data-text=\"macau macao, china or macau, china and macau macau is a chinese city with its own customs territory, like hong kong, so goods can enter it under separate rules. us export controls name china and macau together to close that route, and treat a firm headquartered in either the same way. under the us rules on advanced ai chips, a chip that needs a license for china needs one for macau too.\">\n<dt>Macau<span class=\"aka\">Macao, China or Macau, China and Macau</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Macau is a Chinese city with its own customs territory, like Hong Kong, so goods can enter it under separate rules. US export controls name China and Macau together to close that route, and treat a firm headquartered in either the same way.</p><p class=\"why\">Under the US rules on advanced AI chips, a chip that needs a license for China needs one for Macau too.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-mask-blank\" data-term=\"mask blank\" data-text=\"mask blank mask blanks, euv blank, euv blanks, photomask blank, photomask blanks, blank plate, duv blanks a mask blank is a photomask before any pattern is on it. it is a six-inch square of very flat glass carrying the film that the pattern will be cut into. for extreme ultraviolet that film sits on a mirror of about forty pairs of ultrathin layers, and a particle buried in the mirror cannot be repaired. the japanese glassmaker agc says only three firms supply euv blanks, and agc and hoya, both japanese, are two of them. agc spent more than a decade meeting the blank's requirements before it began mass production in 2017.\">\n<dt>mask blank<span class=\"aka\">mask blanks, EUV blank, EUV blanks, photomask blank, photomask blanks, blank plate, DUV blanks</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A mask blank is a photomask before any pattern is on it. It is a six-inch square of very flat glass carrying the film that the pattern will be cut into. For extreme ultraviolet that film sits on a mirror of about forty pairs of ultrathin layers, and a particle buried in the mirror cannot be repaired.</p><p class=\"why\">The Japanese glassmaker AGC says only three firms supply EUV blanks, and AGC and Hoya, both Japanese, are two of them. AGC spent more than a decade meeting the blank's requirements before it began mass production in 2017.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"photomasks-and-pellicles/\">Read it in Photomasks and Pellicles →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-mask-shop\" data-term=\"mask shop\" data-text=\"mask shop mask shops, mask making, mask maker, mask makers a mask shop is the factory that turns a finished chip design into its set of photomasks. it writes each plate with an electron beam, inspects it and repairs it. no chip can be printed until its masks are made. chipmakers such as tsmc and smic run shops of their own, and independents such as photronics sell to them and to others.\">\n<dt>mask shop<span class=\"aka\">mask shops, mask making, mask maker, mask makers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A mask shop is the factory that turns a finished chip design into its set of photomasks. It writes each plate with an electron beam, inspects it and repairs it.</p><p class=\"why\">No chip can be printed until its masks are made. Chipmakers such as TSMC and SMIC run shops of their own, and independents such as Photronics sell to them and to others.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"photomasks-and-pellicles/\">Read it in Photomasks and Pellicles →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-mask-writer\" data-term=\"mask writer\" data-text=\"mask writer mask writers, multi-beam writer, multi-beam writers, electron-beam writer, e-beam writer, mask writing a mask writer is the machine that uses electrons to draw a chip's pattern into the resist on a photomask blank. a single-beam writer flashes one shape at a time, while nuflare's multi-beam writer for the most advanced masks controls 260,000 beams at once. no new chip can be printed until its masks are written. in 2023 intel said advanced euv requires multi-beam mask writers and called austria's ims nanofabrication the established leader in them. counting all electron-beam mask writers, cset put ims at 46.6 percent of 2025 sales and japan's nuflare at 39.2 percent.\">\n<dt>mask writer<span class=\"aka\">mask writers, multi-beam writer, multi-beam writers, electron-beam writer, e-beam writer, mask writing</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A mask writer is the machine that uses electrons to draw a chip's pattern into the resist on a photomask blank. A single-beam writer flashes one shape at a time, while NuFlare's multi-beam writer for the most advanced masks controls 260,000 beams at once.</p><p class=\"why\">No new chip can be printed until its masks are written. In 2023 Intel said advanced EUV requires multi-beam mask writers and called Austria's IMS Nanofabrication the established leader in them. Counting all electron-beam mask writers, CSET put IMS at 46.6 percent of 2025 sales and Japan's NuFlare at 39.2 percent.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"photomasks-and-pellicles/\">Read it in Photomasks and Pellicles →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-mature-node\" data-term=\"mature node\" data-text=\"mature node mature nodes, mature-node, mature logic, older nodes, older lines, trailing edge a mature node is an older chipmaking process, 28 nm and above, that has run for years and competes on price. most of the world's wafers come off these lines, making power chips, analog parts and microcontrollers. china held 33 percent of the world's logic capacity at 28 nm and above in 2022. in the five years before may 2024, chinese companies invested $63 billion in 73 fabs, mostly for chips above 28 nm, sia and bcg reported.\">\n<dt>mature node<span class=\"aka\">mature nodes, mature-node, mature logic, older nodes, older lines, trailing edge</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A mature node is an older chipmaking process, 28 nm and above, that has run for years and competes on price. Most of the world's wafers come off these lines, making power chips, analog parts and microcontrollers.</p><p class=\"why\">China held 33 percent of the world's logic capacity at 28 nm and above in 2022. In the five years before May 2024, Chinese companies invested $63 billion in 73 fabs, mostly for chips above 28 nm, SIA and BCG reported.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-memory-bandwidth-density\" data-term=\"memory bandwidth density\" data-text=\"memory bandwidth density bandwidth density, bandwidth-density memory bandwidth density is how much data a memory stack can move each second divided by the area of its package or stack, in gigabytes per second per square millimeter. the december 2024 rule controls any stack above 2, and bis said every hbm stack then in production exceeded that. one threshold catches every hbm stack in production, including stacks made outside the united states, so the control reaches all three makers, sk hynix, samsung and micron. a license exception still lets stacks below 3.3 go straight to a chip designer's packaging site. hbm already packaged with a processor falls under the chip rules instead.\">\n<dt>memory bandwidth density<span class=\"aka\">bandwidth density, bandwidth-density</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Memory bandwidth density is how much data a memory stack can move each second divided by the area of its package or stack, in gigabytes per second per square millimeter. The December 2024 rule controls any stack above 2, and BIS said every HBM stack then in production exceeded that.</p><p class=\"why\">One threshold catches every HBM stack in production, including stacks made outside the United States, so the control reaches all three makers, SK hynix, Samsung and Micron. A license exception still lets stacks below 3.3 go straight to a chip designer's packaging site. HBM already packaged with a processor falls under the chip rules instead.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-memory-wall\" data-term=\"memory wall\" data-text=\"memory wall  the widening gap between how fast a processor can calculate and how fast memory can feed it numbers to work on. the cost of arithmetic has fallen faster than the cost of moving numbers. an ai chip reads its whole model from memory for each word it writes, so memory size and speed usually set how many people one chip can serve. memory is also about half the cost of building an nvidia b200, on epoch ai's estimate.\">\n<dt>memory wall</dt>\n<dd><p>The widening gap between how fast a processor can calculate and how fast memory can feed it numbers to work on. The cost of arithmetic has fallen faster than the cost of moving numbers.</p><p class=\"why\">An AI chip reads its whole model from memory for each word it writes, so memory size and speed usually set how many people one chip can serve. Memory is also about half the cost of building an Nvidia B200, on Epoch AI's estimate.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-metal-oxide-resist\" data-term=\"metal-oxide resist\" data-text=\"metal-oxide resist metal-oxide resists, metal oxide resist, tin-oxide resist, metal-oxide euv photoresist a metal-oxide resist is a photoresist built on clusters with a tin-oxide core. it absorbs more extreme ultraviolet light than a chemically amplified resist. that helps because an euv dose arrives as relatively few photons. resist makers aim it at high-na tools and the tightest pitches. the japanese resist maker jsr agreed in 2021 to buy inpria, an oregon maker of these resists. in 2024 a company owned by a japanese state-backed fund took 84.36 percent of jsr.\">\n<dt>metal-oxide resist<span class=\"aka\">metal-oxide resists, metal oxide resist, tin-oxide resist, metal-oxide EUV photoresist</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A metal-oxide resist is a photoresist built on clusters with a tin-oxide core. It absorbs more extreme ultraviolet light than a chemically amplified resist. That helps because an EUV dose arrives as relatively few photons.</p><p class=\"why\">Resist makers aim it at High-NA tools and the tightest pitches. The Japanese resist maker JSR agreed in 2021 to buy Inpria, an Oregon maker of these resists. In 2024 a company owned by a Japanese state-backed fund took 84.36 percent of JSR.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-meti\" data-term=\"meti\" data-text=\"meti ministry of economy, trade and industry, japan's ministry of economy, trade and industry meti is japan's ministry of economy, trade and industry, the ministry that writes japan's export controls and funds its chip industry. it put advanced chipmaking equipment under export license from july 2023. it also supports the chipmaker rapidus and new capacity for mask blanks, the glass plates that photomasks are made from. japan's controls apply to every destination and name no country, and meti decides them.\">\n<dt>METI<span class=\"aka\">Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry, Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry</span></dt>\n<dd><p>METI is Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry, the ministry that writes Japan's export controls and funds its chip industry. It put advanced chipmaking equipment under export license from July 2023. It also supports the chipmaker Rapidus and new capacity for mask blanks, the glass plates that photomasks are made from.</p><p class=\"why\">Japan's controls apply to every destination and name no country, and METI decides them.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-metrology\" data-term=\"metrology\" data-text=\"metrology process control, when grouped with inspection, metrology and inspection, inspection tools measuring what a factory actually built: how wide a printed line came out, how thick a film is, whether this layer sits exactly on top of the last one. inspection is the related job of finding flaws. a fab that cannot buy sensitive inspection tools finds fewer of the defects that lower its yield, so its yield rises more slowly. kla held 56.8 percent of the market for these tools in 2025, by cset's count.\">\n<dt>metrology<span class=\"aka\">process control, when grouped with inspection, metrology and inspection, inspection tools</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Measuring what a factory actually built: how wide a printed line came out, how thick a film is, whether this layer sits exactly on top of the last one. Inspection is the related job of finding flaws.</p><p class=\"why\">A fab that cannot buy sensitive inspection tools finds fewer of the defects that lower its yield, so its yield rises more slowly. KLA held 56.8 percent of the market for these tools in 2025, by CSET's count.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"metrology-and-inspection/\">Read it in Metrology and Inspection →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-microbump\" data-term=\"microbump\" data-text=\"microbump microbumps, solder bump, solder bumps, bumps, bump, bump metrology a microbump is a dot of solder that joins a die to the interposer or substrate beneath it. in intel's 2.5d packages microbumps sit 36 microns apart, less than half a hair's width. each one is an electrical connection that has to survive as the package heats and cools. their spacing limits how many connections fit between stacked or neighboring chips. hybrid bonding, which joins copper straight to copper, would pack connections far closer, but it is not yet ready for hbm.\">\n<dt>microbump<span class=\"aka\">microbumps, solder bump, solder bumps, bumps, bump, bump metrology</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A microbump is a dot of solder that joins a die to the interposer or substrate beneath it. In Intel's 2.5D packages microbumps sit 36 microns apart, less than half a hair's width. Each one is an electrical connection that has to survive as the package heats and cools.</p><p class=\"why\">Their spacing limits how many connections fit between stacked or neighboring chips. Hybrid bonding, which joins copper straight to copper, would pack connections far closer, but it is not yet ready for HBM.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-mm\" data-term=\"mm²\" data-text=\"mm² mm2, square millimeters, square millimeter mm² means square millimeters, the unit chip areas are given in. a lithography scanner prints at most 858 mm² in one shot, and each compute die in an nvidia b200 is about 800 mm². in 2028 tsmc plans to start making chip packages whose base layer, the wiring that links the chips, covers 14 scanner shots. yield, the share of dies that work, falls as die area grows, so the cost of each working chip rises faster than its area.\">\n<dt>mm²<span class=\"aka\">mm2, square millimeters, square millimeter</span></dt>\n<dd><p>mm² means square millimeters, the unit chip areas are given in. A lithography scanner prints at most 858 mm² in one shot, and each compute die in an Nvidia B200 is about 800 mm². In 2028 TSMC plans to start making chip packages whose base layer, the wiring that links the chips, covers 14 scanner shots.</p><p class=\"why\">Yield, the share of dies that work, falls as die area grows, so the cost of each working chip rises faster than its area.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"component-costs/\">Read it in The Economics of AI Chips →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-model-weights\" data-term=\"model weights\" data-text=\"model weights weights, frontier model weights, trained weights model weights are the billions of numbers that make up a trained ai model. they are the file that runs on the chips, so copying the weights copies the model. a chip reads the model's weights from memory for each word it writes, so bigger models need more hbm. the ai diffusion rule also made frontier model weights a controlled item, eccn 4e091.\">\n<dt>model weights<span class=\"aka\">weights, frontier model weights, trained weights</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Model weights are the billions of numbers that make up a trained AI model. They are the file that runs on the chips, so copying the weights copies the model.</p><p class=\"why\">A chip reads the model's weights from memory for each word it writes, so bigger models need more HBM. The AI Diffusion rule also made frontier model weights a controlled item, ECCN 4E091.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-mofcom\" data-term=\"mofcom\" data-text=\"mofcom ministry of commerce, china's ministry of commerce mofcom is china's ministry of commerce, the ministry that writes and administers china's own export controls. its notices put gallium, germanium and seven rare earths under license. in december 2024 it banned exports of gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard materials to the united states. china's retaliation targets inputs such as these minerals, and mofcom signs each notice.\">\n<dt>MOFCOM<span class=\"aka\">Ministry of Commerce, China's Ministry of Commerce</span></dt>\n<dd><p>MOFCOM is China's Ministry of Commerce, the ministry that writes and administers China's own export controls. Its notices put gallium, germanium and seven rare earths under license. In December 2024 it banned exports of gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard materials to the United States.</p><p class=\"why\">China's retaliation targets inputs such as these minerals, and MOFCOM signs each notice.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-multipatterning\" data-term=\"multipatterning\" data-text=\"multipatterning double patterning, quadruple patterning, self-aligned double patterning, self-aligned quadruple patterning, sadp, saqp, lele, multiple patterning, multi-patterning, several passes, several exposures, multiply exposed, duv multipatterning building one chip layer in several patterning steps, because a single exposure cannot print lines that close together. it comes in two kinds. litho-etch multipatterning splits the layer's pattern across two or three masks, then prints and etches each part separately. self-aligned double or quadruple patterning prints one coarser pattern, then deposits and etches thin spacer films along its edges to halve or quarter the line spacing. cut masks then remove the parts of lines the circuit does not need. smic makes its 7 nm-class chips without extreme ultraviolet machines by multipatterning on deep ultraviolet tools. tsmc's first 7 nm process and intel 7 were also made without extreme ultraviolet light. every extra mask or spacer step adds cost and machine time, and each extra litho-etch exposure adds a chance that parts of the layer misalign.\">\n<dt>multipatterning<span class=\"aka\">double patterning, quadruple patterning, self-aligned double patterning, self-aligned quadruple patterning, SADP, SAQP, LELE, multiple patterning, multi-patterning, several passes, several exposures, multiply exposed, DUV multipatterning</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Building one chip layer in several patterning steps, because a single exposure cannot print lines that close together. It comes in two kinds. Litho-etch multipatterning splits the layer's pattern across two or three masks, then prints and etches each part separately. Self-aligned double or quadruple patterning prints one coarser pattern, then deposits and etches thin spacer films along its edges to halve or quarter the line spacing. Cut masks then remove the parts of lines the circuit does not need.</p><p class=\"why\">SMIC makes its 7 nm-class chips without extreme ultraviolet machines by multipatterning on deep ultraviolet tools. TSMC's first 7 nm process and Intel 7 were also made without extreme ultraviolet light. Every extra mask or spacer step adds cost and machine time, and each extra litho-etch exposure adds a chance that parts of the layer misalign.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-nand\" data-term=\"nand\" data-text=\"nand 3d nand, nand flash, flash memory, 128-layer nand nand is the memory that keeps data when the power is off. it is the storage inside a phone, a laptop drive or a data center disk. 3d nand stacks its cells in many layers, made by etching holes far deeper than they are wide. it is slow next to dram and is not used inside an ai accelerator. under the october 2022 us rules, items subject to us export rules bound for a fab in china that makes nand with 128 or more layers need a license. the proposed match act would name ymtc, a chinese nand maker, in the law itself.\">\n<dt>NAND<span class=\"aka\">3D NAND, NAND flash, flash memory, 128-layer NAND</span></dt>\n<dd><p>NAND is the memory that keeps data when the power is off. It is the storage inside a phone, a laptop drive or a data center disk. 3D NAND stacks its cells in many layers, made by etching holes far deeper than they are wide. It is slow next to DRAM and is not used inside an AI accelerator.</p><p class=\"why\">Under the October 2022 US rules, items subject to US export rules bound for a fab in China that makes NAND with 128 or more layers need a license. The proposed MATCH Act would name YMTC, a Chinese NAND maker, in the law itself.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-nanometer\" data-term=\"nanometer\" data-text=\"nanometer nm, nanometers, microns, micrometer, micrometers, angstrom, angstroms, picometer, picometers a nanometer is a billionth of a meter. a micron, or micrometer, is a thousand nanometers, an angstrom is a tenth of a nanometer, and a picometer is a thousandth. lithography light is measured in nanometers, package bumps in microns, and mirror flatness in picometers. node names such as 2 nm no longer describe any feature that size, but the physical limits of printing and stacking are still measured in these units.\">\n<dt>nanometer<span class=\"aka\">nm, nanometers, microns, micrometer, micrometers, angstrom, angstroms, picometer, picometers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A nanometer is a billionth of a meter. A micron, or micrometer, is a thousand nanometers, an angstrom is a tenth of a nanometer, and a picometer is a thousandth. Lithography light is measured in nanometers, package bumps in microns, and mirror flatness in picometers.</p><p class=\"why\">Node names such as 2 nm no longer describe any feature that size, but the physical limits of printing and stacking are still measured in these units.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-neon\" data-term=\"neon\" data-text=\"neon neon gas, semiconductor-grade neon neon, mixed with krypton or argon and fluorine, is the gas inside the lasers that give deep ultraviolet scanners their light. a fab uses it by the cylinder, and those scanners cannot print without it. ukraine supplied about 70 percent of the world's neon before russia invaded in 2022. many chipmakers had added to their gas stockpiles after russia annexed crimea in 2014, and several reported adequate supplies from china.\">\n<dt>neon<span class=\"aka\">neon gas, semiconductor-grade neon</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Neon, mixed with krypton or argon and fluorine, is the gas inside the lasers that give deep ultraviolet scanners their light. A fab uses it by the cylinder, and those scanners cannot print without it.</p><p class=\"why\">Ukraine supplied about 70 percent of the world's neon before Russia invaded in 2022. Many chipmakers had added to their gas stockpiles after Russia annexed Crimea in 2014, and several reported adequate supplies from China.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-nitrogen-trifluoride\" data-term=\"nitrogen trifluoride\" data-text=\"nitrogen trifluoride nf3 nitrogen trifluoride is a gas that cleans process chambers between wafers. split apart in a plasma, it releases fluorine that scours the deposits off the inside of the chamber. a shortage of any one chemical can stop a fab. sk specialty of south korea has made nitrogen trifluoride since 2001, when it became the first company to produce the gas there.\">\n<dt>nitrogen trifluoride<span class=\"aka\">NF3</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Nitrogen trifluoride is a gas that cleans process chambers between wafers. Split apart in a plasma, it releases fluorine that scours the deposits off the inside of the chamber.</p><p class=\"why\">A shortage of any one chemical can stop a fab. SK Specialty of South Korea has made nitrogen trifluoride since 2001, when it became the first company to produce the gas there.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-nm-class\" data-term=\"nm-class\" data-text=\"nm-class 5 nm-class, 7 nm-class, 2 nm-class, nanometer-class, nm class nm-class, as in 7 nm-class, means a process roughly as dense as the foundries' 7 nm generation. the label is used when a maker's own name for the node is different. china's smic builds its 7 nm-class processes without extreme ultraviolet machines, and its most advanced, n+3, reaches the density of tsmc's 6 nm-class process.\">\n<dt>nm-class<span class=\"aka\">5 nm-class, 7 nm-class, 2 nm-class, nanometer-class, nm class</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Nm-class, as in 7 nm-class, means a process roughly as dense as the foundries' 7 nm generation. The label is used when a maker's own name for the node is different.</p><p class=\"why\">China's SMIC builds its 7 nm-class processes without extreme ultraviolet machines, and its most advanced, N+3, reaches the density of TSMC's 6 nm-class process.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-node\" data-term=\"node\" data-text=\"node process node, technology node, for example n2 or 18a, nodes the name a foundry gives one generation of its manufacturing process. the number in the name no longer measures anything on the chip. smic's n+3, a 7 nm-class process, spaces its narrowest wires closer together than intel's panther lake chips on 18a do. comparing two foundries by node name says little. each foundry also picks its own baseline for the density gains it claims.\">\n<dt>node<span class=\"aka\">process node, technology node, for example N2 or 18A, nodes</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The name a foundry gives one generation of its manufacturing process. The number in the name no longer measures anything on the chip. SMIC's N+3, a 7 nm-class process, spaces its narrowest wires closer together than Intel's Panther Lake chips on 18A do.</p><p class=\"why\">Comparing two foundries by node name says little. Each foundry also picks its own baseline for the density gains it claims.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-nvl72\" data-term=\"nvl72\" data-text=\"nvl72 gb200 nvl72, gb300 nvl72, vera rubin nvl72 nvidia's rack-sized product, with 72 accelerators in 18 compute trays joined through nine switch trays so that software can treat the whole rack as one computer. the gb300 version draws up to 142 kilowatts. ai capacity is built and costed by the rack. in july 2026 semianalysis put the cost of owning a vera rubin nvl72 at $3.57 per gpu-hour, against $1.84 for a gb200 and $2.36 for a gb300.\">\n<dt>NVL72<span class=\"aka\">GB200 NVL72, GB300 NVL72, Vera Rubin NVL72</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Nvidia's rack-sized product, with 72 accelerators in 18 compute trays joined through nine switch trays so that software can treat the whole rack as one computer. The GB300 version draws up to 142 kilowatts.</p><p class=\"why\">AI capacity is built and costed by the rack. In July 2026 SemiAnalysis put the cost of owning a Vera Rubin NVL72 at $3.57 per GPU-hour, against $1.84 for a GB200 and $2.36 for a GB300.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-nvlink\" data-term=\"nvlink\" data-text=\"nvlink nvswitch, nvlink 5, nvlink 6, nv-hbi nvidia's own high-speed connection between its accelerators, which lets dozens of them act as one. nvlink 6 carries 3,600 gigabytes per second per gpu, according to nvidia's january 2026 rubin launch. nvidia controls it, while more than 50 makers of systems and components build around its racks. since may 2025 its nvlink fusion program has let other firms' custom chips connect to nvidia gpus over nvlink, and fujitsu and qualcomm plan cpus that do so. ualink is a published open rival.\">\n<dt>NVLink<span class=\"aka\">NVSwitch, NVLink 5, NVLink 6, NV-HBI</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Nvidia's own high-speed connection between its accelerators, which lets dozens of them act as one. NVLink 6 carries 3,600 gigabytes per second per GPU, according to Nvidia's January 2026 Rubin launch.</p><p class=\"why\">Nvidia controls it, while more than 50 makers of systems and components build around its racks. Since May 2025 its NVLink Fusion program has let other firms' custom chips connect to Nvidia GPUs over NVLink, and Fujitsu and Qualcomm plan CPUs that do so. UALink is a published open rival.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-odm\" data-term=\"odm\" data-text=\"odm original design manufacturer, odms, contract manufacturer, contract manufacturers, contract manufacturing, ems, server odm an odm, for original design manufacturer, is a firm such as foxconn, quanta or wistron that designs and builds servers and racks to a customer's specification. the customer's name goes on the box. a contract manufacturer does the assembly only. more than 50 makers of systems and components were gearing up for nvidia's vera rubin nvl72 rack in october 2025, nvidia said. in its filing for the quarter to july 2026, nvidia said the complexity of producing its data center systems had caused production delays.\">\n<dt>ODM<span class=\"aka\">original design manufacturer, ODMs, contract manufacturer, contract manufacturers, contract manufacturing, EMS, server ODM</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An ODM, for original design manufacturer, is a firm such as Foxconn, Quanta or Wistron that designs and builds servers and racks to a customer's specification. The customer's name goes on the box. A contract manufacturer does the assembly only.</p><p class=\"why\">More than 50 makers of systems and components were gearing up for Nvidia's Vera Rubin NVL72 rack in October 2025, Nvidia said. In its filing for the quarter to July 2026, Nvidia said the complexity of producing its data center systems had caused production delays.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-oligopoly\" data-term=\"oligopoly\" data-text=\"oligopoly oligopolies, duopoly, three-firm oligopoly an oligopoly is a market with only a few sellers, so each one's decisions move the price. a duopoly has two. dram, industrial gases, substrates and chip testers are all oligopolies. the fewer the sellers, the more one accident or one license decision moves the market. with a single seller, losing that seller stops the buyer's production line.\">\n<dt>oligopoly<span class=\"aka\">oligopolies, duopoly, three-firm oligopoly</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An oligopoly is a market with only a few sellers, so each one's decisions move the price. A duopoly has two. DRAM, industrial gases, substrates and chip testers are all oligopolies.</p><p class=\"why\">The fewer the sellers, the more one accident or one license decision moves the market. With a single seller, losing that seller stops the buyer's production line.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-operating-margin\" data-term=\"operating margin\" data-text=\"operating margin operating profit, operating loss, operating income operating margin is the share of revenue left after paying both the cost of making the product and the cost of running the company, research and sales included. it is lower than gross margin, which counts only the cost of making. sk hynix's earnings release gives no gross margin, only an operating margin, which was 76 percent in the june 2026 quarter.\">\n<dt>operating margin<span class=\"aka\">operating profit, operating loss, operating income</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Operating margin is the share of revenue left after paying both the cost of making the product and the cost of running the company, research and sales included. It is lower than gross margin, which counts only the cost of making.</p><p class=\"why\">SK hynix's earnings release gives no gross margin, only an operating margin, which was 76 percent in the June 2026 quarter.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"component-costs/\">Read it in The Economics of AI Chips →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-optical-transceiver\" data-term=\"optical transceiver\" data-text=\"optical transceiver optical module, pluggable optics, optical transceivers, transceiver, transceivers, optical modules, 800g optical transceivers a small device that turns electrical signals into laser light for sending down a glass fiber, and turns them back at the far end. every network link longer than a few meters in a large ai cluster needs one at each end. a cluster needs several for each accelerator. one design for 100,000 h100s uses 98,304 just to link its gpus to the first tier of switches. chinese firms assemble the modules in volume, but the lasers inside them were scarce in 2026.\">\n<dt>optical transceiver<span class=\"aka\">optical module, pluggable optics, optical transceivers, transceiver, transceivers, optical modules, 800G optical transceivers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A small device that turns electrical signals into laser light for sending down a glass fiber, and turns them back at the far end. Every network link longer than a few meters in a large AI cluster needs one at each end.</p><p class=\"why\">A cluster needs several for each accelerator. One design for 100,000 H100s uses 98,304 just to link its GPUs to the first tier of switches. Chinese firms assemble the modules in volume, but the lasers inside them were scarce in 2026.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-osat\" data-term=\"osat\" data-text=\"osat outsourced semiconductor assembly and test, osats, outsourced assembly and test, assembly and test firms, assembly and test contractor, assembly and test houses a contract firm that takes finished wafers, cuts them into chips, seals the chips into packages and tests them. it is the back end of chipmaking, done for hire. every chip passes through assembly and test. yet in the june 2026 quarter amkor earned a gross margin of 16.8 percent, and ase's packaging and test segment 27.3 percent. in a trendforce ranking cited by cset, four of the ten largest of these firms by 2024 revenue are headquartered in china.\">\n<dt>OSAT<span class=\"aka\">outsourced semiconductor assembly and test, OSATs, outsourced assembly and test, assembly and test firms, assembly and test contractor, assembly and test houses</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A contract firm that takes finished wafers, cuts them into chips, seals the chips into packages and tests them. It is the back end of chipmaking, done for hire.</p><p class=\"why\">Every chip passes through assembly and test. Yet in the June 2026 quarter Amkor earned a gross margin of 16.8 percent, and ASE's packaging and test segment 27.3 percent. In a TrendForce ranking cited by CSET, four of the ten largest of these firms by 2024 revenue are headquartered in China.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-overlay\" data-term=\"overlay\" data-text=\"overlay overlay error, alignment how precisely one printed layer of a chip lands on top of the layer beneath it. before each exposure the scanner finds marks printed in earlier layers and lines the new layer up on them to within a few nanometers, across a disc 300 millimeters wide. misalignment can ruin whole regions of a wafer, so overlay is one of the specifications that separates an advanced printing machine from an ordinary one. each extra pass on a layer is another chance to misalign.\">\n<dt>overlay<span class=\"aka\">overlay error, alignment</span></dt>\n<dd><p>How precisely one printed layer of a chip lands on top of the layer beneath it. Before each exposure the scanner finds marks printed in earlier layers and lines the new layer up on them to within a few nanometers, across a disc 300 millimeters wide.</p><p class=\"why\">Misalignment can ruin whole regions of a wafer, so overlay is one of the specifications that separates an advanced printing machine from an ordinary one. Each extra pass on a layer is another chance to misalign.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"metrology-and-inspection/\">Read it in Metrology and Inspection →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-panel-level-packaging\" data-term=\"panel-level packaging\" data-text=\"panel-level packaging panel-level, panel level packaging, rectangular panel, rectangular panels panel-level packaging builds packages on a large rectangular sheet instead of a round wafer, so far less area is wasted at the edges and many more packages fit on one carrier. it gets around the size limits of a 300 mm wafer. powertech, a taiwanese assembly and test firm, aims to run the first panel-level packaging line for ai chips in 2027.\">\n<dt>panel-level packaging<span class=\"aka\">panel-level, panel level packaging, rectangular panel, rectangular panels</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Panel-level packaging builds packages on a large rectangular sheet instead of a round wafer, so far less area is wasted at the edges and many more packages fit on one carrier. It gets around the size limits of a 300 mm wafer.</p><p class=\"why\">Powertech, a Taiwanese assembly and test firm, aims to run the first panel-level packaging line for AI chips in 2027.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-pcie\" data-term=\"pcie\" data-text=\"pcie pci express, pcie 6, pcie 7 pcie is the standard connector and link that joins a processor to the cards inside a computer, an accelerator included. in an ai server it carries data between the host processor and the gpus, while faster private links join the gpus to each other. the pcie block is licensed ip that has to be proven on each new node before a chip can use it.\">\n<dt>PCIe<span class=\"aka\">PCI Express, PCIe 6, PCIe 7</span></dt>\n<dd><p>PCIe is the standard connector and link that joins a processor to the cards inside a computer, an accelerator included. In an AI server it carries data between the host processor and the GPUs, while faster private links join the GPUs to each other.</p><p class=\"why\">The PCIe block is licensed IP that has to be proven on each new node before a chip can use it.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-pdk\" data-term=\"pdk\" data-text=\"pdk process design kit, process design kits a process design kit, or pdk, is the set of files a foundry gives designers to describe exactly what its factory can print on one process, or node. it gives the sizes, spacings and electrical behavior of every feature. design software is checked against it before a chip is accepted. foundries develop each kit with the design-software vendors about two years before production starts and specify which tools customers must use for tape-out.\">\n<dt>PDK<span class=\"aka\">process design kit, process design kits</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A process design kit, or PDK, is the set of files a foundry gives designers to describe exactly what its factory can print on one process, or node. It gives the sizes, spacings and electrical behavior of every feature. Design software is checked against it before a chip is accepted.</p><p class=\"why\">Foundries develop each kit with the design-software vendors about two years before production starts and specify which tools customers must use for tape-out.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-pellicle\" data-term=\"pellicle\" data-text=\"pellicle pellicles, euv pellicle a thin transparent membrane on a frame above a photomask, the patterned plate a chip layer is printed from. dust settles on it, far enough out of focus that it does not print, so the pattern stays clean. it works like a lens cap a photographer can shoot through. pellicles already work in high-volume euv manufacturing. but no material is completely transparent to euv light, and the light crosses the membrane twice, so every pellicle costs some output. carbon nanotube membranes, which passed up to 97 percent of the light in one crossing in imec's 2020 tests, are the next step.\">\n<dt>pellicle<span class=\"aka\">pellicles, EUV pellicle</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A thin transparent membrane on a frame above a photomask, the patterned plate a chip layer is printed from. Dust settles on it, far enough out of focus that it does not print, so the pattern stays clean. It works like a lens cap a photographer can shoot through.</p><p class=\"why\">Pellicles already work in high-volume EUV manufacturing. But no material is completely transparent to EUV light, and the light crosses the membrane twice, so every pellicle costs some output. Carbon nanotube membranes, which passed up to 97 percent of the light in one crossing in imec's 2020 tests, are the next step.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"photomasks-and-pellicles/\">Read it in Photomasks and Pellicles →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-performance-density\" data-term=\"performance density\" data-text=\"performance density  an export control test of how densely a chip packs its computing power. it divides the chip's tpp, the export rules' measure of computing power, by its applicable die area in square millimeters. that area counts all logic dies made on a process with non-planar transistors, such as finfets. the test applies only to a chip that reaches 1,600 tpp. it replaced the 2022 test, which was based on interconnect bandwidth, the speed at which a chip exchanges data with its neighbors. it closed a gap that nvidia's china-specific chips, such as the a800 and h800, had used. nvidia had designed those chips to stay under the 2022 interconnect-speed threshold. the top band, eccn 3a090.a, now starts at 4,800 tpp, or at 1,600 tpp with a performance density of 5.92 (88 fr 73458).\">\n<dt>performance density</dt>\n<dd><p>An export control test of how densely a chip packs its computing power. It divides the chip's TPP, the export rules' measure of computing power, by its applicable die area in square millimeters. That area counts all logic dies made on a process with non-planar transistors, such as FinFETs. The test applies only to a chip that reaches 1,600 TPP. It replaced the 2022 test, which was based on interconnect bandwidth, the speed at which a chip exchanges data with its neighbors.</p><p class=\"why\">It closed a gap that Nvidia's China-specific chips, such as the A800 and H800, had used. Nvidia had designed those chips to stay under the 2022 interconnect-speed threshold. The top band, ECCN 3A090.a, now starts at 4,800 TPP, or at 1,600 TPP with a performance density of 5.92 (88 FR 73458).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-photomask\" data-term=\"photomask\" data-text=\"photomask mask, reticle, mask set, photomasks, masks, mask sets, mask blank set the master template for one layer of a chip: a quartz plate, or for the shortest wavelengths a mirror, that carries the pattern projected onto the wafer. a chip needs dozens of them, at least one per layer. in july 2022 semianalysis put a full set above $1 million at 28 nm and above $10 million at 7 nm. in may 2026 it put a leading-edge set at $40 million. the cost of a mask set limits which chips are worth making on a leading-edge process at all. only three firms supply the blank plates for euv masks, and two of them are japanese.\">\n<dt>photomask<span class=\"aka\">mask, reticle, mask set, photomasks, masks, mask sets, mask blank set</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The master template for one layer of a chip: a quartz plate, or for the shortest wavelengths a mirror, that carries the pattern projected onto the wafer. A chip needs dozens of them, at least one per layer. In July 2022 SemiAnalysis put a full set above $1 million at 28 nm and above $10 million at 7 nm. In May 2026 it put a leading-edge set at $40 million.</p><p class=\"why\">The cost of a mask set limits which chips are worth making on a leading-edge process at all. Only three firms supply the blank plates for EUV masks, and two of them are Japanese.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"photomasks-and-pellicles/\">Read it in Photomasks and Pellicles →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-photoresist\" data-term=\"photoresist\" data-text=\"photoresist resist, resists, euv resist, euv resists, resist makers the light-sensitive coating that records a chip's pattern during lithography. a machine spins a thin film of it across the wafer. light shone through a stencil changes the film where it lands, and a wash removes those parts. what remains shows the next machine where to etch. every printed layer of a chip uses it. each resist is tuned to the layers it prints, and even one that passes the first time takes seven to 17 months to approve in a fab. japanese companies held 78 percent of world sales in 2023. in 2024 an investment vehicle of a japanese state-backed fund bought 84.36 percent of the resist maker jsr.\">\n<dt>photoresist<span class=\"aka\">resist, resists, EUV resist, EUV resists, resist makers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The light-sensitive coating that records a chip's pattern during lithography. A machine spins a thin film of it across the wafer. Light shone through a stencil changes the film where it lands, and a wash removes those parts. What remains shows the next machine where to etch.</p><p class=\"why\">Every printed layer of a chip uses it. Each resist is tuned to the layers it prints, and even one that passes the first time takes seven to 17 months to approve in a fab. Japanese companies held 78 percent of world sales in 2023. In 2024 an investment vehicle of a Japanese state-backed fund bought 84.36 percent of the resist maker JSR.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-pitch\" data-term=\"pitch\" data-text=\"pitch pitches, half-pitch, gate pitch, metal pitch, wire pitch, line pitch pitch is the distance from one line on a chip to the next, center to center, so it counts the line and the gap together. half-pitch is half that. a 16 nm pitch means lines 16 nanometers apart. the 2022 us rules set a dram threshold at 18 nm half-pitch. unlike a node name, pitch measures something physical on the chip. but semianalysis calls a single pitch an incomplete metric for comparing processes.\">\n<dt>pitch<span class=\"aka\">pitches, half-pitch, gate pitch, metal pitch, wire pitch, line pitch</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Pitch is the distance from one line on a chip to the next, center to center, so it counts the line and the gap together. Half-pitch is half that. A 16 nm pitch means lines 16 nanometers apart. The 2022 US rules set a DRAM threshold at 18 nm half-pitch.</p><p class=\"why\">Unlike a node name, pitch measures something physical on the chip. But SemiAnalysis calls a single pitch an incomplete metric for comparing processes.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-plasma\" data-term=\"plasma\" data-text=\"plasma plasmas, plasma etch, plasma-enhanced, plasma source a plasma is a gas energized until some of its atoms or molecules break into charged particles. most etch steps and many deposition steps happen in a plasma that an electric field makes inside a vacuum chamber, though batch furnaces mostly work without one. in the chamber, neutral fragments called radicals do most of the chemistry, and charged ions give etch its direction. in an extreme ultraviolet machine, a laser vaporizes droplets of molten tin into a plasma that gives off the 13.5-nanometer light. export controls describe each tool by the process it is designed to run. an extreme ultraviolet source has to make its tin plasma 50,000 times a second to give enough light for production.\">\n<dt>plasma<span class=\"aka\">plasmas, plasma etch, plasma-enhanced, plasma source</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A plasma is a gas energized until some of its atoms or molecules break into charged particles. Most etch steps and many deposition steps happen in a plasma that an electric field makes inside a vacuum chamber, though batch furnaces mostly work without one. In the chamber, neutral fragments called radicals do most of the chemistry, and charged ions give etch its direction. In an extreme ultraviolet machine, a laser vaporizes droplets of molten tin into a plasma that gives off the 13.5-nanometer light.</p><p class=\"why\">Export controls describe each tool by the process it is designed to run. An extreme ultraviolet source has to make its tin plasma 50,000 times a second to give enough light for production.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-polysilicon\" data-term=\"polysilicon\" data-text=\"polysilicon polycrystalline silicon, electronic-grade polysilicon, semiconductor-grade polysilicon, polysilicon feedstock polysilicon is purified silicon that has not yet been grown into one crystal. it comes as gray rods made of many small crystals. it is the raw material that is melted down to pull the single crystal a wafer is cut from. the same material, at lower purity, goes into solar panels. china made about 93 percent of the world's polysilicon in 2023. but the german wafer maker siltronic names five major suppliers of the electronic-grade kind for 2025, and none of them is chinese.\">\n<dt>polysilicon<span class=\"aka\">polycrystalline silicon, electronic-grade polysilicon, semiconductor-grade polysilicon, polysilicon feedstock</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Polysilicon is purified silicon that has not yet been grown into one crystal. It comes as gray rods made of many small crystals. It is the raw material that is melted down to pull the single crystal a wafer is cut from. The same material, at lower purity, goes into solar panels.</p><p class=\"why\">China made about 93 percent of the world's polysilicon in 2023. But the German wafer maker Siltronic names five major suppliers of the electronic-grade kind for 2025, and none of them is Chinese.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"silicon-and-wafers/\">Read it in Silicon and Wafers →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-power-shelf\" data-term=\"power shelf\" data-text=\"power shelf power shelves, rack power shelf a power shelf is a slide-in unit in a rack that converts the incoming supply to the voltage the boards use and feeds it to the busbar. a gb300 nvl72 rack draws its 142 kilowatts through eight of them at 33 kilowatts each. many firms supply the shelves and the boards behind them. the large transformers upstream commonly took three years to arrive in 2024.\">\n<dt>power shelf<span class=\"aka\">power shelves, rack power shelf</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A power shelf is a slide-in unit in a rack that converts the incoming supply to the voltage the boards use and feeds it to the busbar. A GB300 NVL72 rack draws its 142 kilowatts through eight of them at 33 kilowatts each.</p><p class=\"why\">Many firms supply the shelves and the boards behind them. The large transformers upstream commonly took three years to arrive in 2024.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-presumption-of-approval\" data-term=\"presumption of approval\" data-text=\"presumption of approval approval is presumed, presumed approval a presumption of approval means a license is still required but will normally be granted. it is the opposite of a presumption of denial, and one rule can contain both. hbm license applications for macau and country group d:5 are presumed approved when neither the buyer nor its ultimate parent is headquartered in either place, and presumed denied otherwise (15 cfr 742.6(b)(10)(ii)). the split lets hbm reach plants in china owned by firms headquartered elsewhere while holding it back from chinese-owned buyers.\">\n<dt>presumption of approval<span class=\"aka\">approval is presumed, presumed approval</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A presumption of approval means a license is still required but will normally be granted. It is the opposite of a presumption of denial, and one rule can contain both. HBM license applications for Macau and Country Group D:5 are presumed approved when neither the buyer nor its ultimate parent is headquartered in either place, and presumed denied otherwise (15 CFR 742.6(b)(10)(ii)).</p><p class=\"why\">The split lets HBM reach plants in China owned by firms headquartered elsewhere while holding it back from Chinese-owned buyers.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-presumption-of-denial\" data-term=\"presumption of denial\" data-text=\"presumption of denial  a license review policy in which the reviewing agencies start from the position that an application should be refused. an application can still be filed and will be considered, but the exporter has to overcome that starting position. it is the general policy for advanced computing chips going to china and macau under 15 cfr 742.6(b)(10), and for most entity list entries. since january 2026 export applications for some less powerful chips, such as the h200, are reviewed case by case instead. the difference between a presumption of denial and a prohibition decides whether a company files at all. under a presumption of denial an application can still be made, but under a prohibition it cannot.\">\n<dt>presumption of denial</dt>\n<dd><p>A license review policy in which the reviewing agencies start from the position that an application should be refused. An application can still be filed and will be considered, but the exporter has to overcome that starting position. It is the general policy for advanced computing chips going to China and Macau under 15 CFR 742.6(b)(10), and for most Entity List entries. Since January 2026 export applications for some less powerful chips, such as the H200, are reviewed case by case instead.</p><p class=\"why\">The difference between a presumption of denial and a prohibition decides whether a company files at all. Under a presumption of denial an application can still be made, but under a prohibition it cannot.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-printed-circuit-board\" data-term=\"printed circuit board\" data-text=\"printed circuit board pcb, pcbs, printed circuit boards, circuit board, circuit boards, high-multilayer pcb a printed circuit board is the flat green or black card that electronic parts are soldered onto, with its wiring etched from copper sheets and stacked in layers. boards for ai servers can run past 30 layers. it carries the power and the links between gpus. how much signal its laminate absorbs is now a main design limit.\">\n<dt>printed circuit board<span class=\"aka\">PCB, PCBs, printed circuit boards, circuit board, circuit boards, high-multilayer PCB</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A printed circuit board is the flat green or black card that electronic parts are soldered onto, with its wiring etched from copper sheets and stacked in layers. Boards for AI servers can run past 30 layers.</p><p class=\"why\">It carries the power and the links between GPUs. How much signal its laminate absorbs is now a main design limit.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"substrates-and-pcbs/\">Read it in Substrates and PCBs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-probe-card\" data-term=\"probe card\" data-text=\"probe card probe cards a circuit board carrying thousands of fine needles that press onto the contact pads of a chip while it is still part of the wafer. a tester drives signals into the chip through the needles. every card is custom-built for one chip design. because each card is custom-built and slow to qualify, probe card supply and lead time can limit how fast a new accelerator or memory stack reaches full production.\">\n<dt>probe card<span class=\"aka\">probe cards</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A circuit board carrying thousands of fine needles that press onto the contact pads of a chip while it is still part of the wafer. A tester drives signals into the chip through the needles. Every card is custom-built for one chip design.</p><p class=\"why\">Because each card is custom-built and slow to qualify, probe card supply and lead time can limit how fast a new accelerator or memory stack reaches full production.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-pvd\" data-term=\"pvd\" data-text=\"pvd physical vapor deposition, sputtering, sputtering target, sputtering targets, sputter physical vapor deposition, or pvd, coats a wafer with metal in a vacuum. it knocks atoms off a solid slab of metal, the sputtering target, and they fly across and land on the wafer as a thin film. it lays down the metal barriers and seed layers under a chip's copper wiring. every copper wire needs that barrier, because copper seeps into the insulator around it. jx advanced metals puts its own share of the world market for semiconductor sputtering targets at about 65 percent as of fiscal 2026.\">\n<dt>PVD<span class=\"aka\">physical vapor deposition, sputtering, sputtering target, sputtering targets, sputter</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Physical vapor deposition, or PVD, coats a wafer with metal in a vacuum. It knocks atoms off a solid slab of metal, the sputtering target, and they fly across and land on the wafer as a thin film. It lays down the metal barriers and seed layers under a chip's copper wiring.</p><p class=\"why\">Every copper wire needs that barrier, because copper seeps into the insulator around it. JX Advanced Metals puts its own share of the world market for semiconductor sputtering targets at about 65 percent as of fiscal 2026.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-qualification\" data-term=\"qualification\" data-text=\"qualification qualify, qualifies, qualified, qualifying, requalify, requalification, qualification tests, qualification lock-in qualification is the testing a fab or a customer runs before it will accept a new material, tool or supplier. a resist, a slurry, a wafer source or a memory stack is approved for a set use, such as one layer in one fab's process, and switching means running the tests again. even a resist that passes the first time takes seven to 17 months to approve, the semiconductor industry association wrote in 2023, so a second source is slow to add.\">\n<dt>qualification<span class=\"aka\">qualify, qualifies, qualified, qualifying, requalify, requalification, qualification tests, qualification lock-in</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Qualification is the testing a fab or a customer runs before it will accept a new material, tool or supplier. A resist, a slurry, a wafer source or a memory stack is approved for a set use, such as one layer in one fab's process, and switching means running the tests again.</p><p class=\"why\">Even a resist that passes the first time takes seven to 17 months to approve, the Semiconductor Industry Association wrote in 2023, so a second source is slow to add.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-rack\" data-term=\"rack\" data-text=\"rack cabinet, racks, cabinets, rack-scale the standard steel frame that computing equipment is bolted into in a data center, roughly the size of a wardrobe. for ai, a whole rack is wired and sold as one machine, so the rack itself is the product. a gb300 nvl72 rack draws up to 142 kilowatts. nvidia's 800-volt power design is intended for racks of more than a megawatt from 2027. a megawatt rack needs a different busbar, the metal bar that carries power to its equipment. it also changes the weight the floor must bear, the coolant flow and the energy stored in the rack to keep its power draw steady.\">\n<dt>rack<span class=\"aka\">cabinet, racks, cabinets, rack-scale</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The standard steel frame that computing equipment is bolted into in a data center, roughly the size of a wardrobe. For AI, a whole rack is wired and sold as one machine, so the rack itself is the product.</p><p class=\"why\">A GB300 NVL72 rack draws up to 142 kilowatts. Nvidia's 800-volt power design is intended for racks of more than a megawatt from 2027. A megawatt rack needs a different busbar, the metal bar that carries power to its equipment. It also changes the weight the floor must bear, the coolant flow and the energy stored in the rack to keep its power draw steady.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ramp\" data-term=\"ramp\" data-text=\"ramp ramps, ramp-up, ramping, yield at ramp a ramp is the months in which a new process or product climbs from a few wafers a week to full output while the share of working chips rises. yield is lowest at the start of the ramp and improves as engineers find which steps lose dies. whether a new process makes a profit or needs a subsidy depends on its yield in the first year.\">\n<dt>ramp<span class=\"aka\">ramps, ramp-up, ramping, yield at ramp</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A ramp is the months in which a new process or product climbs from a few wafers a week to full output while the share of working chips rises. Yield is lowest at the start of the ramp and improves as engineers find which steps lose dies.</p><p class=\"why\">Whether a new process makes a profit or needs a subsidy depends on its yield in the first year.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-rare-earths\" data-term=\"rare earths\" data-text=\"rare earths rare earth, rare-earth, rare earth elements, medium and heavy rare earths the rare earths are a group of metals, including samarium and yttrium, that go into the strong magnets in motors, disk drives and wind turbines, and into some lasers and glass. beijing put seven of them under export license in april 2025. in october 2025 it claimed jurisdiction over foreign goods containing chinese rare earths worth 0.1 percent or more of their value. that rule is suspended until 10 november 2026.\">\n<dt>rare earths<span class=\"aka\">rare earth, rare-earth, rare earth elements, medium and heavy rare earths</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The rare earths are a group of metals, including samarium and yttrium, that go into the strong magnets in motors, disk drives and wind turbines, and into some lasers and glass.</p><p class=\"why\">Beijing put seven of them under export license in April 2025. In October 2025 it claimed jurisdiction over foreign goods containing Chinese rare earths worth 0.1 percent or more of their value. That rule is suspended until 10 November 2026.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-redistribution-layer\" data-term=\"redistribution layer\" data-text=\"redistribution layer rdl, redistribution wiring, redistribution layers a redistribution layer is a thin sheet of fine copper wiring, laid down in resin, that spreads a die's tightly spaced connections out to a wider pattern the package can handle. cowos-r and cowos-l use it in place of a full silicon interposer. tsmc pushed packages past 3.3 times the reticle size by swapping silicon for redistribution wiring.\">\n<dt>redistribution layer<span class=\"aka\">RDL, redistribution wiring, redistribution layers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A redistribution layer is a thin sheet of fine copper wiring, laid down in resin, that spreads a die's tightly spaced connections out to a wider pattern the package can handle. CoWoS-R and CoWoS-L use it in place of a full silicon interposer.</p><p class=\"why\">TSMC pushed packages past 3.3 times the reticle size by swapping silicon for redistribution wiring.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-reexport\" data-term=\"reexport\" data-text=\"reexport  shipping an item that falls under us export rules, the ear, from one foreign country to another. the term is defined at 15 cfr 734.14. a memory stack subject to the ear moving from korea to china is a reexport, and it needs the same us license a shipment from texas would. the reexport rule lets us controls follow an item after it leaves the united states, so they reach trade between two foreign countries.\">\n<dt>reexport</dt>\n<dd><p>Shipping an item that falls under US export rules, the EAR, from one foreign country to another. The term is defined at 15 CFR 734.14. A memory stack subject to the EAR moving from Korea to China is a reexport, and it needs the same US license a shipment from Texas would.</p><p class=\"why\">The reexport rule lets US controls follow an item after it leaves the United States, so they reach trade between two foreign countries.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-reticle\" data-term=\"reticle\" data-text=\"reticle photomask the patterned plate whose image a lithography machine projects onto the wafer, one chip layer at a time. in practice it means the same as photomask, but the word reticle stresses that the machine steps the same image again and again across the wafer. one exposure from a reticle prints at most 26 by 33 millimeters of the wafer, and every large ai chip has to be designed around that limit.\">\n<dt>reticle<span class=\"aka\">photomask</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The patterned plate whose image a lithography machine projects onto the wafer, one chip layer at a time. In practice it means the same as photomask, but the word reticle stresses that the machine steps the same image again and again across the wafer.</p><p class=\"why\">One exposure from a reticle prints at most 26 by 33 millimeters of the wafer, and every large AI chip has to be designed around that limit.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"photomasks-and-pellicles/\">Read it in Photomasks and Pellicles →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-reticle-limit\" data-term=\"reticle limit\" data-text=\"reticle limit reticle size limit, reticle field, field size, reticle-limited, reticle size, reticles, times reticle the largest chip a lithography machine can print in a single exposure, about 858 square millimeters, or 26 by 33 millimeters. it is set by the machine's optics and is the same for every design. the newer high-na euv machines print half that area. many leading ai accelerators, nvidia's blackwell among them, need more circuitry than this, so they are split into several dies, separate pieces of silicon, and joined back together inside a package.\">\n<dt>reticle limit<span class=\"aka\">reticle size limit, reticle field, field size, reticle-limited, reticle size, reticles, times reticle</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The largest chip a lithography machine can print in a single exposure, about 858 square millimeters, or 26 by 33 millimeters. It is set by the machine's optics and is the same for every design. The newer High-NA EUV machines print half that area.</p><p class=\"why\">Many leading AI accelerators, Nvidia's Blackwell among them, need more circuitry than this, so they are split into several dies, separate pieces of silicon, and joined back together inside a package.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-risc-v\" data-term=\"risc-v\" data-text=\"risc-v risc-v cores, risc-v processor risc-v is an open instruction set, the list of basic commands a processor understands, that anyone may use without a license. companies build their own processor cores on it, and nvidia now uses such cores for small control tasks inside every gpu. it is the license-free alternative to arm's processor designs.\">\n<dt>RISC-V<span class=\"aka\">RISC-V cores, RISC-V processor</span></dt>\n<dd><p>RISC-V is an open instruction set, the list of basic commands a processor understands, that anyone may use without a license. Companies build their own processor cores on it, and Nvidia now uses such cores for small control tasks inside every GPU.</p><p class=\"why\">It is the license-free alternative to Arm's processor designs.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-rtl\" data-term=\"rtl\" data-text=\"rtl register-transfer level, register-transfer-level, register transfer level, rtl description, rtl code rtl, for register-transfer level, is the code in which a chip is first written. it is text, in a language such as systemverilog, that describes what every storage element holds on every tick of the clock. software later turns it into transistors and wires. it defines what the chip does. a large team checks it in simulation and emulation before tape-out, because a mistake found later needs new masks.\">\n<dt>RTL<span class=\"aka\">register-transfer level, register-transfer-level, register transfer level, RTL description, RTL code</span></dt>\n<dd><p>RTL, for register-transfer level, is the code in which a chip is first written. It is text, in a language such as SystemVerilog, that describes what every storage element holds on every tick of the clock. Software later turns it into transistors and wires.</p><p class=\"why\">It defines what the chip does. A large team checks it in simulation and emulation before tape-out, because a mistake found later needs new masks.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-scale-out-network\" data-term=\"scale-out network\" data-text=\"scale-out network back-end network, cluster fabric, scale-out, scale out the network that joins thousands of accelerator groups into one cluster, running at hundreds of gigabits per second over ethernet or infiniband. its ethernet versions use the same standard as ordinary data center networks. it lets thousands of accelerators train one model together. infiniband was the main scale-out network when ai clusters were small. but ethernet capacity has since grown quickly, as broadcom doubled the bandwidth of its switch chips every generation.\">\n<dt>scale-out network<span class=\"aka\">back-end network, cluster fabric, scale-out, scale out</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The network that joins thousands of accelerator groups into one cluster, running at hundreds of gigabits per second over Ethernet or InfiniBand. Its Ethernet versions use the same standard as ordinary data center networks.</p><p class=\"why\">It lets thousands of accelerators train one model together. InfiniBand was the main scale-out network when AI clusters were small. But Ethernet capacity has since grown quickly, as Broadcom doubled the bandwidth of its switch chips every generation.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-scale-up-network\" data-term=\"scale-up network\" data-text=\"scale-up network scale-up fabric, coherent domain, scale-up, scale up, scale-up domain, scale-up switch the network that joins a group of accelerators, from a few dozen in one rack to thousands, so a model too large for a single chip can be spread across them. it runs at terabytes per second. in nvidia's gb300 nvl72 each gpu has nine times as much bandwidth on it as on the scale-out network. the bandwidth of this network limits how efficiently a large model trains. nvidia sells its own nvlink for it, and ualink is a published open standard that competes with nvlink.\">\n<dt>scale-up network<span class=\"aka\">scale-up fabric, coherent domain, scale-up, scale up, scale-up domain, scale-up switch</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The network that joins a group of accelerators, from a few dozen in one rack to thousands, so a model too large for a single chip can be spread across them. It runs at terabytes per second. In Nvidia's GB300 NVL72 each GPU has nine times as much bandwidth on it as on the scale-out network.</p><p class=\"why\">The bandwidth of this network limits how efficiently a large model trains. Nvidia sells its own NVLink for it, and UALink is a published open standard that competes with NVLink.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-scanner\" data-term=\"scanner\" data-text=\"scanner scanners, stepper, steppers, lithography scanner, lithography scanners, lithography machine, lithography system, lithography systems a scanner is the lithography machine itself. it holds the photomask up to a light source and projects a shrunken image of one layer onto the wafer. mask and wafer sweep past each other in a narrow slit of light. an older stepper exposes the whole mask image at once instead of scanning. a standard euv scanner sells for around $200 million. asml makes every euv scanner in the world, so a rule aimed at its scanners reaches all advanced chipmaking.\">\n<dt>scanner<span class=\"aka\">scanners, stepper, steppers, lithography scanner, lithography scanners, lithography machine, lithography system, lithography systems</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A scanner is the lithography machine itself. It holds the photomask up to a light source and projects a shrunken image of one layer onto the wafer. Mask and wafer sweep past each other in a narrow slit of light. An older stepper exposes the whole mask image at once instead of scanning. A standard EUV scanner sells for around $200 million.</p><p class=\"why\">ASML makes every EUV scanner in the world, so a rule aimed at its scanners reaches all advanced chipmaking.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-second-source\" data-term=\"second source\" data-text=\"second source second sources, second-source, multi-sourcing, dual source, single source, sole source, single-source a second source is a second supplier qualified for the same part or material, so that a fab can keep running if the first one stops shipping. a single-source part has none, and adding one means joint development and a fresh qualification. when japan put three chemicals under export licenses for south korea in 2019, south korea bought more from other countries. output of all three chemicals rose at south korean firms and at japanese companies' affiliates in south korea.\">\n<dt>second source<span class=\"aka\">second sources, second-source, multi-sourcing, dual source, single source, sole source, single-source</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A second source is a second supplier qualified for the same part or material, so that a fab can keep running if the first one stops shipping. A single-source part has none, and adding one means joint development and a fresh qualification.</p><p class=\"why\">When Japan put three chemicals under export licenses for South Korea in 2019, South Korea bought more from other countries. Output of all three chemicals rose at South Korean firms and at Japanese companies' affiliates in South Korea.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-serdes\" data-term=\"serdes\" data-text=\"serdes serializer-deserializer, high-speed serial links, serial links, serial link a serdes, for serializer-deserializer, is the circuit at the edge of a chip that turns many slow parallel signals into one very fast stream over a single pair of wires. a serdes at the other end turns the stream back into parallel signals. every link out of an accelerator, to another chip, a switch or an optical module, runs through one. serdes speed sets how much data a chip can move. many chip designers license the blocks as ip, and each design has to be proven in silicon on every new process.\">\n<dt>SerDes<span class=\"aka\">serializer-deserializer, high-speed serial links, serial links, serial link</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A SerDes, for serializer-deserializer, is the circuit at the edge of a chip that turns many slow parallel signals into one very fast stream over a single pair of wires. A SerDes at the other end turns the stream back into parallel signals. Every link out of an accelerator, to another chip, a switch or an optical module, runs through one.</p><p class=\"why\">SerDes speed sets how much data a chip can move. Many chip designers license the blocks as IP, and each design has to be proven in silicon on every new process.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"systems-and-networking/\">Read it in Systems and Networking →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-signoff\" data-term=\"signoff\" data-text=\"signoff sign-off, static timing analysis, timing signoff, timing sign-off, physical verification, signed off signoff is the final set of automated checks a chip design must pass before tape-out. static timing analysis checks that every signal arrives in time at the clock speed promised. physical verification checks that every shape in the layout can be printed. a foundry accepts only layouts that pass physical verification against its rules. at advanced nodes, synopsys holds more than 90 percent of timing signoff, and siemens more than 85 percent of physical verification.\">\n<dt>signoff<span class=\"aka\">sign-off, static timing analysis, timing signoff, timing sign-off, physical verification, signed off</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Signoff is the final set of automated checks a chip design must pass before tape-out. Static timing analysis checks that every signal arrives in time at the clock speed promised. Physical verification checks that every shape in the layout can be printed.</p><p class=\"why\">A foundry accepts only layouts that pass physical verification against its rules. At advanced nodes, Synopsys holds more than 90 percent of timing signoff, and Siemens more than 85 percent of physical verification.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-silicon-bridge\" data-term=\"silicon bridge\" data-text=\"silicon bridge silicon bridges, emib, silicon-bridge, local silicon bridges, embedded bridge a silicon bridge is a small sliver of silicon carrying dense wiring. it is set into the package only where two dies need thousands of connections between them, so the rest of the package can use cheaper wiring. intel calls its version emib, and tsmc's cowos-l uses the same idea. bridges let a package grow past a single interposer's size limit, and cowos-l uses them to package nvidia's blackwell and rubin chips. the bridges in blackwell needed very high placement accuracy, and packaging issues limited its supply.\">\n<dt>silicon bridge<span class=\"aka\">silicon bridges, EMIB, silicon-bridge, local silicon bridges, embedded bridge</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A silicon bridge is a small sliver of silicon carrying dense wiring. It is set into the package only where two dies need thousands of connections between them, so the rest of the package can use cheaper wiring. Intel calls its version EMIB, and TSMC's CoWoS-L uses the same idea.</p><p class=\"why\">Bridges let a package grow past a single interposer's size limit, and CoWoS-L uses them to package Nvidia's Blackwell and Rubin chips. The bridges in Blackwell needed very high placement accuracy, and packaging issues limited its supply.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-silicon-shield\" data-term=\"silicon shield\" data-text=\"silicon shield  the argument that taiwan's lead in advanced chipmaking deters an attack on the island, because so many countries rely on its chips. the idea is central to debate about taiwan's security, and it is contested. it holds only while taiwan's chipmaking is hard to replace, so taiwan keeps its newest chip processes at home first while the united states pushes for more chipmaking on its own soil.\">\n<dt>silicon shield</dt>\n<dd><p>The argument that Taiwan's lead in advanced chipmaking deters an attack on the island, because so many countries rely on its chips.</p><p class=\"why\">The idea is central to debate about Taiwan's security, and it is contested. It holds only while Taiwan's chipmaking is hard to replace, so Taiwan keeps its newest chip processes at home first while the United States pushes for more chipmaking on its own soil.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-small-yard-high-fence\" data-term=\"small yard, high fence\" data-text=\"small yard, high fence small yard with a high fence, small yard the stated design of us technology controls: tightly restrict a narrow set of items that genuinely matter to national security, and leave the rest of trade alone. it gives critics and defenders a test for whether export controls remain targeted security policy or have become general industrial policy.\">\n<dt>small yard, high fence<span class=\"aka\">small yard with a high fence, small yard</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The stated design of US technology controls: tightly restrict a narrow set of items that genuinely matter to national security, and leave the rest of trade alone.</p><p class=\"why\">It gives critics and defenders a test for whether export controls remain targeted security policy or have become general industrial policy.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-soc\" data-term=\"soc\" data-text=\"soc system on a chip, system-on-chip, system-on-a-chip, socs a system on a chip, or soc, is a single chip that combines processor cores, a graphics processor and other circuit blocks that a device needs. the main processor in a smartphone is one. makers of chip testers split their market in two. soc testers check processors and other non-memory chips, and memory testers check memory. advantest put soc testers at about $6.9 billion of a $9.0 billion tester market in 2025.\">\n<dt>SoC<span class=\"aka\">system on a chip, system-on-chip, system-on-a-chip, SoCs</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A system on a chip, or SoC, is a single chip that combines processor cores, a graphics processor and other circuit blocks that a device needs. The main processor in a smartphone is one.</p><p class=\"why\">Makers of chip testers split their market in two. SoC testers check processors and other non-memory chips, and memory testers check memory. Advantest put SoC testers at about $6.9 billion of a $9.0 billion tester market in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-specialty-gases\" data-term=\"specialty gases\" data-text=\"specialty gases specialty gas, electronic specialty gases, bulk gases, bulk gas, electronic gases, process gas, process gases specialty gases are the gases a fab uses in small amounts, each for one job. silane, for example, carries silicon into the chamber to build a film, and nitrogen trifluoride cleans the chamber. they arrive in cylinders. bulk gases, such as nitrogen and oxygen, come by pipeline or from plants built at the fab. specialty gases are shipped to the fab in cylinders, so a government or a war can cut them off. ukraine supplied about 70 percent of the world's neon before russia invaded in 2022.\">\n<dt>specialty gases<span class=\"aka\">specialty gas, electronic specialty gases, bulk gases, bulk gas, electronic gases, process gas, process gases</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Specialty gases are the gases a fab uses in small amounts, each for one job. Silane, for example, carries silicon into the chamber to build a film, and nitrogen trifluoride cleans the chamber. They arrive in cylinders. Bulk gases, such as nitrogen and oxygen, come by pipeline or from plants built at the fab.</p><p class=\"why\">Specialty gases are shipped to the fab in cylinders, so a government or a war can cut them off. Ukraine supplied about 70 percent of the world's neon before Russia invaded in 2022.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-sram\" data-term=\"sram\" data-text=\"sram static random-access memory, cache, on-chip memory, on-die sram, on-die memory, l2 cache sram is the fast memory built from transistors on the logic chip itself, used as a cache that holds the numbers a processor is about to need. it is far faster than the memory stacks beside the chip and holds far less. the cell that holds one bit has barely shrunk since the 5 nm node, which limits how much cache a designer can afford to put on an accelerator.\">\n<dt>SRAM<span class=\"aka\">static random-access memory, cache, on-chip memory, on-die SRAM, on-die memory, L2 cache</span></dt>\n<dd><p>SRAM is the fast memory built from transistors on the logic chip itself, used as a cache that holds the numbers a processor is about to need. It is far faster than the memory stacks beside the chip and holds far less.</p><p class=\"why\">The cell that holds one bit has barely shrunk since the 5 nm node, which limits how much cache a designer can afford to put on an accelerator.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-subject-to-the-ear\" data-term=\"subject to the ear\" data-text=\"subject to the ear  the test for whether an item falls under us export rules at all. under 15 cfr 734.3 it covers anything in the united states and anything of us origin wherever it is. it also covers foreign-made goods that contain more than a permitted share of controlled us content, and foreign-made goods caught by a foreign direct product rule. the test applies to the item, whatever the seller's nationality. the rules follow the item, so a dutch or korean firm shipping between two foreign countries can still need a us license.\">\n<dt>subject to the EAR</dt>\n<dd><p>The test for whether an item falls under US export rules at all. Under 15 CFR 734.3 it covers anything in the United States and anything of US origin wherever it is. It also covers foreign-made goods that contain more than a permitted share of controlled US content, and foreign-made goods caught by a foreign direct product rule. The test applies to the item, whatever the seller's nationality.</p><p class=\"why\">The rules follow the item, so a Dutch or Korean firm shipping between two foreign countries can still need a US license.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-substitutability\" data-term=\"substitutability\" data-text=\"substitutability substitutability rating a four-band rating of how hard it would be for a well-funded state or firm, starting today, to build an alternative to the leading suppliers at one stage of the supply chain. it is judged against four written tests. easy: a second supplier is qualified, meaning approved by customers, and shipping today at the leading node, the most advanced process. moderate: a second supplier exists but is not yet qualified at the leading node, and closing the gap takes about two to five years. hard: no second supplier exists at the leading node, the path to one is known, and closing the gap takes five to ten years. very hard: no second supplier exists, and the path depends on physics, decades of unwritten know-how or protected intellectual property. no one has yet repeated what the leaders did, and closing the gap takes ten years or more. the years are always counted for that same well-funded state or firm, and the count stops at qualification, which comes well after a prototype. it says how long a rival or a government would need to replace a stage. the debate over export controls turns on that question.\">\n<dt>Substitutability<span class=\"aka\">substitutability rating</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A four-band rating of how hard it would be for a well-funded state or firm, starting today, to build an alternative to the leading suppliers at one stage of the supply chain. It is judged against four written tests. Easy: a second supplier is qualified, meaning approved by customers, and shipping today at the leading node, the most advanced process. Moderate: a second supplier exists but is not yet qualified at the leading node, and closing the gap takes about two to five years. Hard: no second supplier exists at the leading node, the path to one is known, and closing the gap takes five to ten years. Very hard: no second supplier exists, and the path depends on physics, decades of unwritten know-how or protected intellectual property. No one has yet repeated what the leaders did, and closing the gap takes ten years or more. The years are always counted for that same well-funded state or firm, and the count stops at qualification, which comes well after a prototype.</p><p class=\"why\">It says how long a rival or a government would need to replace a stage. The debate over export controls turns on that question.</p></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-substrate\" data-term=\"substrate\" data-text=\"substrate package substrate, ic substrate, substrates, build-up substrate, build-up substrates, package substrates, ic substrates, resin substrate the small, dense circuit board at the base of a chip package. the chips sit on it, and it spreads their microscopic connections out to the millimeter-scale solder balls a motherboard can accept. it is built up layer by layer from epoxy film, laser-drilled holes and plated copper. a handful of firms, most of them in asia, build these substrates for others. as packages grow, a substrate warps more and needs more layers, so fewer come out working.\">\n<dt>substrate<span class=\"aka\">package substrate, IC substrate, substrates, build-up substrate, build-up substrates, package substrates, IC substrates, resin substrate</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The small, dense circuit board at the base of a chip package. The chips sit on it, and it spreads their microscopic connections out to the millimeter-scale solder balls a motherboard can accept. It is built up layer by layer from epoxy film, laser-drilled holes and plated copper.</p><p class=\"why\">A handful of firms, most of them in Asia, build these substrates for others. As packages grow, a substrate warps more and needs more layers, so fewer come out working.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"substrates-and-pcbs/\">Read it in Substrates and PCBs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-tape-out\" data-term=\"tape-out\" data-text=\"tape-out tape out, taped out, tapes out, tape-outs, tapeout the moment a chip design is declared finished and the pattern files are sent to the factory to be written into masks. the name survives from when the data physically left on a reel of magnetic tape. each revision after tape-out, called a respin, needs at least some new masks. in may 2026 semianalysis put a single respin at leading-edge nodes at $50 million to $100 million, so designers check everything they can before tape-out.\">\n<dt>tape-out<span class=\"aka\">tape out, taped out, tapes out, tape-outs, tapeout</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The moment a chip design is declared finished and the pattern files are sent to the factory to be written into masks. The name survives from when the data physically left on a reel of magnetic tape.</p><p class=\"why\">Each revision after tape-out, called a respin, needs at least some new masks. In May 2026 SemiAnalysis put a single respin at leading-edge nodes at $50 million to $100 million, so designers check everything they can before tape-out.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-tc-ncf\" data-term=\"tc-ncf\" data-text=\"tc-ncf mr-muf, advanced mr-muf, tc-ncf bonding tc-ncf and mr-muf are two ways of joining the thinned memory chips in an hbm stack. in tc-ncf, thermocompression with non-conductive film, each chip is pressed onto the one below under heat, with a thin insulating film between them. samsung uses it for its twelve-high hbm3e. in mr-muf, used by sk hynix, the chips are stacked first, and a liquid protective material is injected between them and hardened. thinner chips and taller stacks warp more easily, and both methods aim to control that. sk hynix says its advanced mr-muf also dissipates heat well.\">\n<dt>TC-NCF<span class=\"aka\">MR-MUF, Advanced MR-MUF, TC-NCF bonding</span></dt>\n<dd><p>TC-NCF and MR-MUF are two ways of joining the thinned memory chips in an HBM stack. In TC-NCF, thermocompression with non-conductive film, each chip is pressed onto the one below under heat, with a thin insulating film between them. Samsung uses it for its twelve-high HBM3E. In MR-MUF, used by SK hynix, the chips are stacked first, and a liquid protective material is injected between them and hardened.</p><p class=\"why\">Thinner chips and taller stacks warp more easily, and both methods aim to control that. SK hynix says its Advanced MR-MUF also dissipates heat well.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-thermocompression-bonding\" data-term=\"thermocompression bonding\" data-text=\"thermocompression bonding thermocompression, thermo-compression bonding, thermocompression bonder, thermocompression bonders, tcb, die bonder, die bonders, bonder, bonders thermocompression bonding presses one die onto another, or onto a substrate, under heat and force until the tiny solder bumps between them melt and join. it is how memory dies are stacked to make high bandwidth memory (hbm) and a growing way to place chiplets on a package. asmpt says it remained the leader in these bonders in 2025, when its revenue from them rose about 146 percent. it aims for 35 to 40 percent of a market it puts at $1.6 billion in 2028.\">\n<dt>thermocompression bonding<span class=\"aka\">thermocompression, thermo-compression bonding, thermocompression bonder, thermocompression bonders, TCB, die bonder, die bonders, bonder, bonders</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Thermocompression bonding presses one die onto another, or onto a substrate, under heat and force until the tiny solder bumps between them melt and join. It is how memory dies are stacked to make high bandwidth memory (HBM) and a growing way to place chiplets on a package.</p><p class=\"why\">ASMPT says it remained the leader in these bonders in 2025, when its revenue from them rose about 146 percent. It aims for 35 to 40 percent of a market it puts at $1.6 billion in 2028.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-throughput\" data-term=\"throughput\" data-text=\"throughput wafers an hour, wafers per hour, wafers-per-hour throughput is how many wafers a machine can process in an hour. asml's nxe:3800e euv scanner reaches 220. throughput sets the cost of each layer and how many lots, or batches of wafers, a fab can afford to inspect. brighter euv light sources and multi-beam inspection tools both aim to raise it.\">\n<dt>throughput<span class=\"aka\">wafers an hour, wafers per hour, wafers-per-hour</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Throughput is how many wafers a machine can process in an hour. ASML's NXE:3800E EUV scanner reaches 220.</p><p class=\"why\">Throughput sets the cost of each layer and how many lots, or batches of wafers, a fab can afford to inspect. Brighter EUV light sources and multi-beam inspection tools both aim to raise it.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"lithography/\">Read it in Lithography →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-tpp\" data-term=\"tpp\" data-text=\"tpp total processing performance total processing performance, the measure us export rules use for a chip's computing power. it starts from the number of multiply-accumulate operations, a multiply followed by an add, that the chip does each second. that number is doubled, multiplied by the number of bits in each operation, and added up across every processing unit on the chip. the definition is in eccn 3a090, in supplement no. 1 to 15 cfr part 774. the export rules for chip sales to china draw their lines in tpp. the top band, 3a090.a, starts at 4,800 tpp, or at 1,600 tpp with a performance density of 5.92. since 15 january 2026, export applications for chips below 21,000 tpp and 6,500 gb/s of total dram bandwidth, such as the h200, are reviewed case by case for end users in china and macau (91 fr 1684).\">\n<dt>TPP<span class=\"aka\">total processing performance</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Total processing performance, the measure US export rules use for a chip's computing power. It starts from the number of multiply-accumulate operations, a multiply followed by an add, that the chip does each second. That number is doubled, multiplied by the number of bits in each operation, and added up across every processing unit on the chip. The definition is in ECCN 3A090, in supplement no. 1 to 15 CFR part 774.</p><p class=\"why\">The export rules for chip sales to China draw their lines in TPP. The top band, 3A090.a, starts at 4,800 TPP, or at 1,600 TPP with a performance density of 5.92. Since 15 January 2026, export applications for chips below 21,000 TPP and 6,500 GB/s of total DRAM bandwidth, such as the H200, are reviewed case by case for end users in China and Macau (91 FR 1684).</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-tpu\" data-term=\"tpu\" data-text=\"tpu tensor processing unit, tpus google's own ai chip, designed in-house for its data centers and cloud service. its eighth generation, announced in april 2026, is split into two chips, the tpu 8t for training and the tpu 8i for inference. it shows that a large buyer can design its own alternative to chips sold on the open market. ironwood, the seventh generation, carries 192 gb of memory per chip, six times its predecessor's. google says the tpu 8t and tpu 8i deliver up to twice ironwood's performance per watt.\">\n<dt>TPU<span class=\"aka\">Tensor Processing Unit, TPUs</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Google's own AI chip, designed in-house for its data centers and cloud service. Its eighth generation, announced in April 2026, is split into two chips, the TPU 8t for training and the TPU 8i for inference.</p><p class=\"why\">It shows that a large buyer can design its own alternative to chips sold on the open market. Ironwood, the seventh generation, carries 192 GB of memory per chip, six times its predecessor's. Google says the TPU 8t and TPU 8i deliver up to twice Ironwood's performance per watt.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-transistor\" data-term=\"transistor\" data-text=\"transistor transistors the switch every chip is built from. current runs through a channel between two terminals. a voltage on a third terminal, the gate, opens or closes that path, much as a tap opens or closes a pipe. one nvidia blackwell part contains 208 billion of them. the whole chip supply chain exists to make transistors smaller, faster and less leaky. only three companies, tsmc, intel and samsung, make the newest kind in volume.\">\n<dt>transistor<span class=\"aka\">transistors</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The switch every chip is built from. Current runs through a channel between two terminals. A voltage on a third terminal, the gate, opens or closes that path, much as a tap opens or closes a pipe. One Nvidia Blackwell part contains 208 billion of them.</p><p class=\"why\">The whole chip supply chain exists to make transistors smaller, faster and less leaky. Only three companies, TSMC, Intel and Samsung, make the newest kind in volume.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-transistor-density\" data-term=\"transistor density\" data-text=\"transistor density logic density, chip density, transistors per square millimeter, density gain transistor density is how many transistors fit in a square millimeter of chip. semianalysis measured smic's n+3 at 113.4 million, against 107.7 million for tsmc's n6. tsmc says n2p gives 1.2 times the logic density and 1.15 times the chip density of n3e. a16, which adds backside power, gives up to 1.10 times the chip density of n2p. tsmc says a14, planned for 2028, will give more than 20 percent more logic density than n2. density sets how much logic fits on a die of a given size. no foundry publishes wafer prices, so cost per transistor cannot be worked out from public figures.\">\n<dt>transistor density<span class=\"aka\">logic density, chip density, transistors per square millimeter, density gain</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Transistor density is how many transistors fit in a square millimeter of chip. SemiAnalysis measured SMIC's N+3 at 113.4 million, against 107.7 million for TSMC's N6. TSMC says N2P gives 1.2 times the logic density and 1.15 times the chip density of N3E. A16, which adds backside power, gives up to 1.10 times the chip density of N2P. TSMC says A14, planned for 2028, will give more than 20 percent more logic density than N2.</p><p class=\"why\">Density sets how much logic fits on a die of a given size. No foundry publishes wafer prices, so cost per transistor cannot be worked out from public figures.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-tsv\" data-term=\"tsv\" data-text=\"tsv through-silicon via, tsvs, through-silicon vias, through silicon via, through silicon vias a copper column that runs all the way through a chip so that power and signals can pass from its top face to its bottom face. it makes stacking chips vertically possible, in the way an elevator shaft makes a tall building usable. high bandwidth memory depends on these columns. us rules control the tools that cut the holes for them, and define those tools by hole shape and etching speed.\">\n<dt>TSV<span class=\"aka\">through-silicon via, TSVs, through-silicon vias, through silicon via, through silicon vias</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A copper column that runs all the way through a chip so that power and signals can pass from its top face to its bottom face. It makes stacking chips vertically possible, in the way an elevator shaft makes a tall building usable.</p><p class=\"why\">High bandwidth memory depends on these columns. US rules control the tools that cut the holes for them, and define those tools by hole shape and etching speed.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"memory-and-hbm/\">Read it in Memory and HBM →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-twh\" data-term=\"twh\" data-text=\"twh terawatt-hour, terawatt-hours, terawatt hours a terawatt-hour is a billion kilowatt-hours, the unit national electricity use is counted in. us data centers used 192 twh in 2024, 4.7 percent of the country's electricity. lawrence berkeley national laboratory's reference case projects 649 twh in 2030, 11.8 percent of forecast us electricity use, within a range of 521 to 843 twh.\">\n<dt>TWh<span class=\"aka\">terawatt-hour, terawatt-hours, terawatt hours</span></dt>\n<dd><p>A terawatt-hour is a billion kilowatt-hours, the unit national electricity use is counted in. US data centers used 192 TWh in 2024, 4.7 percent of the country's electricity.</p><p class=\"why\">Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory's reference case projects 649 TWh in 2030, 11.8 percent of forecast US electricity use, within a range of 521 to 843 TWh.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"data-centers-and-power/\">Read it in Data Centers and Power →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-ucie\" data-term=\"ucie\" data-text=\"ucie universal chiplet interconnect express, ucie 3.0 ucie is an open standard for the short, very fast link between two chiplets sitting side by side in one package. it lets chiplets from different vendors be wired together, the way pcie lets cards from different vendors share a computer. accelerators too large to print as one chip are built from chiplets, and a shared standard lets more firms supply the pieces.\">\n<dt>UCIe<span class=\"aka\">Universal Chiplet Interconnect Express, UCIe 3.0</span></dt>\n<dd><p>UCIe is an open standard for the short, very fast link between two chiplets sitting side by side in one package. It lets chiplets from different vendors be wired together, the way PCIe lets cards from different vendors share a computer.</p><p class=\"why\">Accelerators too large to print as one chip are built from chiplets, and a shared standard lets more firms supply the pieces.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"design-and-eda/\">Read it in Chip Design, EDA and IP →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-us-person\" data-term=\"us person\" data-text=\"us person us persons, u.s. person, u.s. persons in export law a us person is any american citizen, permanent resident or company, wherever in the world they are, and anyone in the united states. since october 2022 a us person may not service or support an advanced chip fab in china without a license. the rule reaches people as well as goods, so american citizens, residents and companies need a license to support advanced chipmaking in china.\">\n<dt>US person<span class=\"aka\">US persons, U.S. person, U.S. persons</span></dt>\n<dd><p>In export law a US person is any American citizen, permanent resident or company, wherever in the world they are, and anyone in the United States. Since October 2022 a US person may not service or support an advanced chip fab in China without a license.</p><p class=\"why\">The rule reaches people as well as goods, so American citizens, residents and companies need a license to support advanced chipmaking in China.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-utilization\" data-term=\"utilization\" data-text=\"utilization utilization rate, fab utilization utilization is how full a fab's lines are running, as a share of what they could run. most of a fab's costs, such as paying off its tools, stay the same whether it runs full or half empty, so utilization largely decides whether it makes money. smic ran its lines 93.5 percent full in 2025, and its gross margin that year was 21 percent.\">\n<dt>utilization<span class=\"aka\">utilization rate, fab utilization</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Utilization is how full a fab's lines are running, as a share of what they could run. Most of a fab's costs, such as paying off its tools, stay the same whether it runs full or half empty, so utilization largely decides whether it makes money.</p><p class=\"why\">SMIC ran its lines 93.5 percent full in 2025, and its gross margin that year was 21 percent.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-veu\" data-term=\"veu\" data-text=\"veu validated end-user, validated end user, validated end-user status, veu status, veu cover, validated end users an authorization that bis, the us commerce department office that licenses exports, grants to a named foreign facility, so approved items can ship to it without an individual license each time. the approved facilities are listed in supplement no. 7 to 15 cfr part 748, and the procedure is set out in 15 cfr 748.15. it let the china subsidiaries of samsung and sk hynix, and the dalian nand flash memory fab that sk hynix bought from intel, receive us equipment without individual licenses. bis revoked that status effective 31 december 2025 (90 fr 42321). it said it would license those fabs to keep running, but not to expand capacity or upgrade technology (90 fr 42321). in december 2025 bis granted sk hynix an annual license to ship approved us equipment to its china fabs during 2026.\">\n<dt>VEU<span class=\"aka\">Validated End-User, Validated End User, Validated End-User status, VEU status, VEU cover, validated end users</span></dt>\n<dd><p>An authorization that BIS, the US Commerce Department office that licenses exports, grants to a named foreign facility, so approved items can ship to it without an individual license each time. The approved facilities are listed in supplement no. 7 to 15 CFR part 748, and the procedure is set out in 15 CFR 748.15.</p><p class=\"why\">It let the China subsidiaries of Samsung and SK hynix, and the Dalian NAND flash memory fab that SK hynix bought from Intel, receive US equipment without individual licenses. BIS revoked that status effective 31 December 2025 (90 FR 42321). It said it would license those fabs to keep running, but not to expand capacity or upgrade technology (90 FR 42321). In December 2025 BIS granted SK hynix an annual license to ship approved US equipment to its China fabs during 2026.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"geopolitics/\">Read it in Who Controls the Chain →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-vias\" data-term=\"vias\" data-text=\"vias copper vias, vertical vias, vertical copper vias vias are the small vertical holes, filled with metal, that connect one layer of wiring to the layer above or below it. a chip's wiring is full of them. an interposer has them through its whole thickness, and a package substrate has them drilled by laser through each sheet of film. every added layer brings another set of vias that can fail, so yield falls as packages and substrates grow.\">\n<dt>vias<span class=\"aka\">copper vias, vertical vias, vertical copper vias</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Vias are the small vertical holes, filled with metal, that connect one layer of wiring to the layer above or below it. A chip's wiring is full of them. An interposer has them through its whole thickness, and a package substrate has them drilled by laser through each sheet of film.</p><p class=\"why\">Every added layer brings another set of vias that can fail, so yield falls as packages and substrates grow.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"advanced-packaging/\">Read it in Advanced Packaging →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-wafer\" data-term=\"wafer\" data-text=\"wafer silicon wafer, 300 mm wafer, wafers, silicon wafers, 300 mm wafers the polished disc of ultrapure silicon that chips are built on, 300 millimeters across for advanced chips. hundreds of chips are printed on one wafer and cut apart at the end. a flaw wastes more silicon on a large ai chip than on a small one, so ai chips need wafers that are nearly flawless and flat to the edge. the top five wafer makers hold around 75 percent of a market worth $11.4 billion in 2025.\">\n<dt>wafer<span class=\"aka\">silicon wafer, 300 mm wafer, wafers, silicon wafers, 300 mm wafers</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The polished disc of ultrapure silicon that chips are built on, 300 millimeters across for advanced chips. Hundreds of chips are printed on one wafer and cut apart at the end.</p><p class=\"why\">A flaw wastes more silicon on a large AI chip than on a small one, so AI chips need wafers that are nearly flawless and flat to the edge. The top five wafer makers hold around 75 percent of a market worth $11.4 billion in 2025.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"silicon-and-wafers/\">Read it in Silicon and Wafers →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-wafer-fab-equipment\" data-term=\"wafer fab equipment\" data-text=\"wafer fab equipment wfe, front-end equipment, equipment billings, wafer processing equipment, semiconductor equipment, chipmaking tools, chipmaking equipment the collective name for the machines that process wafers inside a fab: printing systems, deposition and etch chambers, cleaning tools and measurement systems. it excludes the packaging and test machines used afterward. spending on it shows how much new chipmaking capacity is being built. world sales of all chipmaking equipment reached $135.1 billion in 2025, and sales of wafer processing tools rose 12 percent.\">\n<dt>wafer fab equipment<span class=\"aka\">WFE, front-end equipment, equipment billings, wafer processing equipment, semiconductor equipment, chipmaking tools, chipmaking equipment</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The collective name for the machines that process wafers inside a fab: printing systems, deposition and etch chambers, cleaning tools and measurement systems. It excludes the packaging and test machines used afterward.</p><p class=\"why\">Spending on it shows how much new chipmaking capacity is being built. World sales of all chipmaking equipment reached $135.1 billion in 2025, and sales of wafer processing tools rose 12 percent.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"deposition-and-etch/\">Read it in Deposition and Etch →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-wafer-sort\" data-term=\"wafer sort\" data-text=\"wafer sort wafer test, probe test, wafer probe wafer sort is the first test a chip gets, while it is still on the wafer. thousands of needles on a probe card press onto the pads of one die, or of several dies at once, and a tester drives signals in and reads the answers. any die that answers wrong is marked and never packaged. proving a die good before it is packaged keeps one bad die from scrapping the memory stacks and substrate it would be joined to.\">\n<dt>wafer sort<span class=\"aka\">wafer test, probe test, wafer probe</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Wafer sort is the first test a chip gets, while it is still on the wafer. Thousands of needles on a probe card press onto the pads of one die, or of several dies at once, and a tester drives signals in and reads the answers. Any die that answers wrong is marked and never packaged.</p><p class=\"why\">Proving a die good before it is packaged keeps one bad die from scrapping the memory stacks and substrate it would be joined to.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"test-and-assembly/\">Read it in Test and Assembly →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-wafers-per-month\" data-term=\"wafers per month\" data-text=\"wafers per month wafers a month, wafer starts, wafer starts per month, wspm, wafer starts a month, million wafers per month wafers per month is how fab capacity is counted: the number of wafers a plant can start through its line each month. a tsmc gigafab runs more than 100,000. in september 2025 semianalysis conservatively put smic's capacity at 7 nm and below at 45,000 a month by the end of 2025. figures are often converted to 8-inch or 12-inch equivalents so plants with different wafer sizes can be compared. in june 2024 the industry association semi forecast china at 10.1 million wafers a month in 2025, the most of any region. in 2026 it projected china would stay largest through 2027, but little of that capacity is advanced.\">\n<dt>wafers per month<span class=\"aka\">wafers a month, wafer starts, wafer starts per month, WSPM, wafer starts a month, million wafers per month</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Wafers per month is how fab capacity is counted: the number of wafers a plant can start through its line each month. A TSMC gigafab runs more than 100,000. In September 2025 SemiAnalysis conservatively put SMIC's capacity at 7 nm and below at 45,000 a month by the end of 2025. Figures are often converted to 8-inch or 12-inch equivalents so plants with different wafer sizes can be compared.</p><p class=\"why\">In June 2024 the industry association SEMI forecast China at 10.1 million wafers a month in 2025, the most of any region. In 2026 it projected China would stay largest through 2027, but little of that capacity is advanced.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"foundries-and-fabs/\">Read it in Foundries and Fabs →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-wet-chemicals\" data-term=\"wet chemicals\" data-text=\"wet chemicals wet chemical, wet processing, wet clean, cleaning chemicals, process chemicals wet chemicals are the liquids a wafer is dipped in or sprayed with between steps: acids that strip a layer, solvents that remove resist, and ultrapure water rinses. wet processing is any step done in liquid. cset's january 2021 brief, drawing on 2019 market reports, put five firms at more than 60 percent of the wet chemicals market. bis controls wet processing tools by how selectively they etch one material over another.\">\n<dt>wet chemicals<span class=\"aka\">wet chemical, wet processing, wet clean, cleaning chemicals, process chemicals</span></dt>\n<dd><p>Wet chemicals are the liquids a wafer is dipped in or sprayed with between steps: acids that strip a layer, solvents that remove resist, and ultrapure water rinses. Wet processing is any step done in liquid.</p><p class=\"why\">CSET's January 2021 brief, drawing on 2019 market reports, put five firms at more than 60 percent of the wet chemicals market. BIS controls wet processing tools by how selectively they etch one material over another.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist/\">Read it in Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist →</a></dd>\n</div><div class=\"gl-entry\" id=\"gl-yield\" data-term=\"yield\" data-text=\"yield die yield, yields, packaging yield, package yield, stack yield the percentage of chips on a wafer that work. flaws land at random, so the larger the chip the more likely it is to catch one, and yield falls steeply as chips get bigger. yield sets the cost of a working ai chip. epoch ai models the blackwell compute die at 40 to 70 percent good, with 60 percent as its central estimate. in the same model, the cost of packages that fail testing, spread across the ones that pass, adds about $1,000 to each b200.\">\n<dt>yield<span class=\"aka\">die yield, yields, packaging yield, package yield, stack yield</span></dt>\n<dd><p>The percentage of chips on a wafer that work. Flaws land at random, so the larger the chip the more likely it is to catch one, and yield falls steeply as chips get bigger.</p><p class=\"why\">Yield sets the cost of a working AI chip. Epoch AI models the Blackwell compute die at 40 to 70 percent good, with 60 percent as its central estimate. In the same model, the cost of packages that fail testing, spread across the ones that pass, adds about $1,000 to each B200.</p><a class=\"gl-link\" href=\"component-costs/\">Read it in The Economics of AI Chips →</a></dd>\n</div>","passages":{"chapters":{"design-and-eda":["Chip Design, EDA and IP","01"],"silicon-and-wafers":["Silicon and Wafers","02"],"chemicals-gases-and-photoresist":["Chemicals, Gases and Photoresist","03"],"lithography":["Lithography","04"],"photomasks-and-pellicles":["Photomasks and Pellicles","05"],"deposition-and-etch":["Deposition and Etch","06"],"metrology-and-inspection":["Metrology and Inspection","07"],"foundries-and-fabs":["Foundries and Fabs","08"],"memory-and-hbm":["Memory and HBM","09"],"advanced-packaging":["Advanced Packaging","10"],"substrates-and-pcbs":["Substrates and PCBs","11"],"test-and-assembly":["Test and Assembly","12"],"systems-and-networking":["Systems and Networking","13"],"data-centers-and-power":["Data Centers and Power","14"],"component-costs":["The Economics of AI Chips","15"],"geopolitics":["Who Controls the Chain","16"]},"paras":[["design-and-eda","Chapter 01 Stage 1 of 14 Extreme concentration · Hard to substitute"],["design-and-eda","Synopsys, Cadence and Siemens EDA make the software used to design every advanced chip. In 2025 they took over 85 percent of its $18 billion market, licensed blocks included."],["design-and-eda","Chip design turns an idea for a new chip into a complete blueprint. A chip holds billions of transistors, tiny electrical switches. The blueprint fixes where each one sits and how it is wired to the others. The chip runs on a clock, and a signal has to cross those wires within one tick, less than a billionth of a second. Software from three companies, Synopsys, Cadence and Siemens, lays out the blueprint, checks it and signs it off. A foundry, a factory that makes chips for other companies, accepts only designs that have passed that software's checks. The foundry prints each layer of the design onto silicon through a stencil called a mask. Changing the blueprint once the masks are made takes new masks and a few months."],["design-and-eda","At advanced nodes, 7 nm and below, Synopsys alone has more than 90 percent of the market for static timing analysis, the check that every signal arrives in time. SemiAnalysis wrote in May 2026 that no startup can replicate a complete design flow by writing it from scratch."],["design-and-eda","Since October 2022 a US license has been needed to export design software specially made for chips with gate-all-around transistors, a transistor design the rule calls key to processes at 3 nm and below. As of 2025, the think tank CSIS found Chinese design tools still far from replacing the full range of advanced capabilities US firms offer, especially for 5 nm and 3 nm chip design. But Chinese design-software companies were winning share at older manufacturing processes, the research firm SemiAnalysis reported."],["design-and-eda","Design is the only stage of the supply chain that happens entirely in software. The US government has restricted it with letters to the companies that sell that software. In late May 2025 the government required a license to sell chip design software to anyone in China. Cadence cut off its Chinese customers until the government lifted the requirement on 2 July."],["design-and-eda","Synopsys Over 90 percent of the timing-signoff market at advanced nodes as of 2026"],["design-and-eda","Cadence 55 to 60 percent of the hardware emulator market at advanced nodes as of 2026"],["design-and-eda","Siemens EDA Over 85 percent of physical verification, the final layout check, at advanced nodes as of 2026"],["design-and-eda","Arm About 50 percent of processor compute at the top cloud firms as of May 2026"],["design-and-eda","Broadcom $16.7 billion of AI semiconductor revenue in the third quarter of fiscal 2026, custom accelerators and networking combined"],["design-and-eda","United States Synopsys, Cadence, Broadcom, Marvell and Nvidia"],["design-and-eda","United Kingdom Arm processor and interconnect designs licensed from Cambridge, and since 2026 its own server chip"],["design-and-eda","Taiwan Alchip, Global Unichip and MediaTek: design services that carry a chip to the factory"],["design-and-eda","Israel Annapurna Labs, the AWS design house behind Trainium and Graviton"],["design-and-eda","India Nearly 20 percent of the world's chip design engineers, on the Indian government's count"],["design-and-eda","China designs its own AI accelerators, but Huawei's most powerful chip in 2026, the Ascend 950, delivers about half the computing performance of Nvidia's H100 from 2022, on Epoch AI's estimate. CSIS found that as of 2025 Chinese design tools were still far from replacing the full range of advanced capabilities US firms offer, especially for 5 nm and 3 nm chips."],["design-and-eda","Synopsys and Cadence, the two largest design-software vendors by 2025 revenue, are American."],["design-and-eda","Design runs in five stages, all in software, and each stage's output is the next one's input."],["design-and-eda","Architecture. Engineers fix the shape of the chip: the width of the block that multiplies numbers, the amount of fast on-chip memory beside it and the number of high-bandwidth memory stacks along the chip's edges. The output is a plan."],["design-and-eda","RTL. Engineers write the plan as register-transfer-level code, RTL, in the hardware language SystemVerilog. A register is a small store on the chip that holds one number. On each tick of the chip's clock, every register takes its next value at the same moment. The code says what every register holds on every tick. The output is a text description of the whole chip."],["design-and-eda","Verification. A large team checks that the code does what the plan says. They run it in simulation and prove parts of it correct with mathematics. They also load it into emulators, large machines full of reprogrammable chips that behave like the design, so the chip's own software can boot before any silicon exists."],["design-and-eda","Physical design. Software swaps each piece of the code for a logic cell, a small ready-made circuit the foundry has already proved it can make. It then places the cells on the chip, wires them together and proves that every signal arrives in time."],["design-and-eda","Tape-out. Engineers hand the finished layout to the foundry, a step called tape-out. After tape-out, software turns the layout into pattern files for the mask shop. First it pre-distorts each shape so that the shape prints as drawn, a step called optical proximity correction. Then it cuts the layout into the files a mask writer reads, a step called mask data preparation."],["design-and-eda","All that checking exists because each revision after tape-out, called a respin, needs at least some new masks. In 2022 SemiAnalysis put a full mask set at more than $1 million at 28 nm and more than $10 million at 7 nm. The nanometer labels name process generations, called nodes, each finer than the last, and no longer measure anything. In 2022 SemiAnalysis also expected 3 nm sets to push into the $40 million range. Its May 2026 primer still puts a leading-edge mask set at $40 million, and a single leading-edge respin at $50 million to $100 million."],["design-and-eda","The same 2022 SemiAnalysis article reported that startups had taken chips on TSMC 7 nm, then a leading-edge process, from design to tape-out for $50 million to $75 million, everything included."],["design-and-eda","Nvidia designs its Blackwell GPU once and sells it to everyone, so the buyer gets mature software and a resale market. A custom accelerator, an ASIC, is built for one company's own workload. It handles a narrower range of tasks and is tuned to that workload. Google's tensor processing units ( TPUs ) are custom accelerators of this kind. Ironwood, the seventh generation, which Google announced in April 2025, carries 192 GB of memory per chip, six times its predecessor's, and delivers twice the performance per watt. In April 2026 Google announced its eighth generation as two chips, the TPU 8t for training and the TPU 8i for inference, with up to twice Ironwood's performance per watt."],["design-and-eda","Chip design software is known as electronic design automation, or EDA. Three complete EDA flows exist, each a set of tools that covers every step from code to signoff. SemiAnalysis wrote in May 2026 that no startup can replicate one by writing it from scratch. Changing the synthesis tool, which swaps the code for logic cells, means re-running the steps that follow: placing and wiring the cells, signoff and physical verification. Foundries also specify which signoff tools their customers must use for tape-out."],["design-and-eda","For chips at advanced nodes, 7 nm and below, one vendor holds most of the market inside some steps of the flow. Synopsys alone has more than 90 percent of the market for static timing analysis, the check that every signal arrives in time at the chip's rated speed. In May 2026 SemiAnalysis put Siemens EDA's Calibre at more than 85 percent of physical verification, the final layout check. It put Cadence's Palladium at 55 to 60 percent of hardware emulation."],["design-and-eda","Design houses license ready-made circuit blocks, known as intellectual property or IP, including the processor cores, the interface controllers and the blocks that drive high-bandwidth memory. The block that drives high-bandwidth memory is hard to design, because its signals have to arrive in time across microscopic solder bumps into a stacked memory die."],["design-and-eda","Arm licenses processor designs. In fiscal 2026 it reported $4.92 billion of revenue, $2.61 billion of it royalties. It said Arm-based designs held about 50 percent of the computing power of central processors (CPUs) at the top cloud firms."],["design-and-eda","In 2026 Arm also launched the Arm AGI CPU, the first finished chip that Arm sells. By May 2026, servers built on it could be ordered from ASRock, Lenovo, Quanta and Supermicro."],["design-and-eda","RISC-V is an open instruction set, the basic list of commands a processor understands, and it needs no license. Small RISC-V processors handle control tasks on the chip, and Nvidia uses them in every GPU."],["design-and-eda","The reticle limit caps the size of a single die, one piece of silicon. That limit is the largest area a scanner, the machine that prints the chip's pattern, can expose in one shot. Many large accelerators are built from chiplets, several smaller dies wired together inside one package. UCIe is an open industry standard for the links between them. Version 3.0 of UCIe adds two faster data rates, 48 and 64 billion transfers per second, written GT/s for gigatransfers per second. In a December 2024 presentation, Broadcom described its 3.5D XDSiP platform, which stacks dies face to face and sets the stacks side by side on an interposer. It said the platform packs more than 6,000 mm² of silicon and 12 high-bandwidth memory stacks into one package."],["design-and-eda","Design software, simulation software and licensed blocks made up an $18 billion market in 2025, on SemiAnalysis's count. Synopsys, Cadence and Siemens EDA took more than 85 percent of it, counting Ansys as part of Synopsys. No other vendor had more than 5 percent of any of the main categories of design software. Siemens EDA is a US-based subsidiary of the German firm Siemens."],["design-and-eda","Synopsys is the largest. Its own results put revenue at $7.054 billion for the fiscal year to 31 October 2025, with Ansys, bought that July, contributing $756.6 million. Cadence, whose year ends in December, took $5.297 billion in calendar 2025."],["design-and-eda","The two fiscal years do not line up, so any total for this market depends on which twelve months are counted. It also depends on how much of Ansys the total includes, because Ansys sells to other industries too. SemiAnalysis puts 31 percent of Ansys's business in semiconductors and high technology, 22 percent in aerospace and 18 percent in automotive. It counts Synopsys at $8 billion for calendar 2025 with Ansys included. On the same count Cadence is second, at $5.30 billion, and Siemens EDA third, at an estimated $2.2 billion to $2.5 billion."],["design-and-eda","Chip firms such as Broadcom build custom accelerators to a customer's design and sell the finished chips. Broadcom booked $16.7 billion of AI semiconductor revenue in the third quarter of fiscal 2026, up 221 percent year over year. That figure covers both its custom AI accelerators and its AI networking chips."],["design-and-eda","Broadcom's custom-chip customers include OpenAI and Meta. In October 2025 OpenAI and Broadcom said they would deploy OpenAI-designed accelerators drawing 10 gigawatts of power. Broadcom would turn the design into silicon and supply the Ethernet networking around it. In April 2026 Broadcom and Meta extended their partnership to multiple gigawatts of MTIA, Meta's custom chip, including what they called the industry's first 2 nm AI accelerator."],["design-and-eda","Marvell, another US firm, also builds custom AI chips to each customer's specifications. Taiwanese design-service houses carry a customer's circuit list, the logic cells and the wires between them, all the way to a finished mask set on TSMC's newest nodes. One of them, Alchip, reported $992 million of revenue in 2025."],["design-and-eda","India has nearly 20 percent of the world's chip design engineers, the Indian government said in July 2025."],["design-and-eda","Before the 2025 letters, a narrower control already applied. Since 14 October 2022, design software specially made for chips with gate-all-around transistors has needed a US export license for national-security reasons. The rule calls that transistor design key to processes at 3 nm and below. That license requirement covers exports to China. The control carried out a December 2021 decision of the Wassenaar Arrangement, a group of countries that coordinate export controls."],["design-and-eda","In late May 2025 the US Bureau of Industry and Security, the agency that issues export licenses, told the design-software vendors that sales to China now needed a license. Cadence got its letter on 23 May. The letter required a license to export design software and technology classified 3D991 and 3E991 to any party in China, or to a Chinese military end user anywhere. Synopsys got its letter on 29 May and a second letter lifting the requirement on 2 July. Unlike the 2022 control, the 2025 requirement came from the United States alone and took effect immediately."],["design-and-eda","Synopsys's China revenue fell from 16 percent of its total in fiscal 2024 to 12 percent in fiscal 2025. SemiAnalysis links the decline to tighter export restrictions and to local design-software companies winning share at mature nodes. SemiAnalysis also quoted Synopsys's management saying that when Synopsys cannot sell to a company, that company looks for alternatives, typically local design-software and licensed-block companies."],["design-and-eda","In October 2025 CSIS found that only three companies, Cadence, Synopsys and Siemens, make design software that supports the entire chip design flow of more than 40 steps. In a January 2021 report built on 2019 market data, the Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET) at Georgetown University found that one Chinese firm, Empyrean, could reportedly run a complete design flow only for some analog and mixed-signal chips. Mixed-signal chips combine analog and digital circuits. For all other chips, Chinese designers then relied on US tools. The report found that other Chinese tools covered only narrow parts of the design flow or supplemented US tools, and largely did not support processes at 14 nm and below."],["design-and-eda","Empyrean says it has covered more of the design flow since then. Its 2025 annual report, filed in April 2026, says it now has complete design flows for analog, memory, radio-frequency and flat-panel display circuits. It says it offers 80 percent of the main tools used in digital design. The same report lists foundry certifications for its circuit simulator at 8, 5 and 4 nm and for its physical verification tool, the final layout check, at 28 nm. But CSIS found that as of 2025 Chinese design tools were still far from replacing the full range of advanced capabilities US firms offer, especially for 5 nm and 3 nm chip design."],["design-and-eda","China can design accelerators, but it cannot finish one at the leading edge without foreign tools, or build what it designs without foreign equipment. SMIC, China's leading foundry, makes chips for Huawei. In June 2024 CSET found that SMIC's limited 7 nm capacity forced Huawei to choose between making its most advanced phone chips and its AI chips."],["design-and-eda","Epoch AI estimates that Huawei trails Nvidia both in what each chip can do and in how many chips it makes. On Epoch's estimates, Huawei's flagship chip for 2026, the Ascend 950, delivers about half the computing performance of Nvidia's H100, which began shipping in 2022. Epoch puts Nvidia's B300 at 6.75 times the 950's theoretical peak performance. Epoch's median estimate is that Huawei will make about 1.5 million Ascend chips in 2026, against 5.9 million for Nvidia. On those estimates, Huawei's 2026 output would carry less than 4 percent of the computing power Nvidia ships that year."],["design-and-eda","Epoch puts Huawei's chips three to four years behind Nvidia's until at least 2030, for three reasons. SMIC cannot pack transistors as densely as TSMC, which makes Nvidia's. Chinese memory makers are only starting to produce high-bandwidth memory. And Huawei's software for programming its chips is far less mature than Nvidia's."],["design-and-eda","A blueprint of the chip that shows where each transistor sits and how the transistors are wired together."],["design-and-eda","A chip factory builds only designs that have passed checks in approved design software. Reread: How it works"],["design-and-eda","Which three companies sell the software used to design leading-edge chips?"],["design-and-eda","Together they held more than 85 percent of the $18 billion market for chip design software and licensed circuit blocks in 2025, counting Ansys as part of Synopsys. Reread: Who makes it"],["design-and-eda","Why is it hard for a new company to compete with Synopsys, Cadence and Siemens EDA?"],["design-and-eda","It would have to write a complete set of design tools from nothing and get a foundry to approve them."],["design-and-eda","Only three complete sets of design tools exist, each covering every step from code to signoff, the final checks. Foundries also specify which signoff tools their customers must use. Reread: The chokepoint"],["design-and-eda","How close are Chinese design tools to replacing US tools for the newest chips?"],["design-and-eda","As of 2025 they were still far from replacing the full range of US tools, especially for 5 nm and 3 nm chips, CSIS found."],["design-and-eda","Only Synopsys, Cadence and Siemens make tools for the entire design flow of more than 40 steps, CSIS found. China's Empyrean says its digital tools cover 80 percent of the main tools for digital design. Reread: The chokepoint"],["design-and-eda","How far behind Nvidia is Huawei's best AI chip?"],["design-and-eda","Three to four years, on Epoch AI's estimate."],["design-and-eda","Huawei's flagship for 2026, the Ascend 950, delivers about half the computing performance of Nvidia's H100, which began shipping in 2022. Reread: The chokepoint"],["design-and-eda","Chip design turns an idea into a blueprint, and a factory builds only designs checked in approved software."],["design-and-eda","Synopsys, Cadence and Siemens EDA sell the software used to design every leading-edge AI chip."],["design-and-eda","To compete with them, a new vendor would have to write a complete set of tools and win a foundry's approval."],["design-and-eda","China designs its own AI chips, but in October 2025 CSIS found its design software still far from replacing US tools, especially for 5 nm and 3 nm chips."],["design-and-eda","Huawei's best AI chip trails Nvidia's by three to four years, on Epoch AI's estimate."],["silicon-and-wafers","Chapter 02 Stage 2 of 14 High concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["silicon-and-wafers","Firms based in Japan, Taiwan, Germany and South Korea make most 300 mm wafers used for advanced chips. China makes most polysilicon, almost all of it for solar cells."],["silicon-and-wafers","Every chip is built on a wafer, a thin round slice of silicon about 30 centimeters across that carries hundreds of chips at once. Making one starts with quartz rock, which is silicon bound to oxygen. The silicon is refined until metal impurities are no more than a few parts per billion. It is then melted, and a small seed crystal is lowered to the surface and drawn slowly back up. The melt freezes onto the seed as one long cylinder, a single crystal with its atoms lined up in one unbroken pattern from end to end. Saws cut the cylinder into discs, and each disc is polished to a mirror finish and made extremely flat across its whole face. In 2025 the top five wafer makers served around 75 percent of the world market, and none of them is American or Chinese."],["silicon-and-wafers","Japanese companies held 53 percent of the world's silicon wafer sales in 2023, by a Fuji Keizai survey that Japan's trade ministry reproduced. Firms based in Taiwan, South Korea and Europe held most of the rest. China's largest maker of 300 mm wafers, Eswin, says it ranked sixth in the world with about 7.7 percent of global 300 mm shipments in the first half of 2026. Chips also need electronic-grade polysilicon, the raw material for wafers. The German wafer maker Siltronic named five major suppliers of it for 2025, and none is Chinese."],["silicon-and-wafers","GlobalWafers of Taiwan opened a $3.5 billion plant in Texas in May 2025, the first fully integrated plant for advanced silicon wafers built in the United States in over twenty years. US Presidential Proclamation 11052 sets a minimum import price of $100 per kilogram for polysilicon ingots and wafers from 4 December 2026."],["silicon-and-wafers","The world market for silicon wafers was $11.4 billion in 2025, on 12,973 million square inches shipped. That is a small fraction of Nvidia's data center revenue, which reached $193.7 billion in the fiscal year to 25 January 2026."],["silicon-and-wafers","Shin-Etsu Handotai Its parent's electronics materials segment, wafers included, had ¥1,015.7 billion of sales in the year to March 2026"],["silicon-and-wafers","SUMCO ¥409,670 million of net sales in 2025"],["silicon-and-wafers","GlobalWafers NT$60.6 billion revenue in 2025"],["silicon-and-wafers","SK Siltron One of the top five wafer makers by revenue in the first three quarters of 2025"],["silicon-and-wafers","Siltronic €1,346.7 million revenue in 2025"],["silicon-and-wafers","Japan Shin-Etsu and SUMCO crystal growth and polishing"],["silicon-and-wafers","Taiwan GlobalWafers headquarters and plants"],["silicon-and-wafers","Germany Siltronic plants in Burghausen and Freiberg, and Wacker semiconductor-grade polysilicon"],["silicon-and-wafers","United States Hemlock polysilicon in Michigan, and GlobalWafers plants in Sherman, Texas and St Peters, Missouri"],["silicon-and-wafers","China made about 93 percent of the world's polysilicon in 2023, and an estimated 98 percent of China's output was solar-grade. Eswin, mainland China's largest maker of 300 mm wafers, says it had about 7.7 percent of world 300 mm shipments in the first half of 2026."],["silicon-and-wafers","None of the five largest wafer makers in 2025 was American. GlobalWafers of Taiwan won CHIPS awards of up to $406 million in December 2024 for wafer plants in Texas and Missouri."],["silicon-and-wafers","An arc furnace melts the quartz rock with carbon, and the carbon takes the oxygen away as gas, leaving rough silicon metal. Refiners turn the metal into a gas, trichlorosilane, and distill it, because the impurities boil at other temperatures and separate out."],["silicon-and-wafers","In the next step, the Siemens process, the clean gas flows over silicon filaments heated inside a bell jar. On the hot surface the gas breaks apart and its silicon settles onto the filaments. Over days the filaments thicken into gray rods of polysilicon. Everything downstream is made from those rods. Polysilicon comes in two ultra-high-purity grades, one for semiconductors and one for solar cells, and chips use the semiconductor grade."],["silicon-and-wafers","A grower melts the polysilicon at about 1,420 degrees Celsius, hotter than lava, and pulls a single crystal out of it by the Czochralski method. The grower lowers a small seed crystal on the end of a rod to the surface of the melt and draws it back up, slowly turning. Silicon freezes onto the seed in the seed's own atomic pattern, and a cylinder, the ingot, grows beneath it. The pull starts with a thin neck so that flaws from the seed's first contact with the melt stay in the neck and never reach the ingot. Boron or phosphorus is stirred into the melt, a step called doping. The added element sets how readily the wafer conducts and whether negative or positive charges carry its current."],["silicon-and-wafers","A wire saw, a web of fine wire running through abrasive, slices the ingot into discs. The maker then laps each disc, grinding both faces flat between rotating plates. It etches off the damaged surface with chemicals, then polishes the disc to a mirror with colloidal silica, a slurry of silica particles far too small to see. Almost every step throws material away."],["silicon-and-wafers","Epitaxial wafers get one more layer of near-perfect silicon, grown on top at about 1,200 degrees Celsius. That is still hot enough to glow orange."],["silicon-and-wafers","A polished wafer is a doped single crystal polished to a mirror finish. An epitaxial wafer is a polished wafer with a thin layer of single-crystal silicon grown on top. The transistors are built in that layer, so flaws in it can make them leak current. SUMCO says an epitaxial wafer suits customers who need a near-perfect crystal or layers that differ in electrical resistance. SEMI, the industry association, credits the 2025 rise in shipments to AI-driven demand for advanced epitaxial wafers for logic chips and polished wafers for high-bandwidth memory."],["silicon-and-wafers","In a silicon-on- insulator (SOI) wafer, a buried layer of oxide, which is glass, separates a thin working layer of silicon from the bulk beneath. Soitec says nearly all SOI wafers sold worldwide are made with its Smart Cut process. Soitec's SOI product lines include RF-SOI for radio chips and fully depleted SOI (FD-SOI). Its markets run from mobile communications to cloud AI. But for logic chips, SEMI credited the AI-driven growth in 2025 to a different kind of wafer, the advanced epitaxial wafer."],["silicon-and-wafers","The Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET) at Georgetown University named five key wafer firms in a January 2021 brief. They were Shin-Etsu and SUMCO of Japan, GlobalWafers of Taiwan, Siltronic of Germany and SK Siltron of South Korea. CSET also listed nine Chinese-owned producers, among them Zhonghuan, Simgui, ZingSEMI and Okmetic, a Finnish firm bought by a Chinese state investment fund. It said Chinese wafer producers made little revenue compared with the five key firms."],["silicon-and-wafers","China's 300 mm wafer industry has grown since 2018. As of 2018, five Chinese firms were making or planning 300 mm wafers. In its October 2025 listing prospectus, Eswin, a Chinese wafer maker, counts seven Chinese firms, itself included, making 300 mm wafers at scale. Their combined capacity was 2.94 million wafers a month at the end of 2024."],["silicon-and-wafers","Japanese companies held 53 percent of the world's silicon wafer sales in 2023. The shares come from a survey of 2023 sales by Fuji Keizai, a Japanese research firm. Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry reproduced the figures in a December 2025 strategy deck. The ministry's chart of the survey prints only Japan's 53 percent, so the other shares are measured from its bars. An earlier page of the ministry's deck prints Europe's share in the same Fuji Keizai survey as 10 percent. The ministry's figures give no separate share to Chinese or US companies."],["silicon-and-wafers","Siltronic's April 2026 investor presentation says the top five wafer makers serve around 75 percent of the market, based on revenue in the first three quarters of 2025. It names the five as Shin-Etsu, SUMCO, GlobalWafers, SK Siltron and Siltronic itself. Siltronic describes itself as the only Western-based maker among the five."],["silicon-and-wafers","The wafer makers' 2025 results show strong AI demand and weak demand for chips made on older, mature nodes."],["silicon-and-wafers","Shin-Etsu. Shin-Etsu Chemical's electronics materials segment, which includes its wafer business, sold ¥1,015.7 billion in the year to March 2026, up 9 percent. AI-related demand stayed strong and demand in other sectors began to rise, lifting sales of silicon wafers, photoresist and photomask blanks. The segment also sells rare earth magnets and other materials, and the results release does not break out wafer sales. So the figure cannot be compared with the wafer revenue of the other firms listed."],["silicon-and-wafers","SUMCO. Sold ¥409,670 million. Its operating profit fell from ¥36,924 million to ¥1,342 million, and it ended the year with a net loss of ¥11,751 million. In the same year it added leading-edge 300 mm capacity and reorganized production of 200 mm and smaller wafers, where demand stayed weak."],["silicon-and-wafers","Siltronic. Lost €77.9 million on €1,346.7 million of sales while investing €369.1 million, with its new Singapore fab as the focus."],["silicon-and-wafers","GlobalWafers. NT$60.6 billion of revenue, down 3.24 percent in local currency."],["silicon-and-wafers","Worldwide, the wafer area shipped rose 5.8 percent in 2025, but revenue fell 1.2 percent. SEMI attributes the softer revenue mostly to traditional chip uses outside AI, where demand and pricing had yet to improve."],["silicon-and-wafers","Polysilicon is the raw material for both wafers and solar cells, and almost all of China's is made for solar cells. In 2023 China made 1.50 million metric tons of polysilicon, about 93 percent of world output. Solar-grade material was an estimated 98 percent of that output and electronic-grade 2 percent. The US Commerce Department found in 2026 that semiconductor-grade polysilicon makes up only 2.4 percent of global production, close to the electronic-grade share of China's output. These figures do not show how much of China's electronic-grade polysilicon ends up in chips."],["silicon-and-wafers","Siltronic put the 2025 market for electronic-grade silicon at $1.4 billion, with five major suppliers, none of them Chinese: Wacker, Hemlock, OCI, Tokuyama and Mitsubishi."],["silicon-and-wafers","GlobalWafers of Taiwan has expanded its wafer making in the United States. It opened a $3.5 billion plant in Sherman, Texas in May 2025, the first fully integrated plant for advanced silicon wafers built in the United States in over twenty years. The same day it announced another $4 billion for phases three and four in Sherman. The US government had awarded it up to $406 million under the CHIPS incentives program for wafer plants in Texas and Missouri."],["silicon-and-wafers","US import rules issued in 2026 on polysilicon products also cover the single-crystal wafers that chips are built on. US Presidential Proclamation 11052, signed 6 August 2026, sets a minimum import price of $100 per kilogram for polysilicon ingots and wafers from 4 December 2026. From the same date it adds an extra 15 percent duty on imported ingots and other listed products made from polysilicon. A September 2026 US Commerce Department rule meant to stop stockpiling before the duties start lists tariff code 3818.00.0040 among the products it covers. That code covers round, doped, single-crystal silicon wafers."],["silicon-and-wafers","The US Commerce Department may approve plans to build US polysilicon, ingot, wafer or solar cell plants whose construction starts by 20 January 2029. Firms with approved plans can import production equipment, and polysilicon, ingots, wafers and solar cells in amounts the department sets to match their new investment, without the new duties."],["silicon-and-wafers","China makes most of the world's polysilicon, but as of 2019 Chinese firms held under 5 percent of the wafer market and under 1 percent of the 300 mm market. As of 2018, Chinese producers made 12 percent of the wafers for Chinese-headquartered 300 mm fabs, against 18 percent for 100 to 200 mm fabs."],["silicon-and-wafers","Eswin, mainland China's largest maker of 300 mm wafers, says it ranked sixth in the world with about 7.7 percent of global 300 mm shipments in the first half of 2026. Its October 2025 Shanghai listing prospectus, drawing on SEMI data, estimates that the five largest makers shipped 79.08 percent of 300 mm wafers in 2024. It puts Eswin at 6.01 percent and all other makers at 14.91 percent."],["silicon-and-wafers","Making the smoothest, high-purity 300 mm wafers takes considerable know-how that is hard to write down. Customers have to qualify a new wafer plant before they buy from it, and Siltronic completed key customer qualifications at its new Singapore fab in July 2025."],["silicon-and-wafers","Almost all fab capacity for advanced chips runs on 300 mm wafers. In SEMI figures from November 2020 cited by CSET, 99.7 percent of world fab capacity at 45 nm and below used 300 mm wafers. SEMI estimated that 300 mm wafers made up about 78.8 percent of all wafer area shipped worldwide in 2025, according to Eswin's 2025 annual report summary."],["silicon-and-wafers","The last increase in wafer size, to 300 mm, happened in 2002. Wafers are still produced in diameters of up to 300 mm. Bigger wafers cut the cost of deposition, etching and other steps, because those steps have to be run fewer times for the same number of chips. So printing, or photolithography, takes a bigger share of the processing cost. A 2013 University of Texas lecture cited by CSET put photolithography at half the cost of processing a 300 mm wafer, against a quarter for a 150 mm one."],["silicon-and-wafers","Large GPU dies and the newest processes need better wafers. Some GPU dies fill the whole area a lithography tool can print in one exposure. One fatal defect on such a die ruins far more silicon than one on a small chip. Extreme-ultraviolet printing also stays in focus over only a tiny range of heights (see Lithography ), so the disc has to be flat at every point. SEMI's wafer group says the move to sub-3nm processes is raising requirements for wafer quality and consistency."],["silicon-and-wafers","A thin disc of pure silicon, about 30 centimeters across, that carries hundreds of chips."],["silicon-and-wafers","It is sliced from a single crystal and polished to a mirror finish. Reread: How it works"],["silicon-and-wafers","Which five companies make most of the world's silicon wafers?"],["silicon-and-wafers","Shin-Etsu and SUMCO of Japan, GlobalWafers of Taiwan, Siltronic of Germany and SK Siltron of South Korea."],["silicon-and-wafers","Together they served around 75 percent of the wafer market in 2025, based on revenue in the first three quarters. None of them is American or Chinese. Reread: Who makes it"],["silicon-and-wafers","Why can a fab not switch wafer suppliers quickly?"],["silicon-and-wafers","A fab has to test and approve, or qualify, a new wafer plant before buying from it."],["silicon-and-wafers","Making the smoothest, high-purity 300 mm wafers takes know-how that is hard to write down. Siltronic, one of the five largest makers, completed key customer approvals for its new Singapore fab in July 2025. Reread: The chokepoint"],["silicon-and-wafers","Why does making most of the world's polysilicon give China little hold over chip wafers?"],["silicon-and-wafers","Chips need electronic-grade silicon, and none of the five major suppliers of that grade is Chinese."],["silicon-and-wafers","China made about 93 percent of the world's polysilicon in 2023, but an estimated 98 percent of it was solar-grade. The five electronic-grade suppliers Siltronic named for 2025 are Wacker, Hemlock, OCI, Tokuyama and Mitsubishi. Reread: The chokepoint"],["silicon-and-wafers","Every chip starts on a wafer, a polished disc of pure silicon about 30 centimeters across."],["silicon-and-wafers","The top five wafer makers, in Japan, Taiwan, Germany and South Korea, served around 75 percent of the market in 2025."],["silicon-and-wafers","Customers have to test and approve a new wafer plant before they buy from it."],["silicon-and-wafers","China makes most of the world's polysilicon, but none of the five major suppliers of electronic-grade silicon, the grade chips need, is Chinese."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Chapter 03 Stage 3 of 14 High concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Japanese companies held 78 percent of world photoresist sales in 2023. Supply of chip chemicals, gases and metals has been disrupted three times since 2019."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Photoresist is a coating that changes wherever light hits it. A machine spins a coat of it, thinner than a soap bubble, across the wafer. Light shines through a stencil onto the coat, and a liquid wash then takes away the parts the light reached. What remains is a pattern, and the next machine cuts that pattern into the wafer beneath, a step called etching. Hundreds of other chemicals, gases and materials lay down layers, strip them off and clean the wafer between steps. The cleaning chemicals are purified until metal and other impurities are down to parts per trillion, the Japanese chemical maker Sumitomo Chemical said in 2021. A chipmaker has to test and approve each new resist in its own factory before using it. Even a resist that passes the first time takes seven to 17 months to approve, the Semiconductor Industry Association wrote in 2023. Japanese companies held 78 percent of world photoresist sales in 2023, by a Fuji Keizai survey that Japan's trade ministry reproduced."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In July 2019 Japan began requiring an export license for each contract to sell photoresist, hydrogen fluoride or fluorinated polyimide to South Korea. Japan's hydrogen fluoride exports to South Korea then fell 87.9 percent, but its photoresist exports did not. Production of all three chemicals rose inside South Korea."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","China banned exports of the metals gallium, germanium and antimony to the United States in December 2024. In Europe, germanium metal averaged an estimated $4,100 a kilogram in 2025, against $1,392 in 2023, on Argus Media prices reported by the US Geological Survey. In November 2025 China suspended the ban until 27 November 2026."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","A chip fab draws on hundreds of chemicals, gases and other materials. A shortage of any one of them can stop it. The French gas company Air Liquide alone supplies more than 200 different chemicals and roughly 50,000 cylinders a year."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","JSR A vehicle of the state-backed Japan Investment Corporation bought 84.36 percent of JSR in April 2024"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Tokyo Ohka Kogyo Resist maker with ¥139,668 million of sales in the first half of fiscal 2026"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Air Liquide €2,465 million of electronics revenue in 2025, 9.1 percent of group sales"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Entegris Bought the polishing-slurry maker CMC Materials in July 2022"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","JX Advanced Metals Says it holds about 65 percent of the world market for semiconductor sputtering targets as of fiscal 2026"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Japan Photoresist, ultra-pure hydrofluoric acid, sputtering targets, polishing slurries"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","United States Entegris polishing slurries, Qnity Electronics resist, Air Products gases"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","France Air Liquide electronics gases and precursors"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","South Korea Dongjin resist, with output of resist and hydrogen fluoride rising after 2019"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","China Gallium, germanium and antimony refining"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In March 2026 the Chinese resist maker Hubei Dinglong said China had yet to reach large-scale production of advanced resist for 248 nm, 193 nm or extreme-ultraviolet printing. Since August 2023 China has required licenses to export gallium and germanium."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In photoresist, American companies ranked a distant second to Japanese companies by sales in 2023. In 2021 JSR of Japan agreed to buy Inpria, an Oregon-based US maker of resist for extreme ultraviolet."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","The resist has to change only where the light lands. It also has to work with very little light, so the scanner, the machine that projects the pattern, can expose each patch of the wafer in milliseconds."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Since the 1990s the standard has been chemically amplified resist. In resists for light with wavelengths of 248 nm and 193 nm, a photon absorbed in the film can free an acid molecule, and little more happens until the wafer is baked. In the bake, each acid molecule sets off hundreds of reactions around itself that turn the film soluble, so a little light does a lot of chemistry. The wash then takes away the exposed film and leaves the rest."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","The 248 nm light comes from a krypton fluoride (KrF) laser. The 193 nm light comes from an argon fluoride (ArF) laser. Immersion scanners also pass it through a layer of water, which sharpens the image."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Chemically amplified resist works less well with extreme ultraviolet (EUV) light (see Lithography ). An absorbed EUV photon instead knocks electrons loose, and a cascade of lower-energy secondary electrons makes the chemical changes in the resist. A 13.5 nm EUV photon carries about fourteen times the energy of a 193 nm one, so the same dose of light arrives as far fewer photons. With fewer photons, random variation in where each one lands matters more. It shows up as ragged line edges and missing contact holes, the tiny holes that link one layer of a chip to the next."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Resist makers responded with metal-oxide resists, which are built on clusters with a tin-oxide core and absorb more of the EUV light than chemically amplified resists. In 2021 the Japanese resist maker JSR agreed to buy Inpria, an Oregon-based US maker of these resists."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","The other chemicals and gases put material on the wafer, take it off or keep it clean. Bulk gases such as nitrogen come by pipeline or from plants built at the fab, and specialty gases come in cylinders. Silane gas carries the silicon for new layers into the chamber that holds the wafer. A plasma splits nitrogen trifluoride, and the fluorine it frees scrubs the chamber walls clean between wafers. Hydrofluoric acid cleans the wafer itself. Polishing slurries grind each new layer flat before the next goes on."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Sputtering targets are slabs of pure metal. A plasma knocks atoms off them, and the atoms settle on the wafer as thin metal films, including the barrier and seed layers for copper wiring. Electroplating then fills in the copper wiring itself. Filters and wafer carriers keep contamination out."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Each resist class is made for one kind of lithography, such as EUV, ArF immersion, ArF, KrF or i-line."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Japanese companies sell most of the world's photoresist, by two different counts. In a January 2021 brief, Georgetown University's Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET) put Japan's share of the semiconductor photoresist market at 90 percent, citing a 2019 estimate. The brief put most of the rest with US and South Korean firms. In a December 2025 strategy presentation, Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry (METI) published figures from a separate survey by Fuji Keizai, a Japanese market research firm. That survey counts sales by company nationality and puts Japanese companies at 77 percent in 2021 and 78 percent in 2023, with American and South Korean companies next."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","CSET's January 2021 brief lists five Japanese resist makers: JSR, Tokyo Ohka Kogyo, Shin-Etsu Chemical, Fujifilm and Sumitomo Chemical. It also lists Dongjin of South Korea, four Chinese firms and three firms it counts as American: DuPont, EMD Performance Materials and Inpria. Qnity Electronics, the former DuPont electronics business, says in its 2025 annual report that it offers lithography materials for every wavelength, including EUV."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In its 2025 annual report summary, the Chinese firm Hubei Dinglong said China had yet to reach large-scale production of advanced resist for 248 nm, 193 nm or EUV printing. But it said three of its own resists for 248 nm and 193 nm printing had moved into stable volume supply."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","A Japanese state-backed fund, Japan Investment Corporation, took control of JSR in April 2024. A company the fund controls bought 84.36 percent of JSR's shares at ¥4,350 each in an offer to all shareholders that closed on 16 April 2024. JSR's shares were delisted from the Tokyo Stock Exchange on 25 June 2024."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Two Japanese suppliers tie their growth to demand for AI chips. Tokyo Ohka Kogyo sold ¥139,668 million in the first half of fiscal 2026, up 25.1 percent, as strong demand for AI servers in data centers raised demand for chips. Fujifilm planned to raise its polishing-slurry capacity at Kumamoto in Japan by about 30 percent from January 2025, to meet demand driven by AI chips. It also scheduled new production and quality-evaluation equipment for EUV resist at Shizuoka in Japan and Pyeongtaek in South Korea to start in October 2025."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","World sales of wafer fabrication materials reached $45.8 billion in 2025, and sales of packaging materials reached $27.4 billion. SEMI counts silicon wafers and photomasks among wafer fabrication materials, along with resists, gases, chemicals and polishing materials."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In electronic gases, CSET named Merck, Air Products and Air Liquide as the market leaders in January 2021. Air Liquide's electronics business sold €2,465 million in 2025, 9.1 percent of group revenue. SK Specialty has made nitrogen trifluoride since 2001, when it became the first company to produce the gas in South Korea. The Japanese firm Kanto Denka Kogyo refines its own fluorine gas and turns it into specialty gases for deposition, etching and cleaning. Stella Chemifa, also Japanese, makes ultra-high-purity hydrofluoric acid for chipmaking. Another Japanese firm, Morita Chemical Industries, sells an electronic-grade hydrofluoric acid."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","A few firms held most of the markets for wet chemicals and polishing slurries in 2019. CSET's January 2021 brief, drawing on a 2019 report by the market research firm Mordor Intelligence, put five firms, KMG Chemicals, BASF, Avantor, Honeywell and Kanto Chemical, at more than 60 percent of the wet chemicals market. Citing a 2019 report by the market research firm Market Reports World, it put DuPont and Cabot Microelectronics at about 56 percent of a $790 million market for polishing slurries. Counting by company nationality, the same Fuji Keizai survey, as published by METI, puts Japanese companies at 51 percent of polishing-slurry sales and 59 percent of high-purity cleaning-liquid sales in 2023. Both shares were 49 percent in 2021."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","The slurry businesses of both leaders CSET named have since moved to other companies. Cabot Microelectronics renamed itself CMC Materials in October 2020. The American firm Entegris completed its purchase of CMC Materials on 6 July 2022. DuPont separated its electronics business into an independent company, Qnity Electronics, on 1 November 2025. Qnity sells polishing slurries and pads."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In sputtering targets for semiconductors, JX Advanced Metals puts its own share of the world market at about 65 percent as of fiscal 2026."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Supply at this stage has been disrupted three times since 2019, twice by governments and once by a war."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In July 2019 Japan put photoresist, hydrogen fluoride and fluorinated polyimide under individual export licenses for South Korea, so each export contract needed its own license. South Korea's chip industry depended heavily on Japan for all three chemicals, and Japanese firms supplied more than 90 percent of South Korea's imports of two of them. Japan's hydrogen fluoride exports to South Korea then fell 87.9 percent. Japanese photoresist exports to South Korea did not fall, possibly in part because Japan allowed three-year bulk licenses for some resist sales in December 2019."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","South Korea bought more hydrogen fluoride from the United States and Taiwan and more photoresist from Belgium. Production of all three chemicals rose inside South Korea. The rise came both from South Korean firms and from Japanese companies' affiliates in South Korea."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Researchers at Japan's Research Institute of Economy, Trade and Industry (RIETI) found that Japanese hydrogen fluoride exports to the United States rose. They say some Japanese supply may have reached South Korea by way of the United States. Japan ended the individual licenses on 23 March 2023, when it put exports of the three chemicals to South Korea under its bulk export license system."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Russia's invasion of Ukraine in 2022 put chipmakers' supply of neon at risk. Before the invasion, Ukraine supplied about 70 percent of the world's neon and 90 percent of the semiconductor-grade neon used by US industry. The fighting forced at least two of Ukraine's three major gas producers, Cryoin and Ingas, to shut their operations in Odesa and Mariupol. That halted a significant part of the world's exports of neon, krypton and xenon. Gas mixtures containing neon fill the lasers used in lithography, but EUV scanners use a tin light source instead. Many chipmakers had added to their gas stockpiles after Russia annexed Crimea in 2014. Samsung, SK hynix, Renesas and Rohm reported adequate neon supplies from China."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","For chipmaking materials, China's export controls cover metals. On 3 July 2023 China announced that exports of gallium and germanium would need licenses from 1 August. On 3 December 2024 it said it would in principle grant no licenses to export gallium, germanium, antimony or superhard materials to the United States. On 9 November 2025 it suspended that ban until 27 November 2026. In February 2026 the US Geological Survey put China's share of world production of primary low-purity gallium at 99 percent."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","The White House set out a trade deal with China on 1 November 2025. It said that under the deal China would issue general licenses for exports of gallium, germanium and antimony for the benefit of US end users and their suppliers."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Most gallium used in the United States goes into chips, and both metals are recovered as byproducts of processing other minerals. Of the gallium used in the United States in 2025, 73 percent went into integrated circuits built on gallium arsenide or gallium nitride. Another 26 percent went into optoelectronic devices such as LEDs and laser diodes. In the United States, germanium goes mainly into fiber optics, infrared optics, semiconductors and solar cells, and radiation detectors. Gallium is recovered mostly as a byproduct of processing bauxite, the ore that aluminum is made from. Germanium is recovered from certain zinc smelter residues and from coal ash. Because both metals are economical to produce only as byproducts, their supply may not rise much when their prices do."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In Europe, germanium metal averaged an estimated $4,100 a kilogram in 2025, against $1,392 in 2023, on Argus Media prices reported by the US Geological Survey. US imports of the metal fell an estimated 67 percent in 2025 because of China's ban. In October 2024 the US Geological Survey estimated that a total Chinese ban on gallium and germanium exports could cut US GDP by $3.4 billion."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","A slower risk is the European Union's proposed restriction on PFAS, the long-lived fluorinated chemicals. These chemicals are used throughout a fab, from some etch gases to seals, filters and the plastic linings of chemical tanks and pipes. Most of the photoacid generators that free the acid in resist contain PFAS too."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Each resist made without PFAS would need full qualification in the chipmaker's fab. The Semiconductor Industry Association wrote in 2023 that photoresist needs the most rigorous qualification of any chemical a chipmaker uses, because each resist is tuned to the layers it prints. The resist maker adjusts its formula over rounds of tests in the fab. A fab could not qualify all the new resists at once, mainly because testing several together can muddle the yield results. So some would have to be qualified one after another."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","The EU proposal may still let chipmakers keep using PFAS where the risks can be controlled. The national authorities of Denmark, Germany, the Netherlands, Norway and Sweden prepared the proposal and updated it after evaluating more than 5,600 comments. ECHA, the EU chemicals agency, published the updated proposal on 20 August 2025. The updated proposal assessed options that would let electronics and semiconductor makers keep using PFAS where the risks can be controlled."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","In March 2026 ECHA's two scientific committees backed an EU-wide restriction with targeted derogations, or exemptions. One committee gave its backing in a final opinion and the other in a draft. Their evaluation is due to finish by the end of 2026. The European Commission will decide in consultation with the member states."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","It is a light-sensitive coating that holds the printed pattern, so the next step can etch that pattern into the wafer."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","A wash removes the parts the light reached. The pattern that remains guides the etch. Reread: How it works"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Which country's companies sell most of the world's photoresist?"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Japanese companies, among them JSR, Tokyo Ohka Kogyo and Fujifilm, held 78 percent of world sales in 2023. Reread: Who makes it"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Why is it slow to switch to a new photoresist supplier?"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Each resist is tuned to the layers it prints, and the chipmaker has to approve it in its own fab."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Even a resist that passes the first time takes seven to 17 months to approve, the Semiconductor Industry Association wrote in 2023. Reread: The chokepoint"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Which two metals has China required a license to export since August 2023?"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","China made 99 percent of the world's primary low-purity gallium, the US Geological Survey said in February 2026. In the United States, 73 percent of the gallium used in 2025 went into chips built on gallium arsenide or gallium nitride. Reread: The chokepoint"],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Photoresist holds the pattern printed by light so the next step can etch it into the wafer."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","Japanese companies held 77 percent of world photoresist sales in 2021 and 78 percent in 2023."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","A chipmaker has to approve each new resist in its own fab, and even one that passes the first time takes seven to 17 months."],["chemicals-gases-and-photoresist","China has required licenses to export gallium and germanium since August 2023."],["lithography","Chapter 04 Stage 4 of 14 Extreme concentration · Very hard to substitute"],["lithography","ASML, a Dutch firm, is the only maker of extreme ultraviolet scanners, the machines that print the finest layers of a chip. It sold 48 of them in 2025."],["lithography","Lithography prints the pattern of a circuit onto the wafer. A machine holds a stencil of one layer of the circuit up to a light source and projects the image, four times smaller, onto the silicon. The shorter the wavelength of the light, the finer the lines a machine can print. Even so, a machine can print lines narrower than its light's wavelength. Immersion scanners, for example, shine the light through a layer of water between lens and wafer, which lets them print smaller features with the same light. ASML rates one of its immersion scanners, the NXT:2150i, at features of 38 nanometers or less, printed with argon fluoride laser light at 193 nanometers. Air soaks up extreme ultraviolet light, the shortest in use, so machines that print with it work in a vacuum. Only ASML, a Dutch company, makes them. Export controls are government rules on who a company may sell to. Every advanced chip passes through ASML's machines, so export controls on ASML affect all advanced chipmaking."],["lithography","Beyond extreme ultraviolet (EUV), ASML holds above 80 percent of the market for deep ultraviolet (DUV) lithography, which uses light of longer wavelength. In July 2026 ASML put its capacity for 2026 at around 65 standard EUV scanners, which caps how many fabs anywhere can add that year. ASML says the production capacity of Zeiss, its sole supplier of optics, limits how many lithography systems it can build."],["lithography","Export controls set up by the United States with allies including the Netherlands block EUV scanners from Chinese chip foundries. In December 2025 Reuters reported a Chinese prototype that had made EUV light but had printed no chip. In July 2026 Reuters reported, citing one unnamed source, that a Shanghai firm with two state shareholders has started producing immersion DUV tools, which shine their light through water."],["lithography","ASML sold 327 lithography systems in 2025. Tools shipped to China made up 33 percent of its net system sales that year, more than any other region."],["lithography","ASML 327 lithography systems sold in 2025, including all 48 EUV (extreme ultraviolet) systems"],["lithography","Canon 234 chip lithography systems sold in 2025"],["lithography","Nikon 22 new chip lithography systems sold in the year to March 2026"],["lithography","Netherlands ASML, the Dutch maker of every EUV scanner"],["lithography","Germany Zeiss SMT optics, Oberkochen, and Trumpf carbon dioxide drive lasers, Ditzingen"],["lithography","United States ASML light-source research and manufacturing, San Diego"],["lithography","Japan Nikon and Canon lithography scanners and steppers"],["lithography","In July 2026 Reuters reported, citing one unnamed source, that a Shanghai firm with two state shareholders had started producing immersion DUV tools. The Center for Technology & Statecraft found in September 2026 that Chinese firms had begun small-batch production of such scanners, but none had yet been shown fit for producing advanced chips. Its central estimate in 2026 was that China would have a commercially viable immersion scanner for 7 nm chips in the mid-2030s, with the early 2030s plausible, and EUV not before the second half of the 2030s. Meanwhile Chinese fabs had built a stockpile of more than 330 immersion DUV systems by the first quarter of 2026, most of them ASML's NXT:1980i."],["lithography","CSET found in 2021 that no American firm made lithography scanners. In September 2026 the Center for Technology & Statecraft found that ASML held about 99 percent of the market for immersion DUV scanners and Japan's Nikon the rest. But every immersion DUV scanner holds a light source from Cymer, a US company now part of ASML, or from Japan's Gigaphoton, so the two governments could stop sales by controlling those parts, the Center for Technology & Statecraft found in September 2026. A US rule published in October 2023 already covers immersion scanners with an alignment error between 1.5 nm and 2.4 nm bound for advanced chipmaking if they hold any American-made parts. The US entity list also requires a license to supply the firms it names."],["lithography","The stencil is called a photomask, and the machine a scanner (see Photomasks and pellicles )."],["lithography","The wafer is coated with photoresist, a film that changes wherever light touches it. The mask holds one layer of the circuit as a pattern of clear and dark areas, drawn at four times its size on the chip. The machine shines light through the mask, shrinks the image four times with a lens, and lands it on the film."],["lithography","A wash then removes the film where the light hit, or, with some films, where it did not, leaving the pattern standing on the wafer. The film then serves as a stencil for the next step, which either etches the pattern into the layer beneath or fires ions into the open areas to change how the silicon conducts. Then the film is stripped and the next mask goes in. Chips are made up of dozens of layers, ASML says. Photronics, a US mask maker, says masks are typically sold in sets, with each layer's pattern on a different mask."],["lithography","The image from one mask covers a patch of up to 26 by 33 mm. The wafer moves under the optics one patch at a time, close to a hundred patches per wafer. ASML's own wafers-per-hour rating for an EUV scanner assumes 96 of them. Before the wafer is exposed, the machine measures alignment marks printed in earlier layers so the new layer lines up with them. For its NXE:3400B EUV scanner, ASML rates the matched-machine overlay, a measure of that alignment, at 2 nm. That model first shipped in 2017."],["lithography","Finer lines need shorter light. Glass and air both absorb the shortest light in use, at 13.5 nm. So an EUV scanner works in a vacuum and uses mirrors instead of lenses, and its masks are mirrors too. Deep ultraviolet (DUV) machines use light with a wavelength more than fourteen times longer. ASML calls its immersion DUV scanners the workhorses of the industry, used in high-volume manufacturing of the most advanced logic and memory chips."],["lithography","When one exposure cannot draw a pattern finely enough, chipmakers use multipatterning. In the litho-etch kind, the pattern is split between two or more masks printed in turn. Each added mask brings more process steps, more cost and a risk that the parts of the pattern misalign. Self-aligned double and quadruple patterning (SADP and SAQP) print the lines with one exposure and then multiply them with deposition and etch steps. In SAQP each printed line ends up as four. Because one exposure places all those lines, they cannot misalign with each other. A later exposure still prints blocks that break them where the circuit needs gaps. ASML says one EUV exposure per layer cuts masks and process steps and lowers cost."],["lithography","Deep ultraviolet (DUV) light comes from gas lasers called excimer lasers: 248 nanometers from krypton fluoride (KrF), 193 from argon fluoride (ArF), shone through air or water. Cymer, an independently run ASML business in San Diego, makes these excimer lasers, which generate the light that scanners use to print patterns on wafers. Gigaphoton, a Komatsu company in Japan, also makes excimer lasers for lithography tools."],["lithography","Of the systems ASML sold in 2025, 131 were ArF immersion, 78 KrF and 16 ArF dry, all deep ultraviolet, and another 54 were older i-line tools. The i-line tools use 365 nm light from a mercury lamp, and ASML says they print features as small as 220 nm."],["lithography","Reuters gives one price for the whole DUV segment, with tools costing roughly $60 million each. ASML's own figures split its DUV sales by tool type. In 2025 the 131 ArF immersion tools it sold made up 42 percent of its system sales, and the 78 KrF tools only 4 percent. In DUV, ASML competes with Nikon and Canon, and it still holds above 80 percent of that market."],["lithography","Chipmakers without EUV build their finest layers on immersion DUV scanners, in several passes per layer. From 1 September 2023, Dutch export licensing covered the most advanced of these scanners, ASML's NXT:2000i and later models."],["lithography","The 13.5 nm light comes from molten tin droplets shot from a generator. A laser hits each droplet twice, first with a low-intensity pulse that flattens it and then with a more powerful one that vaporizes it into plasma. The process repeats 50,000 times a second. Mirrors made by Zeiss, a German optics company, carry the light to the wafer. The largest are a meter across and smooth to within tens of picometers, a picometer being a thousandth of a nanometer."],["lithography","Brighter light means more wafers an hour, and ASML demonstrated the first 1,000-watt EUV source in April 2025. Its TWINSCAN NXE:3800E ships at its full 220 wafers an hour, 37 percent more than the NXE:3600D."],["lithography","High-NA scanners raise the numerical aperture (NA), a measure of how well the optics collect and focus light, from 0.33 to 0.55. That cuts the smallest printable feature from 13 nm to 8 nm. Their optics shrink the mask image four times in one direction and eight in the other, halving the patch of wafer one exposure covers and doubling the exposures per wafer. The second-generation TWINSCAN EXE:5200B runs at 175 wafers an hour, 60 percent above the EXE:5000."],["lithography","Reuters puts a standard EUV tool at around $200 million and a High-NA machine at an estimated $350 to $400 million."],["lithography","ASML sold four High-NA (EXE) systems in 2025, against two in 2024. In its 2025 annual report, filed in February 2026, ASML said it expected High-NA to start supporting high-volume manufacturing in 2027."],["lithography","Intel and TSMC have chosen differently on High-NA:"],["lithography","Intel Foundry says it uses High-NA in volume production for select layers of some Intel 18A products. It installed the first EXE:5200B. By September 2026 it had run more than one million wafers on High-NA tools, a count that includes tool testing and research as well as volume production."],["lithography","TSMC waited, and in September 2026 said it will use High-NA in high-volume manufacturing from 2030."],["lithography","On 8 September 2026 ASML and TSMC announced a move from 6-inch photomasks to 12-inch ones, to remove stitching constraints. Stitching constraints are the design limits that come from printing a large chip in two halves. ASML and TSMC aim for a pilot line for the new masks by 2031 and for High-NA systems that use them to enter production by 2033."],["lithography","ASML's net sales were EUR 32.7 billion in 2025, at a 52.8 percent gross margin. In October 2026 it expected 2026 net sales of EUR 44 to 45 billion, at a gross margin of around 56 percent. Its 2025 annual report lists 5,100 suppliers. Three of them and ASML's own San Diego site make the main parts of the EUV machine:"],["lithography","Zeiss SMT, Oberkochen, Germany, makes the illumination system and the six-mirror projection optics."],["lithography","Trumpf, Ditzingen, Germany, makes the carbon dioxide drive laser that hits the tin droplets. It amplifies a few watts to 40 kilowatts."],["lithography","ASML San Diego, which includes the light-source maker Cymer that ASML bought in 2013, designs the source where the laser turns tin into plasma, and builds the droplet generator."],["lithography","VDL ETG builds the frames that suspend and position the mirrors."],["lithography","ASML says the production capacity of Zeiss, its sole supplier of optics, limits how many lithography systems it can build."],["lithography","Lithography is the stage of the chain that European firms lead, with ASML the only maker of EUV scanners. The bulk of ASML's suppliers are in the Netherlands and the rest of Europe, the Middle East and Africa, the company says."],["lithography","In Japan, Nikon and Canon also make lithography tools. Nikon sold 22 new chip lithography systems in the year to March 2026, in a market it sizes at 570 units for 2025. Its Precision Equipment business made an operating loss in the year to March 2026. Canon sold 234 chip lithography systems in 2025, 188 of them i-line and 46 KrF. Its range runs from KrF scanners to i-line steppers, including some built for advanced packaging. Canon also makes a nanoimprint system, the FPA-1200NZ2C, which stamps the pattern instead of projecting it and can print lines down to 14 nm wide. Canon delivered one in 2024 to the Texas Institute for Electronics, to be used for research and prototypes."],["lithography","In January 2021 CSET, a research center at Georgetown University, found that the United States lacked firms in a few key parts of the chip supply chain, above all lithography tools."],["lithography","Export controls set up by the United States with allies including the Netherlands block ASML from shipping EUV scanners to Chinese foundries. In September 2025 CSIS judged that EUV remained \"firmly out of reach\" for China despite massive state investment. For DUV scanners and other tools, the restrictions came in this order:"],["lithography","Dutch national licensing of advanced DUV took effect on 1 September 2023."],["lithography","A US rule published on 25 October 2023 covered immersion scanners that print features of 45 nm or smaller with an alignment error between 1.5 nm and 2.4 nm. If such a scanner was bound for advanced chipmaking, the rule put it under US export rules when it held any American content at all. The rule did not apply to scanners first exported from a country that lists them on its own export control list."],["lithography","A partial license revocation by the Dutch government, disclosed by ASML on 1 January 2024, stopped shipments of NXT:2050i and NXT:2100i immersion scanners to a few Chinese customers."],["lithography","The Netherlands widened its licensing to more types of deep ultraviolet lithography equipment from 7 September 2024. On 15 January 2025 it announced that from 1 April 2025 the license requirement would also cover a very limited number of further goods, among them specific measuring and inspection equipment."],["lithography","The BIS Affiliates Rule, issued by the US Bureau of Industry and Security, extended entity-list controls to affiliates owned 50 percent or more by listed entities from 29 September 2025. BIS then suspended it until 9 November 2026. Exporting goods covered by US export rules to a firm on the entity list needs a US license."],["lithography","The EU added certain Dutch controls to the EU Control List in November 2025. ASML says this changed nothing for its immersion tools, because they already needed a Dutch license."],["lithography","China's share of ASML's net system sales fell from 41 percent in 2024 to 33 percent in 2025."],["lithography","On DUV, Reuters reported in July 2026, citing one unnamed source, that Shanghai Aishengna Electronic Technology Group has started producing home-grown immersion DUV tools. The firm was registered in August 2023 with 7 billion yuan of capital and two state shareholders, Shanghai Electric Holding and a Shanghai International Trust subsidiary. It has no website and has taken in teams from SMEE, China's older scanner maker, and the startup Yuliangsheng. SMEE is strongest in i-line, the coarsest kind of lithography tool, and even there holds only four percent of the world market."],["lithography","The Center for Technology & Statecraft, a research group, found in September 2026 that none of China's home-grown immersion scanners had yet been shown fit for producing advanced chips. Its central estimate was a commercially viable Chinese immersion scanner for 7 nm chips in the mid-2030s, and EUV not before the second half of the 2030s. Until then Chinese fabs rely on imported tools, and by the first quarter of 2026 they had built a stockpile of more than 330 immersion DUV systems, most of them ASML's NXT:1980i."],["lithography","There is less evidence of Chinese progress on EUV. Reuters reported in December 2025 that a Shenzhen team of former ASML engineers had built a prototype that made extreme ultraviolet light but had printed no chip. To print a chip, a machine also needs mirrors that carry that light to the wafer, and ASML's sole supplier of those mirrors is Zeiss."],["lithography","If ASML stopped shipping, no fab anywhere could add EUV capacity, because no other company makes EUV scanners. The scanners already in fabs would keep printing only as long as they were serviced. ASML has around 10,000 customer support employees who maintain and upgrade those machines around the clock. Serviced this way, ASML's machines stay in use for a long time. In its 2025 annual report ASML said about 95 percent of the systems it had sold in the previous 30 years were still in use. The same report warned that export controls may limit the service ASML can provide for machines already installed."],["lithography","ASML has a chokepoint of its own. Zeiss SMT is its only supplier of lenses, mirrors and other critical optics. ASML says that if Zeiss could not supply them for a long period, ASML would effectively be unable to run its business."],["lithography","ASML's capacity caps how many EUV scanners fabs anywhere can add each year. In July 2026 ASML put its 2026 capacity at around 65 standard (low-NA) EUV scanners and said it plans to add 30 percent for 2027."],["lithography","Leading-edge AI accelerators are made with EUV, which prints their finest layers, the ones that set how densely transistors and wires pack. TSMC expects the number of layers needing High-NA to rise, driven mainly by the more complex transistors that AI chips need."],["lithography","It prints each layer of a chip's circuit onto the wafer."],["lithography","The machine projects the image of a stencil, four times smaller, onto the silicon. Reread: How it works"],["lithography","Why do chipmakers print the finest layers with extreme ultraviolet (EUV) light?"],["lithography","Its shorter wavelength lets one exposure print what deep ultraviolet (DUV) machines need several passes to build."],["lithography","Each added mask brings more process steps, more cost and a risk that the parts of the pattern misalign. ASML says one EUV exposure per layer cuts masks and process steps and lowers cost. Reread: How it works"],["lithography","ASML recorded sales of 48 EUV systems in 2025. The mirrors in these machines come from one supplier, Zeiss. Reread: Who makes it"],["lithography","How do export controls keep EUV machines out of China?"],["lithography","They block ASML, the only maker, from shipping EUV scanners to Chinese foundries."],["lithography","In September 2025 CSIS judged EUV firmly out of reach for China. A Chinese prototype reported that December had made EUV light but had printed no chip. Reread: Controls and China's answer"],["lithography","Lithography prints each layer of a chip's circuit onto the wafer."],["lithography","Extreme-ultraviolet (EUV) light prints the finest layers in fewer steps than deep ultraviolet, but air and glass absorb it, so EUV machines work in a vacuum and use mirrors."],["lithography","ASML of the Netherlands is the only maker of EUV machines, and Zeiss alone supplies their mirrors."],["lithography","Export controls block EUV sales to Chinese chipmakers, and a Chinese prototype reported in December 2025 had printed no chip."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Chapter 05 Stage 5 of 14 Extreme concentration · Hard to substitute"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Only three firms in the world make the blank plates for the masks used to print the finest layers of leading-edge chips. Japan's AGC and Hoya are two of them."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A photomask is the stencil that lithography prints from, at least one for each layer of a chip. The same mask prints its layer on wafer after wafer, so one mask shapes millions of chips. The most complicated layers are printed with extreme ultraviolet (EUV) light, and the rest can often be printed with deep ultraviolet light. For deep ultraviolet the mask is a quartz plate that the light shines through. No glass lets EUV light through, so the mask for EUV layers is a mirror. The mirror is built up from about forty pairs of thin layers, and the light bounces off it. Japan's AGC and Hoya are two of the three firms that make these mirrors. A dark pattern drawn on top of the mirror soaks up the light wherever no line should print. Any speck of dust on the mask repeats on every wafer it prints. So a thin membrane on a frame, called a pellicle, sits just above the mask and catches dust where it is too far out of focus to print."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","On CSET's count from TechInsights data, Austria's IMS Nanofabrication held 46.6 percent of the 2025 world market for electron-beam mask writers, which draw the pattern onto a mask. Hoya says its share of the mask blank market is exceptionally high."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","SemiAnalysis put a full set of masks for a leading-edge chip at $40 million in May 2026. In July 2022 it wrote that more companies will lack the volume to spread the fixed cost of mask sets. On 8 September 2026 ASML and TSMC announced a plan to move from 6-inch to 12-inch masks. They expect the change to raise fab productivity and lower chipmaking costs."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Each EUV layer of an AI accelerator is printed from a mask built on a blank plate. Only three companies worldwide supply those plates, and Japan's AGC is one of them. Hoya, also Japanese, is another. AGC says it is the only company in the world that takes an EUV blank all the way from the glass to the finished coating."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","AGC Ranks itself No.2 worldwide in EUV mask blanks on its own fiscal 2026 estimates"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Hoya Said in its 2026 report that its share of mask blanks is exceptionally high"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Lasertec Launched the world's first tool that inspects patterned EUV masks at the scanner's own wavelength in 2019"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","IMS Nanofabrication CSET puts its 2025 share of the market for all electron-beam mask writers at 46.6 percent, using TechInsights data"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Photronics $849.3 million of revenue in fiscal 2025"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Japan Mask blanks (AGC, Hoya), DUV blanks (Shin-Etsu), inspection (Lasertec), writers (NuFlare), pellicles (Mitsui Chemicals)"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Austria IMS Nanofabrication multi-beam mask writers"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Germany Zeiss mask checking in EUV light (AIMS EUV) and mask repair"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","United States Photronics merchant mask shops, KLA inspection"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Taiwan TSMC, which held 10 percent of IMS at the end of 2024"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","As of 2026 SMIC runs two mask shops of its own in Shanghai. No Chinese firm appears in CSET's 2025 market shares for electron-beam mask writers, the machines that draw the pattern onto a mask."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","In December 2025 Photronics called itself a leading worldwide maker of photomasks. As of 2026 KLA sells tools that inspect EUV masks and optical masks, the quartz masks used with deep ultraviolet light."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A mask starts as a blank, a polished plate with no pattern on it yet. For deep ultraviolet the blank is a window of quartz carrying a light-blocking film such as molybdenum silicide. Japan's Shin-Etsu is one maker of those blanks. For EUV the blank is a mirror of about 40 molybdenum and silicon layer pairs, 7 nm to a pair, laid on glass. A dark tantalum film on top, called the absorber, will carry the pattern."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","The blank is coated with a sensitive film called resist. A mask writer then draws the design into the resist with electrons. A single-beam writer flashes one shape at a time, while NuFlare's multi-beam writer for the most advanced masks controls 260,000 beams at once."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A wash removes the drawn resist. An etch then removes the blocking film or absorber wherever the resist is gone, and the rest of the resist is stripped. The plate now passes light, or reflects it, in the shape of one layer of the chip. On standard EUV scanners the pattern is drawn four times larger than it will print. An inspection tool compares the plate to the design, and a repair tool fixes the stray defects it finds."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Mask 3D effects. Light strikes the mirror at a slant, and the absorber has height, so its edges cast small shadows that distort the printed shape. Software has to correct for the shadows in advance."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Write precision. Every edge of the absorber has to sit within a few nanometers of where the design says."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Particles. Anything on the mirror prints on every wafer until someone finds it."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","High-NA scanners, the newest EUV machines, print finer lines with larger mirrors. To keep masks at their usual size, the scanners ' mirrors shrink the pattern four times in one direction and eight times in the other. So each exposure covers half the area of a standard exposure, and a wafer takes twice as many exposures."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","On 8 September 2026 ASML and TSMC announced a plan to move from the current 6-inch masks to 12-inch masks. They expect the change to raise fab productivity, lower chipmaking costs and remove stitching constraints, the design limits that come from printing a large chip in two halves. They aim to set up a 12-inch mask pilot line by 2031, so that High-NA scanners using 12-inch masks can enter advanced chip production by 2033."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","AGC says it spent more than a decade meeting the blank's requirements, which include near-zero thermal expansion, perfectly smooth and flat surfaces and no particle contamination. It says it began mass production only in 2017."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","AGC publishes no market share figure for EUV blanks. In its data book, AGC ranks itself No.2 worldwide in EUV blanks, based on its own fiscal 2026 estimates. Hoya says its share of the mask blank market is exceptionally high, and it calls itself the primary supplier for leading-edge EUV nodes. It also says customers may gradually start buying EUV blanks from more than one supplier."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","AGC planned to add EUV blank capacity by 2025, and it says its sales reached their target a year early. In April 2023 AGC said its EUV blank capacity would grow by about 30 percent in 2025. The growth would come from a line in Fukushima. METI, Japan's industry ministry, chose the project for a program that supports new plants and equipment in Japan to strengthen supply chains. AGC also said it was aiming for more than ¥40 billion of sales in the business by 2025. Its EUV blank sales grew 50 percent in 2023, AGC said in December 2024. In February 2025 AGC reported that the sales reached ¥40 billion in 2024, which it called a year ahead of its initial target."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","AGC plans to add capacity again after a dip in sales. Its EUV blank sales declined in 2025 and were recovering in 2026, AGC said in June 2026. In August 2026 AGC set out capacity expansions of 20 to 50 percent across EUV blanks, polishing slurry and lens materials for lithography tools. It gave no separate figure for the blanks. Mass production on the added capacity is to begin in 2028."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","An electron-beam writer draws the pattern into the resist on the blank. Multi-beam writers fire many beams at once, and Japan's NuFlare sells them for the 3 nm node."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","In September 2023 Intel, the majority owner of Austria's IMS Nanofabrication, called it the established industry leader in the multi-beam mask writing tools that advanced EUV requires. Counting all electron-beam mask writers, CSET, a research center at Georgetown University, put IMS's share of a $994 million world market at 46.6 percent in 2025, using TechInsights data. NuFlare had 39.2 percent and JEOL 14.2 percent, in the same CSET analysis of TechInsights data."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Intel sold a combined 32 percent of IMS in 2023 and still held the other 68 percent on 27 December 2025. In June 2023 it agreed to sell about 20 percent of IMS to Bain Capital. Intel agreed in September 2023 to sell roughly 10 percent of IMS to TSMC at a valuation of about $4.3 billion. TSMC's subsidiary TSMC Development held that 10 percent at the end of 2024, at a fair value of $432.8 million in TSMC's accounts."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A mask defect cuts the number of good chips on every wafer that mask prints, so masks are checked as blanks, after patterning and again at the fab. Actinic inspection uses 13.5 nm light, the wavelength of EUV lithography. In 2019 Lasertec launched the ACTIS A150, which it calls the world's first actinic inspection system for patterned EUV masks. In October 2025 it launched the ACTIS A200HiT series, which it says triples the A150's inspection speed. Lasertec reported net sales of ¥230,485 million in the year to June 2026."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","As of 2026 KLA's Teron systems for mask shops detect pattern and particle defects on both EUV masks and optical masks, the quartz masks used with deep ultraviolet light."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Zeiss makes AIMS EUV, which checks a mask in EUV light under the scanner's own imaging conditions to judge how a defect will affect printing. Zeiss calls AIMS the only system that tests how a mask will print under conditions equivalent to the scanner's. Zeiss says the tool can be extended to ASML's High-NA scanner, the EXE:5000. Zeiss also sells electron-beam repair tools that work on EUV masks."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A pellicle is a thin membrane on a frame above the mask. Particles land on it, too far out of focus to print, and the pattern below stays clean."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Every photon a pellicle absorbs is light that never reaches the wafer. The light crosses the pellicle twice, on the way in and on the way back off the mirror, so absorption counts double. In 2022 ASML described its most advanced EUV pellicle as a membrane 13 nanometers thick that can withstand up to 500 degrees Celsius in a high vacuum. ASML released its first EUV pellicles in 2016 and calls the pellicle one of the breakthroughs that brought EUV lithography to high-volume manufacturing."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Carbon nanotube membranes are a newer kind of pellicle, aimed at next-generation High-NA, high-output EUV scanners. In 2020 imec, a Belgian chip research center, mounted them on masks and exposed them in an ASML NXE:3300 scanner. The membranes passed up to 97 percent of the light in a single crossing, and imec found their effect on imaging low and correctable."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Mitsui Chemicals began commercial production of silicon-based EUV pellicles under an ASML license in 2021. In 2024 it said it would build a carbon nanotube membrane plant at Iwakuni-Ohtake, tentatively due to finish in December 2025. In December 2025 Mitsui Chemicals said the plant was scheduled for completion in its fiscal 2025, in line with its initial plan. The same presentation lists the plant under March 2026 in its table of key investments. The membranes are designed to pass 92 percent or more of the light and to withstand exposure power above 1 kW."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A mask set costs more at each newer node, by SemiAnalysis's figures. In July 2022 SemiAnalysis put mask sets above $1 million at 28 nm and above $10 million at 7 nm. It expected 3 nm mask sets to reach the $40 million range. Its May 2026 primer still puts a leading-edge mask set at $40 million. The same primer puts a single respin, remaking a chip after a design flaw, at $50 million to $100 million at leading-edge nodes."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Mask costs restrict which firms can use a node. SemiAnalysis wrote that at 5 nm and 3 nm, only firms with large wafer volume see the cost per transistor fall. It wrote that more companies will lack the volume to spread the fixed cost of mask sets. It expected failed chip designs to show up first among AI chip startups, which work on much tighter budgets."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Mask making splits between chipmakers that make masks for their own use and independent merchant firms that sell to them and others. Photronics says that chipmakers' own shops once supplied most of the market, and that production has more recently tended to move toward the independents. TSMC makes masks too, and lists mask making among the services it offers besides making wafers."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Photronics calls itself a leading worldwide maker of masks for chips and flat panel displays. It had $849.3 million of revenue in fiscal 2025, $615.1 million of it from chip masks. The competitors it names in chip and display masks include Dai Nippon Printing, Hoya, Tekscend Photomask and two Chinese firms, Shenzhen Newway Photomask and Shenzhen Qingyi Photomask. It also competes with chipmakers' own mask shops."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Chinese and foreign firms make masks in China, but no Chinese firm appears in CSET's 2025 market shares for electron-beam mask writers, the machines that draw the pattern onto a mask. SMIC, a Chinese foundry, runs two in-house mask shops in Shanghai that make masks for deep ultraviolet and older lithography machines. Photronics began operating two mask plants in China, in Hefei and Xiamen, in 2019. Its chip mask business in Xiamen is a joint venture in which Dai Nippon Printing holds 49.99 percent."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Every EUV mask depends on a handful of firms at each step, from the blank plate to the tool that tests how it will print. Only three firms supply the blank plates for EUV masks. IMS Nanofabrication held 46.6 percent of the 2025 market for electron-beam mask writers and NuFlare 39.2 percent, by CSET's count. In 2019 Lasertec launched what it calls the first tool that inspects patterned EUV masks in EUV light. Zeiss calls its AIMS the only system that tests how a mask will print under conditions equivalent to the scanner's."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Pellicles already work in high-volume EUV manufacturing. But ASML says no material is completely transparent to EUV light, so any pellicle in the light's path costs customers productivity. In 2024 Mitsui Chemicals said it would set up production of carbon nanotube membranes, designed to pass 92 percent or more of the light, for next-generation High-NA, high-output EUV scanners."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","The stencil that lithography prints from, at least one for each layer of a chip."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Each mask prints its layer on wafer after wafer, so any flaw on it repeats on every wafer. Reread: How it works"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","How many firms make the blank plates for EUV masks?"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Three, and two of them are AGC and Hoya of Japan."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A blank is the plate before any pattern is drawn on it. For EUV it is a mirror of about 40 pairs of molybdenum and silicon layers laid on glass. Reread: Blanks"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Why is it hard for a new firm to start making EUV mask blanks?"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","The blank needs near-zero thermal expansion, perfectly smooth and flat surfaces and no particle contamination."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","AGC says it spent more than a decade meeting those requirements before it began mass production in 2017. Reread: The chokepoint"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","What kind of masks does China's SMIC make in its own shops?"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Masks for deep ultraviolet and older lithography machines."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","SMIC runs two in-house mask shops in Shanghai. No Chinese firm appears in CSET's 2025 market shares for electron-beam mask writers, the machines that draw a mask's pattern. Reread: Who makes it"],["photomasks-and-pellicles","A photomask is the stencil for one layer of a chip, and any flaw on it repeats on every wafer."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","Three firms make EUV mask blanks, and Lasertec launched the first tool that checks finished masks in EUV light."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","AGC spent more than a decade learning to make EUV blanks before mass production began in 2017."],["photomasks-and-pellicles","China makes masks for deep ultraviolet machines and older ones, in SMIC's own mask shops and at independent firms such as Shenzhen Qingyi and Shenzhen Newway."],["deposition-and-etch","Chapter 06 Stage 6 of 14 High concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["deposition-and-etch","Deposition and etch tools build a chip layer by layer. China-based toolmakers' share of deposition tools rose from 2 to 7 percent between 2019 and 2024, by CSET's count."],["deposition-and-etch","Deposition and etch build the chip itself, one layer at a time. Deposition lays down a thin film, sometimes only a few atoms thick. Lithography prints a pattern on it. Etch then eats away everything the pattern does not protect, and the next film goes down on top. Making one chip takes 1,000 to 1,500 steps, the Semiconductor Industry Association estimated in 2025. Some of the holes the etch cuts in memory chips are more than 50 times deeper than they are wide, like a finger-wide shaft about a meter deep. The film has to coat them right to the bottom. The etch has to eat one material and leave the one beside it untouched. Applied Materials and Lam Research in the United States, Tokyo Electron in Japan and ASM International in the Netherlands make most of these machines. Chinese toolmakers have gained share in both kinds of tool since 2019."],["deposition-and-etch","American companies held 60.3 percent of the world market for deposition tools in 2025, Japanese companies 14.0 percent and China-based companies 9.8 percent, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. In etch and cleaning tools that year, American companies held 52.6 percent, Japanese companies 32.6 percent and China-based companies 10.1 percent."],["deposition-and-etch","Atomic layer deposition tools coat a hole's walls and floor as evenly as its rim. China-based companies held only 2.6 percent of the world market for them in 2025, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. The December 2024 US export rule targets tools for atomic layer deposition of the metals molybdenum and ruthenium, and for coating holes more than 200 times deeper than they are wide."],["deposition-and-etch","Applied Materials and Lam Research are the two largest deposition and etch suppliers. Applied Materials' revenue across all its businesses was $28.368 billion in fiscal 2025. Lam Research's was $23.233 billion in fiscal 2026, the year to June 2026."],["deposition-and-etch","Applied Materials 82.4 percent of physical vapor deposition tools in 2025, by CSET's count from TechInsights data"],["deposition-and-etch","Lam Research 51.2 percent of conductor etch tools in 2025"],["deposition-and-etch","Tokyo Electron 55.9 percent of dielectric etch tools in 2025"],["deposition-and-etch","ASM International 54.5 percent of atomic layer deposition tools in 2025"],["deposition-and-etch","Naura 14.7 percent of physical vapor deposition tools in 2025"],["deposition-and-etch","United States Applied Materials, Lam Research"],["deposition-and-etch","Netherlands ASM International, atomic layer deposition"],["deposition-and-etch","China Naura, AMEC and Piotech, in the largest equipment market ($49.3 billion in 2025)"],["deposition-and-etch","Chinese toolmakers held 12.4 percent of dry etch in 2025, according to CSET's analysis of TechInsights data. They held 2.6 percent of atomic layer deposition that year, by the same count."],["deposition-and-etch","A December 2024 US rule lists some dry etch, atomic layer deposition and deep-hole deposition tools as controlled exports. Its foreign direct product rule reaches some tools built outside the United States."],["deposition-and-etch","Most etch steps, and many deposition steps, happen in a vacuum chamber that holds one wafer at a time. A pump empties the chamber of air, and a measured flow of gas comes in. A radio-frequency field, an electric field that reverses millions of times a second, turns the gas into a plasma. The field splits the gas into charged ions and into neutral fragments called radicals, which are more reactive than whole molecules."],["deposition-and-etch","In most deposition steps, the gas carries the material the film will be made of. The molecules, or the radicals a plasma splits from them, land on the wafer and stick. The film builds up a few atoms at a time."],["deposition-and-etch","To coat the floor of a deep hole as thickly as its rim, the machine can work in cycles, a method called atomic layer deposition. First one gas settles in a single layer on every surface, and the pump removes the rest. Then a second gas reacts with that layer and nothing else, and the pump empties the chamber again. Each cycle adds a fraction of a layer of atoms wherever the gas reached, so the film grows as evenly on a hole's walls and floor as on its rim."],["deposition-and-etch","Not every step runs one wafer at a time. Batch furnaces such as Tokyo Electron's TELINDY PLUS heat as many as 125 wafers at once, usually without plasma. They grow oxide films and run low-pressure chemical vapor deposition and some atomic layer deposition."],["deposition-and-etch","For etch, the gas attacks one material and leaves the one beside it. Wherever the photoresist covers the wafer, it shields the film beneath. Wherever it does not, the radicals react with the surface and turn it into a gas, which the pump carries away. A second field pulls the ions straight down at the wafer, so the etch cuts vertically and a narrow hole keeps its width as it deepens. When the etch reaches the material underneath, which the gas was chosen not to touch, it slows almost to a stop, and the tool ends the step."],["deposition-and-etch","The market sizes and leading shares below are 2025 figures from Georgetown University's Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET), based on data from the research firm TechInsights. CSET puts the deposition tool market at $26.2 billion. It puts the dry etch market at $21.9 billion."],["deposition-and-etch","Physical vapor deposition (PVD), which knocks atoms off a solid target and lands them on the wafer, was a $4.9 billion market in 2025. Applied Materials held 82.4 percent of it and China's Naura 14.7 percent."],["deposition-and-etch","Chemical vapor deposition (CVD), which reacts gases at the wafer surface to grow a film, was an $11.2 billion market in 2025, led by Applied Materials at 47 percent. The plasma-enhanced version (PECVD) runs cooler and made up most of it, $7.5 billion."],["deposition-and-etch","Atomic layer deposition (ALD) lays down less than one atomic layer at a time. Each step stops once every surface is covered, so it coats vertical walls as evenly as horizontal floors. The US Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS), which writes the export rules, says that even coating makes it important for building 3D structures, such as 3D DRAM, 3D NAND, and the FinFET and gate-all-around transistors in logic chips. ASM International leads it with 54.5 percent of a $4.1 billion market in 2025."],["deposition-and-etch","Epitaxy grows layers that line up with the crystal beneath them, using high-temperature CVD tools. Electroplating deposits the copper used for wiring across the wafer."],["deposition-and-etch","Conductor etch, which cuts gates, metals and silicon, was a $12.2 billion market in 2025, led by Lam at 51.2 percent, by CSET's count from TechInsights data."],["deposition-and-etch","Dielectric etch, which cuts the insulating oxides and nitrides between the conductors, was an $8.7 billion market in 2025, led by Tokyo Electron at 55.9 percent, by CSET's count from TechInsights data."],["deposition-and-etch","High-aspect-ratio etch cuts the deep, narrow channels that let 3D NAND stack layers of memory cells. A channel's aspect ratio is its depth divided by its width. Lam says slight departures from a channel's intended shape can hurt yield. Lam runs this etch well below 0 degrees Celsius. It says its Cryo 3.0 technology can etch channels up to 10 microns deep whose width varies from top to bottom by less than 0.1 percent of their depth."],["deposition-and-etch","AI hardware needs sideways cuts, deeper holes and a second stack of metal wiring on the back of the wafer."],["deposition-and-etch","Gate-all-around transistors need highly selective isotropic etch, which cuts sideways. BIS controls isotropic dry etch tools that remove silicon- germanium at least 100 times faster than silicon, a selectivity of 100:1 or more."],["deposition-and-etch","HBM (high-bandwidth memory) needs holes etched straight through the silicon, called through-silicon vias (TSVs), so chips can be stacked and wired. BIS controls the tools that etch these holes at aspect ratios (depth to width) of 10:1 or more and at rates above 7 microns a minute. The control covers only tools that also keep the holes' depth even to within 2 percent across the wafer."],["deposition-and-etch","Backside power delivery moves the wires that carry power to the back of the wafer. In July 2024 Applied Materials said it expected backside power to add $1 billion to the market for its wiring tools, for every 100,000 wafers a month of new fab capacity."],["deposition-and-etch","The industry association SEMI put world sales of chipmaking equipment at $135.1 billion in 2025, up 15 percent from $117.1 billion. Sales of wafer processing equipment, the category that includes deposition and etch tools, rose 12 percent."],["deposition-and-etch","No one firm dominates deposition and etch the way ASML dominates lithography. In dry etch, CSET's count for 2025 from TechInsights data puts Lam Research at 41.1 percent, Tokyo Electron at 23.4 percent and Applied Materials at 17.4 percent. Tokyo Electron's own results presentation, citing Gartner, gives it 23 percent of dry etch and 27 percent of deposition systems in 2025, a category that includes furnace, ALD and low-pressure CVD tools. Within that category, Tokyo Electron's share of ALD was 15 percent. The same presentation, again citing Gartner, gives it 91 percent of coater/developers in 2025. These machines coat wafers with photoresist and develop the pattern after lithography."],["deposition-and-etch","ASM International, the atomic layer deposition specialist, reached a record EUR 3.2 billion of revenue in 2025 as customers built 2 nm gate-all-around capacity. Molybdenum ALD, a new use of its tools that deposits the metal molybdenum, entered volume production that year."],["deposition-and-etch","China is the tool vendors' largest market, buying $49.3 billion of equipment in 2025, half a percent less than in 2024. Taiwan's spending rose 90 percent to $31.5 billion. South Korea's rose 26 percent to $25.8 billion. China still takes a large share of every major vendor's sales."],["deposition-and-etch","Tokyo Electron: 34.1 percent of sales in the year to March 2026, down from 41.7 percent. It was 30.4 percent in the quarter to June 2026."],["deposition-and-etch","Lam Research: about 34 percent of revenue in the year to June 2026, the same as a year earlier."],["deposition-and-etch","Applied Materials: 28 percent in the third fiscal quarter of 2026, down from 35 percent a year earlier."],["deposition-and-etch","ASM International: more than 30 percent of 2025 revenue."],["deposition-and-etch","Between 2019 and 2024, by CSET's analysis of TechInsights data, China-based suppliers went from 2 to 7 percent of deposition and from under 3 to almost 9 percent of etch and clean. In ALD they gained no share and held less than 1 percent in 2024."],["deposition-and-etch","CSET's newer analysis, of data that TechInsights published in July 2026, puts China-based suppliers at 9.8 percent of deposition in 2025. They held 10.1 percent of etch and clean that year. In dry etch alone their share was 12.4 percent. In ALD they held 2.6 percent in 2025, most of it from Piotech."],["deposition-and-etch","The Chinese toolmaker AMEC alone held 12.4 percent of dielectric etch in 2025, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. Its revenue was RMB 12.385 billion that year, up about 36.62 percent. It spent RMB 3.744 billion on research and development, 30.2 percent of sales."],["deposition-and-etch","The United States tightened its export controls at least five times between 2022 and 2025. The rules describe each deposition or etch tool by the process it is designed to run."],["deposition-and-etch","October 2022. BIS issued a rule on 7 October that required a license to export advanced chipmaking equipment to China. The rule listed that equipment under a new entry, ECCN 3B090. It also required US persons to get a license to ship, transfer or service items used at advanced fabs in China. It defined these as fabs that make logic chips with non-planar transistors or at 16/14 nm or below, NAND memory with 128 or more layers, or DRAM at 18 nm half-pitch or below. The rule extended US license rules to more foreign-made items bound for 28 Chinese entities on the Entity List. That list names the foreign firms that exporters need a license to supply."],["deposition-and-etch","October 2023. A rule issued in October 2023 and effective 17 November rewrote the US control list's entries for chipmaking equipment. It added tools for four processes. The first is dry etch, both sideways (isotropic) and vertical (anisotropic), under ECCN 3B001.c.1. The second is spatial ALD (3B001.d.9), whose design keeps stray particles down to the level advanced chips need. The third is low-fluorine tungsten ALD and CVD (3B001.d.10), which fills deep, narrow gaps in advanced chips with tungsten while keeping resistance low. The fourth is carbon hard mask PECVD (3B001.d.5), which lays down the etch-resistant carbon films that smaller features need."],["deposition-and-etch","December 2024. BIS controlled 24 more types of equipment and three types of software, and added 140 entities to the Entity List. The new equipment entries include TSV etch, and deposition into features with aspect ratios above 200:1. BIS also wrote a foreign direct product rule that reaches some tools built outside the United States. The rule largely exempts foreign-made tools exported by firms located in Japan, the Netherlands and the 31 other countries it lists, whose governments can control these tools themselves. Japan, one of those countries, had added advanced chipmaking equipment to its own control list on 23 July 2023."],["deposition-and-etch","September 2025. BIS removed the Chinese units of Samsung and SK hynix, and Intel Semiconductor (Dalian), from the Validated End-User program, effective 31 December 2025. From that date, US tools bound for them need a license. BIS estimated that the change would add 1,000 license applications a year."],["deposition-and-etch","September 2025. The Affiliates Rule extended Entity List restrictions to any company at least 50 percent owned by a listed entity. BIS then suspended it until 9 November 2026."],["deposition-and-etch","BIS enforces the rules on toolmakers too. In February 2026 BIS said Applied Materials had shipped ion implanters, tools that fire atoms into silicon, to a company in China on the Entity List in 2021 and 2022 without the license the Entity List requires. The tools, worth about $126 million, went to China through Applied's Korean unit. BIS set the penalty at about $252 million, twice their value and the most the law allows. In fiscal 2026 Applied Materials took a $253 million charge to settle an export controls compliance matter with BIS."],["deposition-and-etch","Among deposition and etch tool segments, China-based suppliers have their largest share in dry stripping, which clears leftover photoresist off the wafer. Dry stripping was a $314.6 million market in 2025, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. Japan's Kokusai held 35.7 percent of it, Mattson Technology 22.6 percent and Naura 8.3 percent. Mattson is based in the United States, but Beijing E-Town bought it in 2016. CSET counts Mattson's share as China's."],["deposition-and-etch","Deposition and etch tools are a chokepoint, but a weaker one than lithography, because chipmakers can buy each main tool from more than one maker. In dry etch, Lam Research held 41.1 percent in 2025, Tokyo Electron 23.4 percent and Applied Materials 17.4 percent, by CSET's count. Atomic layer deposition has at least five makers."],["deposition-and-etch","Deposition lays down a thin film, and etch cuts away the parts the printed pattern leaves exposed."],["deposition-and-etch","Making one chip takes 1,000 to 1,500 steps, the Semiconductor Industry Association estimated in 2025. Reread: How it works"],["deposition-and-etch","Which four companies make most deposition and etch tools?"],["deposition-and-etch","Applied Materials, Lam Research, Tokyo Electron and ASM International."],["deposition-and-etch","Applied Materials and Lam Research are American, Tokyo Electron is Japanese and ASM International is Dutch. No one firm dominates the way ASML dominates lithography. Reread: Who makes it"],["deposition-and-etch","What share of the deposition and dry etch tool markets did Chinese toolmakers hold in 2025?"],["deposition-and-etch","9.8 percent of deposition and 12.4 percent of dry etch, by CSET's count."],["deposition-and-etch","Their share of deposition tools rose from 2 percent in 2019 to 7 percent in 2024. Reread: China and the controls"],["deposition-and-etch","What share of atomic layer deposition tools did Chinese toolmakers hold in 2025?"],["deposition-and-etch","Atomic layer deposition coats a hole's walls and floor as evenly as its rim. BIS, which writes the US export rules, says that makes it important for 3D structures such as gate-all-around transistors. Reread: China and the controls"],["deposition-and-etch","Deposition lays down thin films and etch cuts them into patterns. Making one chip takes 1,000 to 1,500 steps, by a 2025 industry estimate."],["deposition-and-etch","Four American, Japanese and Dutch firms make most of these tools, and none dominates."],["deposition-and-etch","Chinese makers held 12.4 percent of dry etch and 9.8 percent of deposition in 2025, on CSET's count."],["deposition-and-etch","Chinese makers held 2.6 percent of atomic layer deposition in 2025, most of it from Piotech."],["metrology-and-inspection","Chapter 07 Stage 7 of 14 High concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA, an American firm, held 56.8 percent of the market for tools that measure and inspect wafers in 2025, by CSET's count."],["metrology-and-inspection","Metrology (measurement) and inspection are a chip factory 's quality control. Between the steps that build a chip, another machine looks the wafer over. It checks whether the lines are the right width, whether this layer landed squarely on the last one, and whether a speck of dirt has killed a circuit. The main chip in an AI accelerator, the one that does the calculating, is one of the largest cut from a wafer. A bigger chip is a bigger target for a speck. In a textbook example with the same density of specks, 49.2 percent of chips 1 centimeter on a side come out flawless, but only 11.3 percent of chips 2 centimeters on a side. In 2025 one American firm, KLA, held 56.8 percent of the market for these tools, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. So a chip factory, or fab, cut off from KLA would find fewer of the faults that make its chips fail."],["metrology-and-inspection","By CSET's count from TechInsights data, defect inspection was the largest kind of measuring and inspection tool in 2025, a $6.7 billion market. KLA held 85.9 percent of it. Chinese makers held 0.7 percent of the whole market that year by the same count. Yet China took 26 percent of KLA's revenue in the June 2026 quarter."],["metrology-and-inspection","Since October 2022 the US has required a license for any tool subject to US export rules bound for Chinese fabs that make advanced logic or memory chips. A December 2024 rule added specific tools to the export control list, among them inspection tools that can find defects of 21 nm or smaller."],["metrology-and-inspection","Process control tools, the machines that measure and inspect wafers and masks, were a $15.7 billion market in 2025, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. CSET is a research center at Georgetown University. KLA puts the whole wafer equipment market, including advanced packaging, at about $120 billion that year."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA held more than half of this market in 2025, several times the share of any rival. CSET's count puts KLA at 56.8 percent and Applied Materials, the next largest, at 11.2 percent. At its March 2026 investor day KLA cited Gartner's figures for 2024, which put its share at 56.5 percent, 6.5 times its nearest competitor's. In April 2026 KLA said its 2025 share was about 7 times the nearest competitor's."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA 56.8 percent of process control tools in 2025 by CSET's count"],["metrology-and-inspection","Applied Materials 11.2 percent of process control tools in 2025"],["metrology-and-inspection","Lasertec 6.4 percent of process control tools in 2025"],["metrology-and-inspection","Hitachi High-Tech 6.2 percent of process control tools in 2025"],["metrology-and-inspection","ASML 5.9 percent of process control tools in 2025"],["metrology-and-inspection","Nova 4.3 percent of process control tools in 2025"],["metrology-and-inspection","Onto Innovation 2.6 percent of process control tools in 2025"],["metrology-and-inspection","United States KLA (Milpitas), Onto Innovation (Wilmington, MA), Applied Materials"],["metrology-and-inspection","Netherlands ASML YieldStar and HMI e-beam, Veldhoven and San Jose"],["metrology-and-inspection","Japan Hitachi High-Tech (CD-SEM), Lasertec (mask inspection), Rigaku (X-ray)"],["metrology-and-inspection","Israel Nova (Rehovot) and Camtek (Migdal Haemek)"],["metrology-and-inspection","China Skyverse (Shenzhen), RSIC and other domestic makers, with 0.7 percent of the market in 2025 by CSET's count"],["metrology-and-inspection","Chinese firms held 0.7 percent of the world market for tools that measure and inspect wafers in 2025, by CSET's count. Skyverse, a Shenzhen maker of inspection and metrology tools, reported 2,053,298,171.74 yuan of revenue in 2025, up 48.75 percent on 2024."],["metrology-and-inspection","In 2025 the American firm KLA was the world's largest maker of metrology and inspection tools. Citing Gartner, KLA puts its 2024 share at 56.5 percent, 6.5 times its nearest rival's share."],["metrology-and-inspection","An inspection tool sweeps a beam of light across the wafer, photographs it, and compares the image of each chip with the image of its neighbors. The chips on a wafer are meant to be identical, so the tool flags anything that shows in one and not the others as a possible defect. It records where each one is. For faults too small for light to show, a second tool scans a beam of electrons across a small patch and builds a picture from the electrons the beam knocks loose from the surface."],["metrology-and-inspection","A metrology tool measures known shapes. It shines light on a test pattern printed beside the circuits and works out from the reflected light how wide the lines are and how thick the film is. It also reads marks printed in this layer and the last to measure how far the two are out of line, which chipmakers call overlay."],["metrology-and-inspection","The fab pays for all this to protect yield, the share of chips on a wafer that work. A wafer loses value two ways: whole regions ruined by mishandling, misalignment or over- etching, and single circuits killed by stray material or an airborne particle."],["metrology-and-inspection","A bigger chip is a bigger target for the second kind, so the cost of each good chip grows faster than its area. Chipmakers call each chip on a wafer a die. In the standard formula, die yield is (1 + D0A/a) to the power minus a. Here D0 is defects per square centimeter, A is die area, and a is a clustering constant of 3 to 4 that says how much defects bunch together. At a defect density of 0.8 per square centimeter, with a set to 3, a 1 square centimeter die yields 49.2 percent and a 2 by 2 centimeter die 11.3 percent. Because the bigger die yields less and fits fewer times on a wafer, it costs 20.1 times as much as the small one."],["metrology-and-inspection","One percentage point of yield can be worth millions of dollars a year. In another textbook example, a fab makes 5,000 wafers a week, each holding 200 dies, and earns $15 from each good die. Each percentage point of yield is then worth $7.8 million a year. Engineers raise yield by finding the process step that is losing dies and fixing it, work called yield learning."],["metrology-and-inspection","Chipmakers can sell more dies than the formula suggests, because its percentages count only dies with no killer defect. A chip built from many identical blocks can carry spares and switch off a faulty block. Nvidia's full H100 design has 144 of its main computing blocks, called streaming multiprocessors, and the SXM5 version it ships has 132 turned on. But the formula shows how fast flawless dies get scarce as chips grow."],["metrology-and-inspection","All the market sizes and shares below are CSET's, for 2025, from TechInsights data."],["metrology-and-inspection","Defect inspection scans a whole wafer with light, or small areas of it with electrons, and compares each die against its neighbors. It is by far the largest family, at $6.7 billion, and KLA held 85.9 percent of it. ASML's HMI eScan 1100 runs 25 electron beams at once, up to 15 times the throughput of single-beam inspection tools, and finds patterning defects down to 7 nm."],["metrology-and-inspection","Film and shape metrology measures how thick each film is and how flat the wafer is, without cutting it open. In this $2.6 billion family KLA held 45.6 percent, Nova 24.6 and Onto Innovation 10.9. Onto paid about $720 million in August 2026 for 27 percent of the Japanese X-ray tool maker Rigaku."],["metrology-and-inspection","Mask inspection and repair has its own tools, because a defect on a mask, the stencil the circuit pattern is printed from, repeats on every die. This $2.2 billion family and overlay metrology are the two where KLA has a close rival. KLA held 45.9 percent, Lasertec 42 and Zeiss 10.1. Lasertec also makes actinic inspection tools, which check EUV masks with the same 13.5 nm light that prints them. Lasertec calls its ACTIS A150 the world's first EUV patterned mask inspection system. KLA's own actinic mask inspection tool was still at an early demo stage at its March 2026 investor day."],["metrology-and-inspection","Overlay metrology measures how well this layer lines up with the one below. Its $991.4 million market was split almost evenly between KLA at 51.5 percent and ASML at 47.9."],["metrology-and-inspection","Critical dimension metrology, also called line-width measurement, measures how wide a printed feature came out. It is the one family Japan leads. Hitachi held 71.9 percent of this $1.2 billion market and Applied Materials 27.5."],["metrology-and-inspection","Electron-beam metrology resolves detail too fine for light. Applied Materials led this $1.3 billion family at 45.1 percent, with ASML at 35.6 and KLA at 18.8."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA says its share grew 3.6 percentage points from 2021 to 2025. It says it gained share again in 2025 across mask, optical wafer and e-beam inspection. Its revenue for fiscal 2026, the year to June 2026, was $13.579 billion, up from $12.156 billion in fiscal 2025."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA's rivals are far smaller, and none holds more than 11.2 percent, by CSET's count from TechInsights data for 2025. Eight of them each held more than 1 percent of the market that year."],["metrology-and-inspection","Applied Materials is the largest of them. It sells e-beam defect review tools, CD-SEMs (electron microscopes that measure line width) and e-beam metrology tools next to the deposition and etch tools whose work they check."],["metrology-and-inspection","Lasertec holds 6.4 percent, almost all of it mask inspection. Hitachi High-Tech holds 6.2 percent, most of it from CD-SEMs. ASML holds 5.9 percent through YieldStar overlay and HMI e-beam metrology."],["metrology-and-inspection","Nova holds 4.3 percent, through film metrology. It took $880.6 million of revenue in 2025."],["metrology-and-inspection","Onto Innovation holds 2.6 percent. It took $1,005.3 million of revenue in 2025."],["metrology-and-inspection","Camtek holds 1.6 percent. It took $496.1 million of revenue in 2025."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA's patterning line, which includes several metrology products and mask inspection, grew 61 percent year on year in the June 2026 quarter."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA says process control's share of spending on chipmaking equipment is still rising. For memory chips, KLA credits the rise to higher performance specifications, fewer spare circuits and more logic circuitry in devices built for high-performance computing."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA says its systems use AI to analyze data and suppress noise, and that this helps chipmakers reach high yield sooner. In April 2026 KLA said it had added AI to every product line over the previous five years."],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA says the AI build-out is making advanced packaging, and the process control it needs, more important. KLA says it became the largest supplier of process control tools for advanced wafer-level packaging in 2025, adding 14 percentage points of share. It expects about $1.1 billion of packaging process control revenue in 2026, up more than 70 percent. In February 2026 Onto said it had signed a volume purchase agreement estimated at over $240 million with a high-bandwidth memory (HBM) maker. The deal covers 2D inspection and 3D bump metrology, which measures the tiny metal bumps that join stacked chips, through 2027."],["metrology-and-inspection","Chinese makers are still small in process control, but one of them is growing fast. CSET's count, built on TechInsights data, puts all Chinese firms at 0.7 percent of the market in 2025. Skyverse (Shenzhen Zhongke Feice), a maker of wafer inspection and metrology tools, reported 2,053,298,171.74 yuan of revenue in 2025. That was up 48.75 percent on 2024. In its 2025 annual report Skyverse says Chinese makers still hold a low share of China's market for these tools and that KLA holds the largest share of it. In the June 2026 quarter China took 26 percent of KLA's revenue and Taiwan 31 percent."],["metrology-and-inspection","Chinese firms held 2 percent or less of each of five kinds of tool in 2025. By CSET's 2025 count from TechInsights data, they held 0.6 percent of defect inspection tools. They held 0.4 percent of line-width measurement tools in 2025. In film and shape metrology they held 2 percent in 2025, all of it from Raintree Scientific Instruments, or RSIC. They held no share of mask inspection and repair tools in 2025. Nor did they hold any share that year of the tools that inspect wafers during advanced packaging."],["metrology-and-inspection","In October 2022 the US began requiring a license for any item subject to US export rules, process control tools included, bound for certain Chinese fabs. The rule covered fabs that made logic chips at 16/14 nm or below, NAND memory with 128 or more layers, or DRAM at 18 nm half-pitch or below."],["metrology-and-inspection","A December 2024 rule added specific process control tools to the export control list. It controls tools for defect inspection and measurement of patterned 300 mm wafers if they can find defects of 21 nm or smaller. The control covers only tools that do this using light with a wavelength below 400 nm, an electron beam with a resolution of 1.65 nm or better, a cold field emission source, or two or more electron-beam sources. The same rule controls overlay metrology accurate to 0.5 nm or better in two cases. One is a tool built into the track, the machine that coats and develops the light-sensitive resist. The other is a tool that can change its measurement wavelength and take a measurement in less than 25 ms. It also controls stand-alone wafer shape metrology that feeds corrections to immersion or EUV scanners. A separate new entry, 3B994, covers optical film and line-width metrology for 300 mm wafers with software for measuring non-planar transistors."],["metrology-and-inspection","BIS, the US Commerce Department bureau that wrote the rule, placed all of these tools in two new entries, 3B993 and 3B994, for items it says also have legitimate uses in older chipmaking. For that reason BIS decided that, unlike tools built only for advanced chips, they do not warrant a license requirement covering a whole country or a presumption that BIS will refuse a license. A new foreign direct product rule extends US jurisdiction to specified foreign-made chipmaking tools bound for Macau or for a Country Group D:5 destination such as China."],["metrology-and-inspection","A fab that can buy scanners and etchers but not sensitive inspection tools finds fewer of the defects that lower its yield, so its yield rises more slowly. Most of those tools come from one firm, KLA, which held more than half the process control market in 2025. KLA led four kinds of process control tool that year, by CSET's count. It held 85.9 percent of defect inspection, the largest kind. Still, every kind of process control tool had a second maker that year, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. KLA says its share of the whole market grew from 2021 to 2025."],["metrology-and-inspection","What do metrology and inspection tools do?"],["metrology-and-inspection","They check each wafer between steps for line width, layer alignment and defects."],["metrology-and-inspection","Their measurements help a fab find out why its chips fail. Reread: How it works"],["metrology-and-inspection","Why do AI chips depend so much on finding defects?"],["metrology-and-inspection","They are among the largest chips made, and a bigger chip is more likely to have a defect."],["metrology-and-inspection","In a textbook example at the same density of defects, 49.2 percent of chips 1 centimeter on a side come out flawless, but only 11.3 percent of chips 2 centimeters on a side. Reread: How it works"],["metrology-and-inspection","Which company leads the market for tools that measure and inspect wafers?"],["metrology-and-inspection","KLA, an American firm, with 56.8 percent of the market in 2025, by CSET's count."],["metrology-and-inspection","Applied Materials, the next largest, held 11.2 percent. A fab cut off from KLA would find fewer of the faults that make its chips fail. Reread: Who makes it"],["metrology-and-inspection","What share of the market for wafer measuring and inspection tools did Chinese makers hold in 2025?"],["metrology-and-inspection","Skyverse, a Chinese maker of these tools, says KLA holds the largest share of China's own market for them. China took 26 percent of KLA's revenue in the June 2026 quarter. Reread: Packaging, AI and China"],["metrology-and-inspection","Metrology and inspection tools check each wafer between steps and help a fab find out why its chips fail."],["metrology-and-inspection","AI chips are among the largest made, so finding defects matters most for them."],["metrology-and-inspection","CSET's count puts KLA of the United States at 56.8 percent of this tool market in 2025, and Applied Materials, the next largest, at 11.2 percent."],["metrology-and-inspection","Chinese makers held 0.7 percent of this tool market in 2025 on CSET's count, though one Chinese maker, Skyverse, grew its revenue 48.75 percent that year."],["foundries-and-fabs","Chapter 08 Stage 8 of 14 Extreme concentration · Hard to substitute"],["foundries-and-fabs","The newest chips need the know-how to build the newest transistors and a fab that costs tens of billions of dollars. Only TSMC, Intel and Samsung have both."],["foundries-and-fabs","A chip factory, or fab, builds the transistors, the billions of tiny switches in every chip, and then wires them together. Each switch works like a valve. Current runs along a narrow strip of silicon called the channel, and a small voltage on a gate above the strip opens or shuts the flow. For decades chipmakers made the strips shorter, so the transistors switched faster and more of them fit on a chip. But once the strip gets short enough, current leaks through even when the gate is off, and the chip burns power doing nothing. The newest kind of transistor, called gate-all-around, cuts this leak by wrapping the gate around all four sides of the strip. A chipmaker needs two things to make the newest chips, and having one does not bring the other. The first is the know-how to build the newest switches, a long sequence of steps that have to run in exact order. In 2026 only TSMC, Intel and Samsung had it. The second is factories that cost tens of billions of dollars each, and in 2022 most of the world's capacity for the most advanced logic chips was in Taiwan. China's SMIC runs factories, but without EUV machines or the know-how for the newest switches, its most advanced chips are 7 nm-class. IBM developed 2 nm technology, but it yields no chips until Rapidus finishes a factory to run it, with mass production planned for 2027. No chip company sells enough of one product to fill such a factory on its own, so chip companies share a handful of them, run by foundries that make chips for other companies. TSMC runs the biggest, and all six of its largest plants are in Taiwan."],["foundries-and-fabs","Since September 2024 the United States has required a license to share the know-how for building gate-all-around transistors, except with countries that impose matching controls. China has announced $43 billion to develop its own extreme ultraviolet (EUV) scanners, but in September 2025 the Center for Strategic and International Studies judged that EUV remains firmly out of reach."],["foundries-and-fabs","SEMI projected in 2026 that China would keep the world's largest installed fab capacity in 2026 and 2027. In July 2026 TSMC raised its planned investment in Arizona to $265 billion across 12 facilities. SIA and BCG projected in May 2024 that the US share of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm would rise from almost none in 2022 to 28 percent by 2032."],["foundries-and-fabs","Nvidia's Blackwell GPU holds 208 billion switches on two dies, each die the largest a lithography machine can print in one shot. Every switch has to turn on fully, let almost no current through when off, and keep doing it for years. Blackwell is made by TSMC, on a custom process called 4NP. TSMC calls a plant a GIGAFAB once it can run more than 100,000 wafers a month, each a 300 mm disc, twelve inches across. It operates six of them, and every one is in Taiwan."],["foundries-and-fabs","TSMC N2, its first nanosheet node, in volume production since 4Q25"],["foundries-and-fabs","Intel 18A in high-volume production in the United States, as of 2026"],["foundries-and-fabs","Samsung Foundry 3 nm gate-all-around process in initial production since June 2022"],["foundries-and-fabs","SMIC $9.327 billion revenue in 2025, with its lines 93.5 percent full"],["foundries-and-fabs","Rapidus 267.6 billion yen raised in February 2026 to reach 2 nm mass production by 2027"],["foundries-and-fabs","Taiwan TSMC's six gigafabs, with N2 at Fab 20 Hsinchu and Fab 22 Kaohsiung, and UMC"],["foundries-and-fabs","South Korea Samsung Foundry, Hwaseong and Pyeongtaek"],["foundries-and-fabs","United States Intel 18A at Fab 52 in Arizona, TSMC Arizona, Samsung Taylor and GlobalFoundries"],["foundries-and-fabs","Japan Rapidus Chitose, Hokkaido, and TSMC Kumamoto"],["foundries-and-fabs","China SMIC Shanghai and Beijing 300 mm lines, and Hua Hong"],["foundries-and-fabs","China's SMIC made its most advanced chips on N+3, a 7 nm-class process built without extreme ultraviolet scanners, SemiAnalysis found in June 2026. SMIC cannot buy those scanners, so it prints its tightest layers in several passes on older deep-ultraviolet machines. China will keep the world's largest installed fab capacity in 2026 and 2027, SEMI projected in its third-quarter 2026 forecast."],["foundries-and-fabs","Intel is the only chipmaker that both develops and manufactures leading-edge logic chips in the United States, by its own account in August 2025. The United States had almost no logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022, and SIA and BCG projected in May 2024 that its share would reach 28 percent by 2032. In July 2026 TSMC raised its planned investment in Arizona to $265 billion across 12 facilities. The US government agreed in August 2025 to buy a passive 9.9 percent stake in Intel, with no board seat."],["foundries-and-fabs","Current leaks in two main ways, straight through the gate insulator and along the channel from end to end while the gate is off. The second leak grows as the channel gets shorter. Three fixes deal with the two leaks:"],["foundries-and-fabs","Better insulator. A thicker hafnium-based film, paired with a metal gate, lets fewer electrons slip straight through yet controls the channel as tightly as before. Intel replaced the silicon dioxide insulator with it at 45 nm in 2007. It said the new film cut leakage through the insulator more than tenfold."],["foundries-and-fabs","More gate. A planar transistor lays the gate on one side of a flat channel, and as the channel shortens the gate loses control of it. A FinFET stands the channel on edge as a fin, so the gate covers three sides, and gate-all-around wraps it around all four."],["foundries-and-fabs","Thinner channel. The fab thins the silicon until no current can flow where the gate cannot reach it."],["foundries-and-fabs","Making the switches is called the front end of line. It builds them in a fixed order, starting with the channel. In a FinFET, the older design, the fab etches the silicon into thin fins that stand up from the wafer, and the gate goes over each one."],["foundries-and-fabs","In a gate-all-around transistor, the fab instead grows alternating layers of silicon and silicon- germanium and cuts the stack into narrow bars. It lays a placeholder, called a dummy gate, across each bar where the real gate will go. On either side of the placeholder it cuts deep trenches where the source and drain, the two ends of the channel, will go. Through those trenches it etches the silicon-germanium layers back a little and fills the gaps with an insulator, the inner spacer, which keeps the gate apart from the source and drain. Then it grows the source and drain as crystal inside the trenches, a step called epitaxy."],["foundries-and-fabs","Only then does the fab remove the placeholder and etch away the silicon-germanium, leaving thin silicon sheets that hang between the source and drain like shelves. The inner spacer shields the source and drain from that etch. The fab coats every sheet with an insulating film a few atoms thick, so the gate can control the channel without touching it. Gate metal then fills the gaps above, below and beside each sheet, covering all four sides. Last come the contacts, small metal plugs down to the source, the drain and the gate, ready for the wiring layers above."],["foundries-and-fabs","The steps have to run in exact order, because later layers cover earlier ones. Once gate metal surrounds a sheet, the insulating film can no longer go between the sheet and the metal. Each step is a separate deposition, etch or implant. An implant step, called ion implantation, fires atoms of boron or phosphorus into chosen patches of silicon so they conduct the way the design needs."],["foundries-and-fabs","A nanosheet transistor lays the channel flat again, stacks two to four thin sheets and wraps gate metal around each one. Each fin in a FinFET adds a fixed amount of current, so a designer who needs more current has to add a whole fin. Nanosheets can be drawn at different widths, so current can be set in finer steps."],["foundries-and-fabs","TSMC's N2, its first nanosheet node, entered volume production in the fourth quarter of 2025. TSMC rates the follow-on N2P at 18 percent more speed at the same power and 36 percent less power at the same speed than its earlier N3E. It gives N2P 1.2 times the logic density of N3E and 1.15 times its chip density, but its technology page does not define either measure. These numbers are TSMC's own claims until someone measures the silicon. Each foundry picks its own baseline, and none publishes a density figure that can be compared with a rival's."],["foundries-and-fabs","Intel and Samsung also make gate-all-around transistors. Intel's version, called RibbonFET, is built into its 18A process, which Intel says is in high-volume production in the United States. Samsung got there first, starting initial production of its 3 nm gate-all-around process in June 2022. But SemiAnalysis reported in February 2023 that, because of yield problems, high-volume chips on Samsung's 3 nm gate-all-around technology were expected only in 2024."],["foundries-and-fabs","SemiAnalysis reported in 2024 that the SRAM cell, which holds one bit in the fast memory on a logic die, had barely shrunk since the 5 nm node. TSMC said in 2025 that its 2 nm SRAM uses a 0.021 square-micrometer cell and gets 1.1 times the density of its previous node by tuning design and process together. See Memory and HBM."],["foundries-and-fabs","In a conventional chip, power and signal share one stack of copper wiring above the transistors, where wide power rails crowd out the signal wires. With backside power, the fab grinds the wafer thin and builds a second network for power underneath it."],["foundries-and-fabs","Intel's version, PowerVia, is part of 18A, and Intel calls it an industry first. It cut routed area, the space a block of circuits takes once its wiring is laid out, by 11 percent and dynamic voltage droop tenfold. Droop is the sag in supply voltage when a block of logic switches on at once. TSMC's Super Power Rail connects the backside network directly to each transistor's source and drain. Against N2P, TSMC rates A16, which uses Super Power Rail, at 8 to 10 percent more speed, 15 to 20 percent less power and up to 1.10 times the chip density."],["foundries-and-fabs","TSMC plans to start A14 production in 2028, with more than 20 percent higher logic density than N2. It said in April 2026 that two more processes, A13 and A12, are scheduled to enter production in 2029."],["foundries-and-fabs","A basic logic circuit needs two transistors that switch on opposite signals, and in production chips the two sit side by side. Complementary field-effect transistors, or CFETs, stack the two on top of each other. The research institute imec sees them as an attractive design for logic nodes beyond 1 nm."],["foundries-and-fabs","Wiring the transistors together is called the back end of line, and it has become as hard to make as the transistor. Copper, the usual wiring metal, seeps into the insulator around it, so every wire needs a barrier, a liner and a cap. As the most critical wiring levels drop below a 20 nm pitch, those extra layers take a large share of the wire's width. Pitch is the distance from the center of one wire to the center of the next. Two metals are moving into those narrow levels."],["foundries-and-fabs","Ruthenium shows promise for use without a barrier, which would keep the wire's resistance low. imec has demonstrated ruthenium lines at a 16 nm pitch."],["foundries-and-fabs","Molybdenum in a thin film has up to 30 percent lower resistivity than tungsten, the metal it is replacing in contacts. It needs no barrier either, so chipmakers are putting it into some contacts and local wiring layers."],["foundries-and-fabs","A foundry makes chips designed by other companies, running all their designs on the same tools. TSMC and UMC, both based in Taiwan, make chips only for other companies. TSMC, founded in 1987, pioneered this pure-play model."],["foundries-and-fabs","Inside a fab, a chip is built up in layers, and a similar loop of steps repeats for each one. Wafers travel in batches, called lots, inside a sealed pod called a FOUP, short for front-opening unified pod. Entegris, a US maker of these pods, offers a standard version that holds 25 wafers. An overhead track carries the pod from tool to tool."],["foundries-and-fabs","At each tool a robot lifts one wafer out and the tool does its one job, such as depositing a film, printing a pattern, etching it, cleaning it or measuring it. Then the robot puts the wafer back, and the pod moves on to the next tool, often across the building. When a layer is finished, the loop starts again with the next one."],["foundries-and-fabs","Turning silicon into a finished, packaged chip takes 1,000 to 1,500 steps, depending on how complex the chip is, the Semiconductor Industry Association said in 2025. In 2021 the association put the time to make a finished wafer at about 12 weeks on average, and up to 14 to 20 weeks for advanced processes. The pod keeps the wafer clean for all of that time, because the wafer never meets the room's air."],["foundries-and-fabs","Each tool is set by a recipe, the list of gases, temperatures and times for one step. A foundry offers every customer the same list of recipes, so every design in the building can run on the same shared tools. The tools run day and night, because an idle tool earns nothing. The finished wafer is tested (see Test and assembly ), then cut and packaged."],["foundries-and-fabs","Chips at 7 nm and below, meaning the newest processes, were 79 percent of TSMC's wafer revenue in the third quarter of 2026. That share split into 33 percent at 3 nm, 28 at 5 nm, 10 at 7 nm and 8 at 2 nm. TSMC's revenue for the quarter was $46.72 billion, at a 66.4 percent gross margin."],["foundries-and-fabs","Intel and Samsung design and sell their own chips and rent out capacity too. Renting out capacity is harder for them, because customers dislike handing their designs to a competitor and each company's own products take its best capacity. Intel Foundry reported $5.8 billion of segment revenue in the second quarter of 2026 and an operating loss of $2.089 billion. Only $293 million of that revenue came from outside customers."],["foundries-and-fabs","A new leading-edge fab costs tens of billions of dollars. In 2023 the Boston Consulting Group (BCG) estimated that a new fab for chips at 2 nm and below, completed in 2026, would cost $35 to $43 billion to build, equip and run over ten years. Building and equipping alone takes as much as $20 to $25 billion of capital for a leading-edge fab, the Semiconductor Industry Association (SIA) told the US Senate in March 2026."],["foundries-and-fabs","Most of TSMC's capacity is in its six GIGAFABs. Together, the plants TSMC and its subsidiaries run had capacity for more than 17 million wafers a year in 2025, counted as if each were the standard 12-inch size. The six largest plants had a combined capacity of more than 13 million. The other plants are five smaller fabs in Taiwan, two in China, two in the United States and one in Japan. In July 2026 TSMC announced another $100 billion for four more fabs at 2 nm or below, taking its planned investment in Arizona to $265 billion across 12 facilities."],["foundries-and-fabs","In 2025 the biggest AI chip designers used most of the world's supply of two inputs but only a small share of its advanced chipmaking. Epoch AI estimated that the four largest used around 90 percent of the world's CoWoS packaging capacity and HBM memory supply. CoWoS is TSMC's packaging for AI chips, and HBM is the stacked memory that sits beside them. The same four used only 12 percent of advanced logic production. See Advanced packaging."],["foundries-and-fabs","AI accelerators have usually trailed the leading edge. A die as large as theirs is more likely to hold a defect. So the share of dies that work, called the yield, gets high enough only once a process has run long enough to cut its defect rate."],["foundries-and-fabs","Nvidia's Blackwell is made on an older TSMC process than AMD's MI455X. Epoch AI estimated in December 2025 that a 300 mm wafer on Blackwell's 4NP process costs $17,000. AMD's MI455X, launched on 23 July 2026, is made on TSMC's 2 nm and 3 nm processes. It spreads its compute across eight separate dies."],["foundries-and-fabs","TSMC, Intel and Samsung build gate-all-around nodes with extreme ultraviolet (EUV) lithography. China's SMIC builds 7 nm-class nodes without it. SemiAnalysis reported in September 2026 that Intel's Panther Lake, Samsung's Exynos 2600 and Apple's A20 Pro, which is made on TSMC's N2, all use gate-all-around transistors."],["foundries-and-fabs","In August 2025 Intel called itself the only semiconductor company that both develops and manufactures leading-edge logic chips in the United States. That month the US government agreed to buy 433.3 million newly issued Intel shares at $20.47 each, or $8.9 billion in all, for a 9.9 percent stake. The stake is passive, with no board seat. The deal also gave the government a five-year warrant to buy a further 5 percent of Intel at $20 a share. It can use the warrant only if Intel's ownership of its foundry business falls below 51 percent."],["foundries-and-fabs","In 2026 Intel began high-volume manufacturing of some of its Panther Lake processors using ASML's High-NA extreme ultraviolet scanners. But it is building fewer fabs than it planned. In July 2025 Intel said it would no longer go ahead with planned projects in Germany and Poland and would slow construction in Ohio."],["foundries-and-fabs","In December 2024 the US Commerce Department awarded Samsung up to $4.745 billion of CHIPS Act funding, to support more than $37 billion of planned investment in Central Texas. That plan covers two new leading-edge logic fabs and a research fab in Taylor, and an expansion of Samsung's existing plant in Austin."],["foundries-and-fabs","China's SMIC has the factories without the know-how for the newest transistors. Its revenue rose 16.2 percent to $9.327 billion in 2025, at a 21 percent gross margin. Its lines ran 93.5 percent full, on monthly capacity above a million wafers counted in the smaller 8-inch size."],["foundries-and-fabs","A node's name, such as 7 nm, does not measure any feature on the chip. SMIC's N+3, its third-generation 7 nm process, sets its narrowest wires 32.5 nm apart, tighter than the 36 nm in Intel's Panther Lake chips on 18A. But the 18A process itself allows wires 32 nm apart. SemiAnalysis called the comparison an incomplete, cherry-picked metric. N+3 packs 113.4 million transistors per square millimeter, against 107.7 for TSMC's N6."],["foundries-and-fabs","Two research groups disagree about where Huawei's Ascend AI chips are made. Georgetown University's Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET) reported in June 2024 that the Ascend 910B was believed to be made on SMIC's N+2 process. But the research firm SemiAnalysis judged in April 2025 that most Ascend 910B and 910C chips were made on TSMC's 7 nm process. It said Huawei got around the sanctions that barred it from TSMC by buying about $500 million of 7 nm wafers through another company, Sophgo."],["foundries-and-fabs","IBM shows the opposite split. Its 2 nm technology yields no chips until Rapidus, a state-backed newcomer in Japan, finishes a factory to run it. The two firms agreed in December 2022 to develop that technology further for production at Rapidus's plant in Japan."],["foundries-and-fabs","In July 2025 Rapidus said it had started making 2 nm prototypes at the plant, in Chitose, Hokkaido, and would begin mass production in 2027. In February 2026 it raised 267.6 billion yen from the Japanese government and 32 companies to reach 2 nm mass production by 2027. By June 2026 Rapidus had raised 424.95 billion yen in equity."],["foundries-and-fabs","A firm that wants to make the newest chips has to develop its own process, because TSMC, Intel and Samsung do not sell their leading-edge process flows. A process flow sets the steps, their order and the tools for each. In September 2024 the United States began requiring a license to share the know-how for building gate-all-around transistors, except with countries that impose matching controls."],["foundries-and-fabs","China has money for chipmaking but cannot buy EUV scanners. It launched its third National Integrated Circuit Fund in May 2024 with 344 billion yuan, about $47 billion. China's 7 nm chips have been made on deep-ultraviolet machines, a generation behind EUV. China had stockpiled those machines from ASML, the Dutch scanner maker, before export restrictions took effect. SMIC gets fine features out of them by building its tightest layers in several patterning steps."],["foundries-and-fabs","In July 2026 Reuters reported that a Shanghai state firm had begun making home-grown immersion deep-ultraviolet scanners. Reuters's own source said the firm's machine still needed testing and was far from matching ASML's models."],["foundries-and-fabs","Domestic EUV is further off. China has announced $43 billion to develop it. In September 2025 the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) judged that EUV remains firmly out of reach despite massive state investment. See Lithography."],["foundries-and-fabs","The factories are concentrated too. In 2022 South Korea and Taiwan held almost all of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm, and the United States had almost none. Taiwan alone held 69 percent. In May 2024 SIA and BCG projected that the US share of that capacity would reach 28 percent by 2032."],["foundries-and-fabs","China leads the world in capacity for logic chips made at 28 nm or older, but little of its capacity is advanced. Most of the world's wafers come off such older lines, which make power devices, analog chips and microcontrollers. Across all nodes, old and new, the industry association SEMI forecast in June 2024 that China would have installed capacity of 10.1 million wafers a month in 2025, the most of any region. It forecast 5.8 million for Taiwan, out of a world total of 33.7 million, all counted in the 8-inch size. In the third-quarter 2026 update of its World Fab Forecast, SEMI projected that China would keep the largest installed capacity in 2026 and 2027."],["foundries-and-fabs","Chip production in Taiwan faces three risks:"],["foundries-and-fabs","Seismic. Taiwan sits on an active plate boundary, and after an earthquake in January 2025 TSMC had to scrap some wafers in process."],["foundries-and-fabs","Power. TSMC says power outages, dips or surges caused by problems at its electricity supplier have at times interrupted its operations."],["foundries-and-fabs","Political. In December 2025 SemiAnalysis put Taiwan's share of the world's advanced-node capacity at over 90 percent, though it did not say which node sizes count as advanced. So a blockade or conflict would cut most of that output off from the world market at once. See Who Controls the Chain."],["foundries-and-fabs","Building capacity outside Taiwan is slow, and TSMC has yet to build a gigafab anywhere else. SemiAnalysis wrote in December 2025 that a foundry needs highly skilled engineers to get the most working chips from each wafer. It judged that finding enough workers remained a major challenge for TSMC in Arizona."],["foundries-and-fabs","What two things does a chipmaker need to make the newest chips?"],["foundries-and-fabs","The know-how to build the newest transistors, and factories that cost tens of billions of dollars."],["foundries-and-fabs","Having one does not bring the other. China's SMIC runs factories, but its most advanced chips are 7 nm-class, and in 2026 only TSMC, Intel and Samsung had both. Reread: How it works"],["foundries-and-fabs","Why do the newest transistors wrap the gate around the channel?"],["foundries-and-fabs","To cut the current that leaks when the switch is off."],["foundries-and-fabs","Shorter channels switch faster but leak more when the gate is off. A gate on all four sides cuts that leak further than a fin, whose gate covers three. Reread: How it works"],["foundries-and-fabs","A company that makes chips designed by other companies."],["foundries-and-fabs","A chip factory, or fab, costs tens of billions of dollars, and no chip company sells enough of one product to fill a fab by itself. Reread: The foundry and the fab"],["foundries-and-fabs","In 2025 they could make more than 13 million wafers a year, out of more than 17 million for the whole company. Taiwan held 69 percent of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022. Reread: Capacity and cost"],["foundries-and-fabs","How does China's SMIC make advanced chips without an EUV machine?"],["foundries-and-fabs","It builds its tightest layers in several patterning steps on deep-ultraviolet tools."],["foundries-and-fabs","China cannot buy EUV scanners. With this method SMIC makes chips on N+3, its third-generation 7 nm process. Reread: The chokepoint"],["foundries-and-fabs","The newest chips need both the know-how to build the newest transistors and factories that cost tens of billions of dollars, and in 2026 only TSMC, Intel and Samsung had both."],["foundries-and-fabs","The newest transistors wrap the gate around all four sides of the channel to cut the current that leaks when the switch is off."],["foundries-and-fabs","A foundry makes chips for other companies, because no chip company sells enough of one product to fill a fab alone."],["foundries-and-fabs","All six of TSMC's largest plants are in Taiwan, which held 69 percent of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022."],["foundries-and-fabs","China's SMIC makes 7 nm-class chips without EUV by building its tightest layers in several patterning steps."],["memory-and-hbm","Chapter 09 Stage 9 of 14 Extreme concentration · Hard to substitute"],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix, Samsung and Micron make nearly all high bandwidth memory (HBM), the stacked memory beside AI chips. SK hynix took 63.2 percent of HBM revenue in 2025."],["memory-and-hbm","High bandwidth memory, or HBM, is where an AI chip keeps the numbers it is working on, and it is built to hand them over fast. A memory maker etches tiny holes into each memory wafer, fills them with copper and grinds the wafer until the copper shows through its back. It tests each of the wafer's chips and stacks up to sixteen good ones into a cube, with every layer wired to the ones below. The cube then sits beside the processor, the chip that does the calculating. Stacking is the hard part because each chip is ground thinner than a human hair and the finished cube has to stay within a height limit of less than a millimeter. One chip that fails after stacking can scrap the whole cube. Only SK hynix, Samsung and Micron make HBM in volume. One US export rule covers HBM from all three, including the two based in South Korea."],["memory-and-hbm","US-based Micron went from 5.8 percent of HBM revenue in 2024 to 23.1 percent in the first quarter of 2026, according to IDC figures in SK hynix's US prospectus. Over the same period, Samsung's share fell from 37.8 percent to 20.5 percent."],["memory-and-hbm","Since December 2024, a US license has been required, unless an exception applies, to export to China any HBM moving more than 2 GB per second per square millimeter of its area. The Institute for Progress reported in October 2025 that China's CXMT planned to produce HBM3 in 2026. Even so, working from TrendForce's estimate of world HBM shipments, the institute projected that producers outside China would make 70 times as much HBM as China in 2026. In June 2026 SemiAnalysis judged that CXMT was still struggling to stabilize supply of eight-high HBM3."],["memory-and-hbm","An AI accelerator moves numbers from memory to its arithmetic units and back. The US export control office wrote in December 2024 that a processor cannot reach its full capabilities unless its memory capacity and bandwidth rise with its speed."],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix 63.2 percent of HBM revenue in 2025"],["memory-and-hbm","Samsung 19.3 percent of HBM revenue in 2025"],["memory-and-hbm","Micron 17.4 percent of HBM revenue in 2025"],["memory-and-hbm","South Korea SK hynix in Cheongju and Icheon, Samsung in Pyeongtaek and Hwaseong"],["memory-and-hbm","United States Micron headquarters and R&D, and an SK hynix packaging plant under construction in Indiana"],["memory-and-hbm","Singapore Micron HBM advanced packaging plant, adding capacity from 2027"],["memory-and-hbm","In June 2026 SemiAnalysis judged that CXMT, China's strongest DRAM maker, was still struggling to stabilize supply of eight-high HBM3. The Institute for Progress had estimated in October 2025 that China would make virtually no HBM that year. Huawei said in September 2025 that its Ascend 950 chips would use two HBM designs of its own, without saying who would manufacture the memory."],["memory-and-hbm","Micron is the only American HBM maker. As of October 2026, License Exception HBM lets US and allied exporters ship HBM below 3.3 GB per second per square millimeter without a license, including to China when the chip designer buys it directly and it goes straight to the packaging site."],["memory-and-hbm","Each layer in the cube is a DRAM chip, the ordinary kind of computer memory. Each layer is ground thin and bonded to the one below through tiny metal bumps called microbumps. The whole stack sits on a base die, a chip that manages it. The copper-filled holes are called through-silicon vias, or TSVs. They let a signal reach any layer without a wire running around the outside."],["memory-and-hbm","An HBM3E cube has a 1,024-bit interface, meaning it exchanges data with the processor over 1,024 wires at once. That is sixteen times wider than a standard DDR5 memory module, the memory stick in a PC. HBM4 doubles that to 2,048 wires. Ordinary memory cannot be made that wide, because the pins would not fit on a circuit board. The stack can, since its wires run down through the TSVs and across a silicon interposer to the processor beside it, with no board in the way. The interposer is a slice of silicon carrying fine wiring, set under both the memory and the processor (see Advanced packaging )."],["memory-and-hbm","A chip needs the width most when it answers a prompt. Training reuses each stored number across a huge multiplication, so a chip can fetch little and compute a lot. But to generate one word of an answer, the chip reads the whole model from memory, plus the whole record of the conversation so far. Then it does a little arithmetic and waits for the next read. That record grows with the length of the conversation and the number of users served at once. So memory size and speed usually set how many people one chip can serve."],["memory-and-hbm","Micron's HBM3E comes in two sizes, 24 GB with eight chips stacked and 36 GB with twelve."],["memory-and-hbm","All three HBM makers run their HBM4 faster than the 8 Gb/s per pin in the industry standard. The standards body JEDEC published JESD270-4 in April 2025, setting the 2,048-bit interface and 2 TB/s per stack at 8 Gb/s per pin. SK hynix says it was first to complete HBM4 development, in September 2025, at over 10 Gb/s per pin. Samsung says it began mass production and shipped the first commercial HBM4 in February 2026, at 11.7 Gb/s per pin, with a 4 nm logic base die. It gives that HBM4 a maximum of 3.3 TB/s per stack. Micron's parts run above 11 Gb/s for more than 2.8 TB/s per stack. Micron says it began volume production of its 36 GB twelve-high HBM4 in fiscal 2026 and expects to ramp volume of HBM4E, the next generation, in calendar 2027."],["memory-and-hbm","Through HBM3E, SK hynix made its own base dies, the chips at the bottom of each stack. For HBM4 it chose TSMC's advanced logic process, so the base die can hold more functions. As a result, TSMC, which does not make HBM, makes the base die for SK hynix's HBM4."],["memory-and-hbm","Etch and thin. Etch vertical holes, the through-silicon vias, into a memory wafer, fill them with copper, then grind the wafer from behind until the copper comes through."],["memory-and-hbm","Stack and join. Makers join the chips through metal bumps by methods such as TC-NCF and MR-MUF. In MR-MUF, short for mass reflow molded underfill, the chips are first connected through microbumps and stacked, and a liquid underfill is then injected to fill every gap at once and cured. SK hynix uses its own version, Advanced MR-MUF, which stacks the chips, injects a liquid protective material between them and hardens it. SK hynix says the process controls warping and dissipates heat well. Samsung said in February 2024 that its twelve-high HBM3E uses TC-NCF, thermocompression with a thin non-conductive film between the chips. Samsung expected TC-NCF to help limit warping as chips get thinner."],["memory-and-hbm","Stay under the height limit. The package specification for HBM4 raised the height allowed for a finished cube from 720 micrometers to 775, still under a millimeter."],["memory-and-hbm","Hybrid bonding is the next step, but it is not ready. It would join the chips copper to copper and insulator to insulator, with no solder and no filler. A tech note on SK hynix's newsroom gives about 20 micrometers as the typical spacing between microbumps, against less than 1 micrometer for hybrid bonds. It says full-scale adoption in HBM is most likely at HBM4E or HBM5, where stacks are projected to pass twenty layers. Taller stacks trap more heat, and removing it becomes a major challenge at 16 to 20 layers. The same tech note says hybrid bonding manages that heat more efficiently."],["memory-and-hbm","Three firms took more than 90 percent of the revenue from ordinary computer memory, or DRAM, in the first quarter of 2026, according to IDC figures in SK hynix's US prospectus. HBM comes from the same three, SK hynix, Samsung and Micron. No other company has both leading-edge DRAM and a stacking line of its own. SK hynix says only a few firms have the expertise and resources to design, make and package memory chips. It says HBM also needs advanced production processes, such as TSV packaging, and must pass the rigorous testing and approval processes its customers set."],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix says it was the first company to mass-produce several generations of HBM, including HBM3 and HBM3E."],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix and Micron are both adding HBM capacity. SK hynix broke ground in August 2026 on an advanced packaging plant in West Lafayette, Indiana, an investment of over $4 billion. Micron is modernizing and expanding its DRAM and HBM production capacity in Taiwan. It has also broken ground on an HBM advanced packaging plant in Singapore to expand its packaging capacity from early 2027."],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix led HBM revenue in 2024, in 2025 and in the first quarter of 2026, and in that quarter Micron passed Samsung for second place. In 2024 SK hynix took 56.4 percent, Samsung 37.8 and Micron 5.8. In 2025 the three took 63.2, 19.3 and 17.4 percent. In the first quarter of 2026 they stood at 56.4, 20.5 and 23.1 percent, which put SK hynix back at its 2024 share. The split is public because SK hynix registered shares in the United States, and its US prospectus credits the research firm IDC."],["memory-and-hbm","As HBM grows, memory makers have less factory capacity left for traditional DRAM. In December 2025 Micron put the HBM market at about $35 billion in 2025 and forecast that it would reach around $100 billion in 2028. Micron says HBM needs more wafers than traditional DRAM, the kind used in PCs and phones, to make the same number of bits. SK hynix says the industry's shift of production capacity to HBM has left traditional DRAM undersupplied. The shortage, it says, helped drive a significant price recovery for that DRAM from the third quarter of 2025."],["memory-and-hbm","The leading accelerators made outside China use HBM from SK hynix, Samsung or Micron. Nvidia's GB300 NVL72 rack carries 20 TB of HBM3E at up to 576 TB/s. Each Nvidia Rubin GPU carries up to 288 GB of HBM4 at up to 22 TB/s. AMD's MI355X carries 288 GB of HBM3E at 8 TB/s."],["memory-and-hbm","A US export rule of December 2024 covers every HBM stack that was in production when it was published. The Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS), the US export control office, published the rule on 5 December 2024. It added an export classification, ECCN 3A090. c, for \"High bandwidth memory (HBM) having a ' memory bandwidth density ' greater than 2 gigabytes per second per square millimeter \". Its technical note defines that density as the memory bandwidth in gigabytes per second divided by the area of the package or stack in square millimeters. The rule also covers stacks made outside the United States, through a foreign direct product rule, which applies US controls to goods made abroad with American technology. BIS stated in the rule that all HBM stacks then in production exceeded that threshold."],["memory-and-hbm","BIS reviews license applications to ship controlled HBM to Macau or a Country Group D:5 destination such as China according to where the buyer is headquartered. It presumes it will deny a license when the buyer or its ultimate parent is headquartered in one of those places, and presumes approval otherwise."],["memory-and-hbm","Two provisions narrow the control. License Exception HBM, at 15 CFR 740.25, applies to exporters headquartered in the United States or a Country Group A:5 ally. It lets them ship HBM below 3.3 GB per second per square millimeter without a license, including to Macau and Country Group D:5 destinations such as China. HBM sent to those destinations must be bought directly by the designer of the chip it will be packaged into. Every shipment under the exception must go straight to the packaging site. The rule also excludes co-packaged chips that combine HBM and logic and whose main function is processing, which other chip controls may cover instead."],["memory-and-hbm","The think tank CSIS said in December 2024 that the rules still allowed HBM2, a generation introduced in 2016, to go to China, with limits on who could buy it and what for. It also said Nvidia's H20, whose HBM3 is packaged with the processor, was then still exportable under the performance limits for AI chips."],["memory-and-hbm","China's strongest DRAM maker, CXMT, was still struggling to make HBM in steady supply by June 2026. In December 2024 CSIS called CXMT one of only two Chinese firms with a credible path to producing advanced HBM, though it did not name the other. The Institute for Progress reported in October 2025 that CXMT was planning to produce HBM3 in 2026. It also estimated that China would make virtually no HBM in 2025. In June 2026 SemiAnalysis judged that CXMT was still struggling to stabilize supply of eight-high HBM3, with even greater challenges at twelve-high."],["memory-and-hbm","Huawei plans to use HBM of its own design in its Ascend 950 AI chips, but when it announced the designs in September 2025 it did not say who would make the memory. The two designs are called HiBL 1.0 and HiZQ 2.0. Huawei said the 950DT, due in the fourth quarter of 2026, would carry 144 GB of HiZQ 2.0 at 4 TB/s."],["memory-and-hbm","High-bandwidth memory, made of memory chips stacked into a cube beside the processor and wired to pass data fast."],["memory-and-hbm","Before stacking, each chip gets holes filled with copper, which wire every layer to the ones below. A stack holds up to sixteen chips. Reread: How it works"],["memory-and-hbm","Why does an AI chip need such fast memory?"],["memory-and-hbm","For each word it writes, it reads the whole model from memory."],["memory-and-hbm","Memory speed and size usually set how many users one chip can serve. Reread: How it works"],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix, Samsung and Micron make nearly all of it."],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix sold 63.2 percent of it in 2025 and Samsung 19.3 percent. A fourth maker would need both the newest DRAM, the kind of memory chip used in PCs and phones, and a line that stacks it. Reread: Who makes it"],["memory-and-hbm","Virtually none, the Institute for Progress estimated in October 2025."],["memory-and-hbm","China's strongest DRAM maker, CXMT, was still struggling to make HBM in steady supply by June 2026. A US export rule of December 2024 controls every HBM stack that was in production when the rule was published. Reread: The chokepoint"],["memory-and-hbm","HBM is memory stacked into a cube beside the processor and wired to pass data fast."],["memory-and-hbm","An AI chip reads its whole model from memory for each word, so memory speed limits it."],["memory-and-hbm","SK hynix, Samsung and Micron make nearly all HBM."],["memory-and-hbm","Since December 2024 US controls have covered the HBM stacks then in production, with two exceptions. The Institute for Progress estimated that China made virtually no HBM in 2025."],["advanced-packaging","Chapter 10 Stage 10 of 14 Extreme concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["advanced-packaging","Epoch AI estimates that in 2025 Nvidia, Google, AMD and Amazon used around 90 percent of the capacity for CoWoS, TSMC's packaging for AI chips."],["advanced-packaging","Packaging joins finished chips into one component and mounts them on a small circuit board, called a substrate, wired far more coarsely than the chips themselves. A lithography machine, which prints a chip's circuits, can cover only a rectangle about the size of a postage stamp in one shot. Many leading accelerators, Nvidia's Blackwell among them, need more logic than fits in that rectangle. So they are built from several chips, called dies, set side by side on an interposer, a layer of much finer wiring that links them and sits on the substrate. Stacks of memory chips sit on the same interposer, a few millimeters away. The interposer is either one piece of silicon or layers of fine copper wiring that often carry small silicon bridges where the links are densest. Silicon expands less than the resin substrate beneath it when heated, so the package can warp and its joints crack. Preventing that in high volume is hard. Nvidia, Google, AMD and Amazon all use TSMC's interposer packaging, called CoWoS, made in Taiwan."],["advanced-packaging","Epoch AI estimates that in 2025 Nvidia used 60.3 percent of all capacity for CoWoS, TSMC's interposer packaging. On the July 2026 earnings call, TSMC's chief executive, C.C. Wei, said its packaging capacity was so tight that it limited customers' growth. Asked about Intel's EMIB -T packaging, he said he hoped it would take some of the load off TSMC."],["advanced-packaging","In a TrendForce ranking by 2024 revenue, which CSET cites, four of the top ten outsourced firms that package and test chips are headquartered in China. But in 2025 Chinese firms had 5.3 percent of the market for advanced packaging fabrication tools, against 65.8 percent for US firms, by CSET's analysis of TechInsights data."],["advanced-packaging","A lithography scanner prints a rectangle 26 mm by 33 mm, or 858 mm², in one exposure. That area is called the reticle field. Every leading AI accelerator, counting its memory stacks, covers more area than that. Packaging is the stage that lets an accelerator be larger than one reticle field, and the packaging method limits how much larger it can be."],["advanced-packaging","TSMC CoWoS packaging used by Nvidia, Google, AMD and Amazon in 2025"],["advanced-packaging","Intel Foveros 3D packaging in volume at Rio Rancho, New Mexico, since January 2024"],["advanced-packaging","ASE Technology NT$389.2 billion assembly, test and materials revenue, 2025"],["advanced-packaging","ASMPT Thermocompression bonders, with $532.1 million of advanced packaging revenue in 2025"],["advanced-packaging","Taiwan TSMC advanced packaging fabs and a cluster of outsourced assembly and test firms"],["advanced-packaging","United States Intel Foveros packaging in volume at Rio Rancho, New Mexico"],["advanced-packaging","China Four of the top ten outsourced assembly and test firms by 2024 revenue are Chinese, in a TrendForce ranking cited by CSET"],["advanced-packaging","Chinese firms had 5.3 percent of the market for fabrication tools built for advanced packaging in 2025, by CSET's analysis of TechInsights data. Between 2019 and 2024 they gained 5 percentage points of share in test tools but lost share in bonding and other conventional assembly and packaging tools."],["advanced-packaging","Intel opened Fab 9 in Rio Rancho, New Mexico, in January 2024 to make its Foveros 3D packages in volume. Amkor broke ground in October 2025 on a $7 billion packaging and test campus in Peoria, Arizona, and expects production to start in early 2028."],["advanced-packaging","A second reason for the interposer is high bandwidth memory (HBM). An HBM4 stack connects through 2,048 data signals, packed too tightly for a standard resin substrate, so the memory sits beside the logic on the interposer. Even Nvidia's H100, whose single logic die is 814 mm² and fits inside one reticle field, carries five HBM stacks. Epoch AI counts TSMC's CoWoS packaging among the three inputs the H100 needs, along with its logic die and its HBM."],["advanced-packaging","CoWoS stands for chip on wafer on substrate, the order in which the parts are joined. For CoWoS-S, the version whose interposer is one piece of silicon, TSMC makes a silicon wafer that carries wiring and vertical copper vias but no transistors. Vias are metal-filled holes that join one layer of wiring to the next."],["advanced-packaging","TSMC bonds the logic dies and memory stacks face down onto that wafer with microbumps. These are dots of solder, and each dot is one electrical joint. In Intel's Foveros 2.5D packaging, which can also set dies side by side on a silicon interposer, the microbumps sit 36 micrometers apart, less than half a hair's width. The spacing differs by design, and SK hynix gives about 20 micrometers as typical for microbumps. Then TSMC cuts the interposer out of the wafer and attaches it to the resin substrate, which later goes onto a circuit board."],["advanced-packaging","One cracked joint can scrap a package holding eight tested HBM stacks and two large, expensive logic dies. Epoch AI estimated in December 2025 that CoWoS-L packaging, the version built with small silicon bridges, added about $1,100 to the cost of building one Nvidia B200. That is more than its estimate of about $900 for the B200's two logic dies. Epoch AI adds about $1,000 more to each B200 for the packages that fail testing, whose logic dies and memory stacks are lost."],["advanced-packaging","In 2.5D packaging the chips sit side by side and connect through an interposer or silicon bridges beneath them. TSMC has run CoWoS in volume since 2012. CoWoS-S has the finest wiring, but its interposer is one unbroken piece of silicon whose yield (the share of interposers that work) falls as the area grows. CoWoS-L replaces that piece of silicon with redistribution layers (RDL) of fine copper wiring and embeds small silicon bridges where the wiring is densest."],["advanced-packaging","Intel's EMIB embeds similar silicon bridges in the resin substrate. SemiAnalysis reported in March 2026 that EMIB was gaining traction, with Amazon's Trainium and Google's TPU both adopting it."],["advanced-packaging","Blackwell was the first high-volume design on CoWoS-L, and packaging problems at TSMC and in Nvidia's design limited its supply. The bridges that carry the 10 TB/s link between the two logic dies must be placed very precisely. The dies, bridges, interposer and substrate also expand at different rates, and that mismatch caused warpage."],["advanced-packaging","In 3D packaging one die sits on top of another, and the joints between them are moving from solder microbumps to hybrid bonding. Intel's Foveros stacks dies face to face and joins them with solder microbumps. Its newer Foveros Direct drops the solder and bonds the copper pads directly, a method called hybrid bonding. Hybrid bonding joins the insulating layer around the pads as well as the copper, with no bumps in between. That lets the connections sit far closer together than microbumps allow. TSMC's SoIC also uses hybrid bonding, and AMD's 3D V- Cache processors use SoIC to attach an extra cache die to the processor die. Stacking also changes how power reaches the top die, which has to draw it up through vertical wires in the die below, called through-silicon vias (TSVs)."],["advanced-packaging","TSMC put SoIC into volume production in 2022, stacking SRAM memory chips on logic wafers. Its 3 nm SoIC entered volume production in 2025. An A14-on-A14 version, stacking dies made on TSMC's 1.4 nm process, is due in 2029. It will carry 1.8 times the die-to-die connection density of SoIC that stacks 2 nm dies on 2 nm dies."],["advanced-packaging","SoIC bonding also brings optics into the package. TSMC's COUPE uses SoIC to join a silicon photonics chip, which sends data as light, to its electrical control chip. In April 2026 TSMC planned to begin producing COUPE on substrate later that year. It also said that putting COUPE inside the package gives twice the power efficiency of a pluggable version on the circuit board."],["advanced-packaging","Panel-level packaging builds packages on a large rectangular panel instead of a round wafer, so rectangular packages fit it with less waste at the edges. See Test and assembly. JEDEC, the semiconductor standards body, published a standard called SPHBM4 on 13 July 2026. It puts HBM4 memory on a base chip carrying 512 data signals instead of 2,048, each running four times as fast to keep the same bandwidth. With fewer signals, the connections can be spaced widely enough to mount the stack on a standard resin substrate instead of the silicon interposer."],["advanced-packaging","TSMC does not publish its CoWoS capacity. Industry estimates from SemiWiki and TrendForce, compiled by Epoch AI, put it at about 65,000 to 75,000 wafers a month at the end of 2025, up from 35,000 to 40,000 a year earlier."],["advanced-packaging","In 2024 TSMC was more than doubling CoWoS capacity and still could not keep up with demand. On the July 2024 earnings call, TSMC's chief executive, C.C. Wei, said TSMC was more than doubling CoWoS capacity in 2024 and would more than double it again in 2025. He said he could not yet balance supply and demand. At its 2024 symposium TSMC had said CoWoS capacity would grow at a 60 percent compound annual rate over the next few years. Asked about that rate on the call, Wei did not repeat it."],["advanced-packaging","In October 2025 Wei would say only that TSMC was still working to increase CoWoS capacity for 2026, and he gave no figure. He said front-end capacity (making the chips) and back-end capacity (packaging them) were both, in his words, very tight."],["advanced-packaging","By Epoch AI's estimate, four chip designers used most of the world's CoWoS capacity in 2025 but only a small share of its advanced chipmaking. Epoch AI compared each chip designer's use of components with world supply. It puts Nvidia at 60.3 percent of all CoWoS capacity in 2025, with a 90 percent confidence interval of 56.5 to 64.3. Google took 13.5 percent, AMD 8.4 and Amazon 7.4. Together those four used around 90 percent of global CoWoS capacity and HBM supply, with HBM measured by value. But they used only 12 percent of advanced logic die production."],["advanced-packaging","In March 2026 the research firm SemiAnalysis judged that front-end capacity had become the dominant bottleneck and that CoWoS constraints were easing. It said TSMC was planning CoWoS capacity around how many wafers N3, its 3 nm process, could produce, because added packaging capacity is of no use without front-end wafers to fill it. It also noted that CoWoS packaging can be, and has been, outsourced to assembly firms such as ASE and Amkor."],["advanced-packaging","TSMC gave a different account four months later. On the July 2026 earnings call, Wei said TSMC's packaging capacity was so tight that it limited customers' growth. Asked about Intel's EMIB-T, he said he welcomed the extra flexibility and hoped it would take some of the load off TSMC. Later in the call he said back-end capacity was still in shortage."],["advanced-packaging","Three kinds of firm package chips. TSMC, which makes chips for others, and Intel, which makes its own, do it in their own back-end fabs. Outsourced assembly and test firms do the rest. Intel opened Fab 9 in Rio Rancho, New Mexico, in January 2024 to make its Foveros 3D packages in volume. It called the plant the only US factory producing the most advanced packaging at scale."],["advanced-packaging","ASE leads the outsourced assembly and test firms, and Amkor is the largest one headquartered in the United States. ASE Technology Holding had revenue of NT$645.4 billion in 2025, about 40 percent of it from its electronics manufacturing arm, a business separate from assembly and test. Its assembly, test and materials business brought in NT$389.2 billion, up from NT$325.9 billion in 2024. Amkor had net sales of $6.71 billion in 2025."],["advanced-packaging","Each of the key packaging tools comes from a small number of makers."],["advanced-packaging","Thermocompression bonding. Pressing dies together under heat and force. ASMPT's advanced packaging revenue reached $532.1 million in 2025, with thermocompression bonder revenue up about 146 percent. ASMPT targets 35 to 40 percent of a market it puts at $1.6 billion in 2028."],["advanced-packaging","Hybrid bonding. Copper pads and the insulator around them bond directly, with no solder. Applied Materials co-developed its Kinex hybrid bonding system with Besi, which Applied calls the industry leader in hybrid bonding."],["advanced-packaging","Grinding and dicing. Disco held 87 percent of the $1.9 billion world market for dicing tools in 2025, by CSET's count from TechInsights data. The category covers the grinders that thin wafers and the saws that cut them into chips. See Test and assembly."],["advanced-packaging","TSMC and Amkor both plan advanced packaging plants in Arizona. TSMC's Arizona commitment reached $265 billion in July 2026 and covers two advanced packaging plants alongside 10 fabs. Amkor started building a $7 billion campus in Peoria, Arizona, in October 2025 and expects production from early 2028. The US Commerce Department awarded Amkor up to $407 million in CHIPS Act funding for the site in December 2024. In October 2025 Wei said a large outsourced packaging partner, which he did not name, was already breaking ground in Arizona. He said its plant was on an earlier schedule than TSMC's own two packaging fabs there."],["advanced-packaging","Four of the top ten outsourced assembly and test firms by 2024 revenue are headquartered in China, by a TrendForce ranking that CSET cites. JCET, a leading Chinese assembly and test firm, had record revenue of RMB 38.87 billion in 2025, up 8.1 percent. JCET says its XDFOI packaging platform has entered high-volume manufacturing with redistribution-layer interposer, silicon interposer and silicon bridge options. Those are the same three kinds of carrier that TSMC sells as CoWoS-R, CoWoS-S and CoWoS-L."],["advanced-packaging","Chinese firms had a small share of the market for advanced packaging tools in 2024 and 2025, and they lost ground in bonding. In 2024 Chinese firms had 7 percent of the market for advanced packaging fabrication tools. Between 2019 and 2024, they gained 5 percentage points of share in test tools and 4 points in fabrication tools built for advanced packaging, by CSET's analysis of TechInsights data. But they lost share in bonding and other conventional assembly and packaging tools, the category where CSET counts hybrid and thermocompression bonders. Within the advanced packaging fabrication tools, Chinese firms gained 10 points in etch and clean tools and 3 points in deposition tools. They lost 2 points each in lithography and polishing ( CMP ) tools. CSET's Chip Explorer, a separate data tool also built on TechInsights data, puts Chinese firms at 5.3 percent of the $6.2 billion world market for advanced packaging fabrication tools in 2025. It puts US firms at 65.8 percent and Japanese firms at 15.3 percent."],["advanced-packaging","TSMC said in April 2026 that it was producing CoWoS at 5.5 times the size of a reticle field and planning larger versions. Each generation on TSMC's roadmap needs a larger interposer."],["advanced-packaging","2028. A 14-reticle interposer, about the area of a compact disc, carrying about ten large compute dies and 20 HBM stacks."],["advanced-packaging","2029. More than 14 reticles, plus a 40-reticle System-on-Wafer. TSMC describes System-on-Wafer as joining different data center chips at the scale of a whole wafer."],["advanced-packaging","Why is an AI accelerator built from several chips in one package?"],["advanced-packaging","Many leading accelerators, Nvidia's Blackwell among them, need more logic than a lithography machine can print in one shot."],["advanced-packaging","Packaging sets the chips and their memory side by side on an interposer, a shared wiring layer, and wires them together through it. Even the H100, built as one chip, uses an interposer to connect its memory. Reread: How it works"],["advanced-packaging","Which company do Nvidia, Google, AMD and Amazon rely on to package their AI accelerators?"],["advanced-packaging","TSMC's packaging process is called CoWoS. Nvidia alone took an estimated 60.3 percent of CoWoS capacity in 2025. Reread: Who makes it"],["advanced-packaging","Why has packaging limited how many AI chips can be made?"],["advanced-packaging","TSMC could not add CoWoS capacity fast enough to meet demand, even while more than doubling it in 2024."],["advanced-packaging","Packaging problems on CoWoS-L also limited the supply of Nvidia's Blackwell, the first high-volume design to use it. In July 2026 TSMC said its packaging capacity was still so tight that it limited customers' growth. Reread: Capacity"],["advanced-packaging","Where are advanced chip packages made in volume in the United States?"],["advanced-packaging","At Intel's Fab 9 in Rio Rancho, New Mexico, which makes Intel's Foveros 3D packages."],["advanced-packaging","Intel calls it the only US factory producing the most advanced packaging at scale. Amkor expects its packaging plant in Peoria, Arizona, to start production in early 2028. Reread: Who makes it"],["advanced-packaging","Many leading accelerators, Nvidia's Blackwell among them, need more logic than one chip can hold, so packaging joins several chips and their memory."],["advanced-packaging","Nvidia, Google, AMD and Amazon all rely on TSMC, in Taiwan, to package their accelerators."],["advanced-packaging","Packaging was one of the main limits on AI chip output in 2025. In July 2026 TSMC said its packaging capacity was still so tight that it limited customers' growth."],["advanced-packaging","No US site yet packages Nvidia-class accelerators with HBM on CoWoS, though Intel makes its own Foveros 3D packages in volume in New Mexico."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Chapter 11 Stage 11 of 14 Extreme concentration · Hard to substitute"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ajinomoto, a Japanese food company, told investors in June 2026 that its build-up film, the insulation inside high-end chip packages, has held over 95 percent of its market since its launch."],["substrates-and-pcbs","A package substrate is the adapter between a chip and the circuit board under it. The chip's connections are finer than a human hair, but the board is wired in millimeters. The substrate is built in layers, like plywood, around a stiff core of glass cloth and resin. Thin sheets of epoxy film are pressed onto both faces of the core. A laser burns holes through each sheet, and copper plated into the holes carries signals from one layer to the next. Every added layer is another set of holes that can fail. A handful of firms build these substrates, and two of the materials inside them come mainly from Japanese makers. Ajinomoto dominates the film, and Nitto Boseki dominates the low-expansion glass cloth in the core."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ajinomoto's third site for making its build-up film, in Gifu Prefecture, is scheduled to start operating in 2032 to meet demand after 2030. Nitto Boseki says market demand seems to have risen about two to three times since it set its plan for fiscal 2024 to 2027. In January 2026 Nikkei Asia reported that Apple and Qualcomm were among the customers worried about Japanese glass cloth supply. In August 2026 Ibiden said it had prospects of a third and fourth glass cloth supplier and expected its material procurement risks to decrease."],["substrates-and-pcbs","The silicon interposer wires chips together inside a package. Beyond the interposer, the wiring runs through a build-up substrate made of epoxy and glass, then a printed circuit board that can have more than 30 layers, then a server rack."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ajinomoto Told investors in June 2026 that its build-up film has held over 95 percent of its market since its launch"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Nitto Boseki Claimed an overwhelming advantage in low thermal expansion glass in its 2025 integrated report"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ibiden Said in May 2026 that it typically takes close to 100 percent of each new generation of interposer-type substrates at launch"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Unimicron Build-up substrates were 52 percent of sales in Q2 2026"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Samsung Electro-Mechanics Package solution sales KRW 771.6bn in Q2 2026, up 37 percent"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Japan Build-up film, low-expansion glass cloth, Ibiden and Shinko substrate plants in Gifu and Nagano"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Taiwan Unimicron and Nan Ya PCB, substrate makers that sell to outside customers"],["substrates-and-pcbs","South Korea Samsung Electro-Mechanics and a planned glass-core joint venture with Sumitomo Chemical's Dongwoo Fine-Chem"],["substrates-and-pcbs","China Most of TTM's circuit board competitors are based in China and Taiwan"],["substrates-and-pcbs","TTM, an American circuit board maker, said in its annual report for 2025 that its circuit board competitors are mostly based in China and Taiwan. Nitto Boseki, a Japanese glass fiber maker, said in its 2025 integrated report that Chinese and Taiwanese companies are aggressively catching up with it in the special glass sector."],["substrates-and-pcbs","The White House's 2021 supply chain review listed no American firm among the key substrate makers. In December 2024 the US Commerce Department finalized an award of up to $75 million to Absolics, an affiliate of Korea's SKC, for a glass substrate plant in Covington, Georgia."],["substrates-and-pcbs","The substrate maker drills the core and plates it with copper before the build-up starts. In each cycle the maker then presses on a film of epoxy, burns holes through it with a laser to connect the layers, and adds copper wiring on top. Each film is about 10 micrometers thick, and a human hair is about 80 micrometers across."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Substrates for AI chips are larger and carry more layers of film than older ones. Ajinomoto counts 11 layers of its film on each side of the core in a 2026 AI package substrate about 100 mm square. A high-performance computing substrate about 70 mm square had nine on each side around 2023. PC substrates had three layers of the film on each side when PCs first adopted it in 1999."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Silicon and epoxy expand at different rates when heated, so the larger the package, the more it warps. Nitto Boseki says its low-expansion T-glass cloth is highly rated as an effective fix for that warping. It says use of the cloth in substrates has increased significantly, without giving a figure."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Substrates built on bismaleimide-triazine laminate, or BT, are the other main family. Mitsubishi Gas Chemical, which makes BT materials, says they go mostly into thin packages for smartphone processors, radio modules and memory. The company says BT also goes into flip-chip substrates for computer CPUs and GPUs. In these the chip is mounted face down, and BT laminate also serves as the core of a build-up substrate, between layers of build-up film. In an October 2024 investor presentation, the company estimated that its BT resins held about 40 percent of what it calls the substrate materials market, the top share."],["substrates-and-pcbs","One company, Ajinomoto, supplies nearly all the insulating film inside package substrates for logic chips. Ajinomoto Build-up Film, or ABF, is the insulating film between the layers of package substrates for logic chips, used in PCs, network equipment, servers and AI equipment. Ajinomoto first developed it in 1999 and says major chipmakers have used it as the de facto standard ever since. On Ajinomoto's own site, its electronic materials division said practically all high-performance computers and servers rely on the film. In June 2026 Ajinomoto told investors that the film has held over 95 percent of its market since its launch."],["substrates-and-pcbs","A glass core expands less with heat than a resin core and stays flatter, so chipmakers and substrate makers are both trying it."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Absolics, a subsidiary of Korea's SKC, has a final US Commerce Department award of up to $75 million for a 120,000-square-foot glass substrate plant in Covington, Georgia. The department finalized the award in December 2024. As of October 2026, the award's project page at NIST, a Commerce Department agency, still said first deliveries to customers were expected in 2025 and production capacity in 2027, without saying whether those deliveries had happened."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Intel said in September 2023 that it planned glass substrates for the latter part of the 2020s."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Samsung Electro-Mechanics signed a joint venture agreement with Sumitomo Chemical's subsidiary Dongwoo Fine-Chem in July 2026 to make glass core substrates. The partners plan to have a supply system in place by the second half of fiscal 2027."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ajinomoto's electronic materials revenue is rising, and it is adding film capacity, but its third production site is not scheduled to open until 2032. Ajinomoto's Healthcare and Others segment, which includes electronic materials such as the film, lifted business profit 45.1 percent to JPY 66.2 billion in the year to March 2026. Ajinomoto attributes the rise mainly to higher electronic materials revenue and higher profit in Bio-Pharma Services & Ingredients. It has set an investment budget of JPY 25 billion between 2023 and 2030 to expand film production. It says it has no concerns about its current supply chain overall and will steadily expand its supply capacity over the medium to long term. In May 2026 it announced the acquisition of land in Gifu Prefecture for a third production site, scheduled to start operating in 2032 to meet demand after 2030."],["substrates-and-pcbs","The glass cloth in the core also has a dominant supplier. Nitto Boseki's T-glass is stiff and expands little when heated, and the company calls it essential for making high-density package substrates. Laminate makers such as Mitsubishi Gas Chemical coat the glass cloth with resin and press it with copper foil into the core laminate that substrate makers build on."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Nitto Boseki says market demand seems to have risen about two to three times since it set its plan for fiscal 2024 to 2027. That plan included about JPY 80 billion of capital spending. The company claims an overwhelming advantage in quality and capacity for low-expansion glass. In August 2025 it decided to expand glass fiber cloth production at its Fukushima Enterprise Center, with production scheduled to begin in the fourth quarter of its fiscal 2026. In May 2026 it forecast capital investment of JPY 45,000 million for the year to March 2027, up from JPY 21,702 million in the year to March 2026."],["substrates-and-pcbs","In January 2026 Nikkei Asia reported that Apple and Qualcomm were among the customers worried about Japanese glass cloth supply. In August 2026 Ibiden, a Japanese substrate maker, said it had used only two glass cloth suppliers, in Japan and Taiwan, but now had prospects of a third and fourth for mass production. Because a Japanese supplier, which Ibiden did not name, also plans to add capacity, Ibiden said it expected its material procurement risks to decrease."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Nitto Boseki says Chinese and Taiwanese companies are aggressively catching up with it in the special glass sector. In July 2026 Nikkei Asia reported that Chinese chip materials makers were competing with Japanese rivals in the market for chip materials, which the industry association SEMI put at $73.2 billion in 2025."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Most of the firms that build substrates for others are Asian. The White House's 2021 hundred-day supply chain review listed build-up substrate among the materials that commenters called vulnerable. It named key substrate makers including Ibiden, Nanya, Shinko, Samsung, Unimicron, Shennan Circuits, Zhuhai Yueya and AKM, none of them American."],["substrates-and-pcbs","A May 2024 report by the Semiconductor Industry Association and Boston Consulting Group found that every major package substrate vendor was headquartered in Japan, Taiwan or mainland China. It counted two in Japan, two in Taiwan, one in mainland China and none in the United States. But TTM Technologies, an American circuit board maker, says it offers package substrates too."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ibiden will invest about JPY 500 billion in high-performance package substrates from fiscal 2026 to fiscal 2028, starting with about JPY 220 billion, mainly at its Gama plant in Gifu Prefecture. In August 2026 it said the Gama plant was scheduled to start operating in stages from the end of fiscal 2027 and to add to its results from fiscal 2028. In May 2026 management said Ibiden typically takes close to 100 percent of each new generation of what it calls interposer-type substrates at launch. It added that this share may decline by 20 to 30 percent after about three to six months. On silicon-bridge substrates, it said wiring the underside is hard enough that Ibiden expects to keep its technical lead at least through fiscal 2030."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Unimicron reported NT$42.9 billion of sales in the second quarter of 2026. By technology, 52 percent came from build-up substrates, and by application, 61 percent came from AI data center work."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Samsung Electro-Mechanics grew package solution sales 37 percent year on year to KRW 771.6 billion in the second quarter of 2026, on substrates for AI accelerators, server processors and cars."],["substrates-and-pcbs","AT&S, an Austrian firm, calls itself a globally leading maker of high-end package substrates. It makes them in China and Malaysia, and since its 2025/26 financial year also in Austria. Citing the research firm Prismark, its annual report for 2025/26 valued the market for flip-chip ball grid array (FC-BGA) substrates at $7.5 billion in 2025, up 18 percent from 2024."],["substrates-and-pcbs","In February 2025 a company owned mainly by funds of JIC Capital launched a tender offer to take Shinko, a Japanese substrate maker, private. JIC Capital is a wholly owned subsidiary of Japan Investment Corporation, an investment company set up in September 2018 under Japan's Industrial Competitiveness Enhancement Act to pursue policy goals such as stronger industrial competitiveness. Fujitsu, which owned 50.02 percent of Shinko, agreed to sell that stake back to Shinko, and the offer covered the shares Fujitsu did not own. The tender offer succeeded in March 2025."],["substrates-and-pcbs","In September 2026 Shinko agreed to buy a plant in Mobara, Chiba Prefecture, from Japan Display, a display maker. Shinko said it would make the site a new core plant for its flip-chip package substrates and would also expand capacity at its plants in Nagano. Production at the Mobara plant is scheduled to start in fiscal 2028."],["substrates-and-pcbs","TTM Technologies says it regularly builds printed circuit boards of more than 30 layers and can go past 70. Those layers carry power to the GPUs and route fast signals between them, so how much signal the laminate absorbs is a main design constraint. Nitto Boseki also makes NE-glass, a low- dielectric glass cloth that absorbs less signal, used in switches and routers in data centers."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Data center computing was 24 percent of TTM's fiscal 2025 revenue of about $2.9 billion, against 14 percent two years earlier."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Board makers are adding plants outside China and Taiwan, where TTM says most of its circuit board competitors are based. In its annual report for 2025, TTM said it was building a plant in Syracuse, New York, to make ultra-high-density circuit boards for national security needs. It expected volume production there in the second half of 2026. Nikkei Asia reported in September 2025 that Thailand aimed to become the biggest circuit board hub outside China as board makers moved to diversify production."],["substrates-and-pcbs","The few firms that build substrates are spending to add capacity, but it takes years. In August 2026 Ibiden said that, with supply short across the industry, the average price of package substrates had risen more than it expected. The materials inside the substrate are harder to replace than the firms that build it. Mitsubishi Gas Chemical, a laminate maker, says chipmakers and electronic device makers further down the chain approve the materials it sells to substrate makers. So a rival to Ajinomoto's film or to Nitto Boseki's low-expansion glass cloth would first need approval from those chipmakers and device makers."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Packages are also getting bigger. TSMC told investors in July 2026 that its CoWoS packaging roadmap goes beyond 14 times the area a lithography machine can print in one shot. A bigger package warps more and needs more layers, so it has more holes that can break the circuit. That lowers yield, the share of substrates that come out working."],["substrates-and-pcbs","It connects a chip's hair-fine contacts to a circuit board wired in millimeters."],["substrates-and-pcbs","It is built in layers of epoxy film and copper around a stiff glass-cloth core. Reread: How it works"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Which company makes nearly all the insulating film inside chip package substrates?"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ajinomoto told investors in June 2026 that the film has held over 95 percent of its market since launch. Nitto Boseki, also Japanese, dominates the low-expansion glass cloth in the substrate's core. Reread: The materials underneath"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Chipmakers and device makers would first have to approve any rival film."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Ajinomoto says major chipmakers have used its film as the standard since 1999. Reread: The chokepoint"],["substrates-and-pcbs","Where are the major package substrate makers based?"],["substrates-and-pcbs","In Japan, Taiwan and mainland China, a May 2024 report by the Semiconductor Industry Association and Boston Consulting Group found."],["substrates-and-pcbs","It counted two in Japan, two in Taiwan, one in mainland China and none in the United States. Reread: Who makes it"],["substrates-and-pcbs","A package substrate connects a chip's fine contacts to a circuit board wired in millimeters."],["substrates-and-pcbs","One Japanese supplier leads the market for the substrate's insulating film, and another leads the market for its glass cloth."],["substrates-and-pcbs","Replacing the film would mean re-approval by every substrate maker and chip customer."],["substrates-and-pcbs","The White House's 2021 supply chain review named no American firm among the key substrate makers. Absolics is building a glass substrate plant in Georgia, and a Commerce Department agency expects its production capacity to come online in 2027."],["test-and-assembly","Chapter 12 Stage 12 of 14 High concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["test-and-assembly","Testing finds bad chips before they go into an expensive package. Japan's Advantest took about 65 percent of 2025 spending on chip testers, by its own estimate."],["test-and-assembly","Before a chip can be sold, a machine called a tester has to check that it works. While the chips are still on the wafer, thousands of needles press onto small metal pads on each one. The tester sends signals through the needles and reads what comes back, and any chip that fails goes no further. A modern AI accelerator is a dozen expensive pieces bonded into one package, and if one piece is bad, all of them are thrown away. So the industry now tests chips earlier, at higher temperatures and for longer, to make weak ones fail during testing before they reach a finished product. Two firms, Advantest in Japan and Teradyne in the United States, sell most of the testers."],["test-and-assembly","In a TrendForce ranking cited by CSET, four of the ten largest chip assembly and test contractors by 2024 revenue are headquartered in China. Georgetown's CSET, analyzing TechInsights data, finds that between 2019 and 2024 Chinese toolmakers gained 5 percentage points of world market share in test tools. Across assembly, test and packaging tools, they still lag significantly behind foreign suppliers in market share. Advantest says that switching to another tester maker means rebuilding a customer's whole test setup, at significant extra cost."],["test-and-assembly","Turning silicon into a finished, packaged chip takes 1,000 to 1,500 steps, depending on how complex the chip is, the Semiconductor Industry Association estimated in 2025. Of all those steps, only test puts electrical signals through the chip, Advantest's investor guide of July 2026 says. The earlier stages of chipmaking make dies, the individual chips on a wafer. The back end of the industry, assembly and test, checks which of them work and puts the good ones into packages."],["test-and-assembly","Advantest About 65 percent of the tester market in 2025, by its own estimate"],["test-and-assembly","Teradyne $2.52 billion of semiconductor test revenue in 2025, service included"],["test-and-assembly","ASE Ran 8,348 testers in Q2 2026, up from 6,797 a year earlier"],["test-and-assembly","Disco 87 percent of the $1.9 billion market for dicing saws and grinders in 2025, on CSET's analysis of TechInsights data"],["test-and-assembly","Taiwan Taiwanese firms such as ASE and Powertech lead outsourced assembly and test"],["test-and-assembly","Japan Advantest testers, Accretech and Tokyo Electron probers, Disco and Accretech dicing and grinding"],["test-and-assembly","United States Test equipment from Teradyne, FormFactor, Cohu and Aehr, and Amkor's planned Arizona packaging plant"],["test-and-assembly","China Four of the top ten assembly and test firms by 2024 revenue, in a TrendForce ranking cited by CSET"],["test-and-assembly","Malaysia Malaysia said in July 2026 that it ships 13 percent of the world's packaged chips"],["test-and-assembly","Georgetown's CSET, analyzing TechInsights data, finds that between 2019 and 2024 Chinese toolmakers gained 5 percentage points of world market share in test tools and 4 points in fabrication tools built for advanced packaging. But they lost share in bonding and other conventional assembly and packaging tools."],["test-and-assembly","American firms held 23.5 percent of the market for test tools in 2025 and Japanese firms 63.0 percent, by CSET's analysis of TechInsights data. Amkor raised its planned investment in an Arizona packaging and test campus to $7 billion in October 2025. In June 2026 it announced a long-term partnership with TSMC, which will buy packaging and test services from it in Arizona."],["test-and-assembly","Each round of test catches failures the round before it cannot see."],["test-and-assembly","Wafer sort. Thousands of needles land on each die while it is still on the wafer. A tester sends in test patterns and checks the answers, and dies that fail go no further."],["test-and-assembly","Burn-in. The part runs hot and at raised voltage for minutes to days, on the wafer or in the package, so that early-life failures happen in the factory, before the part ships."],["test-and-assembly","Final test. The tester checks the packaged part again, because packaging adds failures of its own."],["test-and-assembly","System-level test. The finished part sits in a socket and runs something close to a real workload, because some failures appear only when everything runs at once."],["test-and-assembly","As the parts in a package grow more valuable, finding a bad die before packaging matters more. Aehr, an American maker of burn-in equipment, sells wafer-level burn-in systems that look for early-life and hidden failures before dies are cut from the wafer. Catching those failures early lowers the risk of packaging high-bandwidth memory and an expensive substrate with a processor that may later fail. Aehr says its lead AI customer is moving all burn-in of that customer's AI accelerators from the system level, after packaging, to the wafer. The FOX-XP systems that customer ordered from Aehr in August 2026 each burn in nine 300 mm wafers at a time."],["test-and-assembly","The hard part of wafer sort is the probe card, the circuit board that holds the needles. For a large logic die every needle must sit in the same plane, survive repeated touchdowns without drifting, and do it hot. Each card is built for one chip design, so every new design needs a new card and a new qualification. FormFactor, an American probe card maker, says its cards work at high enough frequencies to compete well in testing high-bandwidth memory, a stack of eight, twelve or sixteen memory dies."],["test-and-assembly","The bigger the package, the more one bad die can cost. TSMC told investors in July 2026 that its CoWoS roadmap includes packages larger than 14 times the area a lithography machine can print in one shot. A die that fails after assembly wastes the memory and substrate joined to it."],["test-and-assembly","Advantest puts its own share at about 65 percent of an estimated $9.0 billion tester market in 2025. Its share of system-on-chip (SoC) testers, the machines that test processors and other non-memory chips, rose about ten points in a year to 66 percent. It held about 60 percent of memory test."],["test-and-assembly","Teradyne, Advantest's main rival, took $2.52 billion of semiconductor test revenue in 2025, service included. Of that, $1.89 billion came from SoC testers and $505 million from memory testers. Teradyne's total revenue grew 13 percent to $3.19 billion in 2025, with fourth-quarter revenue up 44 percent on AI demand."],["test-and-assembly","Georgetown University's Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET) makes a second estimate, from data by the research firm TechInsights. It gives Advantest 62.7 percent of a $9.1 billion market for test tools in 2025 and Teradyne 21.8 percent. Japanese firms held 63.0 percent of that market and American firms 23.5 percent."],["test-and-assembly","The rest of the test and assembly equipment market splits into niches, each with its own suppliers."],["test-and-assembly","Probe cards. FormFactor took $785.0 million of revenue in fiscal 2025, most of it from probe cards. Technoprobe's revenue grew 15.7 percent to EUR 628.4 million in 2025, about 38 percent of it from AI. It aims to double its manufacturing capacity by the end of 2027."],["test-and-assembly","Probers, the machines that move each wafer under the probe card and keep it at a set temperature. Tokyo Seimitsu, which sells under the Accretech name, says its own research gives it the largest global share in probers. Tokyo Electron makes probers too. CSET's analysis of TechInsights data counts handlers and probers as one market, worth $2.9 billion in 2025, and gives Tokyo Electron 19.9 percent of it and Accretech 17.1 percent."],["test-and-assembly","Handlers and burn-in, the machines that feed packaged parts into a tester and hold them at a set temperature, and the systems that run burn-in. Cohu took $453.0 million of revenue in fiscal 2025. Aehr's revenue was $50.0 million in fiscal 2026, but it booked a record $60.7 million of orders in the fourth quarter alone. It expects revenue of $130 million to $150 million in fiscal 2027."],["test-and-assembly","Dicing and grinding. Dicing saws cut wafers into dies, and grinders thin them. CSET's analysis of TechInsights data found that in 2025 Disco held 87 percent and Accretech 8.1 percent of the $1.9 billion market for these machines. Panel-level packaging builds packages on large panels in place of 300 mm wafers, to make more of them at once. In December 2025 Disco announced a saw that cuts such panels, as large as 400 by 400 mm, into individual packages."],["test-and-assembly","Bonding. Kulicke and Soffa took $654.1 million of revenue in fiscal 2025. Besi's second-quarter 2026 revenue rose 68.7 percent to EUR 249.9 million on hybrid bonding and data center demand."],["test-and-assembly","Thermocompression bonders use heat and force to press memory dies into a stack and to attach chiplets to substrates. ASMPT says it remained the leader in that market in 2025 and aims for a 35 to 40 percent share. In its 2025 results it said it expects the market to reach $1.6 billion by 2028. In July 2026 ASMPT announced new bulk orders for more than 50 of its chip-to-substrate bonders for AI chips, from outsourced assembly and test firms. Hanmi Semiconductor in South Korea also sells thermocompression bonders for high-bandwidth memory. See Memory and HBM."],["test-and-assembly","Taiwanese firms lead outsourced assembly and test, the OSAT business, and Chinese firms are large challengers. Taiwan's ASE billed $20,573.4 million in 2025. Packaging made up about 48 percent of that, testing about 11 percent and its electronics manufacturing arm about 40 percent. In a TrendForce ranking that CSET cites, four of the top ten OSATs by 2024 revenue are headquartered in China."],["test-and-assembly","Malaysia is a large center for chip assembly and test. Its investment agency said in July 2026 that the country ships 13 percent of the world's packaged chips. It said a consortium of five Malaysian firms aims to help the country capture 7 percent of world advanced packaging shipments by 2035. A 2024 study by the Semiconductor Industry Association and Boston Consulting Group used a different measure, capacity. It gave Malaysia 7 percent of global assembly, test and packaging capacity in 2022, the largest share in Southeast Asia. The study measured capacity by factory floor space at contractors and chipmakers' own plants."],["test-and-assembly","Taiwan's assembly and test contractors are expanding. ASE ran 6,797 testers in the second quarter of 2025 and 8,348 a year later. It spent $2.7 billion on machinery and $1.4 billion on buildings, facilities and automation in the first half of 2026. In July 2026 it said revenue from leading-edge advanced packaging was running ahead of its $3.5 billion forecast for 2026. Powertech, another Taiwanese assembly and test firm, aims to run the first panel-level packaging line for AI chips in 2027."],["test-and-assembly","Amkor, an American assembly and test contractor, took $6.71 billion of revenue in 2025. Its revenue in the second quarter of 2026 alone was $1.90 billion, up 26 percent year on year. By October 2025 it had raised the planned investment in its Arizona campus to $7 billion."],["test-and-assembly","In October 2024 TSMC and Amkor signed a memorandum of understanding for TSMC to buy packaging and test services from Amkor's planned plant in Peoria, Arizona. TSMC would use those services for its customers, especially those using its Phoenix fabs. The two announced a long-term partnership in June 2026."],["test-and-assembly","Customers can switch tester makers, but at a cost. Advantest says that switching to another tester maker means rebuilding the whole test setup used for development, evaluation and mass production, at significant extra cost to the customer. Still, ASE says it buys testers with similar functions from different makers, including Teradyne and Advantest."],["test-and-assembly","Chinese toolmakers are gaining share in test and advanced packaging tools, but CSET finds they still lag significantly behind foreign suppliers in market share. Between 2019 and 2024 they gained 5 percentage points of world market share in test tools and 4 points in fabrication tools built for advanced packaging, by CSET's analysis of TechInsights data. But they lost share in bonding and other conventional assembly and packaging tools."],["test-and-assembly","Assembly and test contractors such as ASE and Amkor earn a small part of what the chip industry sells. ASE's packaging business took $9,829.2 million from outside customers in 2025, and its testing business $2,292.0 million. Amkor's revenue was $6.71 billion. Global semiconductor sales that year were $791.7 billion."],["test-and-assembly","Why do chipmakers test chips early and often?"],["test-and-assembly","One bad chip can ruin a package that holds a dozen expensive ones."],["test-and-assembly","Testing makes a weak chip fail before it is built into a finished product. Reread: How it works"],["test-and-assembly","Advantest of Japan and Teradyne of the United States."],["test-and-assembly","Advantest puts its own share at about 65 percent of an estimated $9.0 billion tester market in 2025. Reread: Who makes it"],["test-and-assembly","How many of the ten largest chip assembly and test contractors are based in China?"],["test-and-assembly","Four, by 2024 revenue, in a TrendForce ranking that CSET cites."],["test-and-assembly","Taiwanese firms such as ASE lead outsourced assembly and test, and Chinese firms are large challengers. Reread: The back end's geography"],["test-and-assembly","Chips are tested early and often because one bad chip can ruin a package of expensive ones."],["test-and-assembly","Advantest and Teradyne account for most spending on chip testers."],["test-and-assembly","In a TrendForce ranking cited by CSET, four of the top ten outsourced assembly and test firms by 2024 revenue are based in China."],["systems-and-networking","Chapter 13 Stage 13 of 14 High concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["systems-and-networking","Nvidia's and AMD's racks wire 72 AI chips together to run as one computer. Many firms can assemble the racks, but lasers for the optical links were scarce in 2026."],["systems-and-networking","One AI chip is not enough to train a model. So seventy-two of them are wired together in a rack, a cabinet the size of a wardrobe, and run as one computer. Many such racks are then linked to train a large model. Each chip sits on its own board and draws more than a thousand amps, several times the current a whole house is wired to carry. The chips have to swap results with each other all the time. A copper wire can carry those signals only a few meters before they fade, so the longer links send them as light down glass fiber. Many companies can build the rack, but in 2026 the lasers that send the light were scarce."],["systems-and-networking","In March 2026 Nvidia agreed to invest $2 billion in the laser maker Lumentum, alongside a multibillion-dollar purchase commitment and rights to future capacity for advanced laser components. Indium phosphide is used in high-speed lasers for optical communications, and China produced 70 percent of the world's indium in 2025."],["systems-and-networking","On 4 February 2025 China added indium phosphide substrates, the wafers the lasers are grown on, to its export control list. AXT, a US-listed maker of those wafers, does all its manufacturing in China. In its filing for the quarter to June 2026, AXT said it could not estimate when it would resume shipping the wafers to the United States."],["systems-and-networking","Before a chip package can compute, it has to be built into a machine. Building that machine is a separate industry from making the package."],["systems-and-networking","Nvidia NVLink, InfiniBand and Spectrum-X Ethernet, which it credited for data center growth in the quarter to April 2026"],["systems-and-networking","Broadcom $16.7 billion of AI semiconductor revenue in the quarter to August 2026, up 221 percent"],["systems-and-networking","Foxconn World's largest AI server provider, its chairman said in March 2026"],["systems-and-networking","InnoLight High-speed optical modules made in Suzhou and, since 2019, Thailand"],["systems-and-networking","Coherent Lasers and optical networking products, with a $2 billion Nvidia investment agreed in March 2026"],["systems-and-networking","United States Switch and accelerator silicon, system design, indium phosphide lasers"],["systems-and-networking","Taiwan Contract design, rack assembly and high-layer-count circuit boards"],["systems-and-networking","China Optical module assembly and test, and most of the world's indium"],["systems-and-networking","Thailand Chinese module makers' offshore transceiver plants"],["systems-and-networking","Chinese firms such as InnoLight assemble high-speed optical modules in volume, at sites including Suzhou and, since 2019, Thailand. In February 2025 China put indium under new export restrictions. The same month it began requiring export permits for indium phosphide substrates, the wafers that lasers for optical links are grown on."],["systems-and-networking","Coherent broke ground in Sherman, Texas, in June 2026 on an expansion of its factory there, which makes optical devices from indium phosphide. In August 2026 Nvidia said that Wistron's new plant in Fort Worth, Texas, was producing its GB300 superchips and that Foxconn was building a factory in Houston."],["systems-and-networking","An accelerator (the AI chip) ships as a module, the chip package on a small board with the circuits that feed it power. Nvidia calls its version SXM, and the open-standards equivalent is the Open Compute Project's accelerator module. Eight modules bolt onto a baseboard that carries their power and the links between them. On Nvidia's baseboard, switch chips pass data between any two modules at full speed."],["systems-and-networking","Rack-scale systems drop the baseboard and put the chips on trays stacked in the rack. An Nvidia GB300 NVL72 holds 18 compute trays plus nine switch trays, 72 GPUs in all, and draws up to 142 kW. The newer Vera Rubin NVL72 uses the same rack footprint. The research firm SemiAnalysis estimated in August 2025 that a rack of the earlier GB200 NVL72 model cost a typical hyperscaler $3.1 million, or about $3.9 million with networking, storage and other items."],["systems-and-networking","Inside the rack the trays reach each other over copper. Between neighboring racks, the signal can travel up to 7 meters over active electrical cables, a type of copper cable sold by firms such as Credo. Longer links run on glass fiber, with an optical transceiver at each end. A laser in the sending transceiver turns the electrical signal into pulses of light, and a detector in the receiving one turns the pulses back into current."],["systems-and-networking","The accelerators in an AI cluster exchange data over two networks that are not interchangeable. Scale-up connects anywhere from a few dozen accelerators to thousands closely enough that they can read each other's memory. It runs at terabytes per second. Scale-out joins those groups to one another at hundreds of gigabits per second. Scale-up speeds are quoted in bytes and scale-out speeds in bits, and a byte is eight bits. Each GPU in a GB300 NVL72 can send 900 gigabytes per second each way over the scale-up network, or 7,200 gigabits per second. Over the scale-out network it can send 800 gigabits per second. So each GPU has nine times as much bandwidth for scale-up as for scale-out, SemiAnalysis calculated in January 2026."],["systems-and-networking","Scale-up bandwidth limits how efficiently a large model trains. A model too big for one accelerator is split across many. The parts that exchange data constantly stay inside the scale-up group, because they need its high bandwidth. Whole blocks of layers, the stages a model's calculation passes through in turn, can sit on different groups across the slower scale-out network."],["systems-and-networking","The designs differ in how many accelerators can share one pool of memory."],["systems-and-networking","NVLink and NVSwitch. Nvidia's NVLink bandwidth per GPU, counting both directions, went from 900 GB/s in NVLink 4 to 1,800 GB/s in NVLink 5. Across a whole Blackwell NVL72 rack, NVLink moves 130 TB/s. Nvidia's Rubin launch release of January 2026 gives NVLink 6 as 3,600 GB/s per GPU and 260 TB/s for a Vera Rubin NVL72 rack. As of October 2026, Nvidia's NVLink product page still lists preliminary figures of 3,000 GB/s and 216 TB/s."],["systems-and-networking","UALink. The open specification, from the UALink Consortium, runs 200 Gb/s per lane, and four lanes, which it calls a station, carry 800 Gb/s. It can address up to 1,024 endpoints, such as accelerators, in one group. AMD's Helios rack, launched in July 2026, joins 72 GPUs and runs UALink over Ethernet for its scale-up network."],["systems-and-networking","Google's 3D torus. Google wires 64 of its Ironwood TPU accelerators into each rack, called a cube. Inside the cube each chip links directly to six others, in a three-dimensional grid that Google calls a 3D torus. Optical circuit switches, which steer light from one fiber to another, join cubes into superpods of 9,216 chips and can route around a failed cube or link."],["systems-and-networking","Scale-out networks typically use InfiniBand or Ethernet, SemiAnalysis wrote in January 2026. InfiniBand is a specialized network long used in supercomputers. But Ethernet switch capacity has grown quickly. Broadcom's Tomahawk 4 switched 25.6 Tbps on one chip in December 2019. Tomahawk 5 reached 51.2 Tbps in August 2022, and Broadcom said it had doubled the bandwidth about every two years since 2014. Tomahawk 6 doubled it again to 102.4 Tbps in June 2025. In June 2025 the Ultra Ethernet Consortium published its 1.0 specification, a set of Ethernet-based rules for communication in AI and supercomputing. It covers how data is carried, how traffic jams are avoided and how one machine reads or writes another's memory directly."],["systems-and-networking","Nvidia sells switches and network cards for both InfiniBand and Ethernet. Its data center revenue, which counts its GPUs as well as its networking gear, reached $89.0 billion in the quarter to July 2026, up 117 percent from a year earlier. In the quarter before, it credited its data center growth to Blackwell 300 products and to demand for its \"InfiniBand, Spectrum-X Ethernet, and NVLink\" solutions."],["systems-and-networking","Broadcom and Nvidia are moving the optics out of pluggable transceivers and into the switch chip's own package, a design called co-packaged optics. A cluster needs several transceivers, the modules that turn electricity into light and back, for each accelerator. Their power cost is one reason for the change. Broadcom says its Tomahawk 6 Davisson cuts the power used by optical links by 70 percent compared with traditional pluggable modules. It keeps its lasers in field-replaceable modules. Nvidia's Spectrum-X Photonics switches, announced in March 2025, have up to 512 ports of 800 gigabits per second each, and Nvidia says they use four times fewer lasers than traditional designs. Nvidia builds them on its Spectrum-6 switch design. In August 2026 Nvidia said its Spectrum-6 switch systems, with pluggable or co-packaged optics, were arriving at AI data centers around the world."],["systems-and-networking","Chinese makers of optical modules have built plants outside China. InnoLight has run a plant in Thailand since 2019, alongside its sites in Suzhou and Taiwan. The Thai subsidiary of Eoptolink, another Chinese module maker, lists sites in Chonburi and Rayong."],["systems-and-networking","A US rule from July 2026 may reach optical transceivers made by firms on a US security list. The list is the Federal Communications Commission's Covered List of equipment and services judged to pose an unacceptable risk to US national security or to the security and safety of US persons. Under its July 2026 order, the FCC no longer approves new devices for the US market if they contain logic-bearing hardware components made by firms on the list. The order counts as logic-bearing any part that uses digital logic, from a single chip to a whole module, and leaves out parts with no digital function, such as wiring and housings. Commenters in the record named optical transceivers as one such component. As of 16 October 2026, the Covered List did not include InnoLight."],["systems-and-networking","China produces most of the world's indium, the raw material for indium phosphide lasers, and restricts its export. Indium phosphide is used in the high-speed laser diodes and photodetectors for optical communications. China accounted for 70 percent of world indium production in 2025. In February 2025 China's Ministry of Commerce placed indium under new export restrictions."],["systems-and-networking","AI data centers were straining supplies of the lasers inside optical modules and pushing up their prices, Nikkei Asia reported in May 2026. Nvidia had agreed in March 2026 to invest $2 billion in one laser maker, Lumentum, alongside a multibillion-dollar purchase commitment and rights to future capacity for advanced laser components. Coherent, another laser maker, broke ground in Sherman, Texas, in June 2026 on an expansion of its factory there, which makes optical devices from indium phosphide."],["systems-and-networking","Two American firms, Broadcom and Marvell, sell both custom AI chips and Ethernet switch chips. In its annual report for fiscal 2025, Broadcom said its AI chips include Ethernet switch chips as well as custom accelerators, which it builds to each customer's specifications. Its AI semiconductor revenue reached $16.7 billion in the third quarter of fiscal 2026, up 221 percent from a year earlier. Marvell also builds custom AI chips to each customer's specifications and sells Ethernet switch chips, its annual report for fiscal 2026 says. Marvell's five-year agreement with Amazon Web Services, announced in December 2024, covers custom AI chips alongside the optical and networking parts that go with them."],["systems-and-networking","Taiwanese firms do much of the physical assembly. Foxconn booked NT$8.1 trillion of revenue in 2025, up 18 percent, and cloud and networking was its largest product category in the fourth quarter. In the same results release, its chairman called Foxconn the world's largest AI server provider."],["systems-and-networking","Some assembly is moving to the United States. In April 2025 Nvidia said it was building supercomputer manufacturing plants in Texas, with Foxconn in Houston and Wistron in Dallas. It expected mass production to ramp up in the following 12 to 15 months. In August 2026 Nvidia said Wistron's new plant in Fort Worth, Texas, near Dallas, was producing its GB300 superchips, which pair Nvidia's Grace processor with its Blackwell Ultra GPUs. It said Foxconn was building a factory in Houston to make Nvidia's AI systems."],["systems-and-networking","Many firms can build the racks. In October 2025 Nvidia said more than 50 makers of systems and components were gearing up for the Vera Rubin NVL72, which follows MGX, Nvidia's standard design for trays and racks. But in its filing for the quarter to July 2026, Nvidia said the complexity of producing its data center systems had caused production delays."],["systems-and-networking","Four inputs to the rack are harder to source elsewhere."],["systems-and-networking","Indium phosphide laser capacity. Nvidia has secured rights to future capacity from laser makers. Alongside its Lumentum deal, in March 2026 Nvidia agreed to invest $2 billion in Coherent. The deal also includes a multibillion-dollar purchase commitment and rights to future access and capacity for Coherent's advanced laser and optical networking products."],["systems-and-networking","Indium phosphide substrates. China added indium phosphide substrates, the wafers the lasers are grown on, to its export control list on 4 February 2025. AXT, a US-listed maker of these wafers, does all its manufacturing in China. In its filing for the quarter to June 2026, AXT called the need for Chinese export permits the most significant challenge it faces. It said it could not estimate when it would resume shipping the wafers to the United States. The same filing names Sumitomo and JX, both Japanese firms, as AXT's competitors in indium phosphide."],["systems-and-networking","NVSwitch. Nvidia's annual report for fiscal 2026 lists NVLink interconnects and switches among its own networking products. UALink is an open standard designed for accelerator communications within one scale-up group. Since May 2025 Nvidia's NVLink Fusion program has let other firms' custom chips use NVLink, including CPUs that Fujitsu and Qualcomm plan to connect to Nvidia GPUs."],["systems-and-networking","High-layer-count circuit boards. TTM Technologies, an American circuit board maker, says its circuit board competitors are mostly based in China and Taiwan. Nitto Boseki, a Japanese glass fiber maker, makes NE-glass, a glass cloth that absorbs less signal, for the boards in data center switches and routers. See Substrates and PCBs."],["systems-and-networking","Optical module assembly can move, as InnoLight's high-volume plant in Thailand, opened in 2019, shows."],["systems-and-networking","A cabinet of 72 AI chips wired together to run as one computer."],["systems-and-networking","One AI chip is not enough to train a model. Nvidia's GB300 NVL72, one such rack, holds 72 GPUs and draws up to 142 kW. Reread: How it works"],["systems-and-networking","Why do the longer links between AI chips carry signals as light?"],["systems-and-networking","Copper carries the signals only a few meters."],["systems-and-networking","Active copper cables carry the signal up to 7 meters between racks. Beyond that a laser turns the signal into pulses of light that travel down glass fiber. Reread: How it works"],["systems-and-networking","Which part of an AI rack was scarce in 2026?"],["systems-and-networking","Many firms can assemble the rack itself. In March 2026 Nvidia agreed to invest $2 billion in the laser maker Lumentum, with rights to its future capacity. Reread: The chokepoint"],["systems-and-networking","How much of the world's indium did China produce in 2025?"],["systems-and-networking","70 percent. Indium is the raw material for the lasers in optical links."],["systems-and-networking","China put indium under new export restrictions in February 2025. That month it also began requiring permits to export indium phosphide substrates, the wafers the lasers are grown on. Reread: The chokepoint"],["systems-and-networking","An AI rack wires 72 chips together to run as one computer."],["systems-and-networking","Almost every link longer than 7 meters carries its signal as light, because copper fades over longer runs."],["systems-and-networking","Nvidia's NVLink switch chips and the lasers are the hardest parts to replace. In October 2025 more than 50 makers of systems and components were gearing up to build Nvidia's next rack."],["systems-and-networking","China produced about 70 percent of the world's indium in 2025 and has required export permits for indium phosphide substrates since February 2025."],["data-centers-and-power","Chapter 14 Stage 14 of 14 High concentration · Moderately hard to substitute"],["data-centers-and-power","SemiAnalysis forecast in October 2026 that 50 GW of data center capacity would be added in 2027, about as much as the world had built through 2024. The large transformers that connect such sites to the grid commonly took three years to arrive in 2024."],["data-centers-and-power","A data center feeds electricity to the machines inside it and carries away the heat they give off. One rack of AI chips, a cabinet taller than a door, can draw 142 kilowatts. Every watt of it comes back out as heat, and liquid piped through the rack carries the heat away. A large training site already holds more than a hundred thousand chips. The newest sites are planned in gigawatts. One gigawatt is the whole output of a large power station, and Epoch AI projects that OpenAI's seven Stargate sites in the United States will add up to more than nine of them by 2029. Getting that much electricity to the site is harder than putting up the building. Transformers and heavy switches connect a site to the grid, and turbines make the power. All of them come from a few suppliers and take years to arrive."],["data-centers-and-power","Measured by capacity, US factories supplied 29.2 percent of the large power transformers bought in the US in 2023, and imports the rest. GE Vernova's gas equipment backlog and reserved factory slots stood at 116 GW in mid-2026, against planned output of 20 GW a year from the third quarter."],["data-centers-and-power","ERCOT, the grid operator for most of Texas, counted 9,456 MW of big power users approved to energize in its overview for September 2026. Judging by peak monthly use in September, it believed 4,132 MW of that was operating. On 3 August 2026 Governor Greg Abbott ordered an audit of every data center seeking a connection before any data center project moves forward. In September 2026 ERCOT said it had paused approvals to energize data centers of 75 MW or more until the audit and a review of their impact on local communities are complete."],["data-centers-and-power","A wafer passes through a leading-edge fab in months, but in 2024 a large power transformer commonly took three years to arrive. Before the pandemic, the same order took under a year."],["data-centers-and-power","GE Vernova Gas equipment, transformers and switchgear, including through Prolec GE"],["data-centers-and-power","Hitachi Energy Power transformers and switchgear"],["data-centers-and-power","Siemens Energy Grid technologies, transformers, turbines"],["data-centers-and-power","Mitsubishi Power Power generation equipment, including gas turbines"],["data-centers-and-power","Schneider Electric Cooling, through its Motivair division"],["data-centers-and-power","United States The largest data center operators, and GE Vernova turbines and grid equipment"],["data-centers-and-power","Switzerland Hitachi Energy transformers and switchgear, and ABB switchgear"],["data-centers-and-power","Germany Siemens Energy grid technologies and turbines"],["data-centers-and-power","Japan Mitsubishi Power equipment, including gas turbines"],["data-centers-and-power","China used 25 percent of the world's data center electricity in 2024, second to the United States, by the International Energy Agency's estimate. Data centers made up around 3 percent of the growth in China's electricity demand from 2022 to 2024."],["data-centers-and-power","US factories supplied 29.2 percent of the large power transformers bought in the United States in 2023, measured by capacity. Constellation said in August 2026 that it expects to restart the Crane nuclear plant in 2027. Microsoft has agreed to buy the plant's power."],["data-centers-and-power","The rack is the basic unit of AI compute. Nvidia's GB300 NVL72 rack draws up to 142 kW through eight 33 kW power shelves, the rack's own power supplies. Large sites hold many such racks. Colossus 1, an AI data center in Memphis, Tennessee, held an estimated 230,000 Nvidia GPUs by July 2025."],["data-centers-and-power","Power reaches the rack through a chain of heavy equipment, and each piece has its own lead time, the wait between order and delivery. Between the grid and the rack, a substation steps the high voltage down with transformers. Switchgear, the building's heavy circuit breakers, can cut any part of the site off in a fault. Battery-backed supplies keep the racks running for the seconds it takes backup generators to start. Distribution boards split the feed among the rows of racks."],["data-centers-and-power","At the back of each rack, a busbar carries the current down to the server trays. It is a solid copper bar, because an ordinary cable would overheat at that current."],["data-centers-and-power","Heat leaves in water. Cold plates, metal blocks with coolant running through them, sit on the GPU packages and pass the heat to the building's water loop, which releases it outdoors. Nvidia's Rubin racks run coolant at up to 45 °C, warm enough that in many climates the loop can release its heat without turning on chillers, the refrigeration machines that cool water."],["data-centers-and-power","Nvidia is also moving the power that feeds its racks to 800 volts of direct current. Raising the voltage cuts the current needed for the same power, and the heat in copper comes from current. Nvidia said in October 2025 that at 800 volts the same wire can carry 157 percent more power than at 415 volts of alternating current. Inside racks such as the GB300 NVL72, power runs at 54 volts, and at that voltage a one-megawatt rack would need up to 200 kg of copper busbar."],["data-centers-and-power","Air. Heat exchangers in the rack door work when density, the power each rack draws, is moderate, but Nvidia's GB300 NVL72 rack is liquid cooled."],["data-centers-and-power","Direct-to-chip liquid. Nvidia's Rubin platform is 100 percent liquid cooled, and Nvidia says every cloud provider and data center operator building for it is moving to liquid."],["data-centers-and-power","Immersion. The servers sit in a bath of fluid, which makes them hard to service."],["data-centers-and-power","Nvidia says the cooling supply chain is keeping pace with the move to liquid. Motivair, Schneider Electric's cooling division, has worked with Nvidia for nearly a decade, following Nvidia's product roadmap."],["data-centers-and-power","Nvidia's 800-volt DC architecture is designed for racks from 100 kW to more than a megawatt, with megawatt racks from 2027. Nvidia is making the change because the 54-volt distribution in existing racks begins to hit physical limits once racks exceed 200 kW."],["data-centers-and-power","Nvidia names nine data center power system providers for its 800-volt designs for gigawatt-scale data centers, among them ABB, Eaton, Hitachi Energy, Mitsubishi Electric, Schneider Electric, Siemens and Vertiv."],["data-centers-and-power","A megawatt rack changes the busbar, the floor loading, the coolant flow, the leak detection and the energy stored in the rack. Nvidia's Vera Rubin NVL72 rack design adds energy storage to keep power steady."],["data-centers-and-power","Grid interconnection. The slow path in the United States, where the queues to connect are long."],["data-centers-and-power","Behind-the-meter gas, generation on the site itself. The fast path, which at least three of OpenAI's seven US Stargate sites will use to avoid grid queues."],["data-centers-and-power","Nuclear. Existing plants already sell power to data centers. Talen Energy supplies Amazon's data center campus next to the Susquehanna nuclear plant in Pennsylvania under a June 2025 contract expected to reach 1,920 MW no later than 2032. Restarts and new reactors are still to come. Constellation signed a power purchase agreement with Microsoft to restart Three Mile Island Unit 1 as the 835 MW Crane Clean Energy Center. The plant shut in 2019. A $1 billion federal loan that closed in November 2025 partly finances its restart, which is subject to licensing approvals from the US Nuclear Regulatory Commission."],["data-centers-and-power","The largest data center operators pay for the buildout. Capital spending by Alphabet, Amazon, Meta, Microsoft and Oracle came to $448.2 billion in 2025, the sum of quarterly figures compiled by Epoch AI, a research group. If the trend continues, it will reach $770 billion in 2026. The International Energy Agency expected worldwide investment in data centers to reach $580 billion in 2025."],["data-centers-and-power","Epoch AI also projects that OpenAI's seven US Stargate sites will exceed 9 GW by 2029. It expects the site in Abilene, Texas, to grow from an estimated 0.3 GW in April 2026 to 1.2 GW in the fourth quarter of 2026."],["data-centers-and-power","A few large firms make the turbines, transformers and switchgear. GE Vernova builds large gas turbines, and its 2025 annual report names Siemens Energy and Mitsubishi Power among the key competitors of its power generation business. Its electrification business makes power transformers and switchgear, and the report names Hitachi Energy, Siemens Energy, Schneider Electric and ABB among that business's key competitors."],["data-centers-and-power","Equipment makers limit how fast the buildout can go. GE Vernova's gas equipment backlog and reserved factory slots grew from 100 GW to 116 GW in the second quarter of 2026. In the first half of 2026, data center orders for its electrification business, which makes grid equipment, passed $5 billion, more than double that business's data center orders for all of 2025. GE Vernova bought the remaining half of Prolec GE, a transformer maker, in the first half of 2026."],["data-centers-and-power","US data center electricity use is projected to rise steeply by 2030. US data centers used 192 TWh in 2024, 4.7 percent of national electricity, according to a June 2026 estimate by Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory that leaves out cryptocurrency mining. The lab's reference case, its main scenario, projects 464 TWh in 2028 and 649 TWh in 2030, which would be 11.8 percent of forecast US electricity use. Its scenarios for 2030 range from 521 to 843 TWh, or 9.5 percent to 15.3 percent."],["data-centers-and-power","The US Energy Information Administration expects electricity demand to keep rising, but in September 2026 it cut its 2027 forecast for the region that includes Texas. In its October 2026 Short-Term Energy Outlook, it expects US electricity sales of 4,152.0 TWh in 2026 and 4,216.6 TWh in 2027. It expects electricity demand from the commercial sector, which includes data centers, to grow 2.8 percent in 2027 and demand from industry to grow 2.7 percent. Its September outlook had lowered the 2027 electricity sales forecast for the region that includes Texas by 4.7 percent from August. That outlook noted that Texas had paused connecting new data centers to the grid while the state audits proposed projects. The pause, set by the grid operator for most of Texas, covers data centers and crypto mining sites of 75 MW or more."],["data-centers-and-power","By the International Energy Agency's estimate, China accounted for 25 percent of the world's data center electricity use in 2024, second to the United States at 45 percent. Data centers made up around 3 percent of the growth in China's electricity demand from 2022 to 2024, the agency found."],["data-centers-and-power","SemiAnalysis, a research firm, forecast in October 2026 that 50 GW of data center capacity would be added in 2027, which it said was about as much as the world's data center market had built in total through 2024. Just 40 campuses in an advanced stage of construction held more than 24 GW, most of it to be delivered in 2027, it found."],["data-centers-and-power","Better chips do not by themselves cut total energy use. Google says its Ironwood TPU, an AI chip, delivers twice the performance per watt of Trillium, the TPU before it. A token is the chunk of text a model reads or writes. Energy per token can fall while total energy use still rises, if the number of tokens rises faster."],["data-centers-and-power","On the Texas grid, big power users have asked for far more electricity than is connected and running. ERCOT, the grid operator for most of Texas, was tracking about 474 GW of large loads (big power users) seeking a connection in June 2026, roughly 90 percent of it data centers. In its operational overview for September 2026, ERCOT counted 9,456 MW of large loads approved to energize, that is, cleared to switch on. Judging by peak monthly use in September, it believed only 4,132 MW of it was operating."],["data-centers-and-power","Before a big user can connect, engineers must study whether the nearby grid can carry its load. In a preliminary review in July 2026, ERCOT found that about 205 GW of the requests already had such a study, which made them eligible for Batch Zero, the first batch of requests it studies together. In September 2026 ERCOT conditionally classed 66.4 GW of Batch Zero projects as base load and 127.9 GW as studied load, pending final decisions in December. Under ERCOT's Batch Zero rules, base load is demand from projects already running or far enough along to be counted without further study. Studied load is demand that ERCOT will study before giving each project a share of the grid's capacity."],["data-centers-and-power","Texas has paused new connections for large data centers while it audits them. On 3 August 2026 Texas Governor Greg Abbott ordered the state's Public Utility Commission and ERCOT to audit every data center waiting to connect to the grid before any data center project moves forward. ERCOT then paused approvals to energize data centers and crypto mining sites of 75 MW or more until the audit and a review of their impact on local communities are complete. It will report on the audit and the community review to the Public Utility Commission by 10 December 2026."],["data-centers-and-power","Projects in that queue also wait on equipment."],["data-centers-and-power","Large power transformers. In the United States in 2024, lead times of 36 months were commonly quoted and the longest reached 60 months, against under a year before the pandemic. By a US Commerce Department estimate, 82 percent of the units put into US service in 2019 were imported. In an industry survey published in 2025, the International Energy Agency found that large power transformers took up to four years to secure worldwide. It also found that their average lead times had almost doubled since 2021. A transformer's size is given as a power rating in megavolt-amperes (MVA). Measured by capacity, US factories supplied 29.2 percent of the transformers rated 60 MVA and above bought in the US in 2023, and imports supplied the rest."],["data-centers-and-power","Gas turbines. GE Vernova's gas equipment backlog and reserved factory slots stood at 116 GW in mid-2026. In July 2026 it expected to build gas turbines at a yearly rate of 20 GW in the third quarter of 2026, 24 GW in 2028 and 30 GW in 2030."],["data-centers-and-power","Firm generation, the kind that runs whatever the weather. The Nuclear Regulatory Commission has approved a fuel license amendment for the Crane plant. Constellation called the approval a major milestone toward restarting the plant in 2027."],["data-centers-and-power","Memory chips are also in short supply. Micron's quarterly report for the period ended 28 May 2026 says AI-driven growth in demand for memory and storage is outpacing industry supply. The memory shortage and the wait for power equipment both limit how much of the 2026 capital spending turns into working compute."],["data-centers-and-power","One rack can draw 142 kilowatts, and every watt of it comes back out as heat."],["data-centers-and-power","Air cooling works when each rack draws a moderate amount of power. Nvidia's GB300 NVL72 rack, which draws up to 142 kW, is liquid cooled. Reread: Cooling"],["data-centers-and-power","They are planned in gigawatts, and each gigawatt is the output of a large power station."],["data-centers-and-power","Epoch AI projects that OpenAI's seven Stargate sites in the United States will add up to more than nine gigawatts by 2029. Reread: How it works"],["data-centers-and-power","What slows down building an AI data center besides chips?"],["data-centers-and-power","Power equipment, which takes years to arrive."],["data-centers-and-power","In the United States in 2024, lead times of 36 months were commonly quoted for a large power transformer, against under a year before the pandemic. Reread: The chokepoint"],["data-centers-and-power","Which two countries used the most data center electricity in 2024?"],["data-centers-and-power","The United States, with 45 percent of the world's total, and China, with 25 percent."],["data-centers-and-power","Those are the International Energy Agency's estimates. Data centers made up around 3 percent of the growth in China's electricity demand from 2022 to 2024. Reread: Capacity and demand"],["data-centers-and-power","One AI rack can draw 142 kilowatts, too much heat for air, so racks are cooled with liquid."],["data-centers-and-power","The newest AI sites are planned in gigawatts, and each gigawatt is the output of a large power station."],["data-centers-and-power","Power equipment is one of the slow parts of building a data center. In 2024 lead times of 36 months were commonly quoted for a large transformer."],["data-centers-and-power","The United States used 45 percent of the world's data center electricity in 2024 and China 25 percent, by the International Energy Agency's estimate."],["component-costs","Epoch AI estimated in December 2025 that Nvidia's B200 AI chip cost about $6,400 to build, mostly for memory and packaging. Its processor silicon cost about $900."],["component-costs","Most of what it costs to build Nvidia's B200, an AI chip from its Blackwell line, goes to memory and packaging that a few firms supply. A bill of materials is the list of parts inside a product and what each one costs. Epoch AI estimated in December 2025 that the B200 cost about $6,400 to build. The two logic dies, the pieces of silicon that do the calculating, cost about $900 of that. The stacked memory beside them accounted for about half, and the packaging that wires the dies and memory together cost more than the dies. Three firms, SK hynix, Samsung and Micron, dominate the world market for that memory. One Taiwanese firm, TSMC, does that packaging."],["component-costs","Epoch AI says Nvidia's margin on Blackwell may be lower than the gap between the B200's build cost and its selling price suggests. It cites reports from March 2024 that put the B200's selling price at $30,000 to $40,000 per chip. Epoch AI notes that most Blackwell revenue comes from servers and rack-scale systems, which may carry lower margins."],["component-costs","In 2026 Micron's gross margin, the share of sales left after production costs, passed Nvidia's. Micron's rose from 39.8 percent for the year to August 2025 to 80.7 percent for the year to September 2026. It reached 86.8 percent in the last quarter of that year. Nvidia's was 75.0 percent in the quarter to July 2026. Epoch AI's estimate priced memory at $14 to $17 per gigabyte, before the 2026 rise in memory makers' sales and margins."],["component-costs","A B200, one of Nvidia's Blackwell AI chips, sells for far more than it costs to build. In December 2025 Epoch AI estimated that building one cost about $6,400. Epoch AI cites reports from March 2024 that put its selling price at $30,000 to $40,000 per chip. Most B200s are sold inside Nvidia's GB200 rack systems. Epoch AI's chip sales model, with data through October 2025, puts what Nvidia earns per GPU for the computing hardware in those racks at $33,000 to $42,000. That figure leaves out the networking gear in the racks."],["component-costs","Three numbers set the cost of a die, the finished rectangle of circuitry cut out of a wafer."],["component-costs","Wafer price. TSMC does not publish it. TSMC makes Nvidia's Blackwell chips on a custom-built process called 4NP. Epoch AI estimates $17,000 for a 12-inch ( 300 mm ) wafer on that process."],["component-costs","Dies per wafer. A wafer is a circle and dies are rectangles, so the edge of the wafer goes to waste. The bigger the die, the fewer fit. Each of the two logic dies in a B200 is about 800 mm². Nvidia calls them reticle-limited, meaning they are near the largest size a scanner can print in one shot."],["component-costs","Yield. Yield is the share of dies that work. Defects land at random, so a bigger die is more likely to catch one. Epoch AI models Blackwell die yield at 40 to 70 percent, centered on 60."],["component-costs","Together, those three numbers put the two dies inside a B200 at about $900. Epoch AI's estimate for the whole B200 counts only variable costs, which rise with each chip made. It leaves out fixed costs such as research and development."],["component-costs","The largest line on the bill is the 192 GB of high-bandwidth memory beside those dies, a generation called HBM3E. At $14 to $17 per gigabyte it comes to about $2,900, which Epoch AI counts as half of the build cost. Epoch AI says HBM prices are negotiated deal by deal and can vary significantly with volume and contract length. The $14 to $17 range dates from December 2025, before the 2026 rise in memory makers' sales and margins described below. SK hynix said DRAM and NAND flash prices rose significantly in the second quarter of 2026 from the quarter before, led by high-performance products for AI servers."],["component-costs","Few firms make this memory, and one of them says demand has outrun its supply. SK hynix, Samsung and Micron dominate the world market for it. SK hynix said in July 2026 that demand for its products had exceeded its available supply in recent quarters."],["component-costs","CoWoS -L, the TSMC process that mounts dies and memory on one carrier and wires them together, adds about $1,100, more than the logic dies it carries. Epoch AI models packaging yield at 65 to 95 percent. A package that fails testing loses its logic dies and memory stacks. Spreading that loss over the good units adds about $1,000 to each B200. Power delivery hardware, the circuit board, and final assembly and testing add $480. See Advanced packaging for how tight packaging capacity has been."],["component-costs","Epoch AI models each line as a range, deriving the packaging line from TSMC's advanced packaging revenue and Nvidia's share of CoWoS capacity."],["component-costs","Epoch AI says Nvidia's actual margin on Blackwell may be lower than the gap between the B200's build cost and its reported chip price suggests. The estimate covers the accelerator module only and leaves out servers and rack-scale systems. Epoch AI notes that most Blackwell revenue comes from those systems, which may carry lower margins."],["component-costs","Epoch AI's line-by-line estimate covers the B200, which is no longer Nvidia's newest chip. In its results for the quarter to July 2026, Nvidia said its Vera Rubin platform was ramping into full production. Each Rubin GPU carries up to 288 GB of HBM4, a newer generation of the stacked memory."],["component-costs","Each new generation of Nvidia rack costs its owner more per hour than the last. At rack scale, cost is measured per GPU-hour, one GPU running for one hour. For an operator that owns the machine, SemiAnalysis put a Vera Rubin NVL72 at $3.57 per GPU-hour in July 2026, against $1.84 for a GB200 and $2.36 for a GB300."],["component-costs","But SemiAnalysis found Rubin cheaper than GB200 and GB300 per token, a short chunk of text. Rubin stayed cheaper at every level of interactivity SemiAnalysis compared, where interactivity is the number of tokens per second each user receives. That finding rests on early results from the cloud provider CoreWeave running the DeepSeek R1 model, and SemiAnalysis said it had not verified them."],["component-costs","One level up, a cluster needs power and a network as well as servers. SemiAnalysis estimated in June 2024 that a cluster of 100,000 of Nvidia's earlier H100 GPUs cost over $4 billion in servers. The cluster needs more than 150 MW of data center capacity and uses 1.59 TWh a year, which costs $123.9 million at $0.078 per kWh. In the network design Nvidia recommended, 98,304 optical transceivers link the cluster's GPUs to the first layer of switches, called leaf switches."],["component-costs","Gross margin is highest at the memory maker Micron and lowest in assembly and test. The firms in design, equipment and leading-edge wafers earn gross margins of 50.3 to 75.0 percent, and those in assembly and test 16.8 to 27.3 percent. Micron's gross margin rose from 39.8 percent for the year to August 2025 to 80.7 percent for the year to September 2026. It reached 86.8 percent in the last quarter of that year."],["component-costs","Each figure except KLA's comes from the firm's own earnings release. KLA's shareholder letter gives only a non-GAAP gross margin for the quarter, 62.4 percent. KLA's non-GAAP figures adjust its results under US accounting rules, known as GAAP, to leave out items such as acquisition-related charges and restructuring, severance and other charges. For ASE the figure is its packaging and test segment. The company as a whole had a gross margin of 21.0 percent, because about a third of its revenue came from electronics manufacturing services, which earned 8.9 percent."],["component-costs","Two other firms' results give no gross margin. SK hynix's operating margin was 76 percent in the quarter to June 2026, and its revenue was up 257 percent from a year earlier. The substrate maker Ibiden's operating profit was 21.8 percent of net sales in the quarter to June 2026."],["component-costs","World chip sales are forecast to jump in 2026, with memory growing far faster than logic. The Semiconductor Industry Association, using monthly data compiled by World Semiconductor Trade Statistics, counted $791.7 billion of global chip sales in 2025. In its June 2026 forecast, World Semiconductor Trade Statistics put 2025 slightly higher, at $795.6 billion. It forecast $1.51 trillion for 2026, with memory growing about 250 percent and logic 37 percent."],["component-costs","In 2025 capital spending at five large tech firms far exceeded the world's sales of chipmaking equipment. The industry group SEMI counted $135.1 billion of semiconductor equipment billings in 2025. Capital spending at Alphabet, Amazon, Meta, Microsoft and Oracle came to $448.2 billion in 2025, the sum of Epoch AI's quarterly figures. Epoch AI says that spending would reach $770 billion in 2026 if the trend continues. These totals overlap, so they cannot be added together."],["component-costs","Each stage falls into one of three classes, by whether its cost falls as volume grows. A structurally expensive stage stays costly because the work is hard, capacity is short or one firm sets the price. A stage compressible with scale gets cheaper as volume grows. An already commoditized stage has several competing suppliers. The classes are a judgment drawn from the sources in this chapter and the stage chapters."],["component-costs","About $6,400, in Epoch AI's December 2025 estimate."],["component-costs","Reports in March 2024 put its selling price at $30,000 to $40,000 per chip. Epoch AI says Nvidia's margin may be lower than that gap suggests, because most Blackwell revenue comes from servers and racks, which may carry lower margins. Reread: The B200 bill of materials"],["component-costs","What is the most expensive part of an Nvidia B200?"],["component-costs","The stacked memory, about $2,900 in Epoch AI's December 2025 estimate, or about half of the cost to build."],["component-costs","The two logic chips that do the calculating cost about $900. Reread: Memory is the largest line"],["component-costs","Why does packaging add so much to the cost of a B200?"],["component-costs","The CoWoS-L process itself costs about $1,100, more than the $900 logic chips, and a package that fails testing wastes the chips and memory inside it."],["component-costs","In Epoch AI's estimate, spreading the cost of those failed packages over the good ones adds about $1,000 to each B200. Reread: Packaging, substrate and test"],["component-costs","Epoch AI estimated in December 2025 that a B200 cost about $6,400 to build, against a selling price of $30,000 to $40,000 per chip reported in March 2024."],["component-costs","The stacked memory is the most expensive part, about half of the cost."],["component-costs","Packaging costs more than the logic chips, and each package that fails wastes the chips and memory inside it."],["geopolitics","Since 2018 the United States has used export controls to limit China's access to advanced chips and chipmaking tools, and China has been learning to make both."],["geopolitics","Export controls work only when a country's own firms sell something the buyer cannot get elsewhere, so few governments can use them to much effect. An export control is a rule that requires the government's permission for a sale. The government names an item and a country or a buyer. From then on its own companies must hold a license before they ship that item to that country or buyer. The American government extends some of these rules to goods made abroad with American technology. The machines, software and chemicals used to make an advanced chip come from a short list of firms in the United States, the Netherlands and Japan, so those three governments can control who gets them."],["geopolitics","Japan and the Netherlands have aligned their own export controls with the American rules on chipmaking equipment. China has answered by building its own tools and by restricting sales of US chips in China. Chinese toolmakers supplied 35 percent of China's own chipmaking equipment market in 2025, up from 10 to 15 percent before 2022. Nvidia says the Chinese government restricted the sales of its H200 chip that the United States licensed in February 2026."],["geopolitics","The most advanced chips come mainly from Taiwan. It held 69 percent of the world's capacity for logic chips below 10 nanometers in 2022, by the count of the Semiconductor Industry Association and Boston Consulting Group."],["geopolitics","China cannot yet make the most advanced lithography machines, which print a chip 's finest circuits. China's leading lithography maker, SMEE, produces only older, less precise machines, among them some deep-ultraviolet types. China has also yet to show it can make high-bandwidth memory, the stacked memory beside an AI chip, in volume."],["geopolitics","In 2022 the United States changed its aim from staying ahead of China to pushing China's chipmaking back. In September 2022 US National Security Advisor Jake Sullivan said the United States must keep \"as large of a lead as possible\" in foundational technologies such as advanced logic and memory chips. The export rules of October 2022 were the first to apply his doctrine of a small yard with a high fence, meaning strict controls on a narrow set of technologies. Those rules went beyond the old aim of staying two technology nodes ahead of China and tried to push China's capability back below the level it had already reached."],["geopolitics","US license rules can target a single buyer or a whole country, and in 2022 the rules on advanced AI chips and the tools for advanced fabs began to cover all of China. In October 2018, for example, the Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS), the US Commerce Department's export control office, put the Chinese chip company Fujian Jinhua Integrated Circuit on its Entity List. From then on any item under US export rules needed a license to reach the company. The 2022 rules went further and required a license for any advanced AI chip, and any tool for an advanced fab, bound for China. BIS reviewed most applications under a presumption of denial, meaning it would normally refuse them. It reviewed applications for equipment bound for the China fabs of firms headquartered in the United States or allied and partner countries case by case."],["geopolitics","No country leads every segment. The United States leads four of the table's segments. The Netherlands, Japan and Taiwan lead two each, and South Korea and China one each."],["geopolitics","Equipment. TechInsights 2025 revenue by parent-company headquarters, from CSET's ETO Supply Chain Explorer."],["geopolitics","Materials. Fuji Keizai's survey by parent-company headquarters, as Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry published it in December 2025."],["geopolitics","Memory. Figures from the market research firm IDC, as SK hynix's US listing prospectus relays them."],["geopolitics","Logic capacity. The Semiconductor Industry Association and Boston Consulting Group's 2022 measurement of logic capacity, below 10 nm for Taiwan and at 28 nm and above for China."],["geopolitics","Advanced packaging is missing from the table because no public source splits its capacity by country. The Taiwanese chipmaker TSMC does not publish one either."],["geopolitics","US chip controls grew tighter from 2020 to 2024. In August 2020 BIS widened its Foreign Direct Product Rule to require a license for any foreign-made item produced with US technology and bound for Huawei. In 2022 BIS blocked China's access to the most advanced AI chips and to the tools to make them. It tightened those rules in 2023 and 2024. But in August 2025 the US government began licensing some sales of Nvidia's H20 chip to China. In February 2026 it began licensing small amounts of the H200."],["geopolitics","The United States has also approved large AI chip sales in the Gulf. In November 2025 Commerce authorized G42 of the United Arab Emirates and HUMAIN of Saudi Arabia to buy the equivalent of up to 35,000 Nvidia GB300 chips each under security and reporting conditions. On 10 July 2026 BIS moved the United Arab Emirates into Country Group A:5, the export-control group that holds close US allies. It named the Emirati government, G42 and eight US-headquartered AI companies as recipients that need no license for controlled AI chips and systems."],["geopolitics","The Export Controls page has the full timeline, with the legal citation for each rule."],["geopolitics","Firms can use controlled chips without any chip crossing a border, because renting out time on a chip does not count as exporting it. A Singapore data center selling time on an H200 already installed there, for example, moves nothing across a border. The AI Diffusion rule of January 2025 required a license for advanced AI chips bound anywhere in the world. For the data centers it approved, it said that API access to a model, and rented capacity for inference, \"are not prohibited\". On 13 May 2025 the Commerce Department said it would rescind the rule and told BIS officials not to enforce it."],["geopolitics","The American rules reach that trade through the firms holding the chips. A license under the 15 January 2026 rule for H200-class chips bound for China or Macau requires the applicant to obtain a description of the recipient's know-your-customer procedures. These are the recipient's checks on who its customers are. The applicant must also obtain the recipient's list of customers renting computing power in China and seven other places, among them Russia and Iran. The recipient must also promise that no algorithm trained on the chips is served to blacklisted or military end users."],["geopolitics","Smugglers route chips past the controls through Southeast Asia. Since 14 July 2025 Malaysia has required a permit to export, transship or transit any high-performance US-origin AI chip. On 25 March 2026 the Justice Department announced charges against three people accused of using Thai companies' names to order servers with export-controlled chips for China. The orders included one for $170 million that was never completed."],["geopolitics","In July 2025 the US House of Representatives' select committee on China cited estimates that a median of 140,000 chips were smuggled to China in 2024. A bill in Congress, the Chip Security Act, would require location verification on controlled chips within 180 days of enactment. The House Foreign Affairs Committee approved the House version 42-0 on 26 March 2026."],["geopolitics","US tool controls alone would only shift the sales to Dutch and Japanese suppliers, so the campaign depends on those two governments. Both have aligned their own controls on chipmaking equipment with the American rules."],["geopolitics","The Netherlands. The Dutch government began requiring export licenses for advanced deep-ultraviolet tools on 1 September 2023 and widened the controls in September 2024. On 1 April 2025 it extended them to measurement and inspection tools."],["geopolitics","Japan. Japan's controls on advanced manufacturing equipment took effect on 23 July 2023, apply to all destinations and name no country."],["geopolitics","US rules for South Korean fabs in China. BIS revoked the Validated End-User status that let Samsung's and SK hynix's China subsidiaries and Intel Semiconductor (Dalian) receive US equipment without individual licenses, effective 31 December 2025. BIS said it would license those fabs to keep running, but not to expand capacity or upgrade technology. SK hynix, which bought the Dalian fab from Intel, received an annual BIS license in December 2025 to ship approved US equipment to its China fabs during 2026."],["geopolitics","A BIS rule effective 29 September 2025 extended Entity List restrictions to any company at least 50 percent owned by one or more listed firms. The rule reached Nexperia, a Nijmegen chipmaker that supplies Europe's car industry, and the Dutch government said it worked to secure an exemption for the company. On 30 September the Dutch economy minister invoked the Goods Availability Act against Nexperia. He cited governance failures that risked moving technology out of Europe. The order aimed to keep Nexperia's production capabilities available to Europe in an emergency."],["geopolitics","On 4 October the Chinese authorities imposed an export control on Nexperia's operations in China, so deliveries from those operations to customers needed an export license. The Dutch government said uncertainty over licensing and long processing times caused chip shortages among Nexperia's customers and stopped production at some companies."],["geopolitics","Both the US rule and the Dutch order were suspended in November. On 10 November BIS suspended its rule until 9 November 2026. The minister suspended his order on 19 November. He cited constructive meetings with the Chinese authorities and the measures they had taken to ensure the supply of chips to Europe and the rest of the world. Europe holds a chokepoint in leading-edge lithography, but none in the mature-node chips its car industry uses."],["geopolitics","A bill in the US Congress would push allies to match US limits on chipmaking tools sold to China. The MATCH Act, a bill introduced on 8 April 2026, would ban sales of immersion deep-ultraviolet scanners to China. It would also restrict exports to, and servicing of, every chipmaking plant run by five Chinese companies, CXMT, Hua Hong, Huawei, SMIC and YMTC. It would give allies 150 days to match those limits before the United States extends its own controls to foreign-made items that use US software, technology or components."],["geopolitics","China has answered by replacing foreign chips at home, restricting some American suppliers, limiting its exports of minerals and building its own chipmaking tools. In 2024 China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology reportedly told Chinese telecom operators to strip foreign chips out of their networks by 2027."],["geopolitics","China has also taken measures against American suppliers. Micron, the American memory maker, failed a review by the Cyberspace Administration of China (CAC) on 21 May 2023 and lost its critical-infrastructure buyers in China. In September 2025 the CAC reportedly told firms including ByteDance and Alibaba to cancel Nvidia orders. Nvidia says the Chinese government restricted the H200 sales that the United States licensed in February 2026. It says China had earlier restricted licensed H20 sales too."],["geopolitics","China's Ministry of Commerce (MOFCOM) has also restricted exports of minerals."],["geopolitics","3 December 2024. MOFCOM banned exports of gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard materials to the United States, one day after the American chip rules."],["geopolitics","4 April 2025. It required export licenses for seven medium and heavy rare earths."],["geopolitics","9 October 2025. It announced that from 1 December 2025 foreign firms would need its license to export listed goods made abroad with Chinese rare earths worth 0.1 percent or more of their value. MOFCOM suspended that rule on 7 November 2025 until 10 November 2026."],["geopolitics","9 November 2025. MOFCOM suspended its ban on exports of gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard materials to the United States until 27 November 2026. It acted after Donald Trump and Xi Jinping met at the Asia-Pacific summit in October 2025."],["geopolitics","China's suspension of its October 2025 controls did not cover the April 2025 licensing rules for seven rare earths."],["geopolitics","Chinese toolmakers are winning a growing share of their home market. They held 10 to 15 percent of it before 2022, 25 percent in 2024 and 35 percent in 2025. They hold about 40 percent of the Chinese market for etch and deposition tools. But in September 2025 the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) judged that making its own extreme-ultraviolet machines remained firmly out of China's reach despite massive state investment."],["geopolitics","Chinese chipmakers remain behind at the leading edge, where TSMC makes 2 nm chips. SMIC's most advanced process, N+3, reaches the transistor density of TSMC's 6 nm-class process without extreme-ultraviolet scanners. It prints its tightest layers in several passes on deep-ultraviolet tools."],["geopolitics","In September 2025 the research firm SemiAnalysis conservatively put SMIC's capacity at 7 nm and below at 45,000 wafers a month by the end of 2025. It expected 60,000 in 2026 and 80,000 in 2027. Those figures count wafers, and how many working chips they give depends on yield, the share of chips on a wafer that work."],["geopolitics","SemiAnalysis judged that memory would limit China's output of AI chips before logic wafers did. It expected Huawei to ship about 805,000 of its Ascend AI chips in 2025, with dies made by both TSMC and SMIC. SemiAnalysis says Huawei got Ascend dies made at TSMC, in violation of export controls, while SMIC ramped up its own production. By its count, China had procured roughly 13 million memory stacks, enough for about 1.6 million Ascend 910C packages. It expected CXMT, China's own memory maker, to make only about 2 million stacks in 2026, enough for 250,000 to 300,000 more packages."],["geopolitics","Huawei said in September 2025 that its Ascend 950 chips, due in 2026, would carry high-bandwidth memory of its own design. It gave no figure for how much of that memory it would make."],["geopolitics","The US government helps pay for new chip plants with grants and a tax credit. The CHIPS and Science Act authorized about $52.7 billion for manufacturing incentives, research and workforce support. By July 2025 Commerce had awarded $30.9 billion of direct funding to 19 companies for 40 projects. The grants covered a median 14.2 percent of each project's capital cost. Commerce took a federal tax credit, the Advanced Manufacturing Investment Credit, into account when it set the size of those grants. Since the One Big Beautiful Bill Act of 2025, the credit covers 35 percent of qualified investment in an advanced chip plant placed in service after 2025, up from 25 percent."],["geopolitics","On 22 August 2025 the US government agreed to take a 9.9 percent stake in Intel by buying $8.9 billion of its stock. Of that sum, $5.7 billion was to come from CHIPS Act grants that Intel had been awarded but not yet paid. The other $3.2 billion was to come from Intel's award under Secure Enclave, a program to supply trusted and secure chips to the US Department of Defense."],["geopolitics","The United States has also used tariffs to draw chip investment. In January 2026 the American Institute in Taiwan and the Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the United States signed a memorandum on investment. Under it, Taiwanese chip and technology firms are to invest $250 billion in US semiconductor, energy and AI production. In the same memorandum the United States agreed to cap some of its national-security tariffs on Taiwanese goods at 15 percent. On 16 July 2026 TSMC announced another $100 billion for four more Arizona fabs, bringing its total Arizona investment to $265 billion."],["geopolitics","The European Commission says the EU still depends on other countries for advanced chip manufacturing. On 3 June 2026 the Commission proposed a Chips Act 2.0 to support advanced chip production in the EU."],["geopolitics","Japan backs a homegrown chipmaker, Rapidus. Rapidus began prototyping 2 nm gate-all-around transistors at its IIM-1 plant in July 2025. In February 2026 it raised another 267.6 billion yen, about $1.7 billion, from Japan's Information-Technology Promotion Agency (IPA) and 32 companies, aiming for 2 nm mass production by 2027. By June 2026 it had raised 424.95 billion yen in equity in all, after a further 150 billion yen from the IPA."],["geopolitics","CSIS puts China's cumulative state funding for chips since 2014 at an estimated $150 billion and calls the CHIPS Act substantially smaller in scale. The latest round of China's National Integrated Circuit Industry Investment Fund, the Big Fund, reached $47 billion. That round, the fund's third, was set up in May 2024."],["geopolitics","The world relies on Taiwan for most of its advanced chips. Taiwan's foundries held 81.9 percent of the world's contract chipmaking market in 2025, according to the Taiwan Semiconductor Industry Association's August 2026 report. TSMC makes its 2 nm chips only in Taiwan. Taiwan held 69 percent of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022."],["geopolitics","TSMC's advanced packaging capacity could not keep up with demand. Asked in October 2025 how much CoWoS packaging capacity he would add, TSMC's chairman said only that the company was \"working very hard to narrow the gap between the demand and supply\". He called wafer and packaging capacity both \"very tight\"."],["geopolitics","The silicon shield argument holds that this concentration deters an attack on Taiwan, because so many countries rely on its chips. The Stimson Center calls that open to debate, though many Taiwanese believe it."],["geopolitics","With an eye to that shield, Taiwan's rules keep TSMC's newest process at home first. As a result, TSMC's Arizona fabs have run a generation behind its fabs in Taiwan. The Stimson Center expected 2 nm production in Arizona in 2028 at the earliest. TSMC said in October 2025 that it was \"preparing to upgrade our technologies faster to N2 and more advanced process technologies in Arizona\". The four Arizona fabs it announced in July 2026 are to run at 2 nm or more advanced."],["geopolitics","TSMC has also announced two advanced packaging fabs for Arizona. But TSMC's work in Taiwan rests on a local supply chain of more than 300 firms, which the Stimson Center judged extremely difficult to copy in the United States. The US push for chip plants at home has raised fears in Taiwan that the shield could weaken."],["geopolitics","Taiwan and Korea. Fabs built abroad add capacity without taking any away from Taiwan and Korea. TSMC makes its 2 nm chips only in Taiwan. Korean firms took 82.5 percent of the world's high-bandwidth memory revenue in 2025, by the market research firm IDC's count."],["geopolitics","The Netherlands and Japan. Their toolmakers build the controlled machines, so the two governments gain a say in who gets them. China accounts for a falling share of the firms' sales. At ASML, China's share of net system sales fell from 41 percent in 2024 to 33 percent in 2025. That measure leaves out ASML's service and field option sales, which come from servicing and upgrading machines already installed. Against total net sales, the measure in the chart, it fell from 36.1 percent to 29.1 percent. At Tokyo Electron, China's share of sales fell from 44.4 percent in the year to March 2024 to 34.1 percent in the year to March 2026. The company said China's share of its sales dropped to 26.8 percent in the quarter to March 2026 because spending on leading-edge nodes grew faster than spending on mature nodes."],["geopolitics","The United States. The Semiconductor Industry Association, using data from World Semiconductor Trade Statistics, Gartner and Omdia, put US firms' share of all chip sales in 2025 at 53.4 percent, the highest since 1984. US firms also took 65 percent of the world's logic chip sales in 2022. Commerce expects the CHIPS-funded projects to lift the US share of global leading-edge logic chip manufacturing from 0 percent in 2022 to 20 percent by 2030."],["geopolitics","China. Chinese suppliers are replacing foreign ones at home, most visibly in mature-node and commodity chips. In September 2025 SemiAnalysis expected China to make fewer Ascend chips in 2026 than in 2025 unless memory was smuggled in, because its own memory maker could supply too little."],["geopolitics","What does a country need for its export controls to work?"],["geopolitics","Its own firms must sell something the buyer cannot get elsewhere."],["geopolitics","The machines, software and chemicals used to make an advanced chip come from a short list of firms in the United States, the Netherlands and Japan. So those three governments can control who gets them. Reread: Chokepoints and who holds them"],["geopolitics","How do US export controls reach goods made in other countries?"],["geopolitics","Through the Foreign Direct Product Rule, which extends some US rules to goods made abroad with American technology."],["geopolitics","In August 2020 the United States widened the rule to require a license for any foreign-made item produced with US technology and bound for Huawei. Reread: The US export-control campaign, 2018 to today"],["geopolitics","What share of China's own chipmaking equipment market did Chinese toolmakers supply in 2025?"],["geopolitics","35 percent, up from 10 to 15 percent before 2022."],["geopolitics","They hold about 40 percent of the Chinese market for etch and deposition tools. But in September 2025 CSIS judged that making its own EUV machines remained firmly out of China's reach. Reread: China's response"],["geopolitics","What share of ASML's system sales went to China in 2025?"],["geopolitics","33 percent, down from 41 percent in 2024."],["geopolitics","At Tokyo Electron, China's share of sales fell from 44.4 percent in the year to March 2024 to 34.1 percent in the year to March 2026. Reread: Who gains and who pays"],["geopolitics","Taiwan held 69 percent of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022, and TSMC makes its 2 nm chips only in Taiwan. Reread: Taiwan"],["geopolitics","An export control works only when a country's firms sell something the buyer cannot get elsewhere."],["geopolitics","US controls also cover some foreign goods made with American technology."],["geopolitics","Chinese toolmakers' share of China's own chipmaking equipment market rose from 10 to 15 percent before 2022 to 35 percent in 2025."],["geopolitics","China's share of ASML's and Tokyo Electron's sales has fallen since 2024."],["geopolitics","Taiwan held 69 percent of the world's logic capacity below 10 nm in 2022, and TSMC makes its 2 nm chips only there."]]}};
